E["item:bernice-s-necklace"] = {t="item",n="Bernice's Necklace",z="elwynn",s="At Stonefield Farm in Elwynn Forest, Bernice keeps her late husband's necklace close.",h="At Stonefield Farm in Elwynn Forest, Bernice keeps her late husband's necklace close.",sec={{t="A Soldier's Lost Charm",b="Auntie Bernice Stonefield keeps her husband's necklace at Stonefield Farm. He was a veteran of Stormwind's military campaigns and carried the charm into battle for good fortune. Bernice says tragedy came only in his final campaign. That was the one expedition when he forgot to bring it. Since his death, the keepsake has remained among her most cherished possessions.",sp=0},{t="Stolen by Scavengers",b="Young Billy Maclure was exploring near the Fargodeep Mine when the shiny necklace slipped from his grasp. Goldtooth, a prominent kobold inside the mine, spotted it and carried it away. Like other kobolds, he was drawn to bright, valuable trinkets. He kept the necklace among the treasures he had scavenged.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Whose necklace was this originally?",a="Auntie Bernice Stonefield's late husband owned the necklace. He wore it as a good-luck charm during Stormwind's military campaigns.",al={"who owned the necklace","bernice necklace owner","husband necklace"},it="identity"},{q="How did the necklace end up with the kobolds?",a="Billy Maclure saw a large kobold with gold teeth pick up the necklace near the Fargodeep Mine and carry it away. Auntie Bernice hopes it can be recovered.",al={"how was it lost","why does goldtooth have it","who took the necklace"}},{q="Why is the necklace so important to Auntie Bernice?",a="The necklace is a cherished memory of Bernice's late husband. He believed it protected him in battle, and the only time he fell in war was the day he left it behind.",al={"why does bernice want it","bernice husband story","is the necklace magic"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who is Goldtooth?",a="Goldtooth is a prominent kobold scavenger with a lair inside the Fargodeep Mine in Elwynn Forest. He collects shiny baubles and took the necklace after it was dropped nearby.",al={"what is goldtooth","goldtooth lore","who has the necklace"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance farm families in Elwynn Forest, the necklace recalls the toll Stormwind's long military campaigns take on everyday lives."},kw={"auntie bernice","bernice's necklace","billy maclure","fargodeep mine","goldtooth","lucky charm","stonefield"},rel={"npc:auntie-bernice-stonefield","quest:87","subzone:fargodeep-mine","subzone:stonefield-farm","topic:kobold","zone:elwynn","quest:62"},src={"Bernice's Necklace","Goldtooth (quest)"}}
E["item:bloodstone-choker"] = {t="item",n="Bloodstone Choker",z="elwynn",s="In Stormwind, Gakin the Darkbinder’s Bloodstone Choker binds a warlock’s rite to the void. His apprentice stole the talisman and fled to the Defias Brotherhood.",h="In Stormwind, Gakin the Darkbinder’s Bloodstone Choker binds a warlock’s rite to the void.",sec={{t="A Stolen Conduit",b="Gakin the Darkbinder, a warlock mentor beneath Stormwind’s Slaughtered Lamb, once held the Bloodstone Choker. His apprentice Surena Caledon betrayed him and stole it. She fled into Elwynn’s forests and joined the Defias Brotherhood, taking the enchanted talisman with her. Now she is at the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch. The choker must be reclaimed before the bandits use its power.",sp=1},{t="Taming the Void",b="Carved from bloodstone, the choker bridges the mortal world and the twisting shadows of the Twisting Nether. In the crypts beneath the tavern, Gakin channels its magic at the summoning circle. A hostile Voidwalker answers from the void. A warlock must face the furious creature in direct combat and subdue it while wielding the talisman. Only then is the will to command such a guardian proved.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Bloodstone Choker?",a="Warlocks use the Bloodstone Choker, an enchanted bloodstone necklace, as a ritual conduit. Its magic can tear through reality and summon an unruly Voidwalker from the Nether.",al={"bloodstone choker","what is the choker","what does the choker do"},it="identity"},{q="Who originally owned the choker?",a="Gakin the Darkbinder first owned the choker. He trains warlocks in a covert basement beneath The Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind’s Mage Quarter.",al={"who owns the choker","gakin choker","where did the choker come from"}},{q="Why was the choker stolen?",a="Surena Caledon stole the choker from her mentor, Gakin, then fled to join the Defias Brotherhood. She sought power among the bandits hiding in Elwynn Forest.",al={"who stole it","why did surena steal it","surena caledon choker"},it="motive"},{q="How is the choker used in warlock training?",a="A warlock activates the recovered choker over the summoning circle in the crypts beneath The Slaughtered Lamb. It draws out a Voidwalker, which the aspiring warlock must defeat and subdue to command the demon.",al={"how to use choker","voidwalker ritual choker","the binding choker"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is the Bloodstone Choker wanted?",a="Gakin the Darkbinder values the Bloodstone Choker as a potent magical catalyst required to summon and bind a voidwalker. After his former apprentice Surena Caledon stole it to aid the Defias Brotherhood, Gakin seeks its return to restore his arcane authority and test new warlocks in the crypts beneath the Slaughtered Lamb.",al={"why do they want bloodstone choker","who wants the bloodstone choker","why does gakin want the choker"},it="why_wanted",add="9d3659ea"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As an Alliance warlock, recovering the Bloodstone Choker marks a passage from basic spellcraft to command of formidable demonic minions.",["faction:Alliance"]="Surena Caledon’s flight to the Defias Brotherhood shows that outlaws in Elwynn seek dangerous occult relics to strengthen their rebellion against Stormwind."},kw={"bloodstone choker","defias","gakin the darkbinder","surena caledon","the binding","the slaughtered lamb","voidwalker","warlock"},rel={"quest:1471","npc:gakin-the-darkbinder","quest:1688","subzone:slaughtered-lamb","topic:warlock","topic:defias-brotherhood","zone:stormwind","zone:elwynn"},src={"Bloodstone Choker","The Binding (Voidwalker, Stormwind)"}}
E["item:brass-collar"] = {t="item",n="Brass Collar",z="elwynn",s="At the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch, Princess wears the collar Ma Stonefield wants as proof the sow is gone.",h="At the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch, Princess wears the collar Ma Stonefield wants as proof the sow is gone.",sec={{t="A Trophy of Farmyard Rivalry",b="Princess is the Brackwell family’s huge, prize-winning sow. She roams east of the Maclure homestead, and her hunger often carries her into Stonefield Farm’s crops. After losing valuable vegetables to Princess, Ma Stonefield seeks someone willing to slay her. The collar proves the sow has been put down, so she can no longer raid Stonefield’s fields.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Brass Collar come from?",a="Princess wears the collar at the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch in eastern Elwynn Forest, past the Maclure farm.",al={"brass collar source","who drops brass collar","where to get brass collar"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Ma Stonefield want the collar?",a="Princess eats Ma Stonefield’s prize vegetables. The collar proves she has been put down before she can ruin more of Ma Stonefield’s harvest.",al={"why stonefield wants collar","ma stonefield collar purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who owns Princess?",a="Princess belongs to the Brackwell family and roams their pumpkin patch with her smaller boar companions.",al={"princess owner","who owns the pig"}},{q="Can anyone other than Princess drop this item?",a="Only Princess can yield the collar. It is fashioned to fit the Brackwells’ enormous prized sow.",al={"other collar drops","where else find brass collar"},gp=true},{q="What is the Brass Collar?",a="The Brass Collar is the distinctive neckband worn by Princess, a prize-winning sow owned by the Brackwell family. Due to Princess's enormous size and habit of raiding neighboring crops, the collar serves as undeniable proof that the destructive beast has finally been put down.",al={"what is brass collar","brass collar lore","who wears brass collar"},it="identity",add="92e34b72"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer helping Elwynn’s rural folk, taking Princess’s collar helps settle a feud between neighboring farms."},kw={"brackwell pumpkin patch","brass collar","elwynn forest","ma stonefield","princess","princess must die","stonefield farm"},rel={"quest:88","npc:ma-stonefield","subzone:brackwell-pumpkin-patch","subzone:stonefield-farm","zone:elwynn"},src={"Brass Collar","Princess Must Die! (Classic)"}}
E["item:bundle-of-wood"] = {t="item",n="Bundle of Wood",z="elwynn",s="Eastvale Logging Camp needs wood sent west for Stormwind's rebuilding.",h="Eastvale Logging Camp needs wood sent west for Stormwind's rebuilding.",sec={{t="Abandoned Timber",b="Eastvale Logging Camp sends freshly chopped timber west for buildings and other construction in the Kingdom of Stormwind. But bears and wolves have entered the groves northwest of camp. The frightened loggers fled, leaving their Bundles of Wood among the trees. With the shipment deadline near, overseer Raelen needs travelers to recover the timber before the lumber contracts are breached.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why were these bundles of wood abandoned in the woods?",a="Wolves and bears drove off the loggers harvesting timber northwest of Eastvale Logging Camp. The workers left their freshly chopped Bundles of Wood on the forest floor.",al={"why is wood on ground","why abandon wood","abandoned lumber elwynn"},it="origin"},{q="Who needs this wood collected?",a="Raelen, an overseer at Eastvale Logging Camp, needs the wood gathered soon to meet an approaching lumber shipment deadline.",al={"who wants the wood","raelen lumber","wood turn in"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where are these bundles found?",a="The bundles lie among the trees directly northwest of Eastvale Logging Camp, where Elwynn's bears and wolves prowl.",al={"bundle of wood location","where is the wood","eastvale wood spots"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why didn't the town guards clear out the beasts?",a="Raelen asked Deputy Rainer for help, but Elwynn's marshals and guards are stretched thin across the region. The lumber workers need outside help to recover the logs quickly.",al={"why no guards","deputy rainer wood","guards at eastvale"},it="threat"},{q="What is a Bundle of Wood?",a="These are stacks of freshly harvested timber cut and gathered by the laborers of the Eastvale Logging Camp. Prepared for transport and processing, they represent the camp's ongoing lumber operations in eastern Elwynn Forest.",al={"what is bundle of wood","bundle of wood elwynn","what are these wood bundles"},it="identity",add="e892b12c"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, gathering the bundles helps Stormwind rebuild and keeps vital timber shipments on time for settlements across Elwynn and Westfall."},kw={"bundle of wood","eastvale","elwynn","logging camp","lumber","raelen","timber"},rel={"quest:5545","subzone:eastvale-logging-camp","zone:elwynn","npc:deputy-rainer","subzone:westbrook-garrison"},src={"Bundle of Wood","A Bundle of Trouble"}}
E["item:crate-of-horseshoes"] = {t="item",n="Crate of Horseshoes",z="elwynn",s="In Elwynn, Crate of Horseshoes carries fifty iron shoes toward Lakeshire.",h="In Elwynn, Crate of Horseshoes carries fifty iron shoes toward Lakeshire.",sec={{t="A Delivery to Lakeshire",b="Smith Argus forged fifty fresh horseshoes in Goldshire, then packed them into a crate and hammered it shut. Verner Osgood ordered them for Lakeshire, where pressure from gnolls and orcs leaves local craftsmen reliant on Elwynn for essential metal goods. The delivery meets Verner's desperate need for equipment, and Argus includes a stern bill of sale so the Redridge craftsman knows frontier survival comes at a steep price.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside the Crate of Horseshoes?",a="Smith Argus forged fifty iron horseshoes in Goldshire and packed them in the crate. An attached bill demands payment from the buyer.",al={"contents of crate","what is in the crate","horseshoe crate contents"},it="item"},{q="Who ordered this crate?",a="Verner Osgood commissioned the horseshoes. He is a tradesman and craftsman in Lakeshire in the Redridge Mountains, and needs them to keep his work and local draft animals running.",al={"who wants the horseshoes","verner horseshoes","crate recipient"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who crafted these horseshoes?",a="Smith Argus, Goldshire's blacksmith in Elwynn Forest, forged the horseshoes, packed the crate, and prepared it for delivery.",al={"who made the horseshoes","blacksmith in goldshire","smith argus"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Verner need horseshoes from Elwynn?",a="Hostile Blackrock orcs and gnolls besiege Lakeshire, leaving the frontier settlement isolated and short of raw materials and trade goods. Local workers must bring basic supplies from safer settlements such as Goldshire.",al={"why redridge needs shoes","why import horseshoes","lakeshire supply problem"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Crate of Horseshoes?",a="The Crate of Horseshoes is a heavy wooden delivery box containing fifty newly forged horseshoes, packed alongside an invoice note. Smith Argus prepared the shipment in Goldshire to fulfill an order placed by Verner Osgood, who desperately needs fresh iron to keep draft animals and mounts shod in nearby Lakeshire.",al={"what is crate of horseshoes","crate of horseshoes lore","what are the horseshoes for"},it="identity",add="50a21bee"}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="The delivery shows the steady demand for basic smithing goods along frontier roads between towns. Lakeshire depends on Goldshire's anvil to keep its draft animals working.",["faction:Alliance"]="Couriers carrying goods between Elwynn and Redridge keep the kingdom's fragile trade routes open and outlying garrisons equipped, even as Stormwind withholds military reinforcement."},kw={"crate of horseshoes","elwynn forest","goldshire","lakeshire","redridge","smith argus","verner osgood"},rel={"quest:119","quest:118","npc:verner-osgood","zone:elwynn","quest:124","quest:126","quest:122","topic:gnoll"},src={"Crate of Horseshoes","Return to Verner"}}
E["item:crystal-kelp-frond"] = {t="item",n="Crystal Kelp Frond",z="elwynn",s="Murlocs carry Crystal Kelp Fronds from the ocean to Crystal Lake in Elwynn Forest. William Pestle in Goldshire seeks them for an invisibility liquor.",h="Murlocs carry Crystal Kelp Fronds from the ocean to Crystal Lake in Elwynn Forest.",sec={{t="A Rare Aquatic Reagent",b="Crystal Kelp Fronds come from saltwater oceans, which makes them unusual in Elwynn Forest’s fresh water. Along Crystal Lake’s shores, murloc tribes gather and keep the fronds for reasons of their own. Alchemists value the fronds for their strange power to distort sight. William Pestle in Goldshire uses them as the chief ingredient in an invisibility liquor meant to help sweethearts slip past watchful family eyes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does crystal kelp naturally grow?",a="Crystal kelp grows in saltwater oceans. It does not grow naturally in freshwater lakes, though murlocs gather the cuttings and carry them to places such as Crystal Lake.",al={"where does crystal kelp grow","crystal kelp origin","kelp habitat"},it="origin"},{q="Why do the murlocs at Crystal Lake have ocean kelp?",a="The entry gives no reason the murlocs at Crystal Lake have ocean kelp. It says they gather and keep the fronds for reasons of their own.",al={"why do murlocs have kelp","murloc kelp reason"}},{q="Who wants Crystal Kelp Fronds in Goldshire?",a="William Pestle, an apothecary at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, wants Crystal Kelp Fronds. He uses them to brew invisibility liquor for Maybell Maclure, so she can slip away from her family vineyard to meet Tommy Joe Stonefield.",al={"who needs crystal kelp","william pestle kelp"},sp=1,it="target"},{q="What properties does crystal kelp possess?",a="Alchemists value Crystal Kelp Fronds for their ability to distort sight. William Pestle uses them in an invisibility liquor meant to help sweethearts pass unseen.",al={"kelp effects","what does crystal kelp do"},it="power"},{q="What is a Crystal Kelp Frond?",a="A Crystal Kelp Frond is a cutting from crystal kelp, a rare aquatic plant native to the ocean. Although primarily marine vegetation, these fronds are sometimes gathered and kept by murlocs around freshwater bodies such as Crystal Lake. Alchemists value the fronds for their potent, translucent properties, which can be harnessed to brew specialized draughts such as invisibility liquor.",al={"what is crystal kelp frond","crystal kelp info","what is crystal kelp"},it="identity",add="e295764f"},{q="Why does anyone want Crystal Kelp Fronds?",a="William Pestle, the alchemist in Goldshire, requires crystal kelp fronds to brew a potent invisibility liquor. He intends to use the concoction to aid young Maybell Maclure, allowing her to slip away from her family's watchful vineyard undetected to secretly meet her forbidden beau, Tommy Joe Stonefield.",al={"who needs crystal kelp","why gather crystal kelp fronds","use for crystal kelp"},it="why_wanted",add="8bde59b0"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Crystal Kelp Fronds grow in water, unlike herbs rooted in soil, and do not grow in standard herb nodes across Elwynn. Herbalists and gatherers must pry them from local murlocs, who keep the fronds."},kw={"crystal kelp","crystal kelp frond","crystal lake","goldshire","invisibility liquor","murloc","william pestle"},rel={"quest:112","subzone:crystal-lake","npc:william-pestle","item:invisibility-liquor","topic:murloc","subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn","subzone:maclure-vineyards"},src={"Crystal Kelp Frond","Collecting Kelp"}}
E["item:garrick-s-head"] = {t="item",n="Garrick's Head",z="elwynn",s="At Northshire's vineyards, Garrick Padfoot's severed head proves the cutthroat is dead. The authorities at Northshire Abbey require it before they pay the bounty.",h="At Northshire's vineyards, Garrick Padfoot's severed head proves the cutthroat is dead.",sec={{t="A Bandit's End",b="For weeks, Garrick Padfoot and his gang harassed Northshire Valley's farmers and merchants. Stormwind's defenses were stretched thin, and local guards were busy with kobolds and Defias bandits. So Garrick hid in a shack near the vineyards and raided passing trade. Deputy Willem offered a bounty for the outlaw's death, seeking someone to kill him and bring back proof.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Garrick Padfoot?",a="Garrick Padfoot was a cutthroat who terrorized Northshire Valley's farmers, vineyard workers, and traveling merchants. He set up an outpost with his gang east of Northshire Abbey, across the river.",al={"who is garrick","garrick padfoot lore","who was padfoot"},it="identity"},{q="Why is a severed head needed to collect the bounty?",a="Deputy Willem and the Northshire authorities require proof of Garrick's death before paying the bounty.",al={"why his head","proof of death","why take garricks head"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where was Garrick Padfoot hiding?",a="Padfoot hid in a small wooden shack east of Northshire Abbey, across the river bridge near the Northshire vineyards.",al={"where is garrick","garrick shack location","where to find garrick padfoot"},it="place"},{q="Who pays the bounty for Garrick's head?",a="Deputy Willem posted the bounty and pays it when he receives Garrick's head. He is stationed just outside Northshire Abbey's entrance.",al={"who wants garricks head","turn in garricks head","who turned in garrick head"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Garrick's Head?",a="This severed head is the gruesome proof of the demise of Garrick Padfoot, a notorious cutthroat who has terrorized local farmers and merchants across Northshire Valley. Bringing this trophy back to the Abbey confirms his band of brigands has lost its ringleader.",al={"what is garricks head","garrick head item","who does this head belong to"},it="identity",add="cb1a40d1"},{q="Where does Garrick's Head come from?",a="It is claimed directly from Garrick Padfoot himself. The rogue made his camp at a small shack nestled near the Northshire vineyards, across the river to the east, surrounded by loyal thugs protecting his plunder.",al={"where do you get garricks head","who drops garricks head","garricks head source"},it="origin",add="79b2de99"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, taking Padfoot's head strikes an early blow against the lawlessness spreading through Elwynn Forest.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, eliminating Padfoot shows local ruffians that banditry meets deadly, professional blades."},kw={"bounty","deputy willem","elwynn forest","garrick padfoot","garrick's head","northshire abbey","northshire valley"},rel={"quest:6","subzone:northshire-abbey","zone:elwynn"},src={"Garrick's Head","Bounty on Garrick Padfoot"}}
E["item:glyph-of-azora"] = {t="item",n="Glyph of Azora",z="elwynn",s="From the Tower of Azora, Theocritus watches threats beyond Elwynn. His glyphs carry the Eye of Azora's power farther, so he can read enemies' thoughts and plans.",h="From the Tower of Azora, Theocritus watches threats beyond Elwynn.",sec={{t="Eyes Across the Border",b="From his tower in Elwynn Forest, Theocritus watches hostile powers. The Eye of Azora lets him see far away, but it cannot reach the minds or plans of his adversaries. So he places small focuses called Glyphs of Azora on distant surfaces. Each one anchors his magic, letting him read enemy intentions and project his voice across miles to speak with field agents.",sp=0},{t="Espionage in Redridge",b="In the Redridge Mountains, Theocritus places glyphs in hostile territory. He fixes the first to an ancient lion statue overlooking the Tower of Ilgalar. His rival, the dark wizard Morganth, holds that stronghold. Through the glyph, Theocritus enters Morganth's mind and finds a dispute with the Blackrock orcs at nearby Stonewatch Keep. To learn the cause, he sends a second glyph into the heights of the keep's intact watchtower, hidden inside a discarded liquor jar.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Glyph of Azora?",a="Theocritus uses a Glyph of Azora to extend the Eye of Azora's reach. Set in a distant place, it anchors his magic so he can read his adversaries' thoughts and plans and speak with field agents across miles.",al={"what does glyph of azora do","why use glyph of azora","glyph of azora purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Who created the Glyph of Azora?",a="Theocritus created the Glyph of Azora. He lives in the Tower of Azora along Elwynn Forest's eastern border.",al={"who made the glyph","glyph of azora creator","theocritus glyph"},it="origin"},{q="Where are the Glyphs of Azora placed?",a="One glyph is fixed to an ancient lion statue overlooking the Tower of Ilgalar. A second is hidden in a discarded liquor jar in the intact watchtower at Stonewatch Keep.",al={"where do i put the glyph","glyph placement locations","where does glyph go"},it="target"},{q="Why is Theocritus spying on the Tower of Ilgalar?",a="The Tower of Ilgalar is Morganth's stronghold. The rogue dark wizard is Theocritus's rival, and the glyph lets Theocritus read his thoughts and plans.",al={"why spy on morganth","theocritus ilgalar","morganth feud"},it="conflict"},{q="How does the glyph allow Theocritus to speak to people?",a="Fixed to a distant surface, the glyph anchors Theocritus's magic. It lets him project his voice across miles to speak with field agents.",al={"talking glyph","theocritus voice in glyph","can the glyph talk"},it="power"},{q="What is the Glyph of Azora?",a="The Glyph of Azora is an enchanted arcane marker crafted by the wizard Theocritus at the Tower of Azora. Working in tandem with his scrying focus, the Eye of Azora, these inscribed stones serve as remote listening posts. Once affixed to a surface near an area of interest, a glyph allows Theocritus to delve into the minds and thoughts of his targets from across great distances, as well as project his voice to whoever stands beside it.",al={"what is glyph of azora","glyph of azora item","tell me about glyph of azora"},it="identity",add="16152ed3"},{q="Why does Theocritus want you to plant the Glyph of Azora?",a="Theocritus relies on these glyphs to conduct deep espionage against dangerous adversaries in Redridge. While the Eye of Azora lets him view places from afar, it cannot pierce minds without a conduit nearby. Placing a glyph near the Tower of Ilgalar lets him probe the thoughts and future plans of his rival, the renegade mage Morganth, while planting another near Stonewatch Keep helps him unravel Morganth's contention with the Blackrock orcs.",al={"why plant glyph of azora","why does theocritus want the glyph placed","glyph of azora purpose"},it="why_wanted",add="7c5a9e02"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can use arcane divination to extend crystal scrying into targeted telepathy and remote sensory relays.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can use the glyphs to gather intelligence on Morganth and the Blackrock orcs at Stonewatch Keep."},kw={"glyph of azora","morganth","redridge","scrying","stonewatch keep","theocritus","tower of azora","tower of ilgalar"},rel={"npc:theocritus","quest:94","quest:248","subzone:tower-of-ilgalar","quest:249","subzone:stonewatch-keep","topic:mage","zone:elwynn"},src={"Glyph of Azora","A Watchful Eye","Looking Further"}}
E["item:glyphic-letter"] = {t="item",n="Glyphic Letter",z="elwynn",s="At Northshire Abbey, Glyphic Letter calls promising novitiates to arcane study. After serving the garrison, they are summoned upstairs to Khelden Bremen, the resident mage trainer.",h="At Northshire Abbey, Glyphic Letter calls promising novitiates to arcane study.",sec={{t="A Summons to the Arcane",b="Khelden Bremen seals Glyphic Letter with his own insignia. Apprentice spellcasters receive it after proving their discipline in Northshire Valley. The summons draws them from basic field duties into dedicated magical instruction within the abbey.\n\nBefore they take up the arcane, Bremen tests each student's resolve. Its forces are dangerous, its scrutiny unyielding, and its burdens heavy.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Glyphic Letter?",a="Khelden Bremen writes and seals Glyphic Letter as a summons to instruction. It directs aspiring human mages to find him in the upper chambers of Northshire Abbey for formal arcane schooling.",al={"what is this letter","glyphic letter item","khelden letter"},it="identity"},{q="Who sends the Glyphic Letter?",a="Khelden Bremen, the mage trainer at Northshire Abbey, seals the letter with his insignia. Garrison command hands it over after an apprentice proves their mettle against nearby vermin.",al={"who wrote it","who gave me glyphic letter","letter sender"},it="origin"},{q="Where do I take the Glyphic Letter?",a="Take the letter inside Northshire Abbey. Enter behind Marshal McBride, follow the left corridor, climb the stairs, and look toward the back room where Khelden Bremen teaches the arcane.",al={"where to go","where is khelden bremen","khelden location"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Khelden send for young mages?",a="Khelden wants to test your determination. He warns that pursuing the arcane brings fear and respect, and means challenging potent forces. He needs to know you have the will to endure that fate.",al={"why does khelden want me","mage trainer reason","what does khelden want"},it="motive"},{q="Why does Khelden Bremen want the Glyphic Letter delivered to you?",a="The letter serves as an official summons and a trial of resolve for fledgling mages. Sealed with his personal insignia, Khelden Bremen's note lays out the perilous and daunting path of the arcane, warning you of the fear and challenges that accompany the pursuit of forbidden knowledge. Handing it to you ensures you are willing to face that fate before he undertakes your formal training.",al={"why glyphic letter","why was i given the glyphic letter","purpose of glyphic letter"},it="why_wanted",add="4321b6bd"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Mage, this marked dispatch calls you upstairs to begin formal study of the Alliance's arcane traditions under Khelden Bremen.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you begin your service to Stormwind's magical disciplines with this summons. Northshire Abbey has sheltered arcane students throughout the kingdom's history."},kw={"arcane","elwynn forest","glyphic letter","khelden bremen","mage trainer","marshal mcbride","northshire abbey"},rel={"quest:3104","npc:khelden-bremen","subzone:northshire-abbey","npc:marshal-mcbride","topic:mage","zone:elwynn"},src={"Glyphic Letter","Glyphic Letter (quest)"}}
E["item:gold-dust"] = {t="item",n="Gold Dust",z="elwynn",s="In Elwynn Forest, Gold Dust passes from kobold hands to local buyers. Miners still seek whole veins of ore.",h="In Elwynn Forest, Gold Dust passes from kobold hands to local buyers.",sec={{t="A Pouch Full of Scraps",b="Kobolds dig through the Fargodeep and Jasperlode mines beneath Elwynn Forest. Rather than refine the gold dust they find, they keep it in pockets and pouches. Local peddlers and fences want those scraps, hoping to profit without paying official smelting tariffs.",sp=0},{t="Goldshire's Black Market",b="In Goldshire, Remy \"Two Times\" asks travelers to bring him recovered gold dust. He says he offers the best price in town, trading coin and suspicious tokens for raw dust on behalf of unnamed associates. Travelers retrieve the gold from kobolds, while the brokers build wealth beneath the noses of the Stormwind guards.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does Gold Dust come from?",a="Kobolds throughout Elwynn Forest carry Gold Dust. Miners, tunnelers, geomancers, and their leader Goldtooth gather and hoard it as they dig through the hills.",al={"how to get gold dust","gold dust drop","where find gold dust"},it="origin"},{q="Which mines hold the most kobolds carrying Gold Dust?",a="Kobolds carrying dust overrun Fargodeep Mine south of Goldshire and Jasperlode Mine to the northeast.",al={"where are the mines","best mine for gold dust","mine locations"},gp=true},{q="Who buys Gold Dust in Elwynn Forest?",a="Remy \"Two Times,\" a shady dealer outside the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, buys collected pouches of Gold Dust for money and tokens from his associates.",al={"who wants gold dust","remy two times gold dust","turn in gold dust"},gp=true},{q="Why do kobolds carry dust instead of ingots?",a="Kobolds lack the discipline and means to smelt ore properly. As they dig through rock with crude pickaxes, loose gold dust gathers on their belongings and in small pouches they carry as shiny trinkets.",al={"why do kobolds have dust","kobold gold"}},{q="What is Gold Dust?",a="Gold Dust consists of fine, raw flecks of precious gold mined by the kobold infestations lurking beneath Elwynn Forest. Rather than refined currency or poured bullion, it is the raw residue kobolds chip directly out of rich veins in places like the Fargodeep and Jasperlode mines.",al={"what is gold dust","gold dust item","about gold dust"},it="identity",add="38570104"},{q="Why does Remy Two Times want Gold Dust?",a="Remy \"Two Times\" in Goldshire buys up raw gold dust for his own trade and shadowy associates. Kobolds possess little sense for smelting ingots, leaving plenty of untracked mineral wealth on their bodies for anyone bold enough to take it from them and sell it off.",al={"why does remy want gold dust","why want gold dust","remy two times gold dust why"},it="why_wanted",add="4a74ebdb"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you seek solid veins of copper and tin with pick and pan. Kobold dust suggests Elwynn's underground passages hold richer lodes than standard surveys reveal.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can learn how the underworld moves unrefined, untracked dust through shady dealers like Remy \"Two Times,\" hiding raw wealth from Stormwind's magistrates."},kw={"elwynn","fargodeep","gold dust","goldshire","goldtooth","jasperlode","kobold","remy two times"},rel={"quest:47","npc:remy-two-times","topic:kobold","subzone:fargodeep-mine","subzone:jasperlode-mine","subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn","quest:87"},src={"Gold Dust","Gold Dust Exchange"}}
E["item:grape-manifest"] = {t="item",n="Grape Manifest",z="elwynn",s="At Northshire Abbey, Milly Osworth's recovered harvest is bound for the stores after brigands seized it.",h="At Northshire Abbey, Milly Osworth's recovered harvest is bound for the stores after brigands seized it.",sec={{t="A Record of the Harvest",b="Northshire Abbey depends on nearby farms for its food and drink. The lost harvest put its stores in danger. Now the crates are reclaimed, and the quartermasters can balance supplies and ready barrels for fermentation. Milly Osworth's manifest records the quantity they need to plan.",sp=0},{t="The Abbey's Cellarer",b="Brother Neals oversees Northshire Abbey's food and drink. He enjoys sampling its wine in the quiet of the bell tower. Knowing the grapes are coming helps keep the monks and visiting recruits supplied with drink. Each saved bushel strengthens the abbey's stores and brings a blessing from the Holy Light.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Grape Manifest?",a="Milly Osworth's Grape Manifest records the harvest recovered from her overrun vineyard. It tracks the fresh grapes bound for Northshire Abbey.",al={"what is grape manifest","grape manifest item"},it="identity"},{q="Who receives the manifest?",a="Brother Neals receives Milly Osworth's manifest. He oversees the abbey's food and wine stores and often samples vintages in Northshire Abbey's bell tower.",al={"who gets grape manifest","who do i give grape manifest to","where does grape manifest go"},it="target"},{q="Why were the grapes in danger?",a="Defias brigands drove Milly Osworth from her vineyard in Northshire Valley. The harvest was at risk, and the abbey lost its fresh fruit until recruits intervened.",al={"why did grapes need saving","vineyard brigands","what happened to milly harvest"},it="conflict"},{q="What does Brother Neals do with the grapes?",a="Brother Neals uses the grapes to replenish the abbey's food stores and ferment fresh Northshire wine. The wine supplies the resident brotherhood and visiting defenders.",al={"what is grape used for","abbey wine"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does the Grape Manifest come from, and who made it?",a="The manifest is drawn up by Milly Osworth, a farmer working the vineyards of Northshire Valley. After you help her drive back the Defias brigands who overran her fields and recover her harvested crop, she prepares this record to document the saved yield.",al={"who wrote grape manifest","where did the grape manifest come from","grape manifest origin"},it="origin",add="a2f30a46"},{q="Why is the Grape Manifest needed?",a="Brother Neals manages the stores of food and drink for Northshire Abbey. Milly sends the manifest to notify him that her harvest has been rescued from the bandits, allowing the abbey's vintners to count on fresh fruit for pressing their wine.",al={"why does brother neals want the grape manifest","grape manifest purpose","why need grape manifest"},it="why_wanted",add="cbb35726"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can see how field harvests supply the abbey's stores and help feed its monastic community.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you see the early struggles of Stormwind's heartland. Even monastic life and simple harvests need armed defense against roaming outlaws."},kw={"brother neals","elwynn","grape manifest","milly osworth","northshire abbey","vineyard","wine"},rel={"quest:3905","npc:brother-neals","subzone:northshire-abbey","zone:elwynn","topic:light"},src={"Grape Manifest","Grape Manifest (quest)"}}
E["item:hallowed-letter"] = {t="item",n="Hallowed Letter",z="elwynn",s="In Northshire Valley, Priestess Anetta calls young priests to Northshire Abbey. Her letter begins their study of the Holy Light.",h="In Northshire Valley, Priestess Anetta calls young priests to Northshire Abbey.",sec={{t="A Call to Faith",b="Priestess Anetta’s personal mark appears on the Hallowed Letter. It reaches fledgling priests after their first trials against the kobold camps of Northshire Valley. She sees a spark of the Holy Light in each novice and urges them to enter the abbey and serve it. Dark forces still linger across Azeroth after the Third War. The priesthood gathers those who can heal, protect, and guide an empire struggling to keep order.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Hallowed Letter?",a="The Hallowed Letter is Priestess Anetta’s missive to newly arrived priests at Northshire Abbey. It summons them to their first class instruction.",al={"what is hallowed letter","hallowed letter item","priest letter northshire"},it="identity"},{q="Who wrote the letter?",a="Priestess Anetta’s insignia marks the letter. She trains and guides young human priests arriving at Northshire.",al={"who sent the letter","who is the author","letter sender"},it="origin"},{q="Why is the priesthood calling for new initiates right now?",a="Azeroth remains in turmoil, and remnants of the Burning Legion still haunt it. Kalimdor faces new trials, while Stormwind needs compassionate healers and leaders to rebuild and protect its people.",al={"why do priests need help","state of the world","priest lore 25 adp"},it="motive"},{q="What should I do after reading the letter?",a="Carry the letter into Northshire Abbey and speak with Priestess Anetta. She will accept your pledge to the Light and train you in new priestly disciplines as your journey unfolds.",al={"where do i take the letter","hallowed letter quest turn in","who to talk to"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Priestess Anetta want you to have the Hallowed Letter?",a="Priestess Anetta sends the letter to summon promising initiates of the Holy Light within Northshire Abbey. Recognizing that you have shown promise in defending the valley, she wishes to introduce herself, guide your spiritual devotion, and offer deeper instruction in the priesthood's sacred arts.",al={"why hallowed letter","why did anetta send the letter","purpose of hallowed letter"},it="why_wanted",add="0a342f04"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, this missive recognizes you as an instrument of the Holy Light and binds you to Northshire Abbey’s trainers.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you carry on Northshire Valley’s tradition of holy duty, practiced there since before the First War."},kw={"anetta","elwynn forest","hallowed letter","holy light","northshire abbey","priest","priestess anetta"},rel={"quest:3103","npc:priestess-anetta","subzone:northshire-abbey","topic:priest","topic:light","zone:elwynn","topic:burning-legion","topic:kobold"},src={"Hallowed Letter","Hallowed Letter (quest)"}}
E["item:heartswood-core"] = {t="item",n="Heartswood Core",z="elwynn",s="Beneath Stormwind, warlocks use the Heartswood Core to summon a succubus. Gakin the Darkbinder provides the enchanted focus, made from an ancient tree’s wood, to open a passage to the Twisting Nether.",h="Beneath Stormwind, warlocks use the Heartswood Core to summon a succubus.",sec={{t="A Focus for the Nether",b="Beneath the Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind’s Mage Quarter, warlocks perform rites beyond the city watch’s gaze. The Heartswood Core channels the magic that begins a binding ritual. Made from an ancient tree’s wood, it holds enough lingering power to pierce the veil between worlds. At a consecrated summoning circle, an initiate focuses dark arts through the core and opens a passage to the Twisting Nether. A succubus crosses the divide.",sp=0},{t="The Trial of Binding",b="A warlock who summons a demon must prove dominance over its cunning and seductive nature before controlling it. Gakin gives the Heartswood Core to promising practitioners so they can face the summoned demon in combat. Succubi prey on weakness and can overwhelm feeble minds. The encounter is a deadly rite of passage. The aspiring warlock must subdue the fiend and return the spent core to Gakin, proving a will strong enough to bind the servant permanently.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Heartswood Core used for?",a="Warlocks use the Heartswood Core at the summoning circle beneath the Slaughtered Lamb to open a passage to the Twisting Nether. A succubus crosses into our realm, and you must fight and bind it.",al={"what does heartswood core do","heartswood core use","purpose of heartswood core"},it="purpose"},{q="Who provides the Heartswood Core?",a="Gakin the Darkbinder provides the Heartswood Core. He is a master warlock who trains novices in the hidden catacombs beneath the Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind’s Mage Quarter.",al={"where do i get heartswood core","who gives heartswood core"}},{q="Where must the core be used?",a="Use the Heartswood Core at the summoning circle in the crypts beneath the Slaughtered Lamb, deep below Stormwind’s streets.",al={"heartswood core location","where to summon succubus"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after the ritual is finished?",a="After you summon the succubus, defeat it in combat and send it back to the void. Then return the Heartswood Core to Gakin the Darkbinder to learn how to command the demon at will.",al={"what do i do after summoning","turn in heartswood core"},it="next_step"},{q="What is the Heartswood Core?",a="The Heartswood Core is an enchanted occult relic crafted specifically for summoning rituals. Prepared by dark magic practitioners, it acts as a magical catalyst powerful enough to pierce the veil between worlds and draw a succubus out of the Twisting Nether into a summoning circle.",al={"heartswood core lore","what is heartswood core","heartswood item"},it="identity",add="34d5c17e"},{q="Where does the Heartswood Core come from, and who made it?",a="The core is prepared using raw Heartswood recovered from the ruins of Ordil'Aran in Ashenvale, fashioned and empowered under the direction of Gakin the Darkbinder. Gakin entrusts the completed relic to promising warlocks studying beneath the Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind.",al={"who made heartswood core","heartswood core origin","how was heartswood core made"},it="origin",add="a2df89b9"},{q="Why does Gakin want the Heartswood Core used?",a="A warlock seeking to bind a succubus requires an anchor of immense power to open a gateway into the void. Without the Heartswood Core, you cannot complete the ritual spell needed to manifest the demon and subdue its treacherous mind.",al={"why use heartswood core","heartswood core purpose lore","why want heartswood core"},it="why_wanted",add="cef9a99d"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As an Alliance warlock, you use the Heartswood Core to summon and master your first succubus during training."},kw={"gakin the darkbinder","heartswood core","slaughtered lamb","stormwind","succubus","summoning circle","the binding","warlock"},rel={"npc:gakin-the-darkbinder","subzone:slaughtered-lamb","quest:1739","quest:1738","quest:1685","topic:stormwind-kingdom","zone:elwynn"},src={"Heartswood Core","The Binding (Succubus, Stormwind)"}}
E["item:huge-gnoll-claw"] = {t="item",n="Huge Gnoll Claw",z="elwynn",s="In southwestern Elwynn, Hogger's death is proven by his huge claw. Stormwind's authorities in Goldshire require it before paying the bounty.",h="In southwestern Elwynn, Hogger's death is proven by his huge claw.",sec={{t="Bounty Hunter's Proof",b="For months, Hogger has terrorized the southern woodlands of Forest's Edge. Patrols have failed to stop him, and the local garrison cannot corral or subdue the brute. The Stormwind Army is stretched thin across Elwynn, so it has posted an open bounty on his head. Marshal Dughan in Goldshire requires clear proof before paying. Hogger's oversized claw leaves no doubt that the notorious marauder has fallen.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Huge Gnoll Claw used for?",a="Bring Hogger's claw to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire as proof of his death, and collect the posted bounty.",al={"what do i do with hogger claw","huge gnoll claw use","who wants the claw"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Where does this claw come from?",a="Hogger carries the claw. The elite gnoll wanders near the Riverpaw camps along the southwestern borders of Forest's Edge in Elwynn Forest.",al={"who drops the claw","how to get huge gnoll claw","where to find huge gnoll claw"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Marshal Dughan want a claw instead of the head?",a="Hogger is abnormally large for a gnoll, and his immense claws are distinct and instantly recognizable. One proves to the Stormwind Army that the notorious marauder has been slain.",al={"why proof of demise claw","why not hoggers head","dughan bounty proof"},it="motive"},{q="Can I get another claw if I lose it?",a="Yes. If you lose the claw before taking it to Marshal Dughan, you can hunt Hogger again in southwestern Elwynn Forest and claim a replacement.",al={"lost huge gnoll claw","can i get claw again","hogger claw respawn"},gp=true},{q="What is the Huge Gnoll Claw?",a="The Huge Gnoll Claw is severed physical proof of the demise of Hogger, a notorious and massive gnoll terrorizing southwestern Elwynn Forest. Because Hogger has overpowered every attempt at capture by the local authorities, this distinctive talon serves as undeniable evidence for Marshal Dughan that the brute has finally been slain.",al={"what is huge gnoll claw","huge gnoll claw info","hogger claw"},it="identity",add="d9093290"},{q="Why does Marshal Dughan want the Huge Gnoll Claw?",a="Marshal Dughan and the Stormwind Army posted a bounty on Hogger after the giant beast evaded and overpowered their patrols. Dughan requires the gnoll's massive claw as proof of his death before he will disburse the bounty reward in Goldshire, finally putting an end to the headache Hogger caused his men.",al={"why does dughan want the claw","who wants huge gnoll claw","why want huge gnoll claw"},it="why_wanted",add="7983cdb8"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, claiming Hogger's claw rids the kingdom's heartland of its most infamous woodland terror. It proves your valor to Marshal Dughan and the beleaguered garrison at Goldshire.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, securing the claw of a predator who routinely overpowered armed squads shows your skill at tracking and hunting beasts."},kw={"bounty","elwynn forest","goldshire","hogger","huge gnoll claw","marshal dughan","riverpaw"},rel={"npc:hogger","quest:176","npc:marshal-dughan","zone:elwynn","subzone:goldshire","subzone:forest-s-edge","topic:stormwind-army","topic:gnoll"},src={"Huge Gnoll Claw","Wanted: \"Hogger\""}}
E["item:invisibility-liquor"] = {t="item",n="Invisibility Liquor",z="elwynn",s="Maybell Maclure slips from her family's sight with Invisibility Liquor to meet Tommy Joe Stonefield. Their households remain bound by a bitter feud.",h="Maybell Maclure slips from her family's sight with Invisibility Liquor to meet Tommy Joe Stonefield.",sec={{t="A Potion for Star-Crossed Lovers",b="Tommy Joe Stonefield seeks a quiet meeting with Maybell Maclure. But their families' feud keeps the households apart, and their kin watch closely. Ordinary secrecy will not do. Invisibility Liquor lets its drinker cross the disputed farmland unseen.",sp=0},{t="Unorthodox Elwynn Alchemy",b="Crystal Kelp Fronds from waters where murlocs dwell go into the brew. Maybell Maclure drinks the liquor and vanishes from sight. Then she slips into the woods for a secret meeting.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What does Invisibility Liquor do?",a="For a short time, Invisibility Liquor makes the drinker invisible. Its magic is carried in an alcoholic drink.",al={"liquor effects","invisibility brew","what does it do"},it="power"},{q="Who uses the Invisibility Liquor?",a="Maybell Maclure receives Invisibility Liquor so she can leave her family's sight and meet Tommy Joe Stonefield, despite their households' feud.",al={"who drinks it","maybell maclure liquor"},it="target"},{q="How is the liquor made?",a="Crystal Kelp Fronds gathered from riverbeds and lake shores in Elwynn Forest go into the brew. Murlocs hoard the plants.",al={"liquor ingredients","crystal kelp liquor"},it="origin"},{q="Can players drink the Invisibility Liquor themselves?",a="No. Invisibility Liquor is meant for Maybell Maclure, so she can slip away from her family.",al={"can i drink it","drink invisibility liquor"},gp=true},{q="What is Invisibility Liquor?",a="Invisibility Liquor is a potent alchemical draught concocted in Elwynn Forest. While ostensibly an alcoholic beverage, it carries magical properties derived from crystal kelp fronds, temporarily granting whoever drinks it complete invisibility from mortal eyes.",al={"what is invisibility liquor","invisibility liquor lore","what kind of drink is invisibility liquor"},it="identity",add="19edabb3"},{q="Why does anyone want Invisibility Liquor?",a="The liquor is sought to resolve a forbidden romance. Maybell Maclure and Tommy Joe Stonefield are caught on opposite sides of their families' bitter Elwynn feud, and the draught allows Maybell to slip away unseen past her watchful kin to visit her beloved.",al={"why need invisibility liquor","who wants invisibility liquor","why do they want the liquor"},it="why_wanted",add="f0e7bc08"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you know Kirin Tor arcanists spend years mastering illusions and invisibility spells. Elwynn locals make a rough imitation with fermented spirits and waterlogged kelp.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you know the Stonefield and Maclure clans' rural feud reaches bitter extremes."},kw={"crystal kelp","elwynn forest","invisibility liquor","maybell maclure","stonefield feud","the escape","tommy joe stonefield"},rel={"quest:114","npc:maybell-maclure","npc:tommy-joe-stonefield","item:crystal-kelp-frond","zone:elwynn","topic:alliance"},src={"Invisibility Liquor","The Escape (Alliance)"}}
E["item:jennea-s-flask"] = {t="item",n="Jennea's Flask",z="elwynn",s="At the Wizard's Sanctum in Stormwind, Jennea Cannon sends apprentices to Mirror Lake for water. They bring a sample back for arcane study.",h="At the Wizard's Sanctum in Stormwind, Jennea Cannon sends apprentices to Mirror Lake for water.",sec={{t="A Vessel for Arcane Research",b="Arcane currents have been torn from their ancient channels by magical struggles across Azeroth. Jennea Cannon wants to learn how these shifts have affected Elwynn Forest. She gives promising apprentices a glass flask and sends them southwest of Stormwind's gates, to the base of Mirror Lake's waterfall.\n\nThe flask protects the water sample on the journey back to the Wizard's Sanctum. There, Jennea can examine it for arcane disturbances.",sp=0},{t="Guarding the Waters",b="With Jennea's flask, Stormwind's mages can test whether shifting ley lines have tainted Mirror Lake. Harmful magic in the water could bring strange afflictions to the surrounding life and to anyone who drinks from it. A sample may reveal magical residue before tainted currents spread through the countryside.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Jennea's Flask used for?",a="Use Jennea's Flask to gather water from the waterfall at Mirror Lake in Elwynn Forest.",al={"flask purpose","what does the flask do","use of flask"},it="purpose"},{q="Who gives you this flask?",a="Jennea Cannon, a mage trainer in Stormwind City's Wizard's Sanctum, gives you the flask.",al={"who gives flask","jennea flask source"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Jennea want water from Mirror Lake?",a="Recent mystical conflicts have disrupted magic's flow across the world. Jennea fears stray currents may be seeping into Elwynn's waters and endangering anyone who drinks from the lake.",al={"why mirror lake water","why water sample"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where do you fill the flask?",a="Fill the flask at the base of the waterfall that flows into Mirror Lake, southwest of Stormwind's main gates in Elwynn Forest.",al={"where to fill flask","flask location","lake location"},gp=true},{q="What is Jennea's Flask?",a="It is a specialized sample container provided by Jennea Cannon, an instructor in the Mage Quarter of Stormwind. She entrusts it to promising apprentices to collect water directly from the waterfall at Mirror Lake so she can inspect it for magical contamination.",al={"what is jenneas flask","jennea flask","jennea's flask"},it="identity",add="b836f408"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, carrying this flask is one of your first field tasks for the Wizard's Sanctum. It tests your ability to handle delicate arcane research and watch for changes in ley lines."},kw={"elwynn forest","jennea cannon","jennea's flask","mirror lake","stormwind","water sample","wizard's sanctum"},rel={"npc:jennea-cannon","quest:1861","item:mirror-lake-water-sample","quest:1860","zone:elwynn","subzone:stormwind-gate","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Jennea's Flask","Mirror Lake (quest)"}}
E["item:large-candle"] = {t="item",n="Large Candle",z="elwynn",s="In Elwynn's mines, kobolds carry Large Candles for light and wax. Apothecaries value the wax for their work.",h="In Elwynn's mines, kobolds carry Large Candles for light and wax.",sec={{t="Subterranean Light and Wax",b="Kobolds follow candlelight through the dark shafts beneath Elwynn Forest. They fasten the tapers to their heads, and Kobold Miners, Tunnelers, and Geomancers defend them fiercely from intruders. Large Candles from Fargodeep Mine and Jasperlode Mine hold valuable wax, though they are crudely made. Surface tradesmen cannot produce much wax at once, so the candles serve both as tools for kobolds and as a commodity for alchemists.",sp=0},{t="Trade and the Apothecary",b="William Pestle, an apothecary operative from Stormwind City, gathers Large Candles at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire. His family runs an apothecary, and he needs rendered wax for its concoctions, balms, and ointments. Pestle hires passing adventurers to clear the infested mines and take candles from the kobolds.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are Large Candles used for?",a="William Pestle gathers Large Candles in Goldshire for the apothecary he runs with his brother in Stormwind City. They render the candles down for wax used in ointments, balms, and alchemical recipes.",al={"large candle use","why get large candles","who wants large candles"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where can Large Candles be found?",a="Kobolds carry Large Candles in Elwynn Forest's mines, especially Fargodeep Mine south of Goldshire and Jasperlode Mine to the east. Tunnelers, Miners, and Geomancers carry them.",al={"large candle location","where to get large candles","kobold candle drops"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why do kobolds carry candles on their heads?",a="Kobolds use candlelight to dig and find their way through dark underground tunnels. They fasten candles to their heads to keep their hands free for pickaxes, geomantic spellcasting, and weapons.",al={"why do kobolds have candles","kobold head candle lore"},it="history"},{q="Who is William Pestle?",a="William Pestle is an apothecary operative from Stormwind City who conducts business at Goldshire's Lion's Pride Inn. He gathers raw ingredients from the wilderness and mines to supply the apothecary shop he runs with his brother.",al={"william pestle lore","who is the apothecary guy in goldshire"},it="people"},{q="What is a Large Candle?",a="A Large Candle is a crude, substantial wax taper carried by the kobolds dwelling in the mines of Elwynn Forest. Kobolds are notoriously protective of their light sources, using these hefty candles to pierce the darkness of subterranean tunnels like the Fargodeep and Jasperlode mines while they dig for gold and minerals.",al={"what is large candle","large candle elwynn","large candle lore"},it="identity",add="05873d56"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Miners working the veins in Fargodeep and Jasperlode often run afoul of kobold infestations. The kobolds covet both the gold and the light of Large Candles.",["faction:Alliance"]="By taking candles from kobolds in Elwynn, Alliance adventurers weaken the vermin in the mines and supply important materials to Stormwind's apothecary trade."},kw={"fargodeep mine","goldshire","goldtooth","jasperlode mine","kobold candles","large candle","wax","william pestle"},rel={"quest:60","npc:william-pestle","topic:kobold","subzone:fargodeep-mine","subzone:jasperlode-mine","subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn","quest:87"},src={"Large Candle","Kobold Candles"}}
E["item:marshal-haggard-s-badge"] = {t="item",n="Marshal Haggard's Badge",z="elwynn",s="In the hills of Elwynn Forest, Marshal Haggard lives retired from Stormwind's service. Dead-tooth Jack tricked him into surrendering his old badge, which the Defias could use to impersonate city officials.",h="In the hills of Elwynn Forest, Marshal Haggard lives retired from Stormwind's service.",sec={{t="A Stolen Insignia",b="Dead-tooth Jack came to Haggard's farm one night in a Stormwind tabard. The Defias rogue pretended to be Marshal Dughan, Goldshire's garrison commander, and said Haggard's former peers needed the insignia for official business.\n\nThe aging marshal handed it over without suspicion. Jack fled into the woods before Haggard saw through the ruse. In Defias hands, the badge still carries the authority of Stormwind's marshals. Outlaws could use it to pass checkpoints or confuse local patrols.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Marshal Haggard's Badge?",a="Marshal Haggard carried the badge as a sign of his rank while serving the kingdom of Stormwind. Though he is retired, the badge still carries genuine authority.",al={"haggard badge","marshal badge","haggards badge"},it="identity"},{q="How did Dead-tooth Jack get the badge?",a="Dead-tooth Jack came to Marshal Haggard's home at night wearing a Stormwind tabard. Haggard mistook him for Marshal Dughan of Goldshire and handed over the badge when Jack asked for it.",al={"how was badge stolen","who stole the badge","dead-tooth jack trick"}},{q="Why is the badge dangerous in the hands of the Defias?",a="A Defias agent with the genuine badge and a disguise could impersonate a high-ranking Stormwind official. The agent could bypass sentries, enter garrisons, or give false orders to town guards.",al={"why does jack want the badge","defias badge use","badge danger"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is the badge kept?",a="Dead-tooth Jack locked the badge in his strongbox at his campsite south of Marshal Haggard's farm in Elwynn Forest.",al={"badge location","where to find badge","dead tooth strongbox"},it="place",gp=true}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, recovering Haggard's badge proves your mettle to a veteran of Stormwind's military. He rewards promising warriors with well-maintained surplus arms from his fighting days.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, retrieving the badge protects Stormwind's military command and keeps the Defias Brotherhood from undermining local defenses from within."},kw={"dead-tooth jack","defias","elwynn forest","marshal dughan","marshal haggard","marshal haggard's badge","stormwind","strongbox"},rel={"quest:1667","quest:1666","npc:marshal-dughan","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Marshal Haggard's Badge","Dead-tooth Jack"}}
E["item:milly-s-harvest"] = {t="item",n="Milly's Harvest",z="elwynn",s="In the Northshire Vineyards, Milly's Harvest lies abandoned after the Defias arrive. Crates and buckets of grapes risk theft or being crushed beneath the abbey guards' boots.",h="In the Northshire Vineyards, Milly's Harvest lies abandoned after the Defias arrive.",sec={{t="A Fragile Yield",b="Milly Osworth gathers grapes in the Northshire Vineyards. The harvest matters to local vintners and the abbey community. When armed brigands in red masks enter the fields, Milly flees to the abbey grounds. Her fresh-picked grapes lie scattered between the rows.",sp=0},{t="Collateral Damage",b="Stormwind guards watch the valley entrance, but their small numbers leave Northshire vulnerable. The garrison promises to drive out the Defias. Milly fears a long fight between guards and thieves will ruin her harvest. The crates may be trampled or carried off as provisions, costing Northshire one of its few peaceful harvests.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Milly's Harvest?",a="Milly's Harvest is the grapes Milly Osworth picked and packed into crates and buckets before Defias thugs seized the Northshire Vineyards.",al={"millys harvest","what is the harvest","milly osworth grapes"},it="identity"},{q="Why were the crates left behind in the vineyard?",a="Defias bandits raided the vineyards while Milly was harvesting. She had to leave the grapes behind and flee to Northshire Abbey.",al={"why abandoned","why did milly leave the grapes","why leave harvest"},it="origin"},{q="Why couldn't the Northshire guards retrieve the harvest?",a="Northshire's guards are stretched thin by Defias incursions and local threats. Milly also fears their boots could crush the grapes as they drive off the bandits.",al={"why not guards","why cant guards get it","stormwind guards northshire"}},{q="Who are the bandits threatening the harvest?",a="The bandits threatening the harvest belong to the Defias Brotherhood, a ring of outlaws and brigands causing unrest throughout Elwynn Forest.",al={"who took the vineyards","who is attacking the vineyard","vineyard bandits"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Milly want her harvest recovered?",a="Milly Osworth gathered the crop herself and relies on it for her livelihood, but had to abandon it when Defias bandits overran the vineyard. She fears that if the thieves do not make off with the fruit first, the Abbey's guards will trample the fragile grapes into the dirt while driving the brigands out.",al={"why does milly want the harvest","why recover milly's harvest","why are the grapes important"},it="why_wanted",add="1d7cbab4"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The threat to Northshire's farmers shows how thin Stormwind's garrison has become. Everyday people rely on passing adventurers to protect their livelihoods.",["race:Human"]="As a human starting in Northshire, you may first meet the Defias Brotherhood's lawlessness on your own doorstep when you recover Milly's grapes."},kw={"defias","elwynn forest","grapes","milly osworth","milly's harvest","northshire abbey","northshire vineyards"},rel={"quest:3904","quest:3903","subzone:northshire-vineyards","subzone:northshire-abbey","zone:elwynn"},src={"Milly's Harvest","Milly's Harvest (quest)"}}
E["item:mirror-lake-water-sample"] = {t="item",n="Mirror Lake Water Sample",z="elwynn",s="At Mirror Lake in Elwynn Forest, water is gathered for Jennea Cannon in Stormwind. The mages will test it for signs that the arcane currents have altered local water.",h="At Mirror Lake in Elwynn Forest, water is gathered for Jennea Cannon in Stormwind.",sec={{t="Testing the Waters of Elwynn",b="Jennea Cannon sends promising apprentices to collect water from Mirror Lake. The lake lies just southwest of the Stormwind Gate, where they fill a specially prepared flask at the foot of its waterfall.\n\nThe Wizard's Sanctum in Stormwind fears the world's mystic channels remain unsettled after catastrophic conflicts. Its mages will examine the sample for stray magical taint in the waterways people nearby use.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Mirror Lake Water Sample?",a="The Mirror Lake Water Sample is waterfall water from Elwynn Forest, kept in Jennea's Flask. Novice mages gather it for testing at the Wizard's Sanctum.",al={"mirror lake sample","water sample item","jennea water"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Jennea Cannon want this water sample?",a="Recent mystical upheavals across Azeroth disrupted stable magical currents. Jennea Cannon fears rogue magical energy may alter the natural world and poison local drinking water.",al={"why test mirror lake","jennea cannon purpose","magical taint water"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is the sample collected?",a="The sample comes from the foot of the waterfall flowing into Mirror Lake, southwest of the Stormwind Gate in Elwynn Forest.",al={"where to get sample","mirror lake location","sample waterfall"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens if the water turns out to be magically tainted?",a="Jennea Cannon fears that drinking from Mirror Lake for a long time could cause adverse magical effects if ley currents have contaminated the water supply.",al={"tainted water effects","is mirror lake poisoned"},it="threat"},{q="Where does the Mirror Lake Water Sample come from, and who collected it?",a="The sample is collected directly from the base of the waterfall cascading into Mirror Lake, just southwest of Stormwind's gates in Elwynn Forest. Using an empty flask supplied by the mage trainer Jennea Cannon, you scoop up the water yourself on behalf of Stormwind's spellcasters so they can examine the state of the surrounding wild currents.",al={"where does mirror lake water sample come from","who made mirror lake water sample","origin of mirror lake water sample"},it="origin",add="935f4959"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage training under the Wizard's Sanctum, you fetch this sample as an early duty. It teaches you to watch environmental ley lines and recognize wild magical seepage."},kw={"arcane taint","elwynn forest","flask","jennea cannon","mirror lake","stormwind","water sample","wizard's sanctum"},rel={"npc:jennea-cannon","quest:1861","item:jennea-s-flask","zone:elwynn","subzone:stormwind-gate","quest:1860"},src={"Mirror Lake Water Sample","Mirror Lake (quest)"}}
E["item:osric-s-crate"] = {t="item",n="Osric's Crate",z="elwynn",s="At Sentinel Hill, Osric's Crate brings fresh armor from Stormwind to the People's Militia. The defenders face the Defias Brotherhood and marauding gnolls without the Stormwind army.",h="At Sentinel Hill, Osric's Crate brings fresh armor from Stormwind to the People's Militia.",sec={{t="Supplies for the Front",b="Quartermaster Lewis receives the shipment and shares the protective gear among the volunteer fighters. The crown gives the People's Militia no formal support. These freshly made suits are meant to help the volunteers hold their position.",sp=0},{t="Winged Courier Network",b="From Dungar Longdrink's roost in Stormwind's Trade District, a gryphon carries the crate to Thor at Sentinel Hill. The flight avoids dangerous roads through Elwynn Forest and across the Westfall border, where bandits may ambush travelers. Gryphons help keep frontier garrisons supplied during wartime.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside Osric's Crate?",a="Osric's Crate holds protective armor crafted in Stormwind. Quartermaster Lewis receives the delivery and prepares to distribute it among the fighters defending Sentinel Hill.",al={"what's in the crate","contents of osrics crate","osric crate contents"},it="item"},{q="Who is Osric?",a="Osric is an armorer in Stormwind who prepared the shipment for the People's Militia holding Westfall.",al={"who is osric","who sent osrics crate"}},{q="Who receives the crate?",a="Quartermaster Lewis receives the crate. He manages supplies and equipment for the People's Militia at Sentinel Hill in Westfall.",al={"where does the crate go","who do i give osric's crate to","crate recipient"},it="target"},{q="Why is the crate delivered by gryphon?",a="Bandits and outlaws make the roads through Stormwind, Elwynn Forest, and Westfall perilous. A gryphon carries the armor quickly and safely from Dungar Longdrink in Stormwind to Thor at Sentinel Hill.",al={"why fly the crate","why use gryphons","osric crate flight"}},{q="What is Osric's Crate?",a="Osric's Crate is a shipment of armor dispatched from Stormwind City. It is prepared for the defenders stationed at Sentinel Hill in Westfall, who are desperately short on gear while holding out against the Defias Brotherhood.",al={"what is osrics crate","osric crate item","whats in osrics crate"},it="identity",add="34d354cb"},{q="Where does Osric's Crate come from, and who made it?",a="The crate comes from Stormwind City, prepared and dispatched by Osric to supply the People's Militia. Gryphon Master Dungar Longdrink entrusts it to you to carry by gryphon across the kingdom to Westfall.",al={"who made osrics crate","where did osric crate come from","osric crate origin"},it="origin",add="091b5cbb"},{q="Why does anyone want Osric's Crate?",a="Quartermaster Lewis and the People's Militia at Sentinel Hill urgently need the armor inside. With Westfall abandoned by royal forces and overrun by outlaws, every scrap of protective gear is vital to keeping the defenders alive.",al={"why deliver osrics crate","why does lewis want osrics crate","osrics crate purpose"},it="why_wanted",add="11fb3015"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, every shipment of arms and armor that reaches Sentinel Hill helps keep the kingdom's western borders from falling to the Defias Brotherhood."},kw={"dungar longdrink","gryphon","osric","osric's crate","peoples militia","quartermaster lewis","sentinel hill","westfall"},rel={"quest:6285","npc:quartermaster-lewis","subzone:sentinel-hill","zone:westfall","quest:6261","npc:thor","quest:6281","quest:6181"},src={"Osric's Crate","Return to Lewis"}}
E["item:painted-gnoll-armband"] = {t="item",n="Painted Gnoll Armband",z="elwynn",s="At Westbrook Garrison, Painted Gnoll Armbands prove Riverpaw gnolls have been slain. Their packs press against Elwynn Forest's western border.",h="At Westbrook Garrison, Painted Gnoll Armbands prove Riverpaw gnolls have been slain.",sec={{t="Tokens of the Riverpaw",b="Riverpaw warriors and scavengers wear rough bands marked with crude tribal patterns. These armbands come from Riverpaw gnolls along Elwynn Forest's wilderness borders. Stormwind's defenders face a growing threat near Stone Cairn Lake and in the woods south of Westbrook Garrison.",sp=0},{t="Bounty for Westbrook Garrison",b="Stormwind's Army is stretched thin across the kingdom, leaving Westbrook Garrison hard pressed to guard the western border. Deputy Rainer offers a standing bounty for slaying Riverpaw Outrunners and Riverpaw Runts. The painted bands let the deputies tally bounties and thin the packs near nearby farmlands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Westbrook Garrison want these armbands?",a="Deputy Rainer at Westbrook Garrison collects the armbands as proof that Riverpaw gnolls have been slain. Garrison troops cannot manage the encroaching packs alone, so Stormwind pays bounties to those who bring back the tokens.",al={"why armbands","who wants painted gnoll armbands","deputy rainer bounty"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Which gnolls wear these painted armbands?",a="Riverpaw gnolls wear the painted armbands. Riverpaw Outrunners and Riverpaw Runts infest the woods south of Westbrook Garrison and the shores around Stone Cairn Lake.",al={"where do armbands drop","who drops painted gnoll armband","which gnolls have armbands"},it="origin"},{q="Why are Riverpaw gnolls in Elwynn Forest?",a="Riverpaw packs have pushed east along Elwynn Forest's borders, setting up camps near Stone Cairn Lake and the forest margins. With the kingdom's military presence depleted, they hunt, scavenge, and threaten nearby settlements.",al={"why are gnolls here","gnoll invasion elwynn","riverpaw elwynn"}},{q="What is the significance of the paint on the armbands?",a="The paint marks trophies taken from Riverpaw gnolls and helps prove the kills to Deputy Rainer. The patterns have no stated rank or meaning.",al={"why are they painted","gnoll armband markings"}},{q="What is a Painted Gnoll Armband?",a="A Painted Gnoll Armband is a crude piece of personal adornment worn by Riverpaw gnolls. Crafted and painted by the pack, these armbands mark their presence in the borderlands of Elwynn Forest. To the Stormwind Army, they serve as undeniable physical proof that a marauding gnoll has been slain.",al={"what is painted gnoll armband","painted gnoll armband lore","gnoll armband"},it="identity",add="586b453e"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, collecting these armbands helps Westbrook Garrison hold Stormwind's western frontier while the city's standing army is diverted elsewhere."},kw={"bounty","deputy rainer","elwynn forest","gnolls","painted gnoll armband","riverpaw","stone cairn lake","westbrook garrison"},rel={"quest:11","npc:deputy-rainer","subzone:westbrook-garrison","zone:elwynn","subzone:stone-cairn-lake","quest:239","topic:gnoll","topic:stormwind-army"},src={"Painted Gnoll Armband","Riverpaw Gnoll Bounty"}}
E["item:pork-belly-pie"] = {t="item",n="Pork Belly Pie",z="elwynn",s="In Elwynn Forest, Billy Maclure waits for a pie from Stonefield Farm before he speaks of a missing necklace. Auntie Bernice bakes it despite the families’ long feud.",h="In Elwynn Forest, Billy Maclure waits for a pie from Stonefield Farm before he speaks of a missing necklace.",sec={{t="A Bribe Between Feuding Farms",b="The Stonefield and Maclure families have quarreled over land and pride for years. Young Billy Maclure has a weakness for Auntie Bernice’s pork belly pie. When a valuable Stonefield family necklace goes missing, Billy refuses to share what he knows until an adventurer brings him a warm slice. Bernice bakes it reluctantly, wishing the greedy boy would choke on it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Pork Belly Pie used for?",a="Auntie Bernice Stonefield bakes the pie to get young Billy Maclure to talk. He knows something about the missing Stonefield family necklace, but refuses to speak until he gets her cooking.",al={"pie use","why pork belly pie","what do i do with the pie"},it="purpose"},{q="Who bakes the Pork Belly Pie?",a="Auntie Bernice Stonefield bakes the pie at Stonefield Farm. She resents Billy Maclure and his family, but prepares it to help recover her family's lost necklace.",al={"who made the pie","pie baker","granny stonefield pie"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Billy Maclure want food from a rival family?",a="Billy Maclure wants Auntie Bernice's cooking despite the feud between the Stonefields and the Maclures. He wants pork belly pie more than he cares about keeping his family's grudge.",al={"why billy wants pie","why maclure wants stonefield food"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Can players eat the Pork Belly Pie?",a="No. The pie is meant for Billy Maclure and cannot be eaten to restore health or mana.",al={"can i eat it","is pork belly pie edible"},gp=true},{q="What is the Pork Belly Pie?",a="It is a savory meat pie baked with pork belly, renowned for being delicious despite the bitter feud between the two farming households of southern Elwynn Forest. Freshly prepared in the Stonefield kitchen, it serves as a mouth-watering bribe to coax information out of the Maclure boy, Billy, who claims his memory only works on a full stomach.",al={"what is pork belly pie","pork belly pie lore","about pork belly pie"},it="identity",add="6505ed9f"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Auntie Bernice's home-cooked pie holds sway even amid the families' feud, though her recipe remains a secret.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers helping in rural Elwynn, delivering pies reveals the deep-rooted quarrels in Stormwind's farming heartland."},kw={"auntie bernice stonefield","back to billy","billy maclure","elwynn forest","maclure","pork belly pie","stonefield"},rel={"quest:84","npc:billy-maclure","subzone:maclure-vineyards","zone:elwynn"},src={"Pork Belly Pie","Back to Billy"}}
E["item:powers-of-the-void"] = {t="item",n="Powers of the Void",z="elwynn",s="In Northshire, a stolen tome draws Drusilla La Salle's attention. A novice took Powers of the Void from a guarded wing of Northshire Abbey's library while leaving to join the Defias Brotherhood. Drusilla seeks the book for her own study of dark magic.",h="In Northshire, a stolen tome draws Drusilla La Salle's attention.",sec={{t="A Restricted Northshire Text",b="Powers of the Void was kept behind guarded shelves in Northshire Abbey's library. The abbey archives hold holy scripture and clerical records, as well as scholarly works on shadow and nether energies. The archmage Khadgar is believed to have penned the tome. Its subject was dangerous, so abbey authorities kept it under guard and away from casual visitors. That kept Drusilla La Salle, Northshire's warlock mentor, from browsing it without drawing the priesthood's suspicion.",sp=0},{t="Defias Theft and Recovery",b="A Northshire novice carried the tome away when he abandoned his vows to join the Defias Brotherhood. As he fled into the neighboring vineyards, he took several valuable volumes from the abbey. Drusilla sends promising warlock initiates to the Defias bandit camp to recover the book from their tents. She wants its dark knowledge for her own study. The effort tests whether an initiate has the nerve to bind otherworldly demons.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Powers of the Void?",a="Powers of the Void is a rare occult book about shadow and nether energies, believed to have been penned by the archmage Khadgar. Before it was stolen, the tome was kept in a guarded wing of Northshire Abbey's library.",al={"what is powers of the void","powers of the void book","what is the stolen tome"},it="identity"},{q="Why was the book locked up in Northshire Abbey?",a="Northshire Abbey keeps historic archives, including dangerous texts on illicit magic. Books about Void energies and demonology are locked away so novices and wayward practitioners cannot abuse them.",al={"why was it in the abbey","why did the priests have it","northshire library wing"},it="history"},{q="How did the Defias Brotherhood get the book?",a="A Northshire Abbey novice defected to the Defias Brotherhood and took several valuable volumes from the restricted library. He hid them in the bandit camp in the Northshire vineyards.",al={"who stole the book","defias stolen books","how did defias get it"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Drusilla La Salle want Powers of the Void?",a="Drusilla La Salle wants the tome's knowledge for her own dark craft. As Northshire's warlock mentor, she could not enter the abbey's guarded library without raising suspicion.",al={"why does drusilla want it","who wants the book","drusilla la salle stolen tome"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What does retrieving the tome prove to Drusilla?",a="Retrieving the tome tests whether an initiate has the nerve to bind demons. Drusilla uses that test before teaching them to summon their first imp.",al={"why do warlocks need the book","imp summoning test","stolen tome reward"},it="for_you"},{q="Who wrote Powers of the Void?",a="The arcane treatise is believed to have been penned by the legendary archmage Khadgar, who studied many profound and perilous aspects of magic before venturing beyond the Dark Portal. Its forbidden insights into the deeper void were deemed far too dangerous for casual reading, prompting the priests and scholars of Northshire Abbey to seal it away within a protected wing of their library until a treacherous novice stole it.",al={"powers of the void author","who made powers of the void","powers of the void creator"},it="origin",add="082e56cb"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, retrieving the stolen tome tests whether you have the will to earn instruction in summoning an imp.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you can see that Northshire's Holy Order keeps dangerous magical records alongside clerical texts, hidden from novice eyes."},kw={"defias brotherhood","drusilla la salle","imp","khadgar","northshire abbey","powers of the void","stolen books","the stolen tome","warlock"},rel={"quest:1598","npc:drusilla-la-salle","subzone:northshire-abbey","topic:warlock","topic:defias-brotherhood","zone:elwynn","quest:65"},src={"Powers of the Void","The Stolen Tome"}}
E["item:red-burlap-bandana"] = {t="item",n="Red Burlap Bandana",z="elwynn",s="Near the abbey vineyards in Northshire Valley, Deputy Willem gathers red bandanas from slain Defias thieves. The cloth marks the Brotherhood's low-ranking highwaymen and cutpurses.",h="Near the abbey vineyards in Northshire Valley, Deputy Willem gathers red bandanas from slain Defias thieves.",sec={{t="A Mark of the Brotherhood",b="In Northshire, young recruits and common thugs of the Defias Brotherhood wear red burlap masks. The cheap, rough cloth hides their faces and marks their allegiance to the growing rebellion. They carry these scarves into the eastern orchards, where local guards recognize the red fabric as proof of thieves slain nearby.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Deputy Willem want these bandanas?",a="Deputy Willem collects the bandanas as proof that an adventurer has killed Defias thugs near Northshire Abbey. The thieves wear the red cloth openly, confirming the bounty has been claimed.",al={"why collect bandanas","willem bandanas","brotherhood of thieves turn in"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who wears the red burlap bandanas?",a="Footpads and thugs of the Defias Brotherhood wear red burlap bandanas. The coarse cloth conceals their faces and marks their loyalty to the outlaws.",al={"who wears red bandana","defias mask lore","who drops red bandanas"},it="people"},{q="Why are Defias thieves operating in Northshire?",a="Defias scouts and brigands camp across the stream east of Northshire Abbey to scavenge and steal supplies. The abbey garrison is stretched thin, leaving nearby orchards open to highwaymen.",al={"why are defias in northshire","thieves near abbey"},it="motive"},{q="What makes the bandanas red?",a="Crimson dye gives the cheap burlap bandanas their red color. The hue is the Defias Brotherhood's banner and uniform, helping its members recognize one another in the field.",al={"why are defias masks red","red cloth meaning"}},{q="What is a Red Burlap Bandana?",a="A Red Burlap Bandana is the signature cloth mask worn by members of the Defias Brotherhood. Cheaply made from rough burlap and dyed red, it conceals the wearer's face and marks their allegiance to the outlaw guild. In Northshire, it serves as direct proof of a thug's presence and activity east of the river.",al={"red burlap bandana identity","what are red bandanas","defias bandana lore"},it="identity",add="c4ebebb0"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a developing rogue, you can learn from Northshire's clumsy footpads how quickly undisciplined outlaws become easy targets for local law enforcement.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see red bandanas reaching Northshire Abbey's doorstep, a sign that Stormwind is losing control of the kingdom's rural borders."},kw={"bandana","brotherhood of thieves","defias","mask","northshire","red burlap bandana","willem"},rel={"quest:18","topic:defias-brotherhood","npc:willem","subzone:northshire-abbey","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-army"},src={"Red Burlap Bandana","Brotherhood of Thieves"}}
E["item:red-linen-bandana"] = {t="item",n="Red Linen Bandana",z="elwynn",s="Across Elwynn Forest, the red linen bandana marks the Defias Brotherhood and hides its wearers' faces. Sara Timberlain at the Eastvale Logging Camp wants the cloth for garments and bandages.",h="Across Elwynn Forest, the red linen bandana marks the Defias Brotherhood and hides its wearers' faces.",sec={{t="Mark of the Defias",b="In Northshire Valley, initiates and common thugs wear coarse burlap masks. The crimson linen marks the allegiance of full operatives to Edwin VanCleef's rogue fraternity. It also signals rebellion against Stormwind's crown.",sp=0},{t="Repurposed Cloth",b="Sara Timberlain asks travelers to gather bandanas from outlaw encampments. The masks are tied to bandits, but their linen is respectable. Washed and worked with a needle, the cloth can become sturdy clothing and bandages for the forest's working folk.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why do the Defias wear red linen bandanas?",a="Defias operatives wear red linen bandanas to hide their faces. The cloth also marks their allegiance to Edwin VanCleef's brotherhood and their defiance of Stormwind.",al={"defias mask meaning","why red masks","defias red bandana"},it="identity"},{q="How do these differ from the masks worn in Northshire?",a="Northshire Valley thugs wear coarse burlap masks. Established Defias operatives across Elwynn Forest wear finer red linen.",al={"burlap vs linen","northshire masks","burlap bandana"}},{q="Who wants to collect these bandanas?",a="Sara Timberlain at the Eastvale Logging Camp wants the bandanas. She washes and unravels the masks to weave practical garments.",al={"who takes red linen bandanas","sara timberlain bandana","bandana quest turn in"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Which enemies carry red linen bandanas?",a="Defias operatives across Elwynn Forest carry red linen bandanas. They include Defias Bandits, Ambushers, Rogue Wizards, dockworkers, and ringleaders such as Morgan the Collector.",al={"who drops red linen bandana","where to farm bandanas","defias bandana drops"},it="target",gp=true}},ang={["profession:Tailoring"]="In rural Elwynn, weavers can turn the linen from bandit masks into working clothes.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you know the crimson cloth tied across the lower face. It marks highwaymen and cutpurses in the woods around the capital."},kw={"defias mask","eastvale","elwynn forest","linen","red linen bandana","sara timberlain"},rel={"topic:defias-brotherhood","npc:sara-timberlain","subzone:eastvale-logging-camp","zone:elwynn","npc:morgan-the-collector","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:rogue"},src={"Red Linen Bandana","Red Linen Goods"}}
E["item:rolf-and-malakai-s-medallions"] = {t="item",n="Rolf and Malakai's Medallions",z="elwynn",s="In eastern Elwynn, Rolf and Malakai's Medallions bear the realm's insignia, though their owners vanished on patrol. Guard Thomas seeks the tokens to learn what became of his men.",h="In eastern Elwynn, Rolf and Malakai's Medallions bear the realm's insignia, though their owners vanished on...",sec={{t="A Grim Confirmation",b="Guard Thomas commands the station in eastern Elwynn. When Rolf and Malakai vanished along the riverbanks, he feared the worst. Their medallions confirm the guards died at the hands of encroaching murlocs. The Stormwind garrison has lost soldiers who held the line against wilderness threats while the kingdom's military was stretched thin.",sp=0},{t="Tokens of Service",b="Human guards carry identification medallions on city watch and rural patrols. The tokens show their allegiance and authority under the crown. Returning Rolf and Malakai's medallions to Guard Thomas lets him account for his missing men and record their sacrifice in his field report. He can also warn of aggressive murloc tribes settling near the trade roads.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are Rolf and Malakai's Medallions?",a="Rolf and Malakai's Medallions are service identification tokens carried by Stormwind guards. Murlocs ambushed and killed the guards while they were posted in eastern Elwynn Forest.",al={"what are the medallions","rolfs medallion","malakais medallion"},sp=1,it="identity"},{q="Who do these medallions belong to?",a="The medallions belonged to Guards Rolf and Malakai. They served under Guard Thomas, watching the river and roads between Goldshire and the Eastvale Logging Camp.",al={"who were rolf and malakai","whose medallions"}},{q="Who should I bring these medallions to?",a="Bring the medallions to Guard Thomas. He keeps watch at the eastern bridge on the road between Goldshire and the Eastvale Logging Camp.",al={"who wants the medallions","where do i turn these in","medallion turn in"},gp=true},{q="Why are these medallions important to Guard Thomas?",a="Guard Thomas sent both guards on patrol and feared they had met a foul end. Their medallions confirm their deaths, letting him record their sacrifice and warn Stormwind of the rising murloc threat.",al={"why does thomas want them","guard thomas reaction"},sp=1,it="why_wanted"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Even in the heart of the Alliance, local guardsmen face deadly peril while guarding rural trade routes.",["race:Human"]="For humans of Elwynn, these tokens mark the loss of sons and defenders. Their deaths show the kingdom's vulnerability while its military is occupied elsewhere."},kw={"eastvale","elwynn","guard thomas","malakai","medallions","murloc","rolf","stormwind guard"},rel={"npc:guard-thomas","quest:71","quest:39","topic:murloc","zone:elwynn","subzone:eastvale-logging-camp","subzone:goldshire"},src={"Rolf and Malakai's Medallions","Report to Thomas"}}
E["item:stormwind-armor-marker"] = {t="item",n="Stormwind Armor Marker",z="elwynn",s="At Eastvale Logging Camp, Sara Timberlain accepts a Stormwind Armor Marker from those who aid the realm. It lets them claim crafted gear from artisans commissioned by Stormwind.",h="At Eastvale Logging Camp, Sara Timberlain accepts a Stormwind Armor Marker from those who aid the realm.",sec={{t="Military Requisitions",b="Stormwind's commanders issue armor markers to those who serve the realm. Keeping order across Elwynn Forest strains Stormwind's resources. So commanders sometimes use these official slips in place of standard gear at military outposts. A marker confirms the bearer's service and allows a contracted local craftsman to provide tailored armor.",sp=0},{t="Eastvale Provisioning",b="Sara Timberlain and other artisans work under commission from the Stormwind Army at Eastvale Logging Camp. The camp lies on Elwynn's eastern frontier, where they use local materials to make protective cloth and leather garments. Present a marker there to receive custom-fitted defense for guarding the surrounding woodlands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Stormwind Armor Marker?",a="The Stormwind Armor Marker is an official military voucher for those who aid Stormwind's guards. It proves your service and lets you claim protective armor from an artisan contracted by the army.",al={"what is armor marker","marker purpose","stormwind marker use"},it="purpose"},{q="Who accepts the marker?",a="Sara Timberlain accepts the marker at Eastvale Logging Camp, just east across the river in Elwynn Forest. She provides tailored cloth and leather equipment under contract with the Stormwind Army.",al={"who takes the marker","where to turn in marker","sara timberlain marker"},it="target"},{q="Why does Stormwind use markers instead of handing out armor directly?",a="Stormwind uses markers because its outlying guard posts may lack the storage, blacksmithing or tailoring setups to outfit recruits on site. Field commanders can send recruits to local artisans like Sara Timberlain, who have dedicated workshops.",al={"why tokens instead of armor","why army markers","military vouchers elwynn"},it="motive"},{q="What kind of equipment does the marker provide?",a="The marker lets its bearer choose a newly crafted cloth or leather armor piece made to order by an army supplier under contract.",al={"what armor do i get","marker rewards","cloth or leather"},it="power",gp=true},{q="What is the Stormwind Armor Marker?",a="It is an official military voucher issued on behalf of the Stormwind Army. Rather than hauling bulky suits of protective gear across Elwynn Forest, local commanders issue this token as a guarantee of requisition, entitling the bearer to claim freshly crafted cloth or leather armor from an authorized armorer.",al={"what is stormwind armor marker","armor marker","what is the marker"},it="identity",add="e5398b12"},{q="Where does the Stormwind Armor Marker come from, and who made it?",a="The marker is issued on behalf of the Stormwind Army by Guard Thomas at his post by the eastern bridge in Elwynn, awarded to defenders who prove their shrewdness and valor. It carries the authority of the kingdom's army, commissioning local artisans to supply recruits on the crown's coin.",al={"who made the armor marker","where did the marker come from","who gives the armor marker"},it="origin",add="3e7f2980"},{q="Why does Sara Timberlain want the Stormwind Armor Marker?",a="Sara Timberlain has been commissioned by the Stormwind Army to outfit their recruits and volunteers with cloth and leather armor. She requires the marker as official proof of authorization before surrendering her handcrafted gear, ensuring the kingdom's supplies go only to recognized defenders.",al={"why does sara want the marker","why take marker to eastvale","why need armor marker"},it="why_wanted",add="618263b5"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see how Eastvale Logging Camp connects frontier settlements with Stormwind's military command."},kw={"armor marker","cloth and leather armor","eastvale logging camp","elwynn forest","requisition","sara timberlain","stormwind armor marker"},rel={"quest:59","npc:sara-timberlain","subzone:eastvale-logging-camp","topic:stormwind-army","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Stormwind Armor Marker","Cloth and Leather Armor"}}
E["item:surena-s-choker"] = {t="item",n="Surena's Choker",z="elwynn",s="In Stormwind, Gakin the Darkbinder seeks the bloodstone choker he gave his former apprentice, Surena Caledon. She fled with Erlan Drudgemoor to join the Defias Brotherhood, and Gakin now sends aspiring acolytes to take it back by force.",h="In Stormwind, Gakin the Darkbinder seeks the bloodstone choker he gave his former apprentice, Surena Caledon.",sec={{t="A Master's Lost Investment",b="Beneath the Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind, Gakin the Darkbinder once trained Surena Caledon in the dark arts. He saw promise in her youthful charm and magical talent, and gave her a valuable bloodstone choker to aid her studies. But Surena left her training and fled with Erlan Drudgemoor, a rogue aligned with the Defias Brotherhood.\n\nGakin will not let a traitor keep such a potent artifact. Now he sends initiates seeking mastery over the void to find her at the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch and reclaim the choker by force. Their deed will prove where their loyalty lies.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Gakin the Darkbinder want Surena's Choker back?",a="Gakin gave Surena the bloodstone choker while she was his apprentice. She abandoned her studies and fled with a member of the Defias Brotherhood. Gakin will not let a traitor keep a prized artifact of dark magic.",al={"why does gakin want the choker","gakin surena necklace","why steal the choker back"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who is Surena Caledon?",a="Surena Caledon is a former apprentice warlock who showed natural talent under Gakin the Darkbinder in Stormwind. She turned from her tutor and fled with Erlan Drudgemoor, hiding among the Defias outlaws in Elwynn Forest.",al={"who is surena","surena caledon lore","who has the choker"},it="people"},{q="Where can the choker be found?",a="Surena Caledon carries the choker at the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch in eastern Elwynn Forest, where she is holed up among the Defias bandits.",al={"where is surena","choker location","where is surena caledon"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the choker used for after it is retrieved?",a="Taking back the choker proves an acolyte's ruthlessness and loyalty to Gakin the Darkbinder. He has not said what he will do with it. He laments Surena's wasted talent and hopes his investment in a new student brings different results.",al={"what does gakin do with the choker","choker purpose","why do warlocks need the choker"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Surena's Choker?",a="It is an ornate bloodstone necklace originally owned by Gakin the Darkbinder, the master warlock residing in the Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind. Gakin gifted the precious piece of jewelry to his former apprentice, Surena Caledon, when he was infatuated with her youth and beauty before she betrayed him.",al={"what is surenas choker","surena choker what is it","bloodstone choker"},it="identity",add="195efbf9"},{q="Where does Surena's Choker come from, and who made it?",a="The choker's precise artisan is unknown, but it was originally in the possession of Gakin the Darkbinder. Gakin presented the bloodstone necklace to his young student Surena Caledon during her tutelage under him, long before she ran off with a Defias rogue to the pumpkin patch in Elwynn.",al={"who made surenas choker","origin of surenas choker","where did the choker come from"},it="origin",add="7b9593ae"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a Human or Gnome warlock, retrieving Surena Caledon’s choker is a first trial. It shows that sentiment has no place in the pursuit of demonic power."},kw={"bloodstone choker","brackwell pumpkin patch","erlan drudgemoor","gakin the darkbinder","slaughtered lamb","surena caledon","surena's choker"},rel={"quest:1688","npc:gakin-the-darkbinder","quest:1471","quest:1685","subzone:brackwell-pumpkin-patch","zone:elwynn","topic:warlock"},src={"Surena's Choker","Surena Caledon (quest)"}}
E["item:tainted-letter"] = {t="item",n="Tainted Letter",z="elwynn",s="Near Northshire Abbey, Drusilla La Salle sends human warlock initiates a sealed summons for secret tutelage, beyond watchful eyes.",h="Near Northshire Abbey, Drusilla La Salle sends human warlock initiates a sealed summons for secret tutelage...",sec={{t="A Covert Summons",b="Initiates returning from nearby kobold camps carry Drusilla's summons toward Northshire Abbey. Priests, paladins, and soldiers train openly across its lawns, but fel practitioners must keep their path quiet. Town guards and clerics may grow suspicious if novice warlocks draw attention while seeking their mentor near the abbey grounds.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Ambition",b="Drusilla La Salle meets her pupils on the fringes, where sentries are less likely to pry. Elwynn’s ordinary folk distrust warlocks, and the letter begins a lesson in discipline. Arcane and nether magic risk corruption. Those who commune with denizens of the Twisting Nether must temper ambition with patient self-control.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sent the Tainted Letter?",a="Drusilla La Salle, the warlock trainer near Northshire Abbey, sent the letter.",al={"who wrote tainted letter","drusilla letter","sender of tainted letter"},it="origin"},{q="Why is the letter considered tainted?",a="Drusilla La Salle’s insignia and traces of fel magic mark the letter as the work of a practitioner of demonic arts.",al={"why is it tainted","what makes the letter tainted","tainted seal"}},{q="Why are Northshire guards watching Drusilla La Salle?",a="Northshire’s guards and priests distrust fel magic and demonic summoning. Drusilla keeps to the abbey’s outskirts to avoid their close watch.",al={"drusilla guards","why do guards suspect drusilla","warlock hiding in northshire"}},{q="What advice does Drusilla give upon reading the letter?",a="Drusilla warns that dealing with entities from the Twisting Nether brings temptation and corruption. She urges her pupils to use self-control and prudence while holding to their ambition.",al={"drusilla advice","what does drusilla say","drusilla training"}},{q="What is the Tainted Letter?",a="The Tainted Letter is a sealed message left for you upon your return to Northshire Abbey, stamped with the unmistakable personal insignia of Drusilla La Salle. Addressed to fledgling practitioners of the dark arts, the correspondence serves as an urgent summons to speak with her directly. It carries the faint mark of fel corruption, setting it distinctly apart from the pious and orderly affairs of the Holy Light practiced within the abbey's walls.",al={"what is tainted letter","tainted letter identity","about tainted letter"},it="identity",add="63258adc"},{q="Why is the Tainted Letter given to you?",a="The letter is handed to you so you can establish contact with your trainer, Drusilla La Salle, as soon as your initial tasks around Northshire are complete. Drusilla operates quietly on the fringes of the abbey, keeping a watchful eye out for emerging warlocks. The letter directs you to seek her out before other abbey matters distract you, allowing her to impart vital warnings about self-control, ambition, and the corrupting nature of the Twisting Nether.",al={"why do I need tainted letter","who wants the tainted letter","why give tainted letter"},it="why_wanted",add="3c923280"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you receive the Tainted Letter as your introduction to the shadowy craft in the Kingdom of Stormwind. Power over the Nether calls for constant vigilance and discretion.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you live in a society that broadly champions the Holy Light. Practitioners of dark magic train in secret on the margins of places like Northshire Abbey."},kw={"drusilla la salle","elwynn forest","northshire abbey","tainted letter","twisting nether","warlock"},rel={"quest:3105","npc:drusilla-la-salle","subzone:northshire-abbey","zone:elwynn"},src={"Tainted Letter","Tainted Letter (quest)"}}
E["item:the-collector-s-schedule"] = {t="item",n="The Collector's Schedule",z="elwynn",s="Near the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch, The Collector's Schedule marks the passage of illicit gold shipments through Elwynn Forest. Gnolls carry its handwritten itinerary, and Marshal Dughan recognizes the name it records.",h="Near the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch, The Collector's Schedule marks the passage of illicit gold shipments...",sec={{t="Stolen Gold and Secret Shipments",b="Gold still leaves Elwynn's mines on a schedule, though Stormwind has not officially worked them for months. Banditry and creature incursions drove the miners away. The itinerary names the days and hours when a figure called The Collector receives each shipment.\n\nThe trail leads to a camp near the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch in eastern Elwynn Forest. Marshal Dughan recognizes the Collector's name when he sees the schedule. Who pays for the stolen gold remains unknown.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Collector's Schedule?",a="The Collector's Schedule records when gold shipments leave Elwynn Forest's abandoned mines for an operative called The Collector.",al={"what is this note","collectors schedule item","gold schedule"},it="identity"},{q="Where did the schedule come from?",a="Gnolls carry the schedule along Elwynn Forest's riverbanks and hillsides. They may have taken it from a courier or may be involved in moving the gold.",al={"who drops the schedule","where to find schedule"},it="origin"},{q="Who is the Collector?",a="The Collector is an agent stationed near the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch in eastern Elwynn Forest. Marshal Dughan recognizes the name but does not know whom the agent serves.",al={"who is collector","collector identity"},it="people"},{q="Why is Marshal Dughan alarmed by this schedule?",a="Marshal Dughan is alarmed because Stormwind has had no official miners in Elwynn's mines for months, yet substantial gold shipments still leave them. The shipments point to an organized, illicit mining operation within the kingdom.",al={"why does dughan care","elwynn mines gold"},it="why_wanted"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see how little control Stormwind has over its own territory when unauthorized crews take its resources near the capital.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you can see that Elwynn's mines are not idle. Rich gold veins are being stripped and hauled away."},kw={"brackwell","collector","dughan","elwynn","gold","goldshire","mines","schedule"},rel={"quest:123","quest:147","npc:marshal-dughan","subzone:brackwell-pumpkin-patch","subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn","topic:gnoll"},src={"The Collector's Schedule","The Collector (Classic)"}}
E["item:torn-murloc-fin"] = {t="item",n="Torn Murloc Fin",z="elwynn",s="Along eastern Elwynn's waterways, murlocs crowd the banks and the Stormwind Army's bounty is being answered.",h="Along eastern Elwynn's waterways, murlocs crowd the banks and the Stormwind Army's bounty is being answered.",sec={{t="A Bountied Threat",b="Murlocs have grown numerous along eastern Elwynn's streams and lakes. So the Stormwind Army offers a bounty to thin their numbers. Guard Thomas watches the bridge over the eastern river and gathers severed fins as proof. With soldiers stretched thin by unrest at home and nearby threats, local authorities rely on travelers to show that murloc camps have been cleared.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who buys or collects Torn Murloc Fins?",a="At Elwynn Forest's eastern bridge, Guard Thomas collects Torn Murloc Fins for Marshal Dughan and the Stormwind Army.",al={"who wants fins","fin turn in","guard thomas fins"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Where are the murlocs carrying these fins located?",a="The fins come from murloc foragers and lurkers around Stone Cairn Lake to the north and the southern stream fork near eastern Elwynn's border.",al={"where to farm fins","murloc fin locations","fin drops"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Stormwind require fins as proof?",a="Fins are unmistakable and easy to carry. They give the Stormwind Army proof of slain murlocs before it pays the bounty hunters.",al={"why fins","proof of kill murlocs","bounty proof"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why is the Stormwind Army paying for dead murlocs?",a="Murloc villages have spread quickly along the waterways, threatening travelers, fishermen, and local infrastructure. The Stormwind Army's forces are occupied elsewhere.",al={"why murloc bounty","murloc problem elwynn"},it="conflict"},{q="What is a Torn Murloc Fin?",a="A Torn Murloc Fin is a physical trophy sliced from the hide of murlocs infesting eastern Elwynn Forest. Rather than an ornamental trinket or alchemical ingredient, it serves as tangible proof that a roaming amphibian raider has been slain, presenting reliable verification for local authorities offering bounties.",al={"what is torn murloc fin","torn fin lore","about murloc fin"},it="identity",add="afa68c63"},{q="Where do Torn Murloc Fins come from?",a="These fins are harvested directly from the bodies of murloc foragers and lurkers inhabiting the freshwater shallows of Elwynn Forest. In particular, aggressive tribes have established encampments along the shores of Stone Cairn Lake and the southern fork of the eastern rivers, menacing local travelers and farmlands.",al={"torn murloc fin origin","where do murloc fins come from","source of torn murloc fin"},it="origin",add="5ee7d3aa"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, clearing eastern Elwynn's waterways protects the vital routes between Goldshire, Lakeshire, and Stormwind City.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you know local authorities rely more and more on mercenaries to protect homesteads and riverbanks from aggressive murloc settlements."},kw={"bounty on murlocs","elwynn murlocs","guard thomas","murloc fin","murloc forager","murloc lurker","stone cairn lake","torn murloc fin"},rel={"quest:46","npc:guard-thomas","topic:murloc","subzone:stone-cairn-lake","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-army","npc:marshal-dughan","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Torn Murloc Fin","Bounty on Murlocs"}}
E["item:tough-wolf-meat"] = {t="item",n="Tough Wolf Meat",z="elwynn",s="In Northshire and Coldridge, wolves prowl their valleys and provide meat for hungry locals. Tough Wolf Meat is coarse and stringy. People in Elwynn Forest eat it, and dwarven outfitters in Dun Morogh use it to stock their supplies.",h="In Northshire and Coldridge, wolves prowl their valleys and provide meat for hungry locals.",sec={{t="Frontier Rations",b="Wolves prowl near Northshire Valley and Dun Morogh. They threaten nearby settlements, yet their meat offers a hard-won source of food. Coarse, stringy and chewy, it is prized by resource-strapped frontiersmen.\n\nOutside Northshire Abbey, Eagan Peltskinner hates the vicious beasts but cooks their meat into steaks. He trades basic supplies and gear to those who cull the packs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does Tough Wolf Meat come from?",a="Young wolves and timber wolves in Northshire Valley in Elwynn Forest provide Tough Wolf Meat. Ragged wolves in Coldridge Valley in Dun Morogh provide it too.",al={"tough wolf meat source","how to get tough wolf meat","where to farm tough wolf meat"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Who wants to collect this meat in Elwynn Forest?",a="Eagan Peltskinner, outside Northshire Abbey, collects the meat. He hates the wolves, but cooks their meat into steaks and trades spare equipment to new recruits who bring him eight cuts.",al={"who needs wolf meat","eagan peltskinner meat","wolf meat turn in"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Is this meat useful outside of human lands?",a="Yes. Dwarven outfitters in frigid Dun Morogh accept meat from ragged wolves in Coldridge Valley to keep their supplies stocked.",al={"wolf meat dun morogh","dwarf wolf meat","dwarven outfitters meat"}},{q="Is Tough Wolf Meat used in normal cooking recipes?",a="No. Local frontiersmen such as Eagan Peltskinner and Coldridge outfitters seek Tough Wolf Meat as a bounty. It is not an ingredient in standard camp cooking recipes.",al={"can you cook tough wolf meat","tough wolf meat recipes"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What is Tough Wolf Meat?",a="It is coarse, lean meat harvested from wild wolves prowling the wilderness of Northshire and Dun Morogh. While stringy and far from tender, it serves as a hearty staple for local trappers and hungry frontiersmen who know how to cook it into sustaining steaks.",al={"what is tough wolf meat","tough wolf meat lore","tough wolf meat"},it="identity",add="877dd280"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human recruit in Northshire Valley, you can gather wolf meat for Eagan Peltskinner outside the abbey. It is one of the earliest survival tasks beyond its quiet cloisters.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf in Coldridge Valley, you can cull ragged timber wolves for meat to supply local outfitters before setting off across Dun Morogh."},kw={"dun morogh","eagan peltskinner","elwynn forest","northshire abbey","timber wolf","tough wolf meat","young wolf"},rel={"quest:33","quest:5261","quest:179","subzone:northshire-abbey","zone:elwynn","zone:dunmorogh"},src={"Tough Wolf Meat","Wolves Across the Border"}}
E["item:william-s-shipment"] = {t="item",n="William's Shipment",z="elwynn",s="In Goldshire, William's Shipment is bound for his brother Morgan in Stormwind, carrying candles from Elwynn's kobolds.",h="In Goldshire, William's Shipment is bound for his brother Morgan in Stormwind, carrying candles from Elwynn's...",sec={{t="A Familial Trade",b="William Pestle keeps trade moving between Goldshire and the capital. He gathers goods in Elwynn Forest, while his brother Morgan runs Pestle's Apothecary in Stormwind's Trade District. William cannot leave his duties to travel north, so couriers carry the wax and candles into the city.",sp=0},{t="Kobold Wax",b="Kobold candles from Elwynn's mines fill William's shipment. He gathers the large candles for their wax and packs them for Morgan at Pestle's Apothecary. That wax joins the stock used in the capital's alchemical trade.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside William's Shipment?",a="The shipment holds candles gathered from kobolds in Elwynn Forest's mines. William collects them from travelers passing through and packs them as raw ingredients for his family's alchemy shop.",al={"shipment contents","what is in the box","what does william send"},it="item"},{q="Who is William sending this package to?",a="William sends the package to his brother, Morgan Pestle, who runs Pestle's Apothecary in Stormwind City's Trade District.",al={"who gets the shipment","who is the delivery for","shipment destination"},it="target"},{q="Why does an apothecary need so many candles?",a="William says he and his brother need the large candles for their wax. He does not say which preparations will use it.",al={"why candles for alchemy","what does pestle do with candles","candle use"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why doesn't William deliver the package himself?",a="William is busy managing his affairs and gathering goods in Goldshire, leaving no time for the overland trip to Stormwind. He hires travelers bound for the capital to carry the package.",al={"why can't william go","why does william need a courier"},it="why_me"},{q="What is William's Shipment?",a="William's Shipment is a securely packed bundle of large wax candles prepared by William Pestle in Goldshire. The candles were taken from kobolds in Elwynn Forest's mines and boxed up for delivery to Morgan Pestle in Stormwind.",al={"what is williams shipment","williams shipment package","williams delivery"},it="identity",add="bf7eefd8"},{q="Where does William's Shipment come from, and who made it?",a="The shipment comes directly from William Pestle, an alchemist residing at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire. William packed the crates himself using large wax candles taken from the kobolds infesting the nearby Fargodeep and Jasperlode mines.",al={"who made williams shipment","where did williams shipment come from","origin of williams shipment"},it="origin",add="2b07f2a7"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, you can see Goldshire's trade connecting rural hamlets to the capital, Stormwind.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help protect Elwynn's mines from kobolds and supply the capital's shops with raw alchemy goods."},kw={"candles","goldshire","kobold candles","morgan pestle","pestle's apothecary","stormwind","trade district","william pestle","william's shipment"},rel={"quest:61","npc:morgan-pestle","quest:60","subzone:trade-district","topic:kobold","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"William's Shipment","Shipment to Stormwind"}}
E["npc:auntie-bernice-stonefield"] = {t="npc",n="\"Auntie\" Bernice Stonefield",z="elwynn",s="At the Stonefield homestead in south-central Elwynn Forest, “Auntie” Bernice Stonefield keeps watch over the neighborhood. Widowed by the kingdom’s military campaigns, she lives beside Ma Stonefield and is known across the valley for her pork belly pies. She remains deeply suspicious of the rival Maclure family.",h="At the Stonefield homestead in south-central Elwynn Forest, “Auntie” Bernice Stonefield keeps watch over the...",sec={{t="A Life of Hardship",b="War took Bernice’s husband in the Kingdom of Stormwind’s military campaigns. She now lives with her kin at the family homestead. There, she helps Ma Stonefield manage the farm’s daily affairs and keeps the household fed and running. Her pork belly pies have made her famous throughout the valley.",sp=0},{t="The Feud and the Missing Necklace",b="The old bitterness between the Stonefields and the Maclures runs deep for Bernice. When her prized family necklace went missing, she suspected young Billy Maclure had taken it. Yet recovering the necklace proves more complicated than settling a neighbor’s prank. Billy swears he did not steal it, but nearly admits he dropped it near the Fargodeep Mine. There, he saw the gold-toothed kobold Goldtooth snatch it and carry it to his den.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Auntie Bernice Stonefield?",a="“Auntie” Bernice Stonefield is an elder of the Stonefield family who lives at the Stonefield Farm in southern Elwynn Forest. Widowed by the kingdom’s wars, she tends the farm with Ma Stonefield and is known for her pork belly pies.",al={"who is auntie bernice","bernice stonefield lore","stonefield auntie"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to Auntie Bernice's husband?",a="Bernice’s husband fell during a military campaign fought for the Kingdom of Stormwind, leaving her a widow.",al={"auntie bernice husband","who was bernice married to","stonefield widow"},it="history"},{q="What is Auntie Bernice famous for?",a="Bernice is known across the local countryside for her pork belly pies, which even mischievous neighbors will bargain for a slice.",al={"bernice stonefield pie","pork belly pie elwynn"},it="fame"},{q="Why is Auntie Bernice angry with Billy Maclure?",a="Bernice suspects Billy Maclure took her cherished family necklace, deepening the long-standing feud between the Stonefields and the Maclures.",al={"billy maclure feud","bernice necklace thief","why does bernice hate billy"},it="conflict"},{q="Did Billy Maclure actually steal the necklace?",a="Billy swears he did not steal Bernice’s necklace, though he nearly admits he dropped it near the Fargodeep Mine. He says the gold-toothed kobold Goldtooth picked it up and carried it to his den.",al={"did billy steal the necklace","who has the stonefield necklace","goldtooth necklace"},sp=1},{q="Where is Auntie Bernice located?",a="Bernice can be found outside the main farmhouse at Stonefield Farm, south of the road between Goldshire and Westfall, beside Ma Stonefield.",al={"auntie bernice location","where is bernice stonefield"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Auntie Bernice Stonefield on?",a="Auntie Bernice is a loyal subject of the Kingdom of Stormwind and a proud member of the Stonefield family. She firmly stands with her kin in their longstanding, bitter feud against their neighbors, the Maclures, holding little patience for anyone bearing that name.",al={"auntie bernice faction","who does bernice support","bernice stonefield alliance"},it="side",add="0a2ddc6d"},{q="What does Auntie Bernice Stonefield want?",a="Auntie Bernice primarily wants the return of her treasured family necklace, which went missing and caused her to suspect young Billy Maclure. To solve the mystery and retrieve her heirloom, she is willing to bake one of her famous pork belly pies to coax the truth out of him.",al={"what does auntie bernice need","auntie bernice goal","bernice stonefield quest motive"},it="wants",add="0e5ea09d"},{q="Why is Auntie Bernice Stonefield here?",a="The Stonefield Farm is Auntie Bernice's home. Having lost her husband to one of Stormwind's military campaigns, she remains on the family homestead in Elwynn Forest alongside Ma Stonefield and the rest of the clan, tending to domestic chores and farm life.",al={"why is bernice at the farm","bernice stonefield location why","what brings auntie bernice here"},it="why_here",add="f6bb7867"},{q="Who is Auntie Bernice Stonefield tied to?",a="She is an elder matriarch of the Stonefield clan, living side-by-side with Ma Stonefield on their Elwynn farm. Her family is entangled in a bitter, ongoing rivalry with the nearby Maclure household, which colors nearly all her interactions with their kin.",al={"auntie bernice family","bernice stonefield relatives","who is auntie bernice related to"},it="ties",add="21972eac"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Bernice’s pork belly pie is famous across Elwynn Forest as a staple of hearty human frontier cooking.",["race:Human"]="As a human, Bernice shows the resilience of Stormwind’s rural folk, carrying on daily life and family pride after her husband fell in the kingdom’s wars."},kw={"auntie","bernice","elwynn","goldtooth","maclure","necklace","pork belly pie","stonefield"},rel={"subzone:stonefield-farm","npc:ma-stonefield","npc:billy-maclure","quest:85","quest:86","quest:84","quest:87","zone:elwynn"},src={"\"Auntie\" Bernice Stonefield"}}
E["npc:billy-maclure"] = {t="npc",n="Billy Maclure",z="elwynn",s="At Maclure Vineyards, Billy Maclure's pranks stir trouble between two neighboring farms. The young human boy dodges chores and joins the feud between his family and the Stonefields, though fresh pastries can win his help.",h="At Maclure Vineyards, Billy Maclure's pranks stir trouble between two neighboring farms.",sec={{t="A Boy at the Vineyards",b="Billy Maclure spends his days outside the barn at Maclure Vineyards, near farmer Gerard Tiller. He grows up among the grapevines in southern Elwynn Forest, often slipping away from chores to roam the meadows. The Maclures and Stonefields have long been hostile toward each other. Billy turns their feud into a chance for pranks and petty theft.",sp=0},{t="The Stolen Necklace",b="Billy Maclure stole Auntie Bernice Stonefield's treasured heirloom necklace. He lost hold of it while running near Fargodeep Mine. Goldtooth, a massive and vicious kobold, snatched the necklace and vanished into the mine's tunnels. Billy fears the kobolds and the neighboring elders' anger, so he hesitates to confess. Auntie Bernice's hot pork belly pie can coax the truth from him.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Billy Maclure?",a="Billy Maclure is a young human boy at Maclure Vineyards in Elwynn Forest. He dodges farm work, plays pranks, and aggravates the neighboring Stonefields.",al={"who is billy","billy maclure lore","maclure kid"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Billy Maclure be found?",a="Billy waits outside the main barn at Maclure Vineyards, in southern Elwynn Forest east of Stonefield Farm.",al={"billy maclure location","where is billy","find billy maclure"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What did Billy do to Auntie Bernice?",a="Billy stole Auntie Bernice Stonefield's heirloom necklace during the feud between their families.",al={"bernice necklace","what did billy steal","stolen necklace elwynn"},it="conflict"},{q="What happened to the necklace Billy stole?",a="Billy lost the necklace near Fargodeep Mine. Goldtooth picked it up and carried it into the mine.",al={"where is the necklace","lost necklace elwynn","who has bernice necklace"},sp=1,it="motive"},{q="How do you get Billy to confess what happened to the necklace?",a="Offer Billy a freshly baked pork belly pie from Auntie Bernice. His appetite can coax him to confess.",al={"pie for billy","how to bribe billy","bribing billy maclure"},sp=1,it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Who is Goldtooth?",a="Goldtooth is an exceptionally large and vicious kobold leader in Fargodeep Mine. He took Auntie Bernice's necklace near the mine entrance and keeps it in the tunnels.",al={"who is goldtooth","goldtooth lore","fargodeep kobold"},sp=1,it="threat"},{q="Whose side is Billy Maclure on?",a="Billy is a loyal member of the Maclure family in Elwynn Forest, firmly allied with the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance. While his family maintains a bitter and long-standing feud with their neighbors, the Stonefields, Billy is still just a young boy who gets caught between family grudges and his personal appetite.",al={"billy maclure faction","which side is billy on","who does billy support"},it="side",add="324ac528"},{q="What does Billy Maclure want?",a="Billy wants little more than to stay out of trouble and indulge his appetite. Above all, he craves Auntie Bernice Stonefield's famous pork belly pies, despite the fierce rivalry between their families. He is even willing to confess his mischievous misdeeds if someone brings him one of her fresh, savory pies.",al={"what does billy want","what does billy maclure crave","billy maclure favorite food"},it="wants",add="c9c2f9db"},{q="Why is Billy Maclure here?",a="Billy resides at the Maclure Vineyards, which is his family's home and livelihood in Elwynn Forest. He spends his days loitering outside the barn near Gerard Tiller, running errands, and playing around the surrounding countryside when he is not sneaking over toward the neighboring Stonefield farm.",al={"why is billy maclure here","why is billy at maclure vineyards","what is billy doing here"},it="why_here",add="f69aaa51"},{q="Who is Billy Maclure tied to?",a="Billy is part of the Maclure farming family, residing alongside kin and workers like Gerard Tiller at the vineyards. Through his mischievous antics, he is also intimately entangled with the rival Stonefield family, particularly Auntie Bernice Stonefield, whose prized necklace he swiped and whose baking he secretly loves.",al={"billy maclure family","who is billy maclure related to","billy maclure connections"},it="ties",add="275e906f"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, Billy's troubles show the everyday quarrels of the Elwynn countryside. Farm feuds and childhood mischief continue amid Stormwind's political turmoil.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer newly arrived from Northshire, helping with Billy's pranks introduces you to dangers in Fargodeep Mine.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can see how Auntie Bernice's pork belly pie helps settle local disputes and coax confessions from tight-lipped farm boys."},kw={"bernice stonefield","billy maclure","fargodeep mine","goldtooth","lost necklace","maclure vineyards","pork belly pie","stonefield"},rel={"subzone:maclure-vineyards","quest:85","quest:86","quest:87","quest:84","subzone:fargodeep-mine","topic:kobold","npc:gerard-tiller"},src={"Billy Maclure"}}
E["npc:brother-neals"] = {t="npc",n="Brother Neals",z="elwynn",s="At Northshire Abbey, Brother Neals keeps the food and drink stores supplied. He oversees shipments and samples wine from the local vineyard.",h="At Northshire Abbey, Brother Neals keeps the food and drink stores supplied.",sec={{t="Keeper of the Cellar",b="From his rooms in the upper belfry, Brother Neals follows grape manifests from the Northshire vineyards. Frequent tastings let him check each vintage. He also tracks deliveries from the valley’s fields, keeping the abbey’s stores supplied.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Brother Neals?",a="Brother Neals manages Northshire Abbey’s stores of food, drink, and wine for the clergy and recruits in the valley.",al={"brother neals","neals","who is neals"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Brother Neals be found?",a="Brother Neals stays in Northshire Abbey’s uppermost room. Climb the stone staircases inside the main hall to reach his quiet chamber near the top of the tower.",al={"where is brother neals","brother neals location","find neals"},gp=true},{q="What is his role regarding the vineyard?",a="Brother Neals tracks grape harvests and wine shipments from the nearby Northshire Vineyard. He samples the vintage and keeps the ledgers.",al={"grape manifest quest","neals wine","what does neals do"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Brother Neals on?",a="Brother Neals is a loyal member of the Brotherhood of Northshire, serving Northshire Abbey and the Grand Alliance of Stormwind. He carries out his clerical duties peacefully inside the abbey walls.",al={"brother neals faction","who does brother neals serve","brother neals alliance"},it="side",add="340be3c1"},{q="What does Brother Neals want?",a="Brother Neals needs to keep proper accounting of Northshire's stores, in particular the wine inventory from the local vineyard. He requires shipments and records like the grape manifest brought directly up to his quarters so he can manage supplies—and enjoy a generous sample of the abbey's vintage.",al={"brother neals grape manifest","what does brother neals need"},it="wants",add="0d7c1646"},{q="Why is Brother Neals here?",a="As a brother of the abbey, Neals resides in the quiet upper tower of Northshire Abbey to oversee the community's stores of food and drink. His post keeps him close to the cellar reserves and accounting documents necessary to sustain the clergy and new recruits.",al={"why is brother neals in the tower","why is brother neals at northshire"},it="why_here",add="bb6478cd"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As someone who manages the monastery’s provisions and spirits, Brother Neals has a role tied to the culinary arts."},kw={"brother neals","elwynn forest","grape manifest","northshire abbey","northshire valley","vineyard","wine"},rel={"subzone:northshire-abbey","subzone:northshire-valley","quest:3905","zone:elwynn"},src={"Brother Neals"}}
E["npc:brother-wilhelm"] = {t="npc",n="Brother Wilhelm",z="elwynn",s="Behind Goldshire's smithy, Brother Wilhelm guides young paladins into the wider forest. They come from Northshire Abbey to take their first steps in Elwynn.",h="Behind Goldshire's smithy, Brother Wilhelm guides young paladins into the wider forest.",sec={{t="A Guide in Goldshire",b="Brother Wilhelm trains new paladins behind Goldshire's smithy. Northshire Valley shelters those who begin their path in the Light, but many seek his guidance once they enter the wider forest. He teaches them their sacred duties as they leave the abbey. Then they take up the work of protecting the realm.",sp=0},{t="The Path of the Tome",b="Brother Wilhelm guides aspiring paladins toward the Tome of Divinity. Its rite teaches initiates the weight of sacrifice and the power of divine redemption. Through the trials, they test their devotion and learn to wield the Light. They can resurrect fallen comrades and uphold justice across the Kingdom of Stormwind.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Brother Wilhelm?",a="Brother Wilhelm is behind the village blacksmith's workshop in Goldshire, Elwynn Forest. He trains and guides aspiring paladins there.",al={"wilhelm location","where is brother wilhelm","find brother wilhelm"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What services does Brother Wilhelm provide?",a="Brother Wilhelm teaches young paladins new spells, martial blessings, and holy techniques as they travel through Elwynn Forest.",al={"what does wilhelm do","paladin trainer goldshire","brother wilhelm trainer"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Is Brother Wilhelm part of the Brotherhood of Northshire?",a="Brother Wilhelm's title and closeness to Northshire Abbey suggest ties to the Brotherhood of Northshire. From Goldshire, he serves the Church of the Holy Light and the Kingdom of Stormwind.",al={"is wilhelm brotherhood of northshire","wilhelm faction","who does brother wilhelm serve"},it="ties"},{q="What is his role in the Tome of Divinity quest?",a="Brother Wilhelm guides human paladins who have grown in power toward the Tome of Divinity and its trials. Those trials lead to the sacred blessing of resurrection.",al={"tome of divinity wilhelm","resurrection quest wilhelm","goldshire paladin quest"},it="motive",gp=true},{q="Who is Brother Wilhelm?",a="Brother Wilhelm is a human paladin mentor stationed in Goldshire. Devoted to the Holy Light and the defense of the kingdom, he offers guidance and training to fledgling paladins who venture beyond Northshire Valley into the broader regions of Elwynn Forest.",al={"who is brother wilhelm","brother wilhelm identity","who is wilhelm"},it="identity",add="0af03050"},{q="Whose side is Brother Wilhelm on?",a="Brother Wilhelm is firmly aligned with the Alliance and the Kingdom of Stormwind. He serves the holy orders of the Light, dedicating himself to strengthening the realm's paladins against internal strife and regional threats.",al={"who does brother wilhelm serve","wilhelm faction","brother wilhelm alliance"},it="side",add="cccf7116"},{q="Why is Brother Wilhelm in Goldshire?",a="Stationed behind the Goldshire smithy, Brother Wilhelm serves as an instructor for young paladins who have recently left Northshire Abbey. He remains on hand in Elwynn Forest to oversee their continuous development and spiritual readiness as they step into active duty.",al={"why is brother wilhelm here","brother wilhelm goldshire","why is wilhelm in elwynn"},it="why_here",add="3fb91c50"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you find your first mentor in Brother Wilhelm after leaving Northshire Valley. He guides your growth and opens the path to mastering the Tome of Divinity.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you see in Brother Wilhelm the faith of the Church of the Holy Light, which defends Elwynn's heartland."},kw={"brother wilhelm","brotherhood of northshire","elwynn forest","goldshire","holy light","paladin trainer","tome of divinity"},rel={"subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn","quest:2997","topic:light","topic:brotherhood-of-northshire","topic:knights-of-the-silver-hand"},src={"Brother Wilhelm"}}
E["npc:deputy-rainer"] = {t="npc",n="Deputy Rainer",z="elwynn",s="At Westbrook Garrison, Deputy Rainer holds Elwynn's western border against threats from Westfall. The Stormwind Army officer coordinates the local defense, though reinforcements have not arrived.",h="At Westbrook Garrison, Deputy Rainer holds Elwynn's western border against threats from Westfall.",sec={{t="Holding the Western Border",b="Westbrook Garrison guards Elwynn Forest's western edge, where the road crosses into Westfall. Political paralysis in Stormwind City leaves much of the army abroad or caught in bureaucracy, and border posts like this one lack troops. Deputy Rainer organizes the defense outside the tower with the few forces at hand.\n\nRiverpaw gnolls and wandering thieves threaten the local roads. Rainer depends on passing travelers and mercenary adventurers to keep the forest trails secure.",sp=0},{t="The Road to Westfall",b="Deputy Rainer watches for the Riverpaw pack and warns travelers about Hogger, the infamous gnoll chieftain. He also carries word of the troubled lands beyond the river. The chaos at Elwynn's border begins in Westfall's lawless farmlands, so he sends capable volunteers across the border to Gryan Stoutmantle and the struggling People's Militia.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Deputy Rainer?",a="Deputy Rainer is a Stormwind Army officer stationed at Westbrook Garrison on Elwynn Forest's western edge. He oversees road security and hires adventurers to fight nearby threats.",al={"rainer elwynn","who is rainer","westbrook garrison officer"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Westbrook Garrison undermanned?",a="Most of the Stormwind Army is deployed elsewhere, and political disorder in the capital keeps regular reinforcements from reaching outlying regions. Marshal Dughan in Goldshire must rely on independent adventurers to help Rainer.",al={"why no guards at westbrook","why is the garrison struggling","westbrook needs help"}},{q="What threats is Rainer trying to counter?",a="Rainer works to contain the Riverpaw gnolls in the woods south of the garrison, roving thieves, and Hogger, the notorious gnoll chieftain who preys on travelers along the border.",al={"what enemies are near westbrook","riverpaw gnolls westbrook","westbrook gnolls"},it="threat"},{q="Where does Rainer send adventurers after clearing the gnolls?",a="After the gnolls near the garrison are driven back, Rainer sends seasoned adventurers across the western border into Westfall. There they help Gryan Stoutmantle and the People's Militia at Sentinel Hill.",al={"where to go after rainer","rainer quest westfall","after westbrook garrison"},it="next_step"},{q="Whose side is Deputy Rainer on?",a="Rainer is a loyal officer of the Stormwind Army, serving the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance. Stationed at Westbrook Garrison, he answers to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire and strives to protect Elwynn's western marches from encroaching chaos.",al={"deputy rainer faction","who does rainer serve","is rainer alliance"},it="side",add="8453208a"},{q="What does Deputy Rainer want?",a="Rainer wants capable volunteers to defend Elwynn Forest's western border. With the army stretched thin, he seeks to cull the aggressive Riverpaw gnoll pack to the south, secure the trade roads against thieves, and put an end to the menace of Hogger.",al={"what does rainer want","deputy rainer goals","what is rainer asking for"},it="wants",add="b0214c4a"},{q="Why is Deputy Rainer here?",a="Rainer is stationed at Westbrook Garrison to guard the border between Elwynn Forest and Westfall. As beasts and bandits spill eastward across the river, he stands watch outside the guard tower, coordinating patrols and enlisting travelers to hold the frontier.",al={"why is rainer at westbrook","why is deputy rainer here"},it="why_here",add="5835f036"},{q="Who is Deputy Rainer tied to?",a="Rainer reports to Marshal Dughan, commander of the garrison forces in Goldshire. He also cooperates across the border with Gryan Stoutmantle and the People's Militia in Westfall, directing tested fighters westward to aid their struggle against the Defias Brotherhood.",al={"who is rainer affiliated with","rainer connections","who does rainer report to"},it="ties",add="b3def1b5"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance hero, you see how Stormwind's outlying garrisons adapt when regular royal support does not reach them."},kw={"deputy rainer","elwynn forest","gryan stoutmantle","hogger","marshal dughan","riverpaw","westbrook garrison","westfall"},rel={"subzone:westbrook-garrison","quest:11","quest:109","quest:239","quest:176","npc:marshal-dughan","npc:gryan-stoutmantle","zone:westfall"},src={"Deputy Rainer"}}
E["npc:drusilla-la-salle"] = {t="npc",n="Drusilla La Salle",z="elwynn",s="Outside Northshire Abbey, Drusilla La Salle teaches warlocks in the graveyard. The human trainer guides new spellcasters in shadow and summoning, beyond the Holy Order’s reach. When forbidden knowledge leaves the abbey, she moves to claim it.",h="Outside Northshire Abbey, Drusilla La Salle teaches warlocks in the graveyard.",sec={{t="Shadows in Holy Ground",b="Drusilla La Salle teaches novice warlocks among the headstones outside Northshire Abbey. Within, paladins and priests practice beneath stained glass. Warlocks keep to society’s edges because Stormwind forbids demonology and fel magic. Recruits receive tainted correspondence, then Drusilla teaches them to wield shadow without drawing the abbey authorities’ immediate anger.",sp=0},{t="Powers of the Void",b="Northshire Abbey’s library wing holds forbidden books, including Powers of the Void. Drusilla has long wanted the manuscript, but a warlock in the guarded archives would invite suspicion. Her chance comes when an apostate novice flees the abbey to join the Defias Brotherhood with the book. Drusilla sends her apprentices after the turncoat to bring her the grimoire, claiming they are recovering abbey property.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is a warlock allowed near Northshire Abbey?",a="The Church of the Holy Light and Stormwind’s leaders deeply distrust warlocks. Drusilla teaches in the nearby graveyard, away from the priests and clerics studying inside Northshire Abbey.",al={"why is drusilla at abbey","warlock in holy abbey","why is she in the graveyard"},it="why_here"},{q="What book is Drusilla trying to obtain?",a="Drusilla seeks Powers of the Void, a grimoire once locked in a protected part of Northshire Abbey’s Library Wing. A Defias defector steals it, carrying the book beyond the abbey’s reach.",al={"what book does she want","powers of the void book","the stolen tome quest book"},it="wants"},{q="Who stole the book from the library?",a="A novice from Northshire Abbey steals the tome after breaking his vows and joining the Defias Brotherhood. He flees to a nearby camp in Northshire Valley.",al={"who took the tome","defias book thief","who stole powers of the void"}},{q="What role does she play for new human warlocks?",a="Drusilla is the first trainer for human warlocks. She accepts the tainted letters sent to recruits and teaches basic curses and summoned servitors.",al={"human warlock trainer northshire","who trains warlocks in northshire"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Drusilla La Salle?",a="Drusilla La Salle is a human warlock stationed in the abbey graveyard in Northshire Valley. While holy clerics and paladins train within the abbey walls, she quietly instructs novice humans who possess an affinity for darker arts, teaching them to bend fel and shadow energies to their will.",al={"who is drusilla","drusilla la salle lore","drusilla identity"},it="identity",add="fe9579dd"},{q="Whose side is Drusilla La Salle on?",a="She is aligned with the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance. Although the Light-worshipping clergy at Northshire Abbey view warlocks with suspicion, Drusilla serves the realm by training fledgling practitioners to direct their dangerous talents against Stormwind's enemies.",al={"is drusilla evil","drusilla alliance","drusilla faction"},it="side",add="89e305f6"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you learn the dark arts from Drusilla, your first mentor. She teaches practical curses and fel summoning, and urges you to hide your ambition in plain sight.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you see Drusilla outside Northshire’s holy halls, practicing shadow and demonic pacts beside the consecrated graveyard."},kw={"abbey","drusilla la salle","graveyard","northshire","powers of the void","stolen tome","warlock trainer"},rel={"quest:1598","subzone:northshire-abbey","subzone:northshire-valley","subzone:library-wing-northshire","topic:defias-brotherhood","zone:elwynn"},src={"Drusilla La Salle"}}
E["npc:gerard-tiller"] = {t="npc",n="Gerard Tiller",z="elwynn",s="At the Maclure Vineyards, Gerard Tiller tends the grounds and longs for spring water. Bring him a skin of it, and he offers shiny red apples.",h="At the Maclure Vineyards, Gerard Tiller tends the grounds and longs for spring water.",sec={{t="A Thirsty Farmhand",b="Gerard Tiller works outside the barn at the Maclure Vineyards, south of Goldshire. The vineyard is known for its grapes, and keeping the harvest going takes hard labor. His chores leave him thirsty, so he welcomes travelers who bring a skin of fresh spring water. In return, he gives them shiny red apples gathered from local orchards.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gerard Tiller?",a="Gerard Tiller is a human farmhand who works outside the barn at the Maclure Vineyards in southern Elwynn Forest.",al={"gerard tiller identity","who is gerard","tiller elwynn"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Gerard Tiller?",a="Look outside the large wooden barn at the Maclure Vineyards, south of Goldshire and east of the Stonefield Farm.",al={"gerard tiller location","where is gerard","find gerard elwynn"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Gerard Tiller trade?",a="Gerard trades a Shiny Red Apple for a skin of Refreshing Spring Water.",al={"gerard apple trade","gerard tiller water","what does gerard want"},gp=true},{q="Does Gerard get involved in the Maclure and Stonefield feud?",a="No. Gerard works at the Maclure Vineyards and tends to his chores and thirst, apart from the rivalry between the Maclures and Stonefields.",al={"gerard tiller feud","maclure feud gerard"},it="side"},{q="What does Gerard Tiller want?",a="Working under the hot sun at the Maclure Vineyards is parching work, and Gerard wants little more than a simple skin of Refreshing Spring Water to quench his thirst. If you bring him a drink, he will gladly trade you a crisp, Shiny Red Apple from the orchard in return.",al={"what does gerard tiller need","gerard tiller trade","what does gerard want"},it="wants",add="467277ed"},{q="Why is Gerard Tiller here?",a="Gerard Tiller makes his living as a laborer tending the grounds outside the barn at the Maclure Vineyards. While the surrounding lands of Elwynn face unrest, Gerard remains focused on everyday farm work and looking after the harvest.",al={"why is gerard tiller at the vineyards","gerard tiller location reason","what does gerard tiller do"},it="why_here",add="9aadf23d"},{q="Who is Gerard Tiller tied to?",a="Gerard is tied to the Maclure family, working their vineyards south of Stormwind City. Though he labors directly on their land beside their barns, he minds his own business and avoids the bitter feud raging between the Maclures and their neighboring rivals, the Stonefields.",al={"gerard tiller connections","who does gerard tiller work for","gerard tiller allies"},it="ties",add="9f9d4e60"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Gerard trades fresh apples for plain spring water, giving travelers who want simple ingredients a source of fruit."},kw={"elwynn forest","gerard tiller","give gerard a drink","maclure vineyards","refreshing spring water","shiny red apple"},rel={"quest:16","subzone:maclure-vineyards","zone:elwynn"},src={"Gerard Tiller"}}
E["npc:gramma-stonefield"] = {t="npc",n="Gramma Stonefield",z="elwynn",s="At the Stonefield farm in Elwynn, Gramma Stonefield works quietly to ease a family feud.",h="At the Stonefield farm in Elwynn, Gramma Stonefield works quietly to ease a family feud.",sec={{t="A Secret Peacemaker",b="For decades, the Stonefields and Maclures have bickered across the road. Gramma Stonefield, the oldest living member of her clan, sees their rivalry as senseless and harmful. So when her grandson Tommy Joe Stonefield falls in love with Maybell Maclure, she chooses compassion over clan loyalty. She turns to her old friend William Pestle in Goldshire and quietly plans ways for the sweethearts to meet in secret despite the hostility between their farms.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gramma Stonefield?",a="Gramma Stonefield, whose given name is Mildred, is the elderly matriarch of the Stonefield family at their farm in Elwynn Forest. She is Tommy Joe Stonefield's grandmother.",al={"who is gramma","mildred stonefield","stonefield grandma"},it="identity"},{q="How does she feel about the feud with the Maclures?",a="Mildred wants no part in the feud with the Maclures. She sees the grudge as foolish and harmful, and would rather the households live in harmony than keep bickering.",al={"stonefield maclure feud","does she hate maclures"},it="side"},{q="Why is she helping Tommy Joe and Maybell?",a="Mildred loves her grandson Tommy Joe and wants him to be happy. She rejects the family feud and asks her old friend William Pestle to devise a solution for Tommy Joe's romance with Maybell Maclure.",al={"why help tommy joe","gramma love potion","help lovers"},it="wants"},{q="Who is William Pestle to her?",a="William Pestle is an old, trusted friend of Gramma Stonefield. He lives at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, where he works as an alchemist. She sends trusted couriers to ask him for remedies and other help for Tommy Joe.",al={"william pestle connection","william pestle gramma"},it="ties"},{q="Why is Gramma Stonefield here?",a="This cottage is her lifelong home. As the matriarch and oldest living member of the Stonefield clan, Mildred resides right here on the family farmstead in Elwynn Forest, quietly watching over her kin while striving to keep their petty rivalries from destroying young lives.",al={"why is gramma stonefield at the farm","stonefield farm gramma location","why is mildred stonefield here"},it="why_here",add="d471da09"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can see how local conflicts in the heartland call for quiet diplomacy and empathy."},kw={"elwynn","gramma stonefield","maclure","maybell","mildred","stonefield farm","tommy joe","william pestle"},rel={"npc:tommy-joe-stonefield","npc:maybell-maclure","npc:william-pestle","subzone:stonefield-farm","quest:111","zone:elwynn"},src={"Gramma Stonefield"}}
E["npc:guard-thomas"] = {t="npc",n="Guard Thomas",z="elwynn",s="At the bridge west of Eastvale Logging Camp, Guard Thomas watches Elwynn’s eastern frontier. He guards local workers from wild predators and murlocs for the Stormwind Army.",h="At the bridge west of Eastvale Logging Camp, Guard Thomas watches Elwynn’s eastern frontier.",sec={{t="On the Eastern Border",b="Guard Thomas holds a quiet but exposed post at the stone bridge over the river toward Eastvale Logging Camp. Aggressive creatures shelter in the woods nearby, and the logging workers depend on Stormwind’s guard for protection. With the army stretched thin, Thomas relies on travelers to help keep order and carry messages to central command.",sp=0},{t="Frontier Troubles",b="Bears and prowlers threaten lumberjacks and travelers along Elwynn’s eastern treeline. Murloc tribes have made camps by the waterways, so Guard Thomas tracks them and offers bounties to reduce their numbers. Patrols sent along the river sometimes vanish. Thomas must discover what became of his fellow guards as troubles mount in the region.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can I find Guard Thomas?",a="Guard Thomas stands on the stone bridge over the river, just west of Eastvale Logging Camp on Elwynn Forest’s eastern road.",al={"guard thomas location","where is thomas","guard thomas bridge"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Guard Thomas's duty in Elwynn Forest?",a="Guard Thomas protects Elwynn’s eastern frontier for the Stormwind Army. He guards the trade bridge, defends nearby workers from predators, and watches for murlocs along the riverbanks.",al={"what does thomas do","guard thomas role","thomas eastvale"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is Guard Thomas asking for help with lost guards?",a="Patrols sent into the river basins have failed to return. Thomas cannot leave his post without enough guards to replace him, so he asks travelers to search the waterways for his missing comrades.",al={"lost guards elwynn","guard thomas missing scouts","what happened to the guards"},it="motive"},{q="Why are murlocs a problem for Guard Thomas?",a="Murloc tribes are pressing farther up eastern Elwynn’s rivers. They threaten logging work and supply routes, so Thomas offers bounties to keep the waterways clear.",al={"murlocs eastvale","why kill murlocs","guard thomas murloc bounty"},it="threat"},{q="Who does Guard Thomas report to?",a="Guard Thomas serves in the Stormwind Army and reports through its hierarchy to regional command in Goldshire and the capital. As trouble grows along the borders, his dispatches also coordinate with Gryan Stoutmantle in Westfall.",al={"thomas superior","stormwind army chain of command","who does thomas work for"},it="ties"},{q="Where does Guard Thomas send adventurers once their work in Elwynn is done?",a="After threats near Eastvale and the eastern river are dealt with, Thomas directs seasoned travelers toward Westfall to help Gryan Stoutmantle and the struggling People's Militia.",al={"after guard thomas","where to go after eastvale","westfall report"},it="next_step"},{q="Who is Guard Thomas?",a="Guard Thomas is an officer of the Stormwind Army stationed on the eastern frontier of Elwynn Forest. While Stormwind's forces are stretched thin across the kingdom, Thomas holds down the post near Eastvale Logging Camp, safeguarding travelers and workers along the bridge from gnolls and encroaching murlocs.",al={"who is thomas","guard thomas identity","who is guard thomas"},it="identity",add="2ef4fdb3"},{q="Whose side is Guard Thomas on?",a="Thomas serves the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance. As a loyal soldier of the Stormwind Army, he acts under the authority of the throne and works directly to secure the realm's borders for its citizens and laborers.",al={"guard thomas faction","who does guard thomas serve","guard thomas alliance"},it="side",add="26bccfb6"},{q="What does Guard Thomas want?",a="Thomas needs capable hands to protect the eastern edge of Elwynn. Between aggressive river murlocs and hostile gnolls threatening the Eastvale woodcutters, he wants the surrounding wilderness secured, the fate of missing patrolmen discovered, and regular intelligence sent back to high command in Stormwind and Westfall.",al={"what does thomas want","guard thomas goals","what does guard thomas need"},it="wants",add="8313e011"},{q="Why is Guard Thomas here?",a="Thomas is posted at the eastern bridge to guard the main crossing into the Eastvale Logging Camp and the borderlands beyond. With Eastvale vital for Stormwind's timber supply and local beasts pressing in from the rivers and hills, a military presence is necessary to keep the road open.",al={"why is guard thomas at the bridge","why is thomas here","guard thomas location reason"},it="why_here",add="c7700b23"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see how thinly the Stormwind Army is stretched. Guard Thomas holds a vital frontier post with little support from the crown.",["class:Warrior"]="As a young Alliance warrior, you can look to Thomas for an example of frontline discipline and the hard work of defending a regional border."},kw={"eastvale","eastvale logging camp","elwynn forest","guard thomas","lost guards","murloc","stormwind army","thomas"},rel={"subzone:eastvale-logging-camp","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-army","quest:37","quest:46","quest:52","quest:39","npc:gryan-stoutmantle"},src={"Guard Thomas"}}
E["npc:henze-faulk"] = {t="npc",n="Henze Faulk",z="elwynn",s="Near Heroes' Vigil in Elwynn Forest, Henze Faulk lies gravely wounded. He shielded Gazin Tenorm from the Defias Brotherhood and now waits for a paladin's aid.",h="Near Heroes' Vigil in Elwynn Forest, Henze Faulk lies gravely wounded.",sec={{t="A Sacrifice at Heroes' Vigil",b="At Heroes' Vigil, east of Stormwind, Henze Faulk lies near the stone ring. Defias marauders ambushed him and his friend Gazin Tenorm there. Henze took the attack so Gazin could survive, then fell to the bandits' blades. Gazin reached the Cathedral of Light to seek help. Henze remains between life and death, awaiting a paladin carrying a Symbol of Life.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Henze Faulk?",a="Henze Faulk, an Ironforge dwarf, lies gravely wounded near the stone circle at Heroes' Vigil in Elwynn Forest. Defias bandits struck him down while he protected his friend Gazin Tenorm.",al={"henze faulk","dwarf at heroes vigil","dying dwarf elwynn"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Henze Faulk lying on the ground?",a="The Defias Brotherhood ambushed Henze Faulk and Gazin Tenorm as they traveled. Henze took the brunt of the attack so Gazin could escape, and now waits for an initiate of the Holy Light to help him.",al={"why is henze dying","is henze dead","henze faulk dead"},it="why_here"},{q="What is Henze's connection to paladins?",a="Henze Faulk is the subject of a rite of passage for young paladins undertaking the trials of the Tome of Divinity. Paladin initiates carry a Symbol of Life to Elwynn and use it to restore Henze, proving their mastery of the Light's blessing of redemption.",al={"henze paladin quest","tome of divinity dwarf"}},{q="Who is Gazin Tenorm?",a="Gazin Tenorm is Henze Faulk's companion. When Defias outlaws cornered them, Henze protected Gazin, who survived and sought help from the Church of the Holy Light.",al={"who is gazin","gazin tenorm friend"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Henze Faulk on?",a="Henze Faulk is firmly allied with the Alliance and the Holy Light. A loyal friend and fellow dwarf of Gazin Tenorm, he fell while bravely defending his friend from the ruthless outlaws of the Defias Brotherhood in Elwynn Forest.",al={"henze faulk faction","is henze alliance","henze faulk allegiance"},it="side",add="162be787"},{q="What does Henze Faulk want?",a="Having fallen to a vicious ambush by the Defias Brotherhood, Henze Faulk's immediate need is the miracle of the Light to restore his life. Beyond survival, his selfless intent was simply to protect his companion, Gazin Tenorm, from harm.",al={"what does henze want","henze faulk goal","henze faulk objective"},it="wants",add="47ed07eb"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you face a test of mercy when you bring Henze Faulk back from the brink with a Symbol of Life. The Light can aid you in battle and defy death.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, seeing Henze Faulk laid low in human lands reminds you that Defias outlaws threaten travelers of every race, not only Stormwind's people."},kw={"defias","elwynn forest","gazin tenorm","henze faulk","heroes' vigil","resurrection","symbol of life","tome of divinity"},rel={"npc:gazin-tenorm","quest:1641","subzone:heroes-vigil","zone:elwynn","topic:defias-brotherhood","topic:dwarf"},src={"Henze Faulk"}}
E["npc:hogger"] = {t="npc",n="Hogger",z="elwynn",s="In southwestern Elwynn Forest, Hogger leads the Riverpaw gnolls in raids on farms and travelers. The Stormwind Marshals have put a bounty on him for his violent attacks.",h="In southwestern Elwynn Forest, Hogger leads the Riverpaw gnolls in raids on farms and travelers.",sec={{t="Terror of the Riverpaw",b="Hogger commands the Riverpaw pack from Hogger Hill in southwestern Elwynn Forest. Since the Third War, the gnolls have grown bolder and more orderly in their raids on nearby homesteads. Now they fight beside the Defias Brotherhood, trading raw ferocity for arms, tactical direction, and magical support. To guard Elwynn's borders and trade routes from further bloodshed, Marshal Dughan has put a bounty on Hogger's head.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Hogger?",a="Hogger leads the Riverpaw pack in southwestern Elwynn Forest. The massive gnoll raids nearby farmsteads and is wanted by Stormwind authorities for attacking human settlements.",al={"hogger lore","who is hogger","riverpaw leader"},it="identity"},{q="Why is there a bounty on Hogger?",a="Marshal Dughan and the Stormwind guard issued a bounty on Hogger for his raids on rural farms and travelers. Bring his huge claw back to Goldshire as proof.",al={"wanted hogger","why kill hogger","hogger bounty"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Are the Riverpaw gnolls working with the Defias Brotherhood?",a="Yes. The Riverpaw pack has joined forces with the Defias Brotherhood. The Brotherhood supplies refined weapons, tactical guidance, and magical support to weaken Stormwind's hold on the region.",al={"hogger defias","gnoll defias connection","riverpaw defias"},it="ties"},{q="Where does Hogger make his camp?",a="Hogger makes camp atop Hogger Hill in southwestern Elwynn Forest, near the Westfall border, with his Riverpaw packmates.",al={"hogger location","where is hogger","hogger hill"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Hogger on?",a="Hogger leads the Riverpaw gnolls of southern Elwynn, but his pack does not act alone. They are conspiring with the Defias Brotherhood, trading chaos in the woods for weapons, tactical leadership, and arcane assistance. While gnolls fight chiefly for plunder and territory, Hogger's alliance with the Defias aligns his pack directly against the kingdom of Stormwind and its people.",al={"hogger side","who does hogger work for","who is hogger allied with"},it="side",add="cd1f1084"},{q="Why is Hogger in Elwynn Forest?",a="Hogger has established his stronghold on a hill in southwestern Elwynn Forest to oversee his pack's aggressive expansion. From this camp, the Riverpaw gnolls raid nearby human farms and settlements, capitalizing on the kingdom's stretched defenses while coordinating under the influence and backing of the Defias Brotherhood.",al={"why is hogger here","hogger elwynn forest reason","why did hogger come here"},it="why_here",add="3ddc17ac"},{q="Why is Hogger so feared?",a="Hogger is feared throughout Elwynn Forest for his vicious strength and cunning leadership. Unlike ordinary wandering gnolls, he is an exceptionally formidable chieftain who easily overpowers lone travelers and inexperienced adventurers. His raids against local homesteads have proven so destructive that the Stormwind Marshals consider him a priority threat to the realm.",al={"why is hogger famous","why is hogger feared","why is hogger notorious"},it="fame",add="d88533c5"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, facing Hogger is an early trial for Stormwind's young defenders. It answers threats in Elwynn's heartland.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see how Hogger's raids stretch the Stormwind army. The Marshals rely on roaming adventurers to keep order near the capital."},kw={"bounty","defias","dughan","elwynn","gnoll","goldshire","hogger","riverpaw"},rel={"quest:176","topic:riverpaw-pack","zone:elwynn","npc:marshal-dughan","topic:defias-brotherhood","subzone:goldshire","topic:gnoll"},src={"Hogger"}}
E["npc:innkeeper-farley"] = {t="npc",n="Innkeeper Farley",z="elwynn",s="At the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, Innkeeper Farley offers travelers meals, beds, and hearthstones. Well liked and watchful, he keeps misplaced mail and listens to the troubles of the road.",h="At the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, Innkeeper Farley offers travelers meals, beds, and hearthstones.",sec={{t="A Goldshire Fixture",b="Travelers bound for Stormwind, Westfall, and Duskwood find Innkeeper Farley at the Lion's Pride Inn counter in Goldshire. He offers meals, ale, cheese, and a bed, and sets hearthstones for those who need one. Farley welcomes all who pass through this busy waystation and keeps order at the inn.",sp=0},{t="The Courier's Abandoned Chest",b="At the crossroads of Stormwind, Westfall, and Duskwood, Innkeeper Farley hears rumors and meets strange travelers. Once, a courier fled into the night in terror and left his satchel behind. Farley stored the leftover missives safely in an upstairs chest. Among them is an undelivered letter addressed to former schoolmaster Stalvan Mistmantle, a clue for investigators tracing the fallen tutor's movements.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Innkeeper Farley?",a="Innkeeper Farley serves travelers at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, offering rest and supplies to those crossing Elwynn Forest.",al={"innkeeper farley","fredrik farley","who is the goldshire innkeeper"},it="identity"},{q="What does Farley know about Stalvan Mistmantle?",a="Farley recalls a terrified courier who fled the Lion's Pride Inn at night and left several deliveries behind. He stored the abandoned letters safely in an upstairs chest, including an undelivered letter addressed to Stalvan Mistmantle for investigators to retrieve.",al={"farley stalvan","stalvan letter goldshire","legend of stalvan farley"}},{q="What services does Farley provide at the inn?",a="Farley sets hearthstones, rents rooms, and sells drinks, juices, and cheeses from across the Alliance. The cheeses include Alterac Swiss, Dalaran Sharp, and local Stormwind Brie.",al={"lion's pride services","farley food and drink","goldshire hearthstone"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Innkeeper Farley on?",a="Innkeeper Farley is a loyal subject of the Kingdom of Stormwind and a proud member of the Alliance. From the Lion's Pride Inn he offers shelter, food, and hospitality to fellow Alliance citizens, travelers, and soldiers traversing the heartlands of Elwynn.",al={"innkeeper farley faction","who does farley serve","farley alliance"},it="side",add="bf81c39e"},{q="What does Innkeeper Farley want?",a="Farley's primary concern is keeping the Lion's Pride Inn running smoothly. Between breaking up tavern brawls and pouring ale, he wants to provide a warm haven for weary travelers.",al={"what does farley want","farley goals","innkeeper farley motive"},it="wants",add="f8150ed8"},{q="Why is Innkeeper Farley here?",a="Farley runs the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire. As Goldshire sits at the crossroads of Elwynn Forest, Farley remains to tend the hearth and manage one of the realm's busiest taverns.",al={"why is farley at the inn","why is innkeeper farley here"},it="why_here",add="5df540c8"},{q="Who is Innkeeper Farley tied to?",a="Farley is a fixture of Goldshire, well known to the travelers who pass through Elwynn Forest. The traveling bard Falkhaan Isenstrider sends young adventurers his way to rest at the Lion's Pride.",al={"farley family","who is innkeeper farley related to","farley connections"},it="ties",add="a88a382c"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As a fresh recruit leaving Northshire Valley, you can bind your hearthstone and buy provisions at Farley's counter in the Lion's Pride Inn."},kw={"elwynn forest","fredrik farley","goldshire","innkeeper farley","lion's pride inn","stalvan"},rel={"subzone:lion-s-pride-inn","subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn","quest:66","topic:alliance","zone:duskwood"},src={"Innkeeper Farley"}}
E["npc:katie-hunter"] = {t="npc",n="Katie Hunter",z="elwynn",s="At the Eastvale Logging Camp stables, Katie Hunter tends horses for Stormwind and trusted Alliance champions. With Randal Hunter, she keeps travelers and soldiers mounted on the kingdom’s roads.",h="At the Eastvale Logging Camp stables, Katie Hunter tends horses for Stormwind and trusted Alliance champions.",sec={{t="Stables of Eastvale",b="In eastern Elwynn Forest, Katie Hunter tends the horses at the Eastvale Logging Camp. As lumberjacks cut timber for Stormwind’s reconstruction, she raises dependable pintos, mares, and swift steeds for riders. Her horses carry people along the kingdom’s roads and the dangerous routes of southern Azeroth.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Katie Hunter?",a="Katie Hunter breeds and sells horses for the Kingdom of Stormwind at the Eastvale Logging Camp stables in Elwynn Forest.",al={"katie hunter elwynn","who is katie hunter","katie hunter horse vendor"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Katie Hunter?",a="Katie Hunter tends the corral and stables in the northern part of the Eastvale Logging Camp. She works near Randal Hunter, a riding trainer, in eastern Elwynn Forest.",al={"katie hunter location","where is katie hunter","find katie hunter"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Can non-humans buy horses from her?",a="Yes. Non-human buyers need exalted standing with the Kingdom of Stormwind. Human adventurers can buy her horses without special standing.",al={"dwarf buy horse","night elf horse mount","stormwind reputation mount"},gp=true},{q="What horses does she sell?",a="Katie Hunter sells standard riding horses, including pinto, brown, and chestnut varieties. She also sells swift, armored steeds such as the Swift Palomino, Swift Brown Steed, and Swift White Steed.",al={"what mounts does katie sell","katie hunter horse types"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Katie Hunter on?",a="Katie Hunter is a loyal subject of the Kingdom of Stormwind and a member of the Alliance. Operating out of Eastvale Logging Camp, she caters directly to Stormwind's citizens, providing dependable mounts to travelers and champions who have proven their dedication to the crown.",al={"katie hunter faction","is katie hunter alliance","who does katie hunter serve"},it="side",add="d7735dfa"},{q="What does Katie Hunter want?",a="Katie Hunter focuses on tending and selling Eastvale's renowned horses. She seeks to supply capable mounts to reliable adventurers, ensuring that only trusted allies of Stormwind acquire her prized stock to aid their travels across the kingdom.",al={"what does katie hunter want","katie hunter purpose","katie hunter goal"},it="wants",add="d5257f59"},{q="Why is Katie Hunter here at Eastvale Logging Camp?",a="Katie Hunter makes her home at Eastvale Logging Camp in eastern Elwynn Forest to run the camp's stables. Working alongside Randal Hunter, she manages the breeding and care of riding horses away from the bustle of Stormwind City, using the camp's open pasture.",al={"why is katie hunter in eastvale","why is katie hunter here","what is katie hunter doing in elwynn"},it="why_here",add="5cab52df"},{q="Who is Katie Hunter tied to?",a="Katie Hunter works closely with Randal Hunter, who also oversees the stables at Eastvale Logging Camp. Together, they manage the camp's equine trade and serve as the primary source of horses for Stormwind's allies.",al={"katie hunter connections","who is katie hunter related to","katie hunter randal hunter"},it="ties",add="85933b18"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, you can buy a classic Stormwind horse from Katie once you have mastered the basics of horsemanship.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an allied race, you can earn the privilege of riding Katie’s prized steeds into battle by gaining high standing and respect with Stormwind’s court."},kw={"eastvale","elwynn forest","horse vendor","katie hunter","logging camp","mounts","stables","stormwind"},rel={"subzone:eastvale-logging-camp","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Katie Hunter"}}
E["npc:keryn-sylvius"] = {t="npc",n="Keryn Sylvius",z="elwynn",s="On the second floor of Goldshire’s Lion’s Pride Inn, Keryn Sylvius trains young rogues. In the reading room, she teaches stealth and bladecraft and quietly guides promising operatives toward Stormwind’s intelligence service.",h="On the second floor of Goldshire’s Lion’s Pride Inn, Keryn Sylvius trains young rogues.",sec={{t="A Quiet Presence in Goldshire",b="Keryn Sylvius keeps to the reading room above the Lion’s Pride Inn. Below, travelers and town guards fill the common room. Upstairs, she listens to the steady flow of gossip from the road. She mentors rogues learning their trade in Elwynn Forest.\n\nWhen promising operatives outgrow petty theft and roadside skulduggery, Sylvius quietly sends them to Stormwind City. There, they can seek out SI:7.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Keryn Sylvius?",a="Find Keryn Sylvius in the small reading room on the second floor of the Lion’s Pride Inn in Goldshire.",al={"keryn sylvius location","where is keryn","goldshire rogue trainer location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What services does she offer?",a="Keryn Sylvius trains rogues, teaching new abilities and resetting talent specializations. She also guides their progress.",al={"what does keryn do","can she train me","keryn sylvius role"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What connection does she have to SI:7?",a="When operatives prove their abilities, Sylvius directs them to Master Mathias Shaw and SI:7 in Old Town. Stormwind’s covert intelligence network is based there.",al={"keryn si7","is she si:7","does she work for stormwind"},it="ties"},{q="Who is Keryn Sylvius?",a="Keryn Sylvius is a rogue trainer who makes her home on the upper floor of Goldshire's Lion's Pride Inn. Tucked away in the quiet reading room, she observes the comings and goings of Elwynn Forest while passing on the subtle arts of stealth, lockpicking, and subterfuge to promising rogues under the banner of the Alliance.",al={"who is keryn","keryn sylvius lore","who is sylvius"},it="identity",add="74741391"},{q="Whose side is Keryn Sylvius on?",a="Keryn stands firmly with the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance. Her craft serves the realm's interests, quietly directing talented agents to Stormwind's clandestine intelligence network so they can aid the kingdom against internal unrest and outside threats alike.",al={"keryn sylvius alliance or horde","keryn sylvius allegiance","who does keryn sylvius serve"},it="side",add="017a68dc"},{q="What does Keryn Sylvius want?",a="Keryn aims to scout and instruct raw talent in the quiet heart of Elwynn before they run afoul of the law or misuse their deadly skills. Once an apprentice proves capable, her goal is to channel their abilities into organized service by directing them onward to SI:7 headquarters in Old Town.",al={"what does keryn want","keryn sylvius goals","why train rogues"},it="wants",add="90e34396"},{q="Why is Keryn Sylvius here in Goldshire?",a="The Lion's Pride Inn serves as the bustling crossroads of Elwynn Forest, making it an ideal place to quietly identify rogues finding their footing outside Northshire Valley. Stationing herself upstairs gives her a discreet perch to mentor fledglings without drawing undue attention from the local guards or townspeople below.",al={"why is keryn in lions pride inn","why is keryn sylvius in goldshire","keryn goldshire why"},it="why_here",add="f8e496c4"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can learn from Sylvius in Elwynn Forest. When you are ready, she can point you toward SI:7 headquarters in Stormwind City.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can count on Sylvius to watch Elwynn’s main roads from her post above Goldshire’s crossroads."},kw={"elwynn forest","goldshire","keryn sylvius","lion's pride inn","rogue trainer","si:7"},rel={"subzone:lion-s-pride-inn","subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn","quest:2205","quest:2300"},src={"Keryn Sylvius"}}
E["npc:khelden-bremen"] = {t="npc",n="Khelden Bremen",z="elwynn",s="On Northshire Abbey's upper floor, Khelden Bremen teaches human mages their first spells. He prepares novices to serve Stormwind through the arcane arts.",h="On Northshire Abbey's upper floor, Khelden Bremen teaches human mages their first spells.",sec={{t="Tutor of the Arcane",b="In his study, Khelden Bremen teaches novices the discipline and focus to shape raw magical energy safely. Below, clergy and defenders carry on their work. His pupils prepare to travel through Elwynn Forest and continue their studies in Stormwind's Mage Quarter.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Khelden Bremen?",a="Khelden Bremen trains new mages at Northshire Abbey in Elwynn Forest. He teaches their first spells and the foundations of arcane study.",al={"who is khelden","bremen","mage trainer northshire"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Khelden Bremen?",a="Khelden Bremen is on the second floor of Northshire Abbey. Enter the abbey and take the staircase in the second room on the left.",al={"where is khelden","khelden bremen location","northshire mage trainer location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does he play for new adventurers?",a="Human mages arriving in Northshire are directed to Khelden Bremen, often with a Glyphic Letter of introduction. He teaches their first spells and helps them control their magical aptitude.",al={"what does khelden do","bremen quests","glyphic letter recipient"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Khelden Bremen on?",a="Khelden Bremen stands firmly with the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance. Stationed within Northshire Abbey, he serves the realm by mentoring the next generation of spellcasters and preparing them to defend humanity's lands against rising dangers.",al={"khelden bremen faction","who does khelden serve","is khelden bremen alliance"},it="side",add="7cfd66d2"},{q="What does Khelden Bremen want?",a="Khelden's goal is to instruct novice mages in the arcane arts. He seeks dedicated apprentices ready to learn basic incantations, master their burgeoning intellect, and harness their power responsibly for the safety of Elwynn Forest and Stormwind.",al={"khelden bremen goal","what does khelden want"},it="wants",add="032606f2"},{q="Why is Khelden Bremen here at Northshire Abbey?",a="Northshire Abbey acts as a recruitment and training haven for young defenders answering Stormwind's call. Bremen resides on the upper floor of the abbey specifically to receive fledgling human practitioners and guide their initial steps into magic before they venture deeper into the wider realm.",al={"why is khelden in northshire","khelden bremen why here"},it="why_here",add="8660ec47"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a human mage, you receive your first formal arcane instruction from Khelden Bremen before continuing your studies in the towers of Stormwind City."},kw={"arcane","elwynn forest","glyphic letter","khelden bremen","mage trainer","northshire abbey"},rel={"subzone:northshire-abbey","quest:3104","zone:elwynn"},src={"Khelden Bremen"}}
E["npc:lyria-du-lac"] = {t="npc",n="Lyria Du Lac",z="elwynn",s="In Goldshire, Lyria Du Lac trains young warriors behind the village smithy. She guides them as they master their stances and arms.",h="In Goldshire, Lyria Du Lac trains young warriors behind the village smithy.",sec={{t="Warrior Trainer of Goldshire",b="Behind Goldshire's forge, Lyria Du Lac trains warriors fresh from Northshire Abbey. She judges when they are ready and teaches them specialized combat techniques. Those who take up shield and blade for Stormwind must face the dangers of Elwynn Forest.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Lyria Du Lac?",a="In Goldshire, find Lyria Du Lac behind the blacksmith shop, just west of the Lion's Pride Inn.",al={"lyria du lac location","where is lyria","warrior trainer goldshire"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What service does Lyria Du Lac provide?",a="Lyria Du Lac teaches warriors combat maneuvers, stances, and battle disciplines as their skill grows.",al={"what does lyria do","lyria du lac role","what does lyria teach"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What quests involve Lyria Du Lac?",a="Lyria Du Lac gives developing warriors 'A Warrior's Training'. She sends them to veteran Harry Burlguard at the Pig and Whistle tavern in Stormwind's Old Town.",al={"lyria du lac quests","warrior quest goldshire"},gp=true},{q="Who is Lyria Du Lac?",a="Lyria Du Lac is a veteran human warrior who serves as a combat instructor in Elwynn Forest. Stationed behind the smithy in Goldshire, she evaluates and instructs novice fighters making their way into the wider kingdom, teaching them how to harness their martial prowess and survive the threats encroaching on Stormwind's borders.",al={"who is lyria","lyria du lac lore","who is lyria du lac"},it="identity",add="f698c0e4"},{q="Whose side is Lyria Du Lac on?",a="Lyria stands firmly with the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance. By preparing fresh recruits to defend Elwynn Forest from local dangers like bandits and gnolls, she helps reinforce the kingdom's military readiness during a time when regular garrison forces are stretched thin.",al={"lyria du lac faction","lyria du lac allegiance","who does lyria serve"},it="side",add="34434421"},{q="Why is Lyria Du Lac here in Goldshire?",a="Goldshire is the natural staging point for travelers leaving Northshire Valley, making it the ideal post to drill promising adventurers in weaponcraft. Stationed right behind the blacksmith, Lyria ensures that any fledgling warrior who arrives in town is properly conditioned and disciplined before facing greater perils.",al={"why is lyria in goldshire","lyria du lac location purpose","what brought lyria here"},it="why_here",add="afd6a9c2"},{q="What does Lyria Du Lac want?",a="Lyria seeks capable pupils ready to master the art of combat. She wants to see young warriors hone their discipline, master the stances and techniques of battle, and use their training to defend the realm from whatever chaos threatens its peace.",al={"what does lyria want","lyria du lac goal","lyria du lac motive"},it="wants",add="277e5774"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior fresh from Northshire Abbey, you meet Lyria Du Lac, your first major trainer in Elwynn Forest. She helps you master your stance and sharpen your melee tactics.",["faction:Alliance"]="Behind Goldshire's forge, Lyria Du Lac trains local recruits to defend Stormwind's heartland from Defias brigands and gnoll raiders."},kw={"a warrior's training","blacksmith","elwynn forest","goldshire","lyria du lac","warrior trainer"},rel={"subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn","quest:1638"},src={"Lyria Du Lac"}}
E["npc:ma-stonefield"] = {t="npc",n="Ma Stonefield",z="elwynn",s="At Stonefield Farm in western Elwynn, Ma Stonefield tends to troubles close to home. With Auntie Bernice beside her, she faces farm hardships, rivalries with neighbors, and pests.",h="At Stonefield Farm in western Elwynn, Ma Stonefield tends to troubles close to home.",sec={{t="Homestead Troubles",b="Ma Stonefield watches over the farm beside her family's cottage in southwestern Elwynn Forest. Auntie Bernice Stonefield stays at her side. The neighboring Maclure homestead and nearby pumpkin patches bring little peace. Wild boars threaten the Stonefield crops, and Princess causes the greatest trouble. The enormous prize sow tramples fields and devours the harvest the family worked hard to grow.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ma Stonefield?",a="Ma Stonefield is an elder of the Stonefield family. She lives at their farmstead in southwestern Elwynn Forest with relatives such as Auntie Bernice.",al={"who is ma stonefield","ma stonefield","stonefield mother"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Ma Stonefield?",a="Ma Stonefield stands outdoors in front of the main house at Stonefield Farm, west of Goldshire in Elwynn Forest.",al={"ma stonefield location","where is ma stonefield","stonefield farm loc"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What problem does Ma Stonefield need solved?",a="Ma Stonefield wants help stopping Princess, a massive prize pig that repeatedly rampages through nearby fields and devours local crops.",al={"ma stonefield quest","princess sow quest","princess must die questgiver"},it="wants"},{q="Whose side is Ma Stonefield on?",a="Ma Stonefield is a loyal subject of the Kingdom of Stormwind and a member of the Alliance. Like most rural folk living in the heart of Elwynn Forest, her focus remains squarely on her family's farm, though she relies on Alliance adventurers to step in when local troubles grow too big for simple farmers to handle.",al={"is ma stonefield alliance","ma stonefield faction"},it="side",add="51af3003"},{q="Why is Ma Stonefield here?",a="The Stonefield Farm is Ma Stonefield's lifelong home. She lives and works the land in Elwynn Forest alongside her kin, tending to the daily chores of country life right outside the family homestead near \"Auntie\" Bernice Stonefield.",al={"why is ma stonefield at the farm","what does ma stonefield do here"},it="why_here",add="02537c40"},{q="Who is Ma Stonefield tied to?",a="Ma Stonefield is a matriarch of the Stonefield clan, living alongside relatives such as \"Auntie\" Bernice Stonefield at their homestead in Elwynn Forest. Her family has long-standing roots in the valley, though they also share a bitter, enduring feud with their neighbors, the Maclures.",al={"ma stonefield family","who is ma stonefield related to"},it="ties",add="ae4d5db0"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer in Elwynn Forest, you can help hardworking homesteaders like Ma Stonefield protect Stormwind's agricultural backbone."},kw={"bernice stonefield","elwynn forest","ma stonefield","princess","princess must die","stonefield farm"},rel={"subzone:stonefield-farm","npc:auntie-bernice-stonefield","quest:88","zone:elwynn"},src={"Ma Stonefield"}}
E["npc:marshal-dughan"] = {t="npc",n="Marshal Dughan",z="elwynn",s="In Goldshire, Marshal Dughan holds the roads against threats from the mines and woods. He commands Stormwind's small army detachment, stretched thin by kobolds, gnolls, and bandits. To guard the town and nearby farms, he depends on independent adventurers.",h="In Goldshire, Marshal Dughan holds the roads against threats from the mines and woods.",sec={{t="Commander of the Crossroads",b="From Goldshire, Marshal Dughan directs Elwynn Forest's defense outside the Lion's Pride Inn. Stormwind's soldiers are tied up elsewhere as trouble grows in the woods. Kobolds crowd the mines, gnolls gather along the riverbanks, and highwaymen harass travelers on the King's Road. With too few footmen, Dughan sends new recruits to reinforce outposts and scout dangerous ground.",sp=0},{t="Threats on Every Border",b="Kobolds overrun Fargodeep and Jasperlode Mines, threatening Goldshire's mineral supply. West of town, Hogger's Riverpaw gnolls press against Westbrook Garrison. Eastward, Guard Thomas reports vicious murlocs killing patrols along the river. Dughan has too few soldiers to meet each threat, so he needs capable mercenaries to help contain them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Marshal Dughan?",a="Marshal Dughan commands a Stormwind Army detachment in Goldshire. He coordinates Elwynn Forest's defenses against thieves, gnolls, and kobolds.",al={"dughan","marshal dughan lore","goldshire marshal"},it="identity"},{q="Why doesn't Dughan send more guards to help Westbrook Garrison or the east?",a="Stormwind's forces are spread thin, leaving Dughan barely enough guards to keep order in Goldshire. He has too few soldiers for every farm and border post, so he relies on visiting adventurers to scout danger, carry dispatches, and confront local threats.",al={"why no guards","goldshire garrison strength","dughan troops"}},{q="What is Dughan's view on the murloc threat in Elwynn?",a="Dughan first dismissed Remy 'Two Times' warnings that murlocs threatened the region. Guard Thomas's reports of Rolf Hartford and Malakai Stone's deaths along the eastern waterways convinced him of the danger.",al={"dughan murlocs","remy two times murloc","dughan fish men"},sp=1},{q="How does Dughan handle local crime and rowdy civilians?",a="Dughan is charged with keeping peace in Goldshire and the surrounding lands. He says order is hard enough to keep amid Elwynn's new troubles, and focuses on kobolds to the north and gnolls and thieves to the west.",al={"dughan crime","goldshire law","stockade threat"}},{q="Why is Dughan concerned about the mines?",a="Fargodeep Mine and Jasperlode Mine supply Stormwind with gold and ore. Kobolds have overrun both mines, driven out the miners, and threaten to tunnel beneath Elwynn's settlements.",al={"fargodeep mine dughan","jasperlode mine dughan","kobold infestation"}},{q="Does Marshal Dughan coordinate with Westfall?",a="Yes. After you prove capable in Elwynn Forest, Dughan sends you to report to Gryan Stoutmantle at Sentinel Hill in Westfall. The People's Militia needs veteran help against the Defias Brotherhood.",al={"dughan gryan","report to westfall","dughan sentinel hill"}},{q="Whose side is Marshal Dughan on?",a="Marshal Dughan serves the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance. As an officer in the Stormwind Army, he answers directly to the realm's military hierarchy, carrying out the crown's orders to maintain order and protect the heartland despite dwindling royal reinforcements.",al={"dughan faction","who does dughan serve","marshal dughan allegiance"},it="side",add="72888056"},{q="What does Marshal Dughan want?",a="Dughan aims to secure Elwynn Forest and safeguard Goldshire against multiplying threats. With his garrison stretched thin, he seeks capable adventurers to scout the infested Fargodeep and Jasperlode mines, contain the Defias bandits and gnolls in the west, and assess the growing danger along the riverbanks.",al={"dughan goal","what does dughan need","dughan objectives"},it="wants",add="9141816c"},{q="Why is Marshal Dughan stationed in Goldshire?",a="Dughan is stationed in Goldshire as commander of the local Stormwind Army detachment. Tasked with the defense of central Elwynn, he oversees town peacekeeping, coordinates outposts like Westbrook Garrison, and manages the defense against encroaching beasts, kobolds, and criminals who threaten the capital's breadbasket.",al={"why is dughan in goldshire","marshal dughan purpose here","dughan post"},it="why_here",add="8808e7de"},{q="Who is Marshal Dughan tied to?",a="Dughan works closely with local outpost commanders across Elwynn, such as Deputy Rainer at Westbrook Garrison and Guard Thomas along the eastern bridges. Outside Elwynn, he maintains communication with military peers like Gryan Stoutmantle in Westfall, sharing intelligence on regional criminal activity.",al={"dughan connections","who does dughan work with","dughan allies"},it="ties",add="156c33b1"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance recruit in Elwynn, you receive your first military assignments from Marshal Dughan, Stormwind's local authority.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you see Stormwind's footmen hold the line with discipline despite impossible odds and too few soldiers."},kw={"elwynn forest","fargodeep","goldshire","hogger","jasperlode","marshal dughan","stormwind army","westbrook garrison"},rel={"subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn","npc:guard-thomas","npc:remy-two-times","quest:176","subzone:westbrook-garrison","npc:gryan-stoutmantle","topic:stormwind-army"},src={"Marshal Dughan"}}
E["npc:marshal-mcbride"] = {t="npc",n="Marshal McBride",z="elwynn",s="At Northshire Abbey, Marshal Douglas McBride turns to new recruits as kobolds threaten the valley's farms and mines. He commands Stormwind's garrison there, the army's authority in Northshire.",h="At Northshire Abbey, Marshal Douglas McBride turns to new recruits as kobolds threaten the valley's farms and...",sec={{t="Commander of Northshire",b="Marshal McBride has only a handful of sworn guards to keep the valley peaceful and protect its food and resources. Unrest across the kingdom has left military garrisons short of soldiers. Green recruits arrive seeking training under the abbey's masters, so McBride puts them to work defending the valley.",sp=0},{t="The Kobold Incursion",b="Kobolds grow more aggressive around Northshire. They spread through the woods and seize Echo Ridge Mine, an important local resource. With regular soldiers scarce, McBride calls on paladins, warriors, and other novices to drive back the tunneling kobolds. He needs them to learn how far the infestation reaches before the valley is cut off.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Marshal McBride?",a="Marshal McBride commands Stormwind's garrison at Northshire Abbey. He defends Northshire Valley and directs new recruits into service.",al={"marshal mcbride","who is mcbride","northshire commander"},it="identity"},{q="Why is McBride having recruits fight kobolds?",a="Kobolds have overrun the woods around Northshire and seized Echo Ridge Mine. With Stormwind's forces stretched thin, McBride sends newly arrived adventurers to drive them out and secure the area.",al={"why kill kobolds","kobold problem","echo ridge problem"},it="motive"},{q="Where does McBride send recruits next?",a="After a recruit handles the threats in Northshire Valley, McBride sends them south along the road to Goldshire to help Marshal Dughan.",al={"where do i go after mcbride","after northshire","next town"},it="next_step"},{q="What is Echo Ridge Mine?",a="Echo Ridge Mine is a mineral-rich cavern on the northern edge of Northshire Valley. Kobolds have overrun it, and McBride has ordered several efforts to reclaim it.",al={"echo ridge","the mine in northshire"},it="place"},{q="Does McBride command the abbey itself?",a="No. Northshire Abbey is maintained by the holy orders and priests of the Light. McBride commands the military garrison that defends the abbey and the surrounding valley.",al={"does mcbride lead northshire abbey","who is in charge of the abbey"},it="in_charge"},{q="Is McBride concerned about threats beyond kobolds?",a="Kobolds are McBride's most immediate concern, but bandits and outlaws linger at the valley's edges. They are signs of wider unrest across Elwynn Forest.",al={"defias in northshire","is northshire safe"},it="threat"},{q="Whose side is Marshal McBride on?",a="Marshal McBride is a loyal officer of the Stormwind Army and the Grand Alliance. He answers to the crown of Stormwind and stands watch over Northshire Valley to ensure the safety of the kingdom's citizens and training recruits.",al={"who does mcbride serve","mcbride allegiance","what faction is mcbride"},it="side",add="05ea779e"},{q="What does Marshal McBride want?",a="McBride wants to secure Northshire Valley against growing local threats. With the Stormwind Army stretched thin, he seeks to mobilize new recruits, paladins, and volunteers to purge the aggressive kobolds infesting the valley and reclaim Echo Ridge Mine.",al={"mcbride goal","what is mcbride trying to do","mcbride plans"},it="wants",add="b6028054"},{q="Why is Marshal McBride here?",a="McBride is stationed outside Northshire Abbey as the commander of the valley's military garrison. Stormwind tasked him with maintaining order, organizing defenses, and training fresh arrivals before sending proven soldiers into Elwynn Forest and beyond.",al={"why is mcbride in northshire","mcbride post","why is marshal mcbride at the abbey"},it="why_here",add="cc66b2df"},{q="Who is Marshal McBride tied to?",a="McBride is bound to the high command of the Stormwind Army and coordinates with local authorities across Elwynn, eventually directing capable fighters to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire. He works alongside the abbey's clergy and trainers to prepare new defenders for the kingdom.",al={"mcbride connections","who does mcbride report to","mcbride stormwind army"},it="ties",add="307fdf7d"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human beginning in Northshire, you first meet Marshal McBride, Stormwind's royal authority in the valley.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you can serve the kingdom by helping McBride clear kobolds from Echo Ridge's tunnels.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance recruit, you begin at the Grand Alliance's frontier in humanity's heartland. There, McBride brings recruits into the Crown's service."},kw={"douglas mcbride","echo ridge","elwynn","kobold","marshal mcbride","northshire","northshire abbey"},rel={"subzone:northshire-abbey","subzone:northshire-valley","subzone:echo-ridge-mine","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-army","quest:15","quest:21","subzone:goldshire"},src={"Marshal McBride"}}
E["npc:maybell-maclure"] = {t="npc",n="Maybell Maclure",z="elwynn",s="At the Maclure Vineyards, Maybell Maclure loves a Stonefield, though the families’ feud keeps her apart from Tommy Joe Stonefield.",h="At the Maclure Vineyards, Maybell Maclure loves a Stonefield, though the families’ feud keeps her apart from...",sec={{t="Star-Crossed in the Vineyards",b="Maybell Maclure tends her family’s vineyards beside the Stonefield farm. She loves Tommy Joe Stonefield, heir to the neighboring farm. Their families’ long feud keeps them apart, and Maybell seeks a way to speak with him beyond her family’s watchful eyes.",sp=0},{t="A Concoction for True Love",b="Unable to cross between the farms openly, Maybell asks sympathetic travelers and Gramma Stonefield for help. William Pestle, the alchemist in Goldshire, brews an invisibility liquor. Maybell drinks it and slips away from the Maclure homestead unseen to meet Tommy Joe by the riverbank.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why can't Maybell and Tommy Joe see each other?",a="The Maclure and Stonefield families have kept a bitter rivalry for years. Both forbid contact between their households, so Maybell and Tommy Joe hide their romance from their kin.",al={"why family feud","maclure stonefield feud","why cant they be together"},it="conflict"},{q="What prevents Maybell from leaving the vineyard?",a="Maybell’s family watches her closely because of the feud with the Stonefields. She needs help meeting Tommy Joe without drawing their attention.",al={"how does maybell sneak out","invisibility potion elwynn","how does she meet tommy"},sp=1},{q="Where does Maybell meet Tommy Joe?",a="Tommy Joe waits by the riverbank on the border between the Maclure Vineyards and Stonefield Farm, out of direct view of both farmsteads.",al={"meeting spot","where are they meeting","where is tommy joe"},it="place"},{q="Who helps Maybell with her romance?",a="Gramma Stonefield sympathizes with the lovers and sends willing travelers to William Pestle, the alchemist in Goldshire. He provides what they need for a secret meeting.",al={"who helps maybell","stonefield helpers"},sp=1,it="allies"},{q="Who is Maybell Maclure?",a="Maybell Maclure is a young human woman living at the Maclure Vineyards in Elwynn Forest. She is caught in the middle of a bitter, longstanding feud between her family and their neighbors, the Stonefields, after falling deeply in love with Tommy Joe Stonefield.",al={"who is maybell","who is maybell maclure","maybell maclure lore"},it="identity",add="c4338ded"},{q="Whose side is Maybell Maclure on?",a="She is a loyal subject of the Alliance and a daughter of the Maclure household. However, when it comes to the petty, bitter rivalry between the Maclures and the Stonefields, she rejects the hatred entirely, choosing her love for Tommy Joe over her family's grudge.",al={"is maybell alliance","whose side is maybell on","maybell faction"},it="side",add="9f94442c"},{q="What does Maybell Maclure want?",a="Maybell wants nothing more than to be with Tommy Joe Stonefield. Because their families harbor an intense mutual hatred, she seeks the aid of sympathetic travelers and trusted confidants to find ways to meet him in secret without being caught.",al={"what does maybell want","maybell maclure goal","why does maybell need help"},it="wants",add="cbd5fa72"},{q="Why is Maybell Maclure here?",a="Maybell resides at the Maclure Vineyards, her family's estate in southern Elwynn Forest. She remains confined to the vineyard grounds under the watchful eyes of her relatives, hoping for a chance to slip away and see her beloved.",al={"why is maybell maclure here","why is maybell at the vineyards"},it="why_here",add="b079e731"},{q="Who is Maybell Maclure tied to?",a="Maybell is part of the Maclure family of vineyard owners. She is romantically entwined with Tommy Joe Stonefield, the heir to the rival Stonefield farmstead, and maintains secret ties with Gramma Stonefield, who supports the young couple's clandestine romance.",al={"maybell maclure relationships","who is maybell related to","maybell ties"},it="ties",add="26be6d7a"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers crossing Elwynn Forest, Maybell’s romance shows how personal troubles and old grudges endure in the kingdom’s heartlands."},kw={"lovers","maclure","maybell","stonefield","tommy joe","vineyards"},rel={"npc:tommy-joe-stonefield","subzone:maclure-vineyards","npc:gramma-stonefield","npc:william-pestle","quest:114","quest:111","zone:elwynn"},src={"Maybell Maclure"}}
E["npc:merissa-stilwell"] = {t="npc",n="Merissa Stilwell",z="elwynn",s="At Northshire Abbey, Merissa Stilwell greets newcomers to Northshire Valley. The young human offers a cheerful welcome and a helping hand to those training nearby.",h="At Northshire Abbey, Merissa Stilwell greets newcomers to Northshire Valley.",sec={{t="A Welcoming Face in Northshire",b="From Northshire Abbey, Merissa Stilwell welcomes fresh recruits arriving in Northshire Valley. She offers simple hospitality and practical advice on resting and finding the way. Her surname is shared by craftsmen and homesteaders across the kingdom, including the blacksmith Jordan Stilwell and the Westfall defender Daphne Stilwell. Amid the kingdom's rising tensions, Merissa remains a peaceful local presence.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Merissa Stilwell?",a="Merissa Stilwell is a friendly human resident of Northshire Abbey in Elwynn Forest. She welcomes travelers and offers them advice.",al={"merissa stilwell","who is merissa","stilwell girl northshire"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Merissa Stilwell?",a="You can find Merissa Stilwell at Northshire Abbey in Northshire Valley, within Elwynn Forest.",al={"merissa stilwell location","where is merissa","find merissa"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is Merissa related to the other Stilwells in the kingdom?",a="Merissa Stilwell shares her surname with the smith Jordan Stilwell and Daphne Stilwell in Westfall. She lives quietly at Northshire Abbey, welcoming travelers rather than fighting bandits or forging blades.",al={"stilwell family","daphne stilwell relative","jordan stilwell relative"},it="ties"},{q="Does Merissa Stilwell offer any quests?",a="No. Merissa Stilwell has no task for travelers. She simply greets newcomers passing through Northshire.",al={"merissa quests","merissa stilwell quest"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Merissa Stilwell on?",a="Merissa Stilwell is a loyal subject of the Grand Alliance and the Kingdom of Stormwind. Residing peacefully at Northshire Abbey, she welcomes the travelers and recruits arriving in the valley.",al={"merissa stilwell faction","is merissa stilwell alliance"},it="side",add="a071eba0"},{q="Why is Merissa Stilwell in Northshire?",a="Merissa spends her days around Northshire Abbey. Like many ordinary folk of the kingdom, she makes her life in Elwynn Forest and welcomes the newcomers who arrive in the valley.",al={"why is merissa stilwell here","what is merissa doing in northshire"},it="why_here",add="57a6fac4"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance recruit leaving Northshire's sheltered cloister, you find warm hospitality in Merissa before the harsh realities of the Defias threat set in."},kw={"elwynn","merissa","northshire","stilwell"},rel={"zone:elwynn","npc:jordan-stilwell","npc:daphne-stilwell"},src={"Merissa Stilwell"}}
E["npc:morgan-the-collector"] = {t="npc",n="Morgan the Collector",z="elwynn",s="At the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch, Morgan the Collector directs Defias extortion and gathers stolen goods across Elwynn Forest. From the farmhouse, he coordinates the theft while Goldshire's guard watches nearby.",h="At the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch, Morgan the Collector directs Defias extortion and gathers stolen goods across...",sec={{t="The Tithe of Elwynn",b="Morgan the Collector takes gold from Elwynn Forest's mines for the Defias Brotherhood. Common bandits harass travelers on the roads, but Morgan directs organized shakedowns. He gathers stolen coin and supplies for the Brotherhood's wider network. His headquarters is the farmhouse at the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch, where loyal enforcers including Surena Caledon and Erlan Drudgemoor surround him.",sp=0},{t="A Signet of the Past",b="Morgan carries a distinctive signet ring that marks his authority. In Goldshire, investigators see the ring as evidence linking the masked thieves terrorizing the heartland to the disgraced Stonemasons Guild. That guild rebuilt Stormwind City after the Second War. Recovering the ring reveals who directs the bandits in the woods.",sp=1,bt={"q123.3"}}},faq={{q="Who is Morgan the Collector?",a="Morgan is a high-ranking officer in the Defias Brotherhood. He collects gold taken from Elwynn Forest's mines and coordinates bandit activity in the region.",al={"who is morgan","morgan lore","collector in elwynn"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Morgan found?",a="Morgan keeps his stolen goods in the farmhouse at the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch in eastern Elwynn Forest.",al={"morgan location","where is morgan the collector","brackwell pumpkin patch house"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Stormwind hunting him?",a="Marshal Dughan and local authorities want Morgan eliminated to sever Defias leadership in Elwynn and recover proof of who organizes the rural uprisings.",al={"why kill morgan","manhunt target"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is special about the ring he carries?",a="Morgan carries a signet ring that gives authorities evidence as they investigate his activities in Elwynn Forest.",al={"collectors ring","collector signet ring","morgan ring lore"},sp=1,it="item"},{q="Whose side is Morgan the Collector on?",a="Morgan the Collector is a dedicated operative of the Defias Brotherhood. Rather than a common highwayman, he serves as an officer within the criminal organization, working directly against the Kingdom of Stormwind and orchestrating brotherhood activity throughout the heart of Elwynn Forest.",al={"morgan collector faction","what faction is morgan","is morgan defias"},it="side",add="8321821e"},{q="What does Morgan the Collector want?",a="Morgan acts as the ringleader overseeing Defias operations across Elwynn Forest. Bearing the moniker 'the Collector,' his aim is to gather wealth, resources, and influence for the Brotherhood's uprising, establishing a fortified foothold in the pumpkin patch right under the noses of Stormwind's guards.",al={"what is morgan trying to do","morgan collector goal","morgan collector motive"},it="wants",add="5f1d52ce"},{q="Why is Morgan the Collector in Elwynn Forest?",a="Morgan has established himself at the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch to personally direct the Defias Brotherhood's local operations. By taking refuge in the farmhouse alongside lieutenants Surena Caledon and Erlan Drudgemoor, he keeps tight coordination over the bandits spreading throughout the region.",al={"why is morgan at brackwell pumpkin patch","what brought morgan here"},it="why_here",add="2a29f808"},{q="Who is Morgan the Collector tied to?",a="His signet ring becomes evidence in an investigation of the outlaws troubling Elwynn Forest and their connections.",al={"who does morgan work with","morgan collector associates","morgan stonemasons"},it="ties",add="ceb85f69"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a Rogue, you can see how Morgan's discipline turns scattered thieves into an organized underground syndicate that funds an insurgency.",["race:Human"]="As a Human, taking down Morgan strikes back at the traitors who have turned Stormwind's peaceful farms into fortified bandit dens."},kw={"brackwell","brotherhood","defias","dughan","manhunt","morgan","pumpkin patch","signet","the collector"},rel={"quest:147","subzone:brackwell-pumpkin-patch","topic:defias-brotherhood","topic:stonemasons-guild","npc:marshal-dughan","quest:1688","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Morgan the Collector"}}
E["npc:priestess-anetta"] = {t="npc",n="Priestess Anetta",z="elwynn",s="Within Northshire Abbey, Priestess Anetta teaches new priests the first rites of the Holy Light. A human cleric, she belongs to the Brotherhood of Northshire.",h="Within Northshire Abbey, Priestess Anetta teaches new priests the first rites of the Holy Light.",sec={{t="Tender of the Faithful",b="Priestess Anetta keeps to the quiet library wing on Northshire Abbey’s ground floor. Defias bandits and kobolds trouble the valley. She reminds those who pass that the Light may be the one thing that saves them someday.",sp=0},{t="Guiding Novice Priests",b="New human priests come to Priestess Anetta in the cloister with a hallowed letter of introduction. She teaches them holy words to mend flesh and call down smiting radiance against evil. Under her guidance, the young acolytes prepare to carry the Light beyond Northshire’s secluded walls.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Priestess Anetta?",a="Priestess Anetta is a human cleric of the Holy Light and a member of the Brotherhood of Northshire. On Northshire Abbey’s ground floor, she mentors newly arrived priests in their first sacred rites.",al={"who is anetta","priestess anetta lore","priestess anetta northshire"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Priestess Anetta?",a="Priestess Anetta is inside Northshire Abbey in northern Elwynn Forest. Enter the front gates and go into the main hall. Look for her on the ground floor of the library wing.",al={"where is priestess anetta","anetta location","find anetta"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does she play in the Abbey's defense?",a="Stormwind marshals and recruits fight to reclaim the valley from Defias bandits and kobolds. Priestess Anetta trains priests to heal and protect their comrades with the Light.",al={"what does anetta do","anetta role"},it="purpose"},{q="What training does she offer?",a="Priestess Anetta teaches young priests entry-level prayers and clerical spells. They learn to heal and smite enemies in the name of the Holy Light.",al={"can anetta teach me spells","anetta priest spells"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Priestess Anetta on?",a="Priestess Anetta stands firmly with the Kingdom of Stormwind, the Holy Light, and the Brotherhood of Northshire. Serving within Northshire Abbey, she works to aid the realm's defenders and uphold the peaceful sanctuary against surrounding threats.",al={"anetta faction","who does anetta serve","priestess anetta loyalty"},it="side",add="d2501181"},{q="What does Priestess Anetta want?",a="Priestess Anetta wants to prepare a new generation to wield the Holy Light. Her calling is to guide fledgling priests in their spiritual discipline and teach them the fundamentals of healing and protecting others with the Light.",al={"anetta goal","what is anetta trying to do","anetta objective"},it="wants",add="bbb44d1e"},{q="Why is Priestess Anetta here?",a="Priestess Anetta resides at Northshire Abbey as an ordained sacerdotal member of the Brotherhood of Northshire. She remains stationed in the abbey's library wing to pass down the fundamentals of the Light to initiates answering Stormwind's call.",al={"why is anetta at northshire","anetta purpose here","why is priestess anetta in the abbey"},it="why_here",add="00624d11"},{q="Who is Priestess Anetta tied to?",a="Anetta is a devoted member of the Brotherhood of Northshire and serves alongside the abbey's clergy and guards. Through her holy vows and training duties, she remains closely bound to the Church of the Holy Light and the defense of Stormwind.",al={"anetta connections","who is anetta affiliated with","anetta faction ties"},it="ties",add="1b4a2e6e"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a young human priest beginning in Northshire, you meet Priestess Anetta as your first mentor. She affirms your holy calling and teaches you to commune directly with the Light.",["faction:Alliance"]="Priestess Anetta prepares young priests to support those defending Northshire Valley."},kw={"anetta","brotherhood of northshire","elwynn forest","holy light","library wing","northshire abbey","priest trainer","priestess anetta"},rel={"subzone:northshire-abbey","topic:brotherhood-of-northshire","topic:light","subzone:library-wing-northshire","quest:3103","quest:5623","zone:elwynn","topic:alliance"},src={"Priestess Anetta"}}
E["npc:priestess-josetta"] = {t="npc",n="Priestess Josetta",z="elwynn",s="In Goldshire, Priestess Josetta guides young priests beyond their first trials at Northshire. She teaches them faith, devotion, and service to others.",h="In Goldshire, Priestess Josetta guides young priests beyond their first trials at Northshire.",sec={{t="A Beacon in Goldshire",b="From an upstairs room in the Lion's Pride Inn, Priestess Josetta tends to the people of Elwynn Forest. Travelers, guards, and local workers come within her reach there. She gives spiritual care among ordinary folk, serving the Holy Light wherever people need comfort.",sp=0},{t="Guiding Young Acolytes",b="After their first studies at Northshire Abbey, young priests come to Priestess Josetta for guidance. She sends them into the countryside to aid wounded guards and comfort those who suffer. Their work teaches them that priesthood asks for more than prayers learned by heart. They must put the Light to work and help mend a broken world.",sp=0},{t="A Quiet Regret",b="Priestess Josetta regrets that she did not travel farther when she was young. She chose familiar ground over the wider roads of Azeroth. Though content with her sacred service in Goldshire, she urges young disciples to be bolder and carry their faith to distant frontiers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Priestess Josetta?",a="Priestess Josetta lives in a second-floor room beside Michelle Belle at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire.",al={"josetta location","where is priestess josetta","goldshire priest trainer location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does Priestess Josetta serve?",a="After Northshire, Priestess Josetta trains Alliance priests in holy spells, discipline, and the duties of their calling.",al={"what does josetta do","priestess josetta role"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Josetta operate out of an inn instead of a church?",a="Goldshire has no separate chapel, and the Lion's Pride Inn is the town center. From her upstairs room, Josetta cares for weary travelers, injured guards, and local residents.",al={"why in an inn","why lions pride inn"},it="why_here"},{q="What personal regret does Josetta share with disciples?",a="Priestess Josetta regrets that she lacked the courage to leave home and travel when she was young. She urges young adventurers to explore beyond Elwynn.",al={"josetta backstory","josetta travel regret"}},{q="What kind of duties does Josetta assign to new priests?",a="Priestess Josetta sends acolytes to help wounded defenders in the field. They learn healing prayers and see that the Light must reach those in need.",al={"josetta quests","garments of the light quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Does Josetta teach racial priest spells?",a="Yes. As a human priestess in Elwynn, Josetta teaches human priests prayers favored by their people, including Desperate Prayer.",al={"desperate prayer trainer","human priest spells"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Priestess Josetta on?",a="Priestess Josetta stands firmly with the Holy Light, the Church, and the Grand Alliance. Operating within Goldshire under the banner of Stormwind, she dedicates herself to mentoring aspiring priests of the Kingdom, ensuring they uphold their holy vows in service to their people and allies.",al={"priestess josetta faction","is priestess josetta alliance","who does josetta serve"},it="side",add="41d8cc17"},{q="What does Priestess Josetta want?",a="Priestess Josetta desires to foster devotion and discipline in the next generation of holy practitioners. Though she privately regrets lacking the courage to wander Azeroth when she was younger, she channels her purpose into guiding you and other novitiates to aid the wounded and carry the Light far beyond Goldshire.",al={"what are josetta's goals","what does priestess josetta want","josetta motive"},it="wants",add="165cad46"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest leaving Northshire, you can learn core spells from Josetta and put your healing vows into practice.",["race:Human"]="As a human priest, you hear the Church of the Light's teachings in Josetta's counsel and learn prayers from your people's traditions.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member in Elwynn, you can turn to Josetta for spiritual and healing support for local defenders."},kw={"desperate prayer","elwynn forest","goldshire","holy light","josetta","lion's pride inn","priest trainer","priestess josetta"},rel={"subzone:lion-s-pride-inn","subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn","topic:light","quest:5624","quest:5634","quest:5623","quest:5628"},src={"Priestess Josetta"}}
E["npc:remy-two-times"] = {t="npc",n="Remy \"Two Times\"",z="elwynn",s="In Goldshire, Remy \"Two Times\" trades goods and buys raw materials. He came from the Redridge Mountains, and earned his name by repeating the ends of his sentences twice.",h="In Goldshire, Remy \"Two Times\" trades goods and buys raw materials.",sec={{t="A Merchant with an Odd Quirk",b="Travelers passing through Goldshire can strike a deal with Remy \"Two Times\". He seeks profit in troubled Elwynn Forest, and his trade puts coin in their hands. His unusual way of speaking may amuse them.",sp=0},{t="Business in Troubled Waters",b="Trade in Elwynn suffers as kobolds overrun the local gold mines and aggressive murlocs infest the riverbanks. Remy pays travelers for pouches of gold dust gathered from kobolds in the mines. Near Crystal Lake, he watches for suspicious murloc movements.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is he called 'Two Times'?",a="Remy earned his nickname by habitually repeating the final words of his sentences twice when he speaks.",al={"remy two times name","why does remy repeat words","two times meaning"},it="name"},{q="Where does Remy come from originally?",a="Remy came to Goldshire from the Redridge Mountains to trade in Elwynn Forest.",al={"remy origin","where is remy from"},it="origin"},{q="What does Remy do with all the gold dust he buys?",a="Remy collects gold dust gathered from kobolds in local mines to smelt, trade, or resell for profit.",al={"why does remy want gold dust","gold dust exchange lore"},it="purpose"},{q="Where can Remy be found in Goldshire?",a="Remy can be found outdoors in Goldshire near the Lion's Pride Inn, ready to barter with passing travelers.",al={"where is remy two times","remy location goldshire"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Remy \"Two Times\"?",a="Remy \"Two Times\" is a human merchant who has set up shop in Goldshire. Originally from the Redridge Mountains, he is known around Elwynn Forest for his eccentric verbal tic of repeating the final words of his sentences twice.",al={"who is remy","remy two times identity","who is remy two times"},it="identity",add="99a83a18"},{q="Whose side is Remy \"Two Times\" on?",a="Remy is loyal to the Grand Alliance and the Kingdom of Stormwind. He conducts his trade openly in Goldshire, dealing peacefully with local authorities, townspeople, and passing adventurers.",al={"remy two times faction","is remy alliance","who does remy work for"},it="side",add="e326d54d"},{q="What does Remy \"Two Times\" want?",a="As an enterprising merchant, Remy wants profitable commodities and local security. He eagerly trades with travelers for gold dust gathered from nearby mines, and he is keen to resolve any nearby perils that threaten commerce in Goldshire.",al={"what does remy want","remy two times goals","why does remy need adventurers"},it="wants",add="85133ed8"},{q="Why is Remy \"Two Times\" in Goldshire?",a="Having traveled down from his home in the Redridge Mountains, Remy settled in Goldshire to pursue trade. The busy crossroads village offers a steady stream of miners, travelers, and adventurers willing to buy, sell, and run errands.",al={"why is remy in goldshire","why did remy leave redridge","remy two times why here"},it="why_here",add="7f55543c"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="If you work in the Fargodeep or Jasperlode mines, you may meet Remy, who trades for gold dust gathered from the kobolds there.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance recruit arriving in Goldshire, you can take on Remy's straightforward work to help clear local threats and earn quick coin."},kw={"elwynn","gold dust","goldshire","merchant","murloc","redridge","remy","two times"},rel={"subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn","quest:47","quest:40","zone:redridge"},src={"Remy \"Two Times\""}}
E["npc:sara-timberlain"] = {t="npc",n="Sara Timberlain",z="elwynn",s="At Eastvale Logging Camp, Sara Timberlain sews gear for Stormwind's soldiers. She makes useful armaments from salvaged cloth and leather.",h="At Eastvale Logging Camp, Sara Timberlain sews gear for Stormwind's soldiers.",sec={{t="Needlework on the Frontier",b="On the western edge of Eastvale Logging Camp, Sara Timberlain sews outside a small cottage. Axes ring through the camp as workers fell trees. Though the settlement lies far from other settled lands, wolves and murlocs prowl nearby. Sara still welcomes travelers.\n\nShe turns scraps of linen and salvaged bandanas into sturdy gear. Her skill has earned official recognition. Stormwind's military forces commission her to supply armaments made of cloth and leather.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sara Timberlain?",a="Sara Timberlain is a skilled seamstress at Eastvale Logging Camp in Elwynn Forest. She makes practical gear from reclaimed fabrics and has contracts to supply the Stormwind Army.",al={"who is sara timberlain","sara timberlain","eastvale tailor"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Sara Timberlain?",a="Sara Timberlain sits outside a house on the western side of Eastvale Logging Camp. The camp lies in eastern Elwynn Forest along the road to Redridge.",al={"sara timberlain location","where is sara timberlain","timberlain house"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Sara gathering cloth for the army?",a="The Stormwind Army relies on local crafters to maintain its equipment stores. Sara uses salvaged cloth, including linen gathered by travelers, to make sturdy garments and armor linings for the kingdom's soldiers.",al={"why does sara need linen","stormwind army armor","cloth and leather armor quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Sara Timberlain on?",a="Sara is loyal to the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance. Stationed at the Eastvale Logging Camp, she works directly to support the realm's defense, fulfilling tailoring commissions for the Stormwind Army to keep its soldiers equipped with sturdy armor.",al={"sara timberlain faction","who does sara timberlain serve","sara timberlain alliance"},it="side",add="693a4fc8"},{q="What does Sara Timberlain want?",a="Sara needs raw crafting materials, particularly bolts of linen cloth salvaged from local bandits, to continue her tailoring work. By turning reclaimed cloth into tailored goods and armor, she helps supply the realm's fighting forces while rewarding travelers who bring her supplies.",al={"what does sara timberlain need","sara timberlain materials","why does sara want linen"},it="wants",add="94680b13"},{q="Why is Sara Timberlain at the logging camp?",a="Sara resides on the western side of the Eastvale Logging Camp, where she plies her trade away from the crowded streets of Stormwind City. The frontier outpost offers a quiet place to work her needle while keeping her close to travelers and local suppliers who gather the salvaged materials she relies upon.",al={"why is sara in eastvale","sara timberlain eastvale logging camp","why is sara timberlain here"},it="why_here",add="414da08e"},{q="Who is Sara Timberlain tied to?",a="Sara maintains close ties with the Stormwind Army, which has officially commissioned her to craft both cloth and leather armor for their troops. She also works alongside the local woodsmen and loggers stationed at the Eastvale Logging Camp.",al={"sara timberlain connections","who does sara timberlain work for","sara timberlain stormwind army"},it="ties",add="59756f86"},{q="Why is Sara Timberlain famous?",a="Sara is renowned throughout the region for her exceptional tailoring skills, specifically her rare talent for transforming rough, salvaged scraps of cloth into finely crafted garments and reliable armor worthy of the realm's standing army.",al={"sara timberlain reputation","is sara timberlain well known","what is sara timberlain famous for"},it="fame",add="42dfe0df"}},ang={["profession:Tailoring"]="Sara shows how frontier tailors turn scraps of rough linen and bandit cloth into useful garments for military commissions.",["faction:Alliance"]="Outlying settlements such as Eastvale help defend the kingdom. Local craftspeople supply basic armor to the under-resourced Stormwind Army."},kw={"eastvale","linen","logging camp","sara timberlain","seamstress","stormwind army","tailor"},rel={"subzone:eastvale-logging-camp","zone:elwynn","quest:59","quest:83","topic:stormwind-army","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Sara Timberlain"}}
E["npc:smith-argus"] = {t="npc",n="Smith Argus",z="elwynn",s="At Goldshire's forge, Smith Argus keeps travelers and local smiths supplied. He repairs gear, trains new smiths, and sends horseshoes to Redridge while coordinating with Stormwind craftsmen.",h="At Goldshire's forge, Smith Argus keeps travelers and local smiths supplied.",sec={{t="The Anvil of Goldshire",b="Near the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, Smith Argus works the forge. Gnolls, kobolds, and Defias bandits threaten the area, so he keeps the local militia and passing adventurers equipped. He mends armor and makes sturdy tools. As a blacksmithing trainer, he teaches new smiths to work copper and bronze.",sp=0},{t="Inter-Town Trade and Demands",b="Goldshire's central position makes Smith Argus a link in Stormwind's regional supply. Craftsmen in nearby settlements come to him for specialized gear and raw materials. Farrier Verner Osgood in Redridge depends on Argus for horseshoes for pack animals and cavalry. Metalworkers in Stormwind's Dwarven District also arrange deliveries through him.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Smith Argus?",a="Smith Argus works at the outdoor anvil and forge behind the armor shop in Goldshire, near the Lion's Pride Inn in central Elwynn Forest.",al={"argus location","where is smith argus","smith argus elwynn"},it="why_here",gp=true},{q="What services does Smith Argus provide?",a="Argus teaches new blacksmiths the fundamentals. His Classic title is Journeyman Blacksmith.",al={"what does argus teach","argus trainer","goldshire blacksmith trainer"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Why does a blacksmith in Redridge send me to Smith Argus?",a="Verner Osgood, a craftsman in Lakeshire, needs horseshoes to keep supply wagons and mounts moving against the Blackrock orc threat. He contracts Argus in Goldshire to forge and supply them.",al={"the price of shoes quest","verner horseshoes","why argus horseshoes"},it="ties"},{q="What is Argus's connection to Stormwind City?",a="Argus coordinates supply runs with dwarven smiths in Stormwind City, including Grimand Elmore in the Dwarven District.",al={"elmore's task","stormwind gryphon argus"},it="ties"},{q="Can Smith Argus train advanced or expert blacksmithing?",a="Argus teaches the early stages of blacksmithing. Advanced techniques require more experienced masters in larger settlements.",al={"argus expert blacksmith","how high can argus train"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Does Smith Argus belong to any particular guild?",a="Argus is a loyal subject of the Kingdom of Stormwind and belongs to the local craftsmen community serving the Alliance in Elwynn Forest.",al={"argus faction","argus guild"},it="side"},{q="Who is Smith Argus?",a="Smith Argus is a blacksmith serving the Kingdom of Stormwind from the forge in Goldshire. A reliable fixture in Elwynn Forest, he shapes iron and steel for local defenders while training aspiring craftsmen and maintaining supply lines with fellow smiths across human lands.",al={"who is argus","smith argus lore","who is smith argus"},it="identity",add="07d5dba5"},{q="Whose side is Smith Argus on?",a="Smith Argus is loyal to the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance. Stationed at the bustling crossroads of Goldshire, he works closely with regional craftsmen to keep Stormwind's outlying settlements supplied and fortified against gathering threats.",al={"smith argus faction","argus alliance or horde","who does argus serve"},it="side",add="79448098"},{q="Why is Smith Argus here?",a="Argus operates the vital forge in Goldshire, positioning him directly along the trade route linking Stormwind City to Redridge and Westfall. From here, he can readily supply regional outposts, shoe horses, and instruct new smiths essential to the kingdom's defense.",al={"why is argus in goldshire","what brought smith argus here"},it="why_here",add="bbf4c38d"},{q="What does Smith Argus want?",a="Smith Argus wants to keep his forge running smoothly and maintain active trade with distant colleagues like Verner Osgood in Redridge. Whether fulfilling specialized orders for horseshoes or exchanging technical shipments, he works to ensure the kingdom's settlements remain well-equipped.",al={"argus motive","what does argus need","smith argus goals"},it="wants",add="d8765a7e"}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="For Alliance characters starting in Elwynn, Argus may be their first forge teacher. He teaches initial recipes for rough copper gear and useful items.",["profession:Mining"]="Miners bring metal to Goldshire's forge, where Argus teaches new smiths to shape it into useful tools.",["race:Human"]="Argus reflects the hard work of Elwynn's tradesmen amid political neglect and bandit unrest."},kw={"blacksmith","elwynn forest","forge","goldshire","horseshoes","lion's pride","smith argus","trainer","verner osgood"},rel={"subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn","quest:118","quest:119","quest:1097","quest:6181","zone:redridge"},src={"Smith Argus"}}
E["npc:supervisor-raelen"] = {t="npc",n="Supervisor Raelen",z="elwynn",s="At Eastvale Logging Camp, Supervisor Raelen keeps timber moving toward Stormwind. She directs the laborers, tracks their daily quotas, and watches over the lumber supply.",h="At Eastvale Logging Camp, Supervisor Raelen keeps timber moving toward Stormwind.",sec={{t="Keeping the Camp on Schedule",b="Supervisor Raelen directs the woodcutters at Eastvale Logging Camp, near Marshal Patterson and the camp’s wagons. The camp lies on eastern Elwynn’s edge, near the Redridge Mountains, where the work brings trouble. Raelen coordinates the crews and keeps them focused on their quotas despite hazards in the surrounding woods. She sees that gathered timber is processed, bundled, and sent toward Stormwind.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Supervisor Raelen?",a="Supervisor Raelen oversees the logging crews at Eastvale Logging Camp in eastern Elwynn Forest. She manages their work and keeps their timber quotas on schedule.",al={"who is raelen","raelen elwynn","eastvale supervisor"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Supervisor Raelen?",a="Supervisor Raelen is in the center of Eastvale Logging Camp, near the loaded wood wagons and Marshal Patterson.",al={"where is raelen","supervisor raelen location","find raelen"},gp=true},{q="Why does Supervisor Raelen need help from adventurers?",a="Timber gathering near the forest’s edge can be dangerous. When wildlife or other disruptions trouble the workers, cut lumber bundles may be abandoned or scattered among the trees.",al={"raelen quest","bundle of trouble quest","why help raelen"},it="wants"},{q="What role does the Eastvale Logging Camp play in Elwynn Forest?",a="Eastvale Logging Camp is the main logging operation in eastern Elwynn Forest. Its lumber supports rebuilding and maintenance in Stormwind and nearby settlements.",al={"what is eastvale","eastvale logging role","why is eastvale important"},it="place"},{q="Whose side is Supervisor Raelen on?",a="Supervisor Raelen is loyal to the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance. She manages lumber operations on behalf of the kingdom at the Eastvale Logging Camp, working directly alongside Stormwind guards and laborers to keep timber flowing to the capital.",al={"raelen faction","who does supervisor raelen serve","is raelen alliance"},it="side",add="5e9ae7c9"},{q="Why is Supervisor Raelen here at Eastvale?",a="Raelen oversees day-to-day logging at the Eastvale Logging Camp. She directs the local laborers, monitors lumber wagons, and ensures wood collection meets Stormwind's quotas, keeping the operation running despite the surrounding wilderness hazards.",al={"why is supervisor raelen here","raelen purpose eastvale","what does raelen do here"},it="why_here",add="93ff040d"},{q="Who is Supervisor Raelen tied to?",a="Raelen works closely with the local Stormwind authorities stationed at Eastvale, notably Marshal Patterson, who oversees the camp's defense. She also directs the camp's workforce of local peasants and woodcutters.",al={"raelen connections","who does raelen work with","supervisor raelen allies"},it="ties",add="e5fd1368"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Stormwind needs timber for its defenses and construction, so Raelen’s lumber quotas matter to the kingdom’s war effort."},kw={"a bundle of trouble","eastvale","eastvale logging camp","elwynn forest","lumber","raelen","supervisor raelen","wood quotas"},rel={"subzone:eastvale-logging-camp","quest:5545","zone:elwynn"},src={"Supervisor Raelen"}}
E["npc:theocritus"] = {t="npc",n="Theocritus",z="elwynn",s="At the Tower of Azora in eastern Elwynn, Theocritus watches over Stormwind's kingdom and opposes Morganth. The eccentric human archmage lives independently, apart from everyday concerns, with servants and magical scrying devices.",h="At the Tower of Azora in eastern Elwynn, Theocritus watches over Stormwind's kingdom and opposes Morganth.",sec={{t="Master of the Tower",b="Archmage Theocritus keeps his own stronghold in Stormwind's kingdom. He lives in the Tower of Azora, near the eastern road to Redridge. Eccentric in his habits, he enjoys a comfortable life with a large household staff. Among them are gnomish attendants and his clothier, Morley Eberlein. Though apart from local villagers' everyday concerns, his magic guards eastern Elwynn.",sp=0},{t="The War Against Morganth",b="The fallen mage Morganth is Theocritus's greatest concern. Morganth works from the Tower of Ilgalar in the nearby Redridge Mountains. Theocritus sees him as both a personal enemy and a danger to Stormwind. For months, arcane research has helped Theocritus undermine him.\n\nWith scrying devices such as the Eye of Azora, he watches Morganth's actions and probes his thoughts. He also studies the magical pendants worn by Morganth's Shadowhide gnolls, hoping an arcane pulse can turn their master's creations against him and immobilize the entire pack.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Theocritus?",a="Archmage Theocritus lives independently in the Tower of Azora in eastern Elwynn Forest. Eccentric and somewhat isolated, he turns his magic toward protecting the region from dark magical threats.",al={"theocritus lore","who is the mage in the tower","tower of azora mage"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Theocritus live in Elwynn Forest?",a="Theocritus keeps his own sanctum in the Tower of Azora in eastern Elwynn. His household attends him as he pursues his studies and watches the border with Redridge, where his rival Morganth lives in the Tower of Ilgalar.",al={"why is theocritus in elwynn"}},{q="Who is Theocritus fighting against?",a="Theocritus's chief rival is Morganth, a fallen human mage who practices dark magic in the Tower of Ilgalar across the border in Redridge. Theocritus regards Morganth as a personal enemy and a grave threat to Stormwind.",al={"theocritus enemy","who is morganth","theocritus rival"}},{q="What is the Eye of Azora?",a="The Eye of Azora is a scrying device housed atop Theocritus's tower. He uses it to peer into distant lands, track threats, and try to read Morganth's thoughts.",al={"eye of azora lore","how does theocritus spy","theocritus crystal ball"},it="item"},{q="Why does Theocritus want Shadowhide gnoll pendants?",a="The Shadowhide gnolls serve Morganth and wear enchanted pendants linked to him. Theocritus studies the pendants to learn how that link works, hoping to send an arcane attack through it and paralyze the gnolls in battle.",al={"gnoll pendants theocritus","theocritus retrieval","why collect gnoll pendants"}},{q="Who serves Theocritus in his tower?",a="Theocritus's household includes gnomish servants who tend to his daily affairs and his personal clothier, Morley Eberlein, who cares for his wardrobe.",al={"tower of azora staff","who lives in tower of azora","theocritus servants"}},{q="Whose side is Theocritus on?",a="Archmage Theocritus acts independently, pursuing his own esoteric studies. While he remains detached from the day-to-day politics of Stormwind and the Alliance, he still considers it his duty to defend the realm against dark sorcery. He stands firmly against the rogue wizard Morganth and the dark forces encroaching on Elwynn and Redridge.",al={"theocritus alliance or horde","who does theocritus serve","theocritus faction"},it="side",add="ffea707c"},{q="What does Theocritus want?",a="Theocritus focuses his formidable arcane skills on countering his bitter rival, the fallen mage Morganth. Through the magical scrying device known as the Eye of Azora and recovered Shadowhide gnoll pendants, he seeks to penetrate Morganth's mind and disrupt the dark wizard's control over the gnolls terrorizing the region.",al={"theocritus goal","what is theocritus trying to do","theocritus purpose"},it="wants",add="09c566f6"},{q="Why is Theocritus in Elwynn Forest?",a="Theocritus established himself in the Tower of Azora in eastern Elwynn Forest. The secluded tower provides him a tranquil sanctum to conduct research in isolation, surrounded by his gnomish attendants, while keeping watch over the nearby border with Redridge.",al={"why is theocritus in elwynn","why is theocritus here","theocritus tower of azora why"},it="why_here",add="a72df9dd"},{q="Who is Theocritus tied to?",a="Though eccentric and solitary, Theocritus is attended in his tower by a devoted staff of gnomish servants and his personal tailor, Morley Eberlein, while remaining locked in a deep personal enmity with the rogue mage Morganth.",al={"theocritus connections","theocritus friends","theocritus dalaran allies"},it="ties",add="f1864285"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Theocritus shows how a wizard can work independently, without belonging to an order. He keeps a private sanctum and uses magic to scry across long distances.",["faction:Alliance"]="Though eccentric and aloof, Theocritus uses his arcane vision and resources to defend eastern Elwynn and Redridge from rogue spellcasters.",["race:Human"]="The conflict between Theocritus and Morganth reflects two paths for human sorcery: disciplined study devoted to defense, and corruption driven by dark ambition."},kw={"archmage","elwynn forest","eye of azora","morganth","morley eberlein","shadowhide","theocritus","tower of azora"},rel={"subzone:tower-of-azora","quest:178","quest:94","quest:249","zone:elwynn","topic:gnoll","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Theocritus"}}
E["npc:tommy-joe-stonefield"] = {t="npc",n="Tommy Joe Stonefield",z="elwynn",s="On the river west of Stonefield Farm, Tommy Joe Stonefield longs for Maybell Maclure. Their families have feuded for years, so he depends on secret notes and quiet riverbanks to keep their love hidden.",h="On the river west of Stonefield Farm, Tommy Joe Stonefield longs for Maybell Maclure.",sec={{t="A Star-Crossed Feud",b="Tommy Joe Stonefield waits by the river west of Stonefield Farm, watching the Maclure homestead across the water. The Stonefields and Maclures have clashed for years over land, pride, and farmyard squabbles. Their elders keep the feud alive, yet Tommy Joe has fallen in love with Maybell Maclure. The two cannot meet openly without angering both households. Gramma Stonefield, Tommy Joe’s sympathetic grandmother, helps them exchange secret notes and tokens of affection.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tommy Joe Stonefield?",a="Tommy Joe Stonefield is a young human who lives on Stonefield Farm in Elwynn Forest. He is secretly in love with Maybell Maclure, daughter of his family’s bitter rivals.",al={"tommy joe","who is tommy joe","stonefield son"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Tommy Joe Stonefield?",a="Tommy Joe Stonefield stands on the riverbank west of Stonefield Farm, looking across the water toward the Maclure farmstead where Maybell lives.",al={"tommy joe location","where is tommy joe","find tommy joe"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the Stonefields and Maclures fighting?",a="No one says what began the feud. The Stonefields and Maclures have kept up their bitter rivalry for years, and neither family wants its young ones associating with the other.",al={"family feud","why do they hate each other","stonefield maclure feud"},it="conflict"},{q="Who helps Tommy Joe and Maybell meet?",a="Gramma Stonefield knows of their affection and helps their secret courtship. She uses travelers to carry discreet messages between Tommy Joe and Maybell.",al={"gramma stonefield help","secret lovers help","who helps the lovers"},it="allies"},{q="Whose side is Tommy Joe Stonefield on?",a="He belongs to the Stonefield family, but his heart is not in their bitter feud. While he lives upon the Stonefield farm, his loyalty is torn between his kin and his love for Maybell Maclure, who belongs to their sworn rivals.",al={"tommy joe allegiance","which family tommy joe","stonefield or maclure"},it="side",add="3c95bb6e"},{q="What does Tommy Joe Stonefield want?",a="Tommy Joe desires nothing more than to be with Maybell Maclure. The long-standing hatred between the Stonefields and the Maclures keeps them apart, so he longs to find a way to meet her in secret and keep their love alive despite the feud.",al={"what does tommy joe want","tommy joe goal","tommy joe wish"},it="wants",add="8a9aad66"},{q="Why is Tommy Joe Stonefield here?",a="Tommy Joe waits quietly along the riverbank near his family's farmstead. Tucked away from prying eyes, it is a secluded spot where he can slip away from his chores and hope for a chance to rendezvous with Maybell away from their warring kin.",al={"why is tommy joe at the river","what is tommy joe doing here","tommy joe stonefield location why"},it="why_here",add="96565570"},{q="Who is Tommy Joe Stonefield tied to?",a="He is a member of the Stonefield clan, closely guided by his grandmother, Gramma Stonefield, who actively aids him. His most significant tie, however, is to Maybell Maclure, the daughter of his family's bitter rivals, with whom he is deeply in love.",al={"tommy joe connections","tommy joe family","who is tommy joe related to"},it="ties",add="b663afb0"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer in southern Elwynn, you may find Tommy Joe’s secret romance a reminder of the quiet personal lives that continue amid banditry and political unrest."},kw={"elwynn forest","gramma stonefield","maybell maclure","stonefield farm","tommy joe stonefield","young lovers"},rel={"npc:maybell-maclure","npc:gramma-stonefield","subzone:stonefield-farm","quest:111","zone:elwynn"},src={"Tommy Joe Stonefield"}}
E["npc:willem"] = {t="npc",n="Willem",z="elwynn",s="Outside Northshire Abbey, Willem sends recruits to face the threats gathering in the valley. He serves under Marshal McBride as the Defias Brotherhood presses into Northshire.",h="Outside Northshire Abbey, Willem sends recruits to face the threats gathering in the valley.",sec={{t="A Watchman at the Abbey",b="Deputy Willem watches the gates of Northshire Abbey, where the Stormwind Army holds a foothold in the valley. The kingdom's soldiers are spread across many territories, so small groups like Marshal McBride's garrison must defend the land nearby.\n\nWillem greets incoming volunteers and sends them to aid residents and guard the valley's edges.",sp=0},{t="Confronting the Defias",b="The Defias Brotherhood is Willem's most pressing concern. Bandits in red bandanas have entered Northshire, stolen supplies, threatened farmer Milly Osworth, and taken footholds among nearby vineyards and hills.\n\nWillem offers bounties on known cutthroats such as Garrick Padfoot. He hopes to break their leadership before they can take the abbey grounds.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Deputy Willem?",a="Deputy Willem serves in the Stormwind Army outside Northshire Abbey in Elwynn Forest. Under Marshal McBride, he directs recruits against threats in the valley.",al={"who is willem","deputy willem role","willem northshire"},it="identity"},{q="Who does Deputy Willem report to?",a="Deputy Willem reports to Marshal McBride, who commands Northshire Valley's defense and military operations.",al={"willem commander","who is willems boss","willem leader"},it="ties"},{q="Why is Willem issuing bounties on the Defias?",a="The Defias Brotherhood has entered Northshire Valley, threatening the abbey and terrorizing local laborers. Willem sends fighters after bandits and leaders such as Garrick Padfoot to restore order.",al={"why defias bounty","willem red bandanas","willem defias"},it="wants"},{q="Where can Deputy Willem be found?",a="Willem waits outside the main entrance of Northshire Abbey in northern Elwynn Forest. There he greets travelers and recruits entering the courtyard.",al={"willem location","where is deputy willem","find willem"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How does Willem assist the local workers?",a="Willem sends fighters to aid residents whose livelihoods are threatened, including orchardist Milly Osworth and peltskinner Eagan.",al={"willem milly osworth","willem eagan","willem quests"},it="purpose"},{q="Why are troops like Willem struggling to maintain order alone?",a="Stormwind faces internal strain, political tension, and distant military commitments. With King Varian missing, garrisons like Northshire must rely on untested recruits and volunteers to handle unrest at home.",al={"why is stormwind army weak","why northshire undefended","stormwind manpower northshire"},it="conflict"},{q="Whose side is Deputy Willem on?",a="Deputy Willem is a loyal soldier of the Stormwind Army, serving the Alliance. Standing guard outside Northshire Abbey, he upholds the kingdom's laws and directs able-bodied recruits to defend the valley from brigands and thieves.",al={"willem faction","who does deputy willem serve","willem alliance or horde"},it="side",add="cea9f32f"},{q="Why is Deputy Willem here in Northshire?",a="Deputy Willem is stationed outside Northshire Abbey to maintain order and direct new recruits to where they are needed most. With the kingdom's defenses stretched thin, he serves as the primary liaison organizing the valley's response to local threats.",al={"why is willem in northshire","what brought willem here","deputy willem duty"},it="why_here",add="29d9c6b5"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human stepping out of Northshire Abbey, you may meet Deputy Willem, one of the first Stormwind officers to welcome you into the kingdom's service.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see through Willem how the Defias unrest reaches even Elwynn's peaceful heartland.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you can serve under Willem's direction, driving out bandits and restoring order to the realm."},kw={"defias","deputy willem","elwynn forest","garrick padfoot","marshal mcbride","northshire","northshire abbey","willem"},rel={"npc:marshal-mcbride","subzone:northshire-valley","quest:783","quest:18","quest:6","topic:defias-brotherhood","topic:stormwind-army","zone:elwynn"},src={"Willem"}}
E["npc:william-pestle"] = {t="npc",n="William Pestle",z="elwynn",s="At the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, William Pestle gathers supplies for Stormwind's apothecary. He and his brother Morgan run the shop in the Trade District. William hires travelers to find candles, kelp, and herbs.",h="At the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, William Pestle gathers supplies for Stormwind's apothecary.",sec={{t="Apothecary Abroad",b="William works from the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire. His brother Morgan Pestle tends the counter at Pestle's Apothecary in Stormwind City's Trade District. In Elwynn Forest, William works with local gatherers to secure raw materials for the city's shops. He sends regular shipments to Stormwind, where citizens rely on restorative salves, draughts, and powders.",sp=0},{t="Curious Reagents",b="Common garden herbs do not always meet William's needs. He hires newcomers to gather wax candles carried by Elwynn's kobolds and crystal kelp from the murlocs of Crystal Lake, just east of Goldshire. The ingredients may seem strange to those unfamiliar with alchemy. William believes they have potent virtues in a mixture.",sp=0},{t="A Concoction for Young Love",b="William is an old friend of Mildred Stonefield. When Maybell Maclure and Tommy Joe Stonefield are caught between their families' bitter feud, William agrees to brew an Invisibility Liquor. Kelp gathered from local waters goes into the brew. It lets Maybell slip away unseen to meet Tommy Joe.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is William Pestle?",a="William Pestle is an alchemist who works from the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire. He and his brother Morgan gather and prepare supplies for Stormwind City's apothecary.",al={"william pestle","goldshire alchemist","who is pestle"},it="identity"},{q="Where can William Pestle be found?",a="William Pestle can be found inside the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, in Elwynn Forest.",al={"pestle location","where is william pestle","william pestle goldshire"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does William do with kobold candles?",a="William gathers wax candles carried by kobolds in Elwynn's mines. He melts them and refines the tallow for alchemical mixtures and the apothecary's stock.",al={"why does pestle want candles","kobold candles use"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does William need Crystal Kelp?",a="William uses Crystal Kelp from local Elwynn lakes to make an Invisibility Liquor. It helps Maybell Maclure slip past her family to meet Tommy Joe Stonefield.",al={"collecting kelp why","murloc kelp use"},sp=1,it="motive"},{q="What is William Pestle's connection to Stormwind City?",a="William and his brother Morgan run the apothecary in Stormwind City's Trade District. William gathers ingredients in Goldshire and sends shipments to the city shop.",al={"pestle stormwind","william pestle apothecary shop"},it="ties"},{q="How is William involved with the Stonefields and Maclures?",a="William is an old friend of Mildred Stonefield. He brews a covert drink to help Tommy Joe Stonefield and Maybell Maclure get around their families' bitter feud.",al={"stonefield maclure pestle","william pestle love quest"},sp=1},{q="Whose side is William Pestle on?",a="William is a loyal subject of the Kingdom of Stormwind and a proud member of the Alliance. Operating out of the Lion's Pride Inn, he serves his local community by providing alchemical expertise, brewing remedies, and assisting local townsfolk with their everyday troubles.",al={"william pestle faction","is william pestle alliance","william pestle loyalty"},it="side",add="520b1b0a"},{q="What does William Pestle want?",a="William seeks rare and unconventional reagents for his alchemical concoctions. He often enlists passing adventurers to gather large supplies of kobold candles for their wax and crystal kelp from the local lakes, putting these ingredients to use in brews such as his potent Invisibility Liquor.",al={"what does william pestle need","william pestle goals","william pestle ingredients"},it="wants",add="2d067923"},{q="Why is William Pestle in Goldshire?",a="While William and his brother Morgan manage an apothecary shop in Stormwind City's Trade District, William stays at Goldshire's Lion's Pride Inn to gather rural reagents firsthand and assist long-time friends like Mildred Stonefield in the Elwynn countryside.",al={"why is william pestle here","why is william in goldshire","why is william pestle at lions pride inn"},it="why_here",add="8d6a9bd2"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist in Goldshire, you can see how gathering plants serves William's trade. He turns wild growth and strange aquatic kelp into useful mixtures.",["faction:Alliance"]="William helps supply Stormwind's Trade District with medicines and other goods. He depends on Alliance recruits passing through Goldshire to gather materials from the surrounding forest."},kw={"apothecary","collecting kelp","goldshire","kobold candles","lion's pride inn","maclure","morgan pestle","pestle","stonefield","william pestle"},rel={"npc:morgan-pestle","subzone:lion-s-pride-inn","subzone:goldshire","quest:60","quest:112","quest:114","quest:61","npc:maybell-maclure"},src={"William Pestle"}}
E["npc:zaldimar-wefhellt"] = {t="npc",n="Zaldimar Wefhellt",z="elwynn",s="Upstairs at the Lion's Pride Inn, Zaldimar Wefhellt guides young mages through their first spells. When they outgrow his lessons, he sends them to Stormwind City for further training.",h="Upstairs at the Lion's Pride Inn, Zaldimar Wefhellt guides young mages through their first spells.",sec={{t="The Mage in Goldshire",b="Upstairs at the Lion's Pride Inn, Zaldimar Wefhellt teaches novice mages the first arts of arcane, fire, and frost. Once an apprentice outgrows those lessons, he sends them north to Stormwind's Mage Quarter. There, Jennea Cannon can teach them more.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Zaldimar Wefhellt?",a="At the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, Zaldimar Wefhellt teaches novice mages their first spells. He guides them toward further training in Stormwind City.",al={"who is zaldimar","zaldimar wefhellt role","goldshire mage trainer"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Zaldimar Wefhellt?",a="Zaldimar Wefhellt is on the second floor of the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, in the leftmost room at the top of the stairs.",al={"zaldimar location","where is zaldimar","how to find zaldimar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Where does Zaldimar send novice mages?",a="After a mage learns the basics, Zaldimar sends them to Stormwind's Mage Quarter. There, they can speak with Jennea Cannon in the Wizard's Sanctum.",al={"zaldimar quest","who does zaldimar send you to","speak with jennea quest"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Is Zaldimar related to any other mages?",a="No relatives of Zaldimar are known. He teaches at the Lion's Pride Inn.",al={"wefhellt family","zalna wefhellt","zaldimar relatives"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Zaldimar Wefhellt on?",a="Zaldimar is a loyal member of the Grand Alliance and serves the Kingdom of Stormwind. Stationed right in the heart of Elwynn Forest, he dedicates his arcane craft to mentoring young spellcasters stepping forward to defend the realm and uphold the crown's authority.",al={"zaldimar wefhellt faction","is zaldimar alliance"},it="side",add="10a0eae6"},{q="What does Zaldimar Wefhellt want?",a="Zaldimar wants to guide fledgling mages through the perils of arcane study. Once apprentices grasp the foundational principles of spellcasting in Goldshire, he directs them onward to more advanced instructors, such as Jennea Cannon in the Mage Quarter of Stormwind, to further refine their craft.",al={"zaldimar wefhellt motive","what does zaldimar want"},it="wants",add="063cda12"},{q="Why is Zaldimar Wefhellt in Goldshire?",a="Zaldimar stays on the upper floor of the Lion's Pride Inn to serve as Goldshire's resident mage trainer. Goldshire is an essential stopping ground for adventurers fresh out of Northshire Valley, making it the ideal post for him to intercept budding wizards and tutor them in essential arcane spells.",al={"why is zaldimar here","zaldimar lions pride inn"},it="why_here",add="d06c7379"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a young human mage leaving Northshire Abbey, you first meet Zaldimar in the wider world. He teaches you early spells, then directs you to the Wizard's Sanctum in Stormwind.",["faction:Alliance"]="At the Lion's Pride Inn, Zaldimar teaches Alliance spellcasters in Elwynn Forest. You can learn magic before traveling to Stormwind."},kw={"elwynn forest","goldshire","lion's pride inn","mage trainer","wefhellt","zaldimar"},rel={"subzone:lion-s-pride-inn","subzone:goldshire","quest:1860","zone:elwynn","npc:marshal-dughan"},src={"Zaldimar Wefhellt"}}
E["quest:106"] = {t="quest",n="Young Lovers",z="elwynn",s="Maybell Maclure loves Tommy Joe Stonefield, though their families are bitter rivals. She asks you to carry her letter to him by the river.",h="Maybell Maclure loves Tommy Joe Stonefield, though their families are bitter rivals.",sec={{t="A Forbidden Romance",b="The Stonefields and the Maclures have held their grudge for years in southern Elwynn's farm country. Maybell cannot visit Tommy Joe without stirring her family's anger. So she trusts travelers to carry her letters across the line between the two farms.",sp=0},{t="The Riverbank Rendezvous",b="Tommy Joe stays beyond his relatives' sight on the quiet riverbank just west of Stonefield Farm. A letter from Maybell brings relief and fresh longing. Being apart grows more than he can bear, and the pair begin seeking ways to meet in secret.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Young Lovers?",a="Maybell Maclure gives it at the Maclure Vineyards in Elwynn Forest. She loves Tommy Joe Stonefield, but their families are bitter rivals, so they cannot meet openly.",al={"who gives young lovers","who starts young lovers","young lovers questgiver"}},{q="Where can Tommy Joe Stonefield be found?",a="Tommy Joe Stonefield waits on the riverbank just west of Stonefield Farm, which lies due west of the Maclure Vineyards. There he stays out of his family's sight.",al={"where is tommy joe stonefield","find tommy joe","tommy joe location"}},{q="Why are Maybell and Tommy Joe kept apart?",a="The Stonefields and the Maclures have held a grudge against each other for years. Neither family lets its children mix, so the young couple writes secret letters.",al={"why are families fighting","stonefield maclure feud","why can't maybell and tommy joe see each other"}},{q="What item do you deliver during this quest?",a="You carry Maybell's Love Letter to Tommy Joe Stonefield at the river. It tells him of her affection and devotion, feud or no feud.",al={"what is maybell's letter","what do you deliver in young lovers","love letter elwynn"}},{q="How does Tommy Joe react to the letter?",a="Tommy Joe is thrilled and calls Maybell the light of his dull life. Her words make being apart more than he can bear, so he begins looking for a way for them to meet.",al={"how does tommy joe react","tommy joe response","what happens when you deliver the letter"}},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="The story unfolds in southern Elwynn Forest, between the Maclure Vineyards and the river by Stonefield Farm. This quiet farming corner of the human kingdom is troubled by a petty family quarrel.",al={"where does young lovers take place","young lovers zone","stonefield farm location"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member passing through Elwynn, you may carry messages between the feuding Stonefields and Maclures. Even with the kingdom in danger, small heartaches go on.",["race:Human"]="As a human who knows Elwynn, you have heard of the old grudge between the Stonefields and the Maclures. Maybell and Tommy Joe's romance is a delicate scandal among the neighbors."},kw={"elwynn forest","feud","love letter","maclure vineyards","maybell maclure","stonefield farm","tommy joe stonefield","young lovers"},rel={"npc:tommy-joe-stonefield","subzone:stonefield-farm"},m={faction="Alliance",id=106},src={"In-game quest text: Young Lovers"},fv=true}
E["quest:107"] = {t="quest",n="Note to William",z="elwynn",s="In southern Elwynn, Mildred asks William Pestle to help two young lovers. Her note travels to the apothecary in Goldshire, where she hopes he can help Maybell and Tommy Joe unite despite their families’ feud.",h="In southern Elwynn, Mildred asks William Pestle to help two young lovers.",sec={{t="Star-Crossed in Elwynn",b="Tommy Joe Stonefield and Maybell Maclure hide their love from their feuding families. The Stonefields and Maclures have lived as neighbors in southern Elwynn Forest for years. Yet their bitter rivalry makes even ordinary relations difficult. Gramma Mildred Stonefield pities the young lovers and seeks another way to bring them together.",sp=0},{t="An Appeal to Goldshire",b="Mildred sends a courier north to the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, where William Pestle works as an alchemist and apothecary. She has known him for many years, and believes persuasion alone cannot sway the feuding families. Her message asks for his help. When William receives it, Maybell and Tommy Joe's plight moves him, and he resolves to use his alchemical knowledge on their behalf.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is William Pestle?",a="William Pestle is an alchemist and apothecary at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire. He has known Gramma Mildred Stonefield for many years and makes herbal remedies and specialized draughts.",al={"who is william pestle","william pestle goldshire","alchemist goldshire"}},{q="Who sent the note to William?",a="Gramma Mildred Stonefield wrote the note and sent it to William Pestle. She hopes he can find a way to help Maybell Maclure and Tommy Joe Stonefield.",al={"who sent note","gramma stonefield note","mildred stonefield"}},{q="Why are Maybell and Tommy Joe unable to be together openly?",a="Maybell Maclure and Tommy Joe Stonefield love each other, but their families are locked in a bitter rivalry that has lasted for years. Gramma Stonefield hopes William Pestle can find a potion or plan to help them be together despite that hostility.",al={"why help maybell and tommy joe","young lovers quest elwynn","stonefield maclure feud"}},{q="Where can William Pestle be found?",a="William Pestle stays at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, a town in Elwynn Forest.",al={"where is william pestle","pestle location","lion's pride inn alchemist"}},{q="What is Gramma Stonefield's real name?",a="Her first name is Mildred. William Pestle says he has not seen Mildred in years when he receives her letter.",al={"what is gramma stonefield first name","gramma stonefield name"}},{q="How does William Pestle react to the note?",a="William says he has not seen Mildred in years, then wonders what her note has to say. She hopes his alchemical craft can help the young lovers.",al={"what does william do with note","william pestle reaction"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer in Elwynn Forest, you may help local farming families with personal troubles while the guards focus on military threats.",["race:Human"]="As a human in Elwynn, you see how the Stonefield and Maclure feud divides neighbors. Sympathetic elders rely on discreet couriers."},kw={"elwynn forest","goldshire","gramma stonefield","lion's pride inn","maybell maclure","mildred stonefield","note to william","tommy joe stonefield","william pestle"},rel={"npc:william-pestle","npc:gramma-stonefield","quest:106","subzone:lion-s-pride-inn","subzone:goldshire"},m={faction="Alliance",id=107},src={"In-game quest text: Note to William"},fv=true}
E["quest:11"] = {t="quest",n="Riverpaw Gnoll Bounty",z="elwynn",s="In western Elwynn, Riverpaw Gnoll Bounty calls for help against gnolls pressing the border. Deputy Rainer offers a reward at Westbrook Garrison for painted armbands taken from Riverpaw packs in the woods and by the water.",h="In western Elwynn, Riverpaw Gnoll Bounty calls for help against gnolls pressing the border.",sec={{t="A Threat on the Border",b="Westbrook Garrison guards Elwynn Forest's border with Westfall. Its depleted forces struggle to contain the growing Riverpaw presence. The gnolls camp south of the guard tower and farther east around Stone Cairn Lake. From those camps, they threaten travelers and nearby homesteads.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Order",b="Deputy Rainer cannot spare regular infantry to sweep the woods, so he offers a bounty on the raiders. He requires painted armbands from slain gnolls as proof of each kill. Wandering adventurers and recruits are hired to thin the pack before the Riverpaws overrun the western marches.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can Riverpaw gnolls be found in Elwynn Forest?",a="Riverpaw gnolls gather in two parts of Elwynn. Look in the woods south of Westbrook Garrison near the riverbanks, and farther east around Stone Cairn Lake.",al={"gnoll locations","where are the gnolls","riverpaw locations"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the garrison asking adventurers for help with gnolls?",a="Westbrook Garrison is understaffed and pressed along Elwynn's borders. With too few guards to patrol and sweep the woods, Deputy Rainer asks independent champions to hunt the gnolls.",al={"why deputy rainer needs help","why garrison hiring mercenaries"},it="why_me"},{q="What proof does Deputy Rainer require?",a="Deputy Rainer requires eight Painted Gnoll Armbands as proof that the gnolls have been killed.",al={"bounty proof","what to collect for rainer"},it="item"},{q="Who are the Riverpaw gnolls?",a="The Riverpaws are a vicious tribe of hyena-like humanoids that infest river valleys and borders across human lands. They raid settlements, travelers, and farmlands for food and plunder.",al={"what are riverpaw gnolls","riverpaw tribe lore"},it="target"},{q="Does this quest connect to any other threats in Elwynn?",a="The bounty concludes the short Westbrook Garrison alert chain. Deputy Rainer and the garrison also watch for other lawless threats in the area, including the outlaw Hogger.",al={"quest continuation","what comes after riverpaw bounty"},it="threat"},{q="Who pays the bounty for these gnolls?",a="The Stormwind Army backs and authorizes the bounty. It allows local garrisons to commend and compensate those who help pacify royal territories.",al={"who funds the bounty","bounty reward source"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why does Deputy Rainer want the gnolls culled?",a="Deputy Rainer views the Riverpaw gnolls as brutish interlopers who have no business on Elwynn's borders. With large packs entrenching themselves south of the guard tower and east near Stone Cairn Lake, they directly threaten Westbrook Garrison's perimeter and surrounding settlers. Rainer wants them culled to halt their encroaching infestation before the outpost is completely overrun.",al={"why cull gnolls","deputy rainer motive","why does rainer want riverpaws dead"},it="motive",add="139c22ee"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, you help protect Elwynn's frontiers by hunting Riverpaws and supporting the overextended crown guards.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you build standing with the Stormwind Army by taking border bounties and help secure trade routes through the heart of the kingdom."},kw={"bounty","deputy rainer","elwynn","gnoll","painted gnoll armband","riverpaw","stone cairn lake","westbrook garrison"},rel={"npc:deputy-rainer","subzone:westbrook-garrison","quest:239","subzone:stone-cairn-lake","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-army","topic:gnoll","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Deputy Rainer",faction="Alliance",id=11,ri={"Painted Gnoll Armband"}},src={"Riverpaw Gnoll Bounty"}}
E["quest:111"] = {t="quest",n="Speak with Gramma",z="elwynn",s="Tommy Joe Stonefield asks Gramma Stonefield for a way to reach Maybell Maclure. Their families keep them apart, and he hopes to meet her without drawing their kin into conflict.",h="Tommy Joe Stonefield asks Gramma Stonefield for a way to reach Maybell Maclure.",sec={{t="A Feud and Forbidden Love",b="Tommy Joe and Maybell hide their love from their families. He turns to Gramma Stonefield, hoping she can find them a chance to meet in secret. Their kin must not discover the romance and turn old hostility into violence.",sp=0},{t="Gramma's Cunning",b="Gramma Stonefield knows the families cannot truly unite while their bad blood remains. Still, she will not let that end the young couple's hopes. She begins seeking small chances to bring Tommy Joe and Maybell together.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Tommy Joe want me to speak with his Gramma?",a="Tommy Joe loves Maybell Maclure, but their families' feud keeps them apart. He hopes his grandmother can arrange secret meetings without stirring an uproar.",al={"why gramma","tommy joe gramma","speak with gramma purpose"},it="motive"},{q="Where can Gramma Stonefield be found?",a="Gramma Stonefield stays inside the main Stonefield farmhouse, south of Goldshire and east of the riverbank where Tommy Joe hides.",al={"gramma stonefield location","where is gramma","find gramma stonefield"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the feud between the Stonefields and the Maclures?",a="The neighboring farming families carry a long personal and territorial grudge. They accuse each other of theft and compete over crops, while distrust keeps both households near violence. Their children must keep any contact secret.",al={"stonefield maclure feud","why are they fighting","family feud elwynn"},it="conflict"},{q="Does Gramma Stonefield oppose Tommy Joe's relationship?",a="No. Gramma knows the feud makes a lasting future difficult, but she cares for the young lovers and will devise ways for them to meet.",al={"is gramma against maybell","does gramma support lovers"},it="ties"},{q="What happens after speaking to Gramma?",a="Gramma begins planning to bring Tommy Joe and Maybell together in secret. She sends you to gather what she needs for an invisibility liquor to get past their watchful families.",al={"what next speak with gramma","gramma quest follow up"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who is Maybell Maclure?",a="Maybell Maclure is the daughter of the rival family, living across the road from the Stonefields. She is secretly courting Tommy Joe Stonefield.",al={"who is maybell","maybell maclure"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Tommy Joe need an outsider to speak with his grandmother?",a="Tommy Joe is hiding on the riverbank near the Stonefield Farm to secretly rendezvous with Maybell Maclure. Returning to the family farmhouse himself risks drawing attention to his forbidden romance, especially with tensions running high between the two feuding families. As a passing traveler, you can approach Gramma Stonefield quietly without alerting the rest of the household.",al={"why me tommy joe","why send player to gramma","why can't tommy talk to gramma"},it="why_me",add="ba5df8a9"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human in Elwynn, you see how deeply local grudges run in Stormwind's heartlands, even amid troubles across the realm.",["faction:Alliance"]="While Stormwind faces Defias unrest and beast attacks, you may find yourself mediating quarrels between neighboring farmers."},kw={"elwynn forest","gramma stonefield","maclure vineyards","maybell maclure","speak with gramma","stonefield farm","tommy joe stonefield","young lovers"},rel={"npc:gramma-stonefield","npc:tommy-joe-stonefield","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Tommy Joe Stonefield",["end"]="Gramma Stonefield",faction="Alliance",id=111},src={"Speak with Gramma"}}
E["quest:112"] = {t="quest",n="Collecting Kelp",z="elwynn",s="In Goldshire, Maybell Maclure seeks to visit Tommy Joe Stonefield unseen. William Pestle needs rare crystal kelp to brew her an invisibility liquor.",h="In Goldshire, Maybell Maclure seeks to visit Tommy Joe Stonefield unseen.",sec={{t="A Remedy for Forbidden Love",b="The feud between the Stonefield and Maclure families keeps Maybell Maclure and Tommy Joe Stonefield from meeting openly. Maybell wants to see the one she loves without bringing their kin into an armed clash. So she seeks a way to cross the valley unseen. William Pestle, an herbalist and apothecary at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, plans to brew an invisibility liquor, but its rare ingredients are not in the inn's cupboards.",sp=0},{t="The Scavengers of Crystal Lake",b="William Pestle needs crystal kelp as the catalyst for his brew. Its fronds usually grow far out in saltwater oceans, but tribal murlocs have carried stashes inland to their crude camps along Crystal Lake, just east of Goldshire. Their peculiar instincts draw them to haul the marine plants to the freshwater shore. You need to recover enough fronds from the murlocs before returning to Goldshire with them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does William Pestle need crystal kelp?",a="William Pestle needs crystal kelp to brew an invisibility liquor for Maybell Maclure. The drink is meant to help her leave her family's vineyard unseen and visit Tommy Joe Stonefield.",al={"why crystal kelp","what is kelp for","william pestle ingredients"},it="item"},{q="Why is ocean kelp found near freshwater Crystal Lake?",a="Crystal kelp grows in the ocean, but tribal murlocs around Crystal Lake scavenge the fronds and carry them inland. They hoard the kelp in lakeside camps, the only local source near Goldshire.",al={"why is kelp at crystal lake","kelp in fresh water","murloc kelp lore"},it="place"},{q="Who are Maybell Maclure and Tommy Joe Stonefield?",a="Maybell Maclure and Tommy Joe Stonefield are young lovers from rival farming families in southern Elwynn Forest. Their families despise each other, so the pair rely on secrecy and alchemical tricks to meet.",al={"who is maybell","who is tommy joe","maclure stonefield feud"},it="people"},{q="Where is Crystal Lake located?",a="Crystal Lake lies just east of Goldshire in central Elwynn Forest. Hostile murlocs infest its waters and shores.",al={"where is crystal lake","crystal lake location","find crystal lake"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after collecting the kelp?",a="After you deliver four crystal kelp fronds, William Pestle distills them into an Invisibility Liquor. Then he asks you to bring it to Maybell Maclure so she can slip away unseen.",al={"next quest after kelp","what does pestle make"},it="next_step"},{q="Who is William Pestle?",a="William Pestle is an apothecary and alchemical dabbler at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire. He helps locals with folk remedies, strange potions, and confidential favors.",al={"who is william pestle","pestle goldshire"},it="identity"},{q="Why does William Pestle want to help Maybell and Tommy Joe?",a="William Pestle is Goldshire's local apothecary and alchemist, and he is willing to lend his craft to help the young lovers. Maybell Maclure and Tommy Joe Stonefield are caught on opposite sides of their families' bitter, long-standing feud. A secret potion of invisibility offers Maybell a clever way to slip away from her family's watchful eyes at the Maclure Vineyards without provoking further strife between the clans.",al={"why help maybell","william pestle motive","why does william care"},it="motive",add="ff0f7883"},{q="Why are murlocs gathered at Crystal Lake?",a="Murlocs have crept inland from the coastlines, establishing camps along Elwynn Forest's freshwater bodies like Crystal Lake and Stonecairn Lake. With Stormwind's military stretched thin defending borders elsewhere, these aggressive amphibians have grown bold, encroaching on local settlements and scavenging materials—including ocean kelp they carry with them inland.",al={"why are murlocs at crystal lake","crystal lake murlocs","murlocs in elwynn"},it="target",add="cc419076"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="For you as a gatherer, crystal kelp is an odd find: an ocean herb taken from the pouches of freshwater murlocs, not from soil or seabed.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, clearing the murloc camps around Crystal Lake for Pestle helps quiet the aggressive menace near Goldshire's eastern road."},kw={"collecting kelp","crystal kelp","crystal lake","goldshire","invisibility liquor","maybell maclure","murloc","tommy joe stonefield","william pestle"},rel={"npc:william-pestle","subzone:crystal-lake","quest:114","subzone:goldshire","subzone:maclure-vineyards","topic:murloc","zone:elwynn"},m={start="William Pestle",faction="Alliance",id=112,ri={"Crystal Kelp Frond"}},src={"Collecting Kelp"}}
E["quest:114"] = {t="quest",n="The Escape",z="elwynn",s="Maybell Maclure seeks a way to leave her family and meet Tommy Joe Stonefield. You bring her William Pestle's Invisibility Liquor, brewed with crystal kelp gathered across the region.",h="Maybell Maclure seeks a way to leave her family and meet Tommy Joe Stonefield.",sec={{t="A Concoction for True Love",b="The Maclures and Stonefields have feuded for generations, leaving no room for courtship. Gramma Stonefield asks William Pestle, an alchemist at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, for help. Crystal kelp from nearby lakes gives Pestle what he needs to brew Invisibility Liquor. The brew can hide Maybell's escape from the Maclure homestead.",sp=0},{t="Vanishing into the Woods",b="Maybell Maclure takes the flask and slips into the trees toward Tommy Joe. Guilt at deceiving her kin troubles her, but devotion outweighs her fear of discovery. She drinks the liquor and vanishes before your eyes. Now she has a few moments with Tommy Joe beyond the watchful eyes of their feuding elders.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest The Escape?",a="William Pestle, an apothecary and alchemical assistant at Goldshire's Lion's Pride Inn, gives you Invisibility Liquor after you bring him crystal kelp.",al={"quest giver the escape","who starts the escape","where to pick up the escape"},gp=true},{q="What is the Invisibility Liquor used for?",a="The Invisibility Liquor lets Maybell Maclure turn invisible long enough to leave her family's farm and visit Tommy Joe Stonefield without provoking her relatives.",al={"why invisibility liquor","what does the potion do","invisibility liquor purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Why do Maybell and Tommy Joe have to hide their relationship?",a="The Maclure and Stonefield families are bitter rivals, and their deep hostility forbids an open courtship between their children.",al={"why are they hiding","stonefield maclure feud","why can't maybell and tommy joe be together"},it="conflict"},{q="What happens when you deliver the potion to Maybell?",a="Maybell thanks you, torn between guilt and excitement, then drinks the brew. She vanishes before your eyes and slips away toward Tommy Joe.",al={"what happens at the end","does maybell vanish","the escape quest completion"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What quest leads directly into The Escape?",a="The Escape follows Collecting Kelp. There, you gather crystal kelp from murlocs at Crystal Lake for William Pestle to brew the invisibility potion.",al={"prerequisite for the escape","quest before the escape","what leads to the escape"},gp=true},{q="Does this quest resolve the feud between the families?",a="No. The potion gives the lovers only a brief, secret meeting. The feud between Gramma Stonefield and the Maclures remains bitter and unresolved.",al={"do the families make peace","is the feud over","does the feud end"},sp=1,it="history"},{q="Why does William Pestle help Tommy Joe and Maybell?",a="William Pestle is an apothecary who is willing to lend a sympathetic hand to young love. After Gramma Stonefield sent him a note asking for a way around the bitter Stonefield and Maclure family feud, William agreed to brew a batch of Invisibility Liquor once provided with crystal kelp. He has nothing personal to gain other than helping the two star-crossed lovers meet in secret without triggering another brawl between their warring kin.",al={"why does william help","william pestle motive","why help maybell escape"},it="motive",add="245b9158"},{q="Why does William Pestle send you to deliver the liquor instead of doing it himself?",a="William runs his busy shop out of the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire and cannot easily abandon his trade to run errands across the forest. More importantly, wandering onto the Maclure vineyards carrying suspicious alchemical draughts would immediately draw the suspicion of Maybell's protective relatives. You, as a wandering adventurer who already served as the courier between the lovers and gathered the ingredients, can slip unnoticed onto the farm to hand her the draught.",al={"why does william send you","why do i deliver the invisibility liquor","why cant william deliver the potion"},it="why_me",add="53ceb805"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer starting in Elwynn Forest, helping Tommy Joe and Maybell offers a lighthearted break from fighting Defias bandits and gnolls. Rural grudges persist even near Stormwind.",["race:Human"]="As a human in Elwynn, you know stubborn family grudges run deep. Small acts of secret aid between neighbors can help keep the peace."},kw={"elwynn forest","invisibility liquor","maclure vineyards","maybell maclure","stonefield farm","the escape","tommy joe stonefield","william pestle"},rel={"npc:maybell-maclure","npc:tommy-joe-stonefield","npc:william-pestle","quest:112","zone:elwynn"},m={start="William Pestle",["end"]="Maybell Maclure",faction="Alliance",id=114},src={"The Escape (Alliance)"}}
E["quest:119"] = {t="quest",n="Return to Verner",z="elwynn",s="Smith Argus has finished fifty horseshoes, and you carry them from Goldshire to Verner Osgood in Lakeshire. Redridge needs them for its hard-pressed mounts.",h="Smith Argus has finished fifty horseshoes, and you carry them from Goldshire to Verner Osgood in Lakeshire.",sec={{t="A Courier Across the Border",b="You carry the crate east across the border into Redridge. There, supply shortages and gnoll attacks threaten the town. The fifty iron shoes keep horses and draft animals working on rugged mountain roads, which Redridge needs to face those dangers.",sp=0},{t="The Note on the Crate",b="Verner Osgood is relieved when the horseshoes arrive. Then he finds the bill Smith Argus attached to the crate. Verner is annoyed that the Goldshire smith expects payment. With dangers pressing around Redridge, there is little time to argue over the charge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do I take the Crate of Horseshoes?",a="Take the crate to Verner Osgood in Lakeshire, in the Redridge Mountains just east of the bridge and lakeside docks.",al={"where is verner","turn in location","who gets horseshoes"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Who sent this delivery back to Redridge?",a="Smith Argus, the blacksmith outside the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, sends the crate after finishing the horseshoes.",al={"who gave the quest","smith argus","quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Verner upset when he receives the crate?",a="Smith Argus attached a bill demanding payment for all fifty horseshoes, and Verner is irritated. He had apparently hoped for a free favor or easier terms.",al={"why is verner mad","argus note","verner reaction"},it="motive"},{q="What quests open up after completing this delivery?",a="After this delivery, Verner offers work against local threats: hunt the Redridge gnolls in 'A Baying of Gnolls' and fetch 'Underbelly Scales'.",al={"next quest","followup quests","what unlocks"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Lakeshire need supplies imported from Goldshire?",a="Gnolls and Blackrock orcs besiege Lakeshire, stretching local craftsmen thin. The town often needs everyday goods like bulk iron horseshoes from quieter places such as Goldshire.",al={"why elwynn shoes","why import horseshoes","redridge supplies"},it="purpose"},{q="Does Smith Argus accompany you back to Redridge?",a="No. Smith Argus stays at his forge in Goldshire while you carry the crate to Redridge.",al={"does argus come with","escort smith argus"},gp=true},{q="Why does Smith Argus want this crate delivered to Verner?",a="Smith Argus is fulfilling Verner Osgood's urgent request for fifty horseshoes, but not out of sheer goodwill. He has boxed them up and attached a pointed bill demanding payment for his labor and materials. Handing the delivery over to you ensures Redridge gets its supplies while making sure Verner knows the ironwork in Goldshire does not come for free.",al={"why does argus send horseshoes","smith argus motive","argus horseshoes verner why"},it="motive",add="a0846e84"},{q="Why does Smith Argus ask you to carry the horseshoes instead of delivering them himself?",a="Argus is Goldshire's resident blacksmith, tied to his anvil and forge keeping travelers and local guards outfitted. Hauling a heavy crate of fifty iron horseshoes across the border through the Redridge passes takes time away from his work and exposes a lone artisan to gnolls and brigands along the road. You are an able adventurer already headed east.",al={"why doesn't argus deliver the shoes","why me return to verner","why send player to lakeshire"},it="why_me",add="f67540ab"}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you know frontier mounts need a steady supply of horseshoes when local forges are overwhelmed by war.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help keep outlying settlements like Lakeshire connected to the kingdom's heart through supply lines between Elwynn Forest and Redridge."},kw={"crate of horseshoes","elwynn forest","goldshire","lakeshire","redridge","smith argus","the price of shoes","verner osgood"},rel={"quest:118","npc:verner-osgood","npc:smith-argus","quest:124","quest:122","quest:126","zone:elwynn","topic:gnoll"},m={start="Smith Argus",["end"]="Verner Osgood",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=119},src={"Return to Verner"}}
E["quest:123"] = {t="quest",n="The Collector",z="elwynn",s="In Elwynn Forest, gold shipments leave the abandoned mines under cover of gnoll raids. An intercepted dispatch names their overseer as 'The Collector' and points to an organized operation near Stormwind's garrison.",h="In Elwynn Forest, gold shipments leave the abandoned mines under cover of gnoll raids.",sec={{t="A Paper Trail in the Paws of Gnolls",b="Riverpaw gnolls in western Elwynn Forest carry a parchment called the Gold Pickup Schedule. It sets dates and times for gold taken from local mines. The intercepted note directs each shipment to an overseer known only as 'The Collector.'",sp=0},{t="Unsettling News for Goldshire",b="At the Lion's Pride Inn, Marshal Dughan learns that gold is still being mined and moved. Official mines across Elwynn have been closed for months because of gnoll attacks, kobold infestations, and roaming bandits. Gnolls with shipping schedules point to an organized criminal network stealing the kingdom's wealth.",sp=0},{t="Eyes on the Brackwell Patch",b="The schedule places the suspected Collector near the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch in eastern Elwynn Forest. Marshal Dughan has heard whispers of the name, but has no clear proof of who leads the ring or where the gold goes. The dispatch gives the garrison its first solid lead in the search for whoever directs the shipments.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Gold Pickup Schedule?",a="The Gold Pickup Schedule is an intercepted note carried by gnolls in Elwynn Forest. It lists dates and times for mined gold to be handed over to a figure called 'The Collector.'",al={"pickup schedule","collector note","elwynn gold schedule"},it="item"},{q="Who is 'The Collector'?",a="'The Collector' is a criminal figure believed to be near the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch in eastern Elwynn Forest, coordinating an illicit gold trade.",al={"collector identity","who is the collector","brackwell collector"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Marshal Dughan shocked by the schedule?",a="Marshal Dughan is shocked because gold is still being mined and shipped despite the official mines being closed for months. Gnoll attacks, kobold infestations, and roaming bandits forced the closures, so the schedule reveals a hidden operation stealing from the crown.",al={"why is dughan surprised","dughan reaction","elwynn mines closed"},it="motive"},{q="Why do gnolls have this note?",a="The Riverpaw gnolls of western Elwynn appear to carry the schedule as couriers, guards, or collaborators in the gold smuggling, bearing orders for the pickups.",al={"gnolls gold","why gnolls drop schedule","gnoll involvement"},it="ties"},{q="Where does this investigation lead next?",a="Giving the schedule to Marshal Dughan leads to Manhunt, which sends you to find and eliminate the Collector near the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch.",al={"collector follow up","manhunt quest","after the collector"},it="next_step"},{q="Where is the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch located?",a="The Brackwell Pumpkin Patch lies in eastern Elwynn Forest, north of the river and east of the Maclure and Stonefield vineyards.",al={"brackwell location","where is brackwell","pumpkin patch elwynn"},it="place",gp=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Every ounce of gold smuggled from Elwynn denies the Crown tax revenue and raw materials while the kingdom struggles to protect its borders.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can read the intercepted schedule and trace contraband through the criminal networks in Elwynn's wilderness.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you know Elwynn's shuttered mines still hold copper and precious metals. Someone is working those veins unlawfully while honest miners stay home in fear."},kw={"brackwell pumpkin patch","elwynn forest","gold pickup schedule","goldshire","manhunt","marshal dughan","mines","the collector"},rel={"quest:147","npc:marshal-dughan","subzone:brackwell-pumpkin-patch","subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn","topic:gnoll"},m={start="Gold Pickup Schedule#Classic",["end"]="Marshal Dughan",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=123},src={"The Collector (Classic)"}}
E["quest:147"] = {t="quest",n="Manhunt",z="elwynn",s="In Elwynn Forest, Marshal Dughan sends you to find the Collector, a Defias bagman. He works from the overrun Brackwell Pumpkin Patch and sends stolen gold from the forest's mines to the Brotherhood.",h="In Elwynn Forest, Marshal Dughan sends you to find the Collector, a Defias bagman.",sec={{t="Justice in the Pumpkin Patch",b="Marshal Dughan sends you to Brackwell Pumpkin Patch after Elwynn's gnolls are found carrying a schedule for gold pickups. Defias bandits and gnolls have taken over the once quiet homestead. The Collector hides among its overgrown vines, skimming ore from the kingdom's mines and arranging shipments for the growing rebellion.",sp=0},{t="An Artisan's Seal",b="After you slay the Collector, you recover his ring and deliver it to Marshal Dughan. The marshal is bewildered: its band bears the mark of Stormwind's old Stonemasons Guild, not a common criminal crest. The ring suggests the highwaymen choking Elwynn Forest are more than opportunists. Some were craftsmen who turned bitter and became outlaws after Stormwind was rebuilt.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can I find the Collector?",a="The Collector hides at Brackwell Pumpkin Patch in southeastern Elwynn Forest, just east of the Maclure Vineyards and north of the river boundary.",al={"collector location","where is collector","collector spot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the Collector stealing gold from Elwynn's mines?",a="The Collector gathers smuggled ore and extortion payments from the kobold-infested Fargodeep and Jasperlode mines to fund the Defias Brotherhood's covert operations across the kingdom.",al={"why steal gold","defias mines","what is collector doing"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the significance of the Collector's ring?",a="The ring is a membership ring of the old Stonemasons Guild, whose craftsmen rebuilt Stormwind City after the First War. Marshal Dughan cannot explain why a lowly thief working with the Defias carries an artisan guild ring, and hopes the question will one day be answered.",al={"collectors ring lore","stonemason ring","what does the ring mean"},sp=1,it="item"},{q="Does Marshal Dughan figure out who is behind the Brotherhood?",a="Not immediately. Marshal Dughan recognizes the artisan insignia on the ring, but cannot explain why a common thief carries an artisan guild signet. The wider conspiracy remains an open question in Goldshire.",al={"does dughan know","dughan reaction","marshal dughan Stonemasons"},sp=1},{q="Who sends you on this manhunt?",a="Marshal Dughan, the garrison commander at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, offers you this work after you recover the Defias pickup schedule.",al={"who gives manhunt","quest giver manhunt","marshal dughan quest"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to the Brackwell family?",a="The Brackwell Pumpkin Patch lies in ruin, abandoned by its owners and occupied by Defias rogues, bandits, and encroaching Riverpaw gnolls that prowl the southeastern woodlands.",al={"brackwell lore","who owns pumpkin patch","brackwell farm"},it="history"},{q="Why does Marshal Dughan want the Collector stopped?",a="Gold plundered from Elwynn's mines is property of the kingdom of Stormwind. By systematically siphoning that wealth, the Collector is actively robbing the realm and funding illicit operations. Marshal Dughan cannot permit thieves to freely loot Crown resources, especially when the stolen coin suggests an organized conspiracy behind the local banditry.",al={"why kill the collector","marshal dughan motive manhunt","why does dughan care about the collector"},it="motive",add="1901992d"},{q="Who is the Collector and why is he at the pumpkin patch?",a="The Collector is an operative working with the Defias thieves to gather and transport illicit gold extracted from Elwynn's mines. He is using the abandoned Brackwell Pumpkin Patch as a secluded hideout, waiting for shipments according to the pickup schedule before smuggling the kingdom's wealth out of the forest.",al={"who is the collector","why is the collector at brackwell pumpkin patch","target of manhunt"},it="target",add="535c4316"},{q="Why does Marshal Dughan send an adventurer instead of the Stormwind guards?",a="The Stormwind City Guard and Goldshire's garrison are stretched perilously thin across Elwynn Forest, bogged down by gnoll incursions, kobold infestations in the mines, and rampant Defias bandits. Dughan simply lacks the spare soldiers to dispatch a manhunt to a remote pumpkin patch, forcing him to rely on capable, trustworthy adventurers.",al={"why does dughan need me","why send adventurers manhunt","why don't guards kill the collector"},it="why_me",add="e23a6feb"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can see how the Collector's covert work reflects the growing network of highwaymen and cutpurses taking root throughout Elwynn Forest.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help protect Stormwind's local resources. Stopping the Collector cuts off an illicit flow of kingdom gold meant to fund rebellion near the capital.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you may feel the weight of recovering the Stonemason's ring. It recalls the bitter labor disputes that divided the kingdom after Stormwind was rebuilt."},kw={"brackwell pumpkin patch","collector","defias","goldshire","manhunt","marshal dughan","ring","stonemasons guild"},rel={"quest:123","npc:marshal-dughan","subzone:brackwell-pumpkin-patch","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Marshal Dughan",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=147},src={"Manhunt (Classic)"}}
E["quest:15"] = {t="quest",n="Investigate Echo Ridge",z="elwynn",s="Kobolds gather in force at Echo Ridge Mine, so Marshal McBride sends you north. The mine supplies ore and raw materials to Northshire Abbey and the Stormwind guard stationed there.",h="Kobolds gather in force at Echo Ridge Mine, so Marshal McBride sends you north.",sec={{t="A Deepening Infestation",b="Scattered vermin have troubled the valley's forested edge near Northshire. Now the scouts report a more organized gathering. At the entrance, you face kobold workers and see how deeply they have settled into the mine.",sp=0},{t="Threat to the Abbey's Wealth",b="The kobolds have seized the tunnels and stopped the digging. Their presence strains the Northshire brotherhood's defenses. McBride asks you to cull ten workers, but the infestation reaches farther into the shafts than a surface patrol can reach.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me on this mission?",a="Marshal McBride, commander of the Stormwind guards at Northshire Abbey, sends you north after scouts report kobolds gathering there.",al={"quest giver","who gives quest","marshal mcbride"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the Echo Ridge Mine located?",a="Echo Ridge Mine lies in the far north of Northshire Valley, in the foothills above the abbey and its vineyards.",al={"echo ridge location","where is the mine","find echo ridge"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are kobolds dangerous to Northshire?",a="Kobolds breed rapidly and swarm through underground tunnels in huge packs. Their hold on Echo Ridge Mine stops vital mining and threatens to overwhelm Northshire's undermanned valley.",al={"why kill kobolds","what makes kobolds a threat","kobold danger"},it="threat"},{q="What happens after I defeat the workers outside?",a="When you return, Marshal McBride's worst suspicions are confirmed: the mine is thoroughly infested. He enlists your aid for a deeper push into the shafts in Skirmish at Echo Ridge.",al={"what next","follow up quest","next quest"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why doesn't the Stormwind army clear the mine themselves?",a="With King Varian Wrynn missing and resources stretched thin across Elwynn and neighboring frontiers, Northshire's garrison is too small to spare full patrols for pest control. The guards rely on capable new recruits.",al={"where are stormwind guards","why use recruits","stormwind garrison"},it="why_me"},{q="What kind of kobolds are found around the mine entrance?",a="Kobold workers labor around the mine entrance and upper passages. They dig tunnels and gather candle wax for their underground colony.",al={"kobold types","what enemies to kill","kobold worker"},it="target"},{q="Why does Marshal McBride want the Echo Ridge Mine investigated?",a="Marshal McBride's scouts discovered that the kobold infestation is far larger than Northshire's garrison initially realized. The creatures have moved beyond minor camps and set up near the Echo Ridge Mine, threatening a vital local resource. McBride needs you to cull their front ranks and assess whether an even larger force is entrenching itself deeper within the mine before the valley's defenses are completely overrun.",al={"why clear echo ridge","mcbride motive","why investigate echo ridge mine"},it="motive",add="ffd728b0"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Copper from Echo Ridge Mine is essential to Northshire's smiths. Clearing its underground tunnels matters to miners' livelihoods.",["faction:Alliance"]="Kobolds have reached close to Stormwind's spiritual heart in Northshire. Their presence shows the kingdom's vulnerability while its regular forces are stretched thin.",["race:Human"]="As a young human beginning service in Northshire Valley, defending Echo Ridge from underground pests gives you an early chance to prove your worth to the kingdom."},kw={"echo ridge","elwynn","kobold","kobold worker","marshal mcbride","mine","northshire","northshire valley"},rel={"subzone:echo-ridge-mine","npc:marshal-mcbride","quest:21","topic:kobold","zone:elwynn"},m={level="3",faction="Alliance",id=15},src={"Investigate Echo Ridge"}}
E["quest:1598"] = {t="quest",n="The Stolen Tome",z="elwynn",s="At Northshire Abbey, Drusilla La Salle seeks a stolen tome from the Defias camp in the vineyards. Powers of the Void could aid her teaching, and bringing it back will prove your skill.",h="At Northshire Abbey, Drusilla La Salle seeks a stolen tome from the Defias camp in the vineyards.",sec={{t="A Forbidden Opportunity",b="Warlocks in Stormwind's lands keep their craft and their research from prying eyes. Northshire Abbey guards forbidden grimoires in its archives. Drusilla cannot risk suspicion from the clerics and paladins by entering the protected wing herself. She covets Powers of the Void and needs another to retrieve it.",sp=0},{t="Defias Opportunism",b="An abbey novice joined the Defias Brotherhood and stole several valuable texts as he left. He fled to the Northshire Vineyards and took refuge near the Defias campsite. The thieves keep their prize in a field tent, unaware of the danger in the book's dark arts.",sp=0},{t="The First Binding",b="Recovering Powers of the Void tests your nerve and opens the way to darker knowledge. Returning the tome satisfies Drusilla's ambition and proves you are ready to practice the dark arts. She rewards you with the rites to summon and bind an imp, the first demon an apprentice learns to command.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Powers of the Void?",a="Powers of the Void is a forbidden grimoire about dark magic and control of the planes. The guarded wing of Northshire Abbey's library holds knowledge Drusilla La Salle covets for her study and teachings.",al={"powers of the void book","what is the book","what did the novice steal"},it="item"},{q="Why didn't Drusilla La Salle steal the book herself?",a="Drusilla La Salle must protect her standing at Northshire Abbey. Entering the library's secured archives would alert the clerics and paladins. When a novice stole the tome and joined the Defias, she had a chance to acquire it through an apprentice.",al={"why drusilla didn't steal it","why send me"},it="why_me"},{q="Where is the stolen tome hidden?",a="The Defias hid the tome in a tent at their campsite in the Northshire Vineyards, east of the abbey.",al={"where is the book","tome location","stolen tome tent"},gp=true},{q="Why did a Northshire novice join the Defias Brotherhood?",a="Discontent and strife across the kingdom drive laborers, farmers, and church students to join the Defias Brotherhood. The novice abandoned his vows, stole several important books from the library, then fled to the vineyard bandits.",al={"why novice joined defias","abbey defias traitor","who stole the book"},it="history"},{q="What reward does a warlock get for retrieving the tome?",a="Returning the tome proves you have the nerve and resilience to practice the dark arts. Drusilla rewards you with the teachings to summon an imp, your first demon.",al={"what do you learn","warlock quest reward","why do this quest"},gp=true},{q="Do the Defias know how to use the book?",a="The bandits treat the stolen books as valuable plunder from the abbey. Though the Defias employ renegade spellcasters, the novice and his comrades tucked the tome into a tent crate instead of mastering its dark secrets.",al={"can defias use the tome","what defias do with book"}},{q="Why does Drusilla La Salle want the Powers of the Void?",a="Drusilla has long coveted the forbidden knowledge locked inside the Powers of the Void, but it was kept in a secured, protected wing of Northshire Abbey's library where she couldn't reach it without drawing suspicion. Having a stray novice steal it gave her the perfect opportunity to finally claim its dark secrets for herself while simultaneously testing whether you have the fortitude to study the warlock arts.",al={"why does drusilla want the book","drusilla la salle motive","why steal the tome"},it="motive",add="1f0061ae"},{q="Who are you sent against to recover the tome?",a="You are sent against the Defias Brotherhood bandits encamped in the Northshire Vineyards. A wayward Abbey novice stole several valuable volumes from the protected library before fleeing to join their rebellion, hiding the tome among their tents.",al={"who took the book","defias in vineyards","who stole the powers of the void"},it="target",add="a46315b9"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you prove you can cross dangerous ground without flinching. Securing the tome earns you the rites to call your first imp.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you see the Defias Brotherhood's reach in Northshire, where even abbey students steal sacred texts and join the insurrection.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you tread softly around Northshire's paladins and clerics, using outlaws' mistakes to claim restricted occult knowledge."},kw={"defias brotherhood","drusilla la salle","northshire abbey","novice thief","powers of the void","stolen book","vineyards","warlock imp"},rel={"npc:drusilla-la-salle","topic:defias-brotherhood","quest:65","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Drusilla La Salle",level="4",faction="Alliance",cl={"WARLOCK"},id=1598,ri={"Powers of the Void"}},src={"The Stolen Tome"}}
E["quest:16"] = {t="quest",n="Give Gerard a Drink",z="elwynn",s="At the Maclure Vineyards, Gerard Tiller works long days in the fields and needs fresh spring water. Passing travelers bring water and trade it for apples.",h="At the Maclure Vineyards, Gerard Tiller works long days in the fields and needs fresh spring water.",sec={{t="Thirsty Work in the Vineyard Fields",b="Elwynn's farms supply grain, fruit, and vegetables to Stormwind's townsfolk and garrisons. The work is hot beneath the open sky. At the Maclure Vineyards, Gerard Tiller tends the crops, keeps pests away, and manages the harvest. With little time to reach the town wells, he depends on passing recruits to bring clean spring water so he can keep working.",sp=0},{t="The Economy of Barter",b="Gerard trades provisions for water instead of coin. Travelers with extra flasks of Refreshing Spring Water can exchange them for fresh apples from his orchard. The kingdom stretches its resources to keep order and feed its army. So barter between smallholders and recruits remains a practical way to get by in rural Elwynn.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gerard Tiller?",a="Gerard Tiller farms at the Maclure Vineyards in southern Elwynn Forest. He tends the fields and orchards that supply local residents.",al={"gerard tiller","who is tiller","gerard"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Gerard need water?",a="Working in the fields under the sun all day is exhausting. Gerard relies on passing travelers for fresh spring water so he can stay hydrated without leaving his chores.",al={"why spring water","gerard thirsty","why need drink"},it="motive"},{q="Where can Refreshing Spring Water be found?",a="Food and drink vendors and innkeepers throughout Elwynn Forest commonly sell Refreshing Spring Water. Brother Danil sells it inside Northshire Abbey.",al={"where get water","spring water source","how to get water"},gp=true},{q="Is this trade repeatable?",a="Yes. Gerard keeps working the fields and trades fresh orchard apples for more bottles of water you can spare.",al={"repeatable quest","can i do this again","turn in more water"},gp=true},{q="What does Gerard offer in return for the drink?",a="Gerard trades a Shiny Red Apple for fresh water.",al={"gerard reward","what do i get","trade reward"},gp=true},{q="Where is Gerard located?",a="Gerard is outside the barn at the Maclure Vineyards in southern Elwynn Forest.",al={"gerard tiller location","where is gerard","where is the farm"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Refreshing Spring Water used for?",a="Tending the fields at the Maclure Vineyards is exhausting labor, and Gerard Tiller simply needs a reliable supply of fresh, clean water to quench his thirst while working under the sun. Rather than leaving his crops unattended to fetch drink himself, he is glad to barter with passing travelers who carry some to spare.",al={"refreshing spring water use","why spring water","gerard spring water"},it="item",add="d51fec31"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Supporting Elwynn's farmers at places like the Maclure Vineyards helps feed the forest's homesteads and garrisons while the kingdom defends itself.",["race:Human"]="As a human starting in Northshire, helping neighbors like Gerard Tiller shows the communal spirit that holds Elwynn together."},kw={"apples","barter","elwynn forest","gerard tiller","maclure vineyards","refreshing spring water"},rel={"npc:gerard-tiller","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Gerard Tiller",["end"]="Gerard Tiller",faction="Alliance",id=16,ri={"Refreshing Spring Water"}},src={"Give Gerard a Drink"}}
E["quest:1667"] = {t="quest",n="Dead-tooth Jack",z="elwynn",s="In eastern Elwynn Forest, retired Marshal Haggard needs your help: Dead-tooth Jack tricked him into giving up his badge. Jack wore a Stormwind tabard and pretended to be Marshal Dughan. Haggard fears the Defias Brotherhood will use the badge to impersonate Stormwind officials.",h="In eastern Elwynn Forest, retired Marshal Haggard needs your help: Dead-tooth Jack tricked him into giving up...",sec={{t="A Con in the Dark",b="At night, a figure wearing a Stormwind tabard came to Haggard's isolated cottage on Elwynn's eastern ridges. The stranger claimed to have official business and asked for Haggard's old marshal's badge. Haggard believed he was handing it to a fellow officer, so he gave it over. The figure laughed and vanished into the woods. He was a Defias rogue called Dead-tooth Jack.",sp=0},{t="The Threat of False Authority",b="Marshal Haggard has retired, but his badge still carries Stormwind's legal authority. Defias bandits are creeping across Elwynn, Westfall, and Redridge. With the badge, they could pass guard checkpoints, redirect patrols, or take command of supplies. Jack retreated to a camp to the south and locked the badge in a strongbox. Haggard needs it back before the Defias cause serious harm.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Dead-tooth Jack?",a="Dead-tooth Jack is a Defias operative in eastern Elwynn Forest. At night, he posed as Marshal Dughan and tricked retired Marshal Haggard into handing over his official Stormwind badge.",al={"dead tooth jack","who is dead tooth","dead tooth jack lore"},it="target"},{q="Why does Marshal Haggard need his badge back?",a="Marshal Haggard needs his badge back because it is an authentic sign of Stormwind authority. He fears the Defias will use it to impersonate officials, bypass military patrols, and cause havoc across the realm.",al={"why recover badge","haggards badge","why does the badge matter"},it="motive"},{q="How did Jack manage to fool Marshal Haggard?",a="Jack came to Haggard's cottage at night wearing a Stormwind tabard. In the poor light, Haggard mistook him for Marshal Dughan of Goldshire and gave him the badge, believing he was helping a fellow officer.",al={"how did he fool haggard","haggard tricked","why did haggard give the badge"},it="history"},{q="Where does Jack keep the stolen badge?",a="Jack keeps the stolen badge locked in a strongbox at his bandit camp south of Marshal Haggard's house. He carries the key on his person.",al={"badge location","where is the badge","dead tooth camp"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who sent you to Marshal Haggard in the first place?",a="Harry Burlguard, a veteran warrior who frequents the Pig and Whistle Tavern in Stormwind, sends adventurers to Marshal Haggard. He knows the retired marshal may trade spare weaponry for help.",al={"who sends you here","burlguard","questgiver start"},it="ties"},{q="What happens once the badge is returned?",a="Marshal Haggard is greatly relieved that the Defias cannot use his identity or rank against the kingdom. He salutes you in thanks and offers your choice of well-maintained military weapons from his years in service.",al={"quest turn in","haggard reaction","badge returned"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is Marshal Haggard's Badge for?",a="Marshal Haggard's badge is a retired mark of high authority in the Stormwind Army. In honest hands, it is a treasured heirloom from Haggard's years of service. In the grip of the Defias Brotherhood, however, an official marshal's insignia allows thieves and bandits to impersonate Stormwind officers, bypass checkpoints, and orchestrate dangerous deceptions across the kingdom.",al={"haggards badge purpose","what does the badge do","why is the badge dangerous"},it="item",add="5b8b35d8"},{q="Why does Marshal Haggard need you to recover his badge?",a="Haggard is long retired and lives out in an isolated cottage, embarrassed that a rogue tricked him in the dark. Asking the town garrison or Marshal Dughan for help would mean admitting he handed his official badge straight to a Defias thief, and Stormwind's guards are already stretched thin defending the township. You arrived looking for his spare weapons, giving him the perfect capable, discreet hand to settle the score.",al={"why does haggard need me","why doesn't haggard get it himself","why not use guards"},it="why_me",add="55355d07"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human of Stormwind, you can see how vulnerable the kingdom's rural borders are to Defias infiltrators. They wear the crown's own colors to deceive retired veterans.",["class:Warrior"]="Marshal Haggard was once a veteran frontline fighter. As a warrior, you can earn his thanks and choose from the spare arms he kept from his years of service.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can see that Dead-tooth Jack's caper depends on disguise, deception, and impudence as much as crude highway robbery."},kw={"badge","dead-tooth jack","defias","elwynn forest","guard burlguard","impersonation","marshal dughan","marshal haggard","strongbox"},rel={"quest:1666","npc:marshal-dughan","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Marshal Haggard",level="10",faction="Alliance",cl={"WARRIOR"},id=1667,ri={"Marshal Haggard's Badge"}},src={"Dead-tooth Jack"}}
E["quest:1685"] = {t="quest",n="Gakin's Summons",z="elwynn",s="In Stormwind, Gakin's Summons draws promising warlocks beneath the Slaughtered Lamb. Remen Marcot brings Gakin the Darkbinder's message, sending fledgling practitioners to the crypts under the tavern in the Mage Quarter for further occult training.",h="In Stormwind, Gakin's Summons draws promising warlocks beneath the Slaughtered Lamb.",sec={{t="A Discrete Message",b="Demonology is forbidden in Stormwind's settled districts, yet its practitioners work near the city guard. When a warlock shows skill with introductory imps, word reaches senior warlocks in secret. Remen Marcot carries their message quietly and urges new practitioners to keep the meeting place private as they make their way beneath the Mage Quarter.",sp=0},{t="The Crypts of the Slaughtered Lamb",b="Cellars and hidden catacombs lie behind the Slaughtered Lamb's modest front. Gakin the Darkbinder teaches Stormwind's warlocks there, beyond the reach of Kirin Tor mages and the Cathedral's inquisitors. Under his guidance, warlocks learn to command a voidwalker. The rite demands dangerous stolen reagents and perilous summoning circles.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Gakin the Darkbinder summon warlocks?",a="Gakin summons budding warlocks once they have gained enough experience. He sees the untrained as a danger, liable to lose their heads, and teaches them the complex ritual for binding a voidwalker to their service.",al={"why gakin summons","what is gakin summons for","voidwalker quest start"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is Gakin the Darkbinder located?",a="Gakin is hidden in deep crypts beneath the Slaughtered Lamb, a tavern in Stormwind's Mage Quarter.",al={"where is gakin","gakin location","slaughtered lamb basement"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Remen Marcot?",a="Remen Marcot is an associate of Stormwind's warlock coven. He stays in the cellar of the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, seeking promising candidates and quietly guiding them to Gakin's hidden enclave.",al={"remen marcot","who starts gakin summons"},it="identity"},{q="Why must the location be kept secret?",a="Fel magic and demon summoning are forbidden in the Kingdom of Stormwind. The Silver Hand, the Cathedral of Light, or the city guards could discover the coven, bringing imprisonment or execution.",al={"why secret","warlock secrecy stormwind"},it="why_here"},{q="What comes after answering Gakin's summons?",a="After you report to Gakin, he sends you to the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch in Elwynn Forest. There, you are to recover a bloodstone choker from Surena Caledon, essential to the voidwalker binding ritual.",al={"next quest after gakins summons","what happens next"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Can non-warlocks receive this summons?",a="No. Only warlocks who have mastered their basic imp companion receive the summons and advanced occult instruction.",al={"can mages get this","who can do gakins summons"},gp=true},{q="Why does Remen Marcot want you to see Gakin?",a="Remen Marcot is acting purely on orders from Master Gakin the Darkbinder. He spent all day scouring the city to track you down, growing thoroughly frustrated in the process. His only stake is fulfilling his task so he can stop chasing after you and return to his own business, warning you to report quickly before your master loses patience.",al={"why does remen send you to gakin","remen marcot motive","why is remen looking for you"},it="motive",add="0d517c2f"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you are moving beyond parlor tricks and minor imps. The trials ahead prepare you to enslave a voidwalker to shield you in battle.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know Stormwind tolerates a hidden cabal of shadow-weavers. Their fel expertise gives the Alliance an edge against its enemies."},kw={"demonology","gakin the darkbinder","mage quarter","remen marcot","slaughtered lamb","stormwind","voidwalker","warlock"},rel={"npc:gakin-the-darkbinder","subzone:slaughtered-lamb","quest:1688","quest:1471","subzone:mage-quarter","quest:1715","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Remen Marcot",["end"]="Gakin the Darkbinder",level="10",faction="Alliance",cl={"WARLOCK"},id=1685,xg=1715},src={"Gakin's Summons (Voidwalker)"}}
E["quest:176"] = {t="quest",n="Wanted: \"Hogger\"",z="elwynn",s="In southwestern Elwynn, Hogger has turned back every local attempt to bring him down. The Alliance bounty posted outside Goldshire seeks the head of this massive, savage gnoll chieftain.",h="In southwestern Elwynn, Hogger has turned back every local attempt to bring him down.",sec={{t="A Menace in the Woods",b="Banditry and kobold infestations trouble Elwynn Forest, while gnolls in the south grow bolder and more organized under Hogger's brutal leadership. Taller than typical Riverpaw gnolls, he has made camp near the Forest's Edge. From there, he ambushes travelers and overpowers the local militia patrols sent to subdue him.",sp=0},{t="Goldshire's Desperation",b="The Stormwind Army is stretched thin and cannot spare regular forces to police the capital's outskirts. So Marshal Dughan has taken the unusual step of posting an open bounty on Hogger. Hunting him means venturing into deeply hostile gnoll territory. His ferocity has earned him a fearsome reputation among novice adventurers in Elwynn.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Hogger?",a="Hogger is an unusually large and savage gnoll leader who terrorizes southwestern Elwynn Forest. He commands local packs around the Forest's Edge and has violently defeated every previous attempt by Stormwind guards to capture or kill him.",al={"who is hogger","hogger lore","what is hogger"},it="target"},{q="Where can Hogger be found?",a="Hogger wanders among the gnoll encampments in southwestern Elwynn Forest, near the southern borders known as Forest's Edge. The area lies just north of the river boundary with Westfall and Duskwood.",al={"hogger location","where is hogger","find hogger"},gp=true},{q="Why is there a bounty on Hogger?",a="Hogger has overpowered local patrols and poses a lethal danger to travelers, prompting the Stormwind Army to place a bounty on him. With official troops stretched thin across the kingdom, Marshal Dughan has turned to independent adventurers and bounty hunters to eliminate the threat.",al={"why kill hogger","wanted poster hogger","who put bounty on hogger"},it="motive"},{q="Who collects the proof of Hogger's death?",a="Bring proof of Hogger's demise, his Huge Gnoll Claw, directly to Marshal Dughan. He commands the local garrison stationed in Goldshire.",al={"turn in hogger","where to turn in hogger","who wants hogger claw"}},{q="Why is Hogger so dangerous compared to other gnolls?",a="Hogger is far larger and more brutal than the common gnolls prowling Elwynn. He hits significantly harder and can withstand far more punishment, often overwhelming anyone who faces him alone and underestimates him.",al={"is hogger strong","why is hogger elite"},it="danger"},{q="Why can't the Stormwind guards handle Hogger themselves?",a="The kingdom's military resources are severely depleted and tied down defending major borders or dealing with the missing King Varian Wrynn. Marshal Dughan's small detachment in Goldshire lacks the manpower to hunt down such a resilient monster safely.",al={"why doesn't dughan kill hogger","where is stormwind army"},it="why_me"},{q="What is the Huge Gnoll Claw for?",a="The Huge Gnoll Claw serves as undeniable proof of Hogger's death. Because the brute has overpowered every attempt at his capture, Marshal Dughan and the Stormwind Army require unmistakable physical evidence before handing over the posted bounty reward.",al={"huge gnoll claw","why do i need hoggers claw","hogger claw use"},it="item",add="fccb34f1"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance heroes, taking down Hogger is a rite of passage as they test their mettle defending Stormwind's heartland.",["race:Human"]="For humans of Elwynn, slaying Hogger secures homesteads and road trade that gnoll ambushes have terrorized for months."},kw={"bounty","dughan","elwynn","forest's edge","gnoll","goldshire","hogger","wanted"},rel={"npc:marshal-dughan","subzone:goldshire","subzone:forest-s-edge","topic:gnoll","topic:stormwind-army","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Wanted Poster",["end"]="Marshal Dughan",level="11",faction="Alliance",id=176,ri={"Huge Gnoll Claw"}},src={"Wanted: \"Hogger\""}}
E["quest:1787"] = {t="quest",n="The Tome of Divinity",z="elwynn",s="You are proving your devotion to the Light through a trial for Alliance paladins. After helping an injured scout in Elwynn Forest, you face Defias Rogue Wizards and seek papers that threaten the realm.",h="You are proving your devotion to the Light through a trial for Alliance paladins.",sec={{t="A Paladin's Trial",b="As a paladin in training, you are being tested in Elwynn Forest. Henze was injured while watching illicit activity on an island. Help him learn how far the Defias have spread there.",sp=0},{t="Infiltrators in Elwynn",b="Henze found Defias Rogue Wizards studying secret papers on the island, but his injuries leave him unable to fight. You are sent to defeat the rogue spellcasters and recover their script. Then bring the intelligence safely to Gazin Tenorm in Stormwind.",sp=1},{t="Defending the Kingdom",b="The Defias Script confirms the brotherhood threatens nearby lands, including Heroes' Vigil. Bring the stolen intelligence to the Cathedral of Light. Your return proves your devotion to the Light and that Henze survived.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is involved in this quest?",a="You meet Henze Faulk, who lies injured on an island in Elwynn Forest. Afterward, report to Gazin Tenorm in the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind.",al={"who gives this quest","who gives tome of divinity","where do i get tome of divinity"}},{q="Who is Henze?",a="Henze is an ally in the paladin trials who was injured while watching Defias activity. Unable to fight, he sends you to secure proof of the brotherhood's infiltration.",al={"who is henze","henze faulk lore","who is the injured guy"}},{q="Who is Gazin Tenorm?",a="Gazin Tenorm is Henze's friend and a friend of Duthorian Rall. He can be found near the altar in Stormwind's Cathedral of Light. He barely escaped the Defias at Heroes' Vigil and wants to know Henze is safe.",al={"who is gazin tenorm","where is gazin tenorm","gazin stormwind"}},{q="Why are Defias Rogue Wizards operating on the island?",a="The Defias Brotherhood has positions throughout Elwynn Forest. Its rogue wizards study plans and coordinate operations, and their documents show what they intend in the region.",al={"why are defias in elwynn","defias rogue wizards","defias script"}},{q="What is Heroes' Vigil?",a="Heroes' Vigil is a place in Elwynn Forest threatened by Defias operations. Gazin Tenorm hopes that stopping nearby rogue wizards and taking their papers will protect it from further harm.",al={"what is heroes vigil","heroes vigil elwynn","is heroes vigil safe"}},{q="What is the Defias Script?",a="The Defias Script is written orders or correspondence carried by Defias Rogue Wizards. It proves their infiltration and details their immediate schemes in Elwynn Forest.",al={"what is defias script","what are the papers","defias papers elwynn"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you face a trial of devotion and courage. It tests your resolve to protect the innocent and uphold the Light against threats such as the Defias Brotherhood.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help uncover Defias movements and documents in Elwynn Forest. This intelligence goes to Stormwind's defenders."},kw={"defias rogue wizards","defias script","elwynn forest","gazin tenorm","henze faulk","heroes' vigil","paladin quest","tome of divinity"},rel={"npc:gazin-tenorm","subzone:heroes-vigil","topic:light","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={faction="Alliance",cl={"PALADIN"},ra={"Human"},id=1787},src={"In-game quest text: The Tome of Divinity"},fv=true}
E["quest:18"] = {t="quest",n="Brotherhood of Thieves",z="elwynn",s="Across Northshire's eastern river, the Defias Brotherhood has begun to trouble the valley. Deputy Willem sends recruits to face the brigands, whose red burlap bandanas give Stormwind its first clear sign of their organized presence.",h="Across Northshire's eastern river, the Defias Brotherhood has begun to trouble the valley.",sec={{t="Bandits in the Valley",b="Northshire Valley has long been a safe haven in Elwynn Forest. Stormwind guards it, and recruits and Clerics of the Holy Light train there. Lately, though, the valley's watch has grown thin. Vagrants and thieves cross the eastern river and hide near the woods. They make small camps close to the abbey.\n\nDeputy Willem keeps order, but the guards cannot watch every corner of the valley. He needs volunteers to help hold the line.",sp=0},{t="The Crimson Sigil",b="The outlaws move together and wear matching red burlap bandanas. They call themselves the Defias Brotherhood, and the cloth marks their allegiance. Deputy Willem sends recruits to drive back the brigands and recover their masks. He hopes to slow their advance and learn how far the Defias have reached into the kingdom's heartland.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who are the Defias Brotherhood?",a="The Defias Brotherhood is an organized band of brigands and outlaws active across Elwynn Forest and Westfall. At first, Northshire's authorities see bold thieves, but the bandits wear matching red burlap masks and follow coordinated leadership.",al={"who are the defias","what is defias brotherhood","defias lore"},it="people"},{q="Why is Deputy Willem asking recruits for help instead of using the Stormwind Army?",a="The Stormwind Army and city guards are stretched thin across the kingdom. Unrest rises in neighboring regions, and Stormwind City's leaders are under strain. Local deputies turn to eager volunteers and novice recruits to push back the bandits.",al={"why willem needs help","where are stormwind guards","why no army"},it="why_me"},{q="Where are these thieves coming from?",a="The thieves gather across the river east of the abbey. They skulk around the edges of local farmsteads and campsites near the vineyard.",al={"where are the bandits","defias location northshire"},it="origin"},{q="Why do the thieves wear red burlap bandanas?",a="The red burlap bandana marks a thief's allegiance to the Defias Brotherhood and hides their identity. It also signals that allegiance to fellow outlaws across the human territories.",al={"why red bandanas","meaning of red masks","red burlap"},it="item"},{q="What happens after completing this quest?",a="Deputy Willem and the locals soon see that the bandit threat reaches farther into Northshire. Recruits then help Milly Osworth with her ruined harvest and track down Garrick Padfoot, a specific ringleader.",al={"what comes next","after brotherhood of thieves"},it="next_step"},{q="Does Deputy Willem know who leads the Defias?",a="Willem does not know the full reach of the organization. He knows the brigands call themselves the Defias Brotherhood, and suspects their presence near the abbey bodes ill for Stormwind.",al={"does willem know vancleef","who leads defias northshire"},it="leader"},{q="Why does Deputy Willem want you to fight the thieves?",a="Deputy Willem is tasked with protecting Northshire Abbey and the surrounding valley. A brazen criminal gang calling itself the Defias Brotherhood has crept into the eastern woods across the river, threatening the security of the abbey and local workers. Willem wants them suppressed immediately before they gain a stronger foothold or launch a direct assault on the valley.",al={"why does willem want this","willem motive","why stop the defias here"},it="motive",add="e491bbee"},{q="Who are the thieves across the river?",a="You are dispatched against the Defias Thugs, outlaws belonging to the Defias Brotherhood who have set up camp in the woods across the stream east of Northshire Abbey. They have gathered near the vineyards and surrounding fields, scouting the valley and harassing the locals while establishing an armed presence right under Stormwind's nose.",al={"who are the thieves","who am i fighting","defias in northshire"},it="target",add="4db9a478"}},ang={["race:Human"]="For humans beginning their training in Northshire, the Defias show how the Kingdom of Stormwind's safety is slipping from within.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stormwind's authorities rely on newly arrived Alliance recruits to keep peace in Northshire while the kingdom's formal military is stretched thin.",["class:Rogue"]="For novice rogues, the Defias offer a glimpse of organized criminal networks working in the shadows of the human heartland."},kw={"bandanas","brotherhood of thieves","defias","deputy willem","elwynn","northshire","stormwind army"},rel={"npc:willem","topic:defias-brotherhood","subzone:northshire-abbey","quest:783","quest:65","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-army","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Deputy Willem",level="4",faction="Alliance",id=18,ri={"Red Burlap Bandana"}},src={"Brotherhood of Thieves"}}
E["quest:1860"] = {t="quest",n="Speak with Jennea",z="elwynn",s="In Stormwind, novice mages from Goldshire come to Jennea Cannon after advancing beyond basic training in Elwynn Forest. Zaldimar Wefhellt sends them to her.",h="In Stormwind, novice mages from Goldshire come to Jennea Cannon after advancing beyond basic training in...",sec={{t="A Call to the Wizard's Sanctum",b="In the Mage Quarter, the Wizard's Sanctum gathers the kingdom's senior mages for study and instruction in the arcane arts. They coordinate magical matters across the realm, and your training now has a place within that wider work.",sp=0},{t="Matters of Kingdom Security",b="Jennea Cannon oversees local assignments, including reports on the security of Elwynn Forest and Stormwind, as well as your studies. Cautious about sharing grand secrets with a newly arrived apprentice, she receives your report as the beginning of your service to the wizarding order.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me on this quest?",a="Zaldimar Wefhellt, the mage trainer at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, sends you once your arcane skills have advanced enough.",al={"quest giver","who gives quest","zaldimar"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Jennea Cannon?",a="Jennea Cannon is in the Wizard's Sanctum, in the center of Stormwind City's Mage Quarter.",al={"jennea cannon location","where is jennea","find jennea"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Wizard's Sanctum?",a="The Wizard's Sanctum is a prominent magical spire in Stormwind's Mage Quarter. The kingdom's mages and arcane scholars use it as an academy, library, and base of operations.",al={"what is wizards sanctum","mage tower stormwind"},it="place"},{q="Why does Zaldimar send me to Jennea instead of handling it himself?",a="Zaldimar teaches young mages the fundamentals in Goldshire. Higher-ranking scholars such as Jennea Cannon oversee larger regional threats and specialized work affecting the realm from the capital.",al={"why go to stormwind","why jennea"},it="why_me"},{q="What happens after reporting to Jennea Cannon?",a="Jennea sends you to investigate mysterious magical anomalies around Mirror Lake in Elwynn Forest.",al={"what next","follow up quest","next step"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Is this quest available to any class?",a="No. Only mages receive this rite of passage from village training into Stormwind's arcane society.",al={"can non mages do this","mage only","class requirement"},gp=true},{q="Why does Zaldimar Wefhellt want you to speak with Jennea?",a="Zaldimar Wefhellt acts out of concern for the safety of both Stormwind City and Elwynn Forest. An urgent matter has arisen that requires the attention of capable mages, but rather than managing it directly, he directs promising apprentices to Jennea Cannon in the Wizard's Sanctum, who oversees the details of this delicate mission.",al={"zaldimar motive","why see jennea","why send to jennea"},it="motive",add="8f9ffa7f"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you leave rural spellcasting in Goldshire for formal work with the high mages at Stormwind's Wizard's Sanctum.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you rely on arcane vigilance from the capital to help protect Elwynn Forest and Stormwind."},kw={"elwynn forest","goldshire","jennea cannon","mage quarter","speak with jennea","stormwind","wizard's sanctum","zaldimar wefhellt"},rel={"npc:jennea-cannon","npc:zaldimar-wefhellt","quest:1861","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Zaldimar Wefhellt",["end"]="Jennea Cannon",level="10",faction="Alliance",cl={"MAGE"},id=1860,xg=1860},src={"Speak with Jennea"}}
E["quest:21"] = {t="quest",n="Skirmish at Echo Ridge",z="elwynn",s="At Echo Ridge, Marshal McBride sends you into a mine overrun by kobolds. Left alone, the garrison fears, they will tighten their hold.",h="At Echo Ridge, Marshal McBride sends you into a mine overrun by kobolds.",sec={{t="Purging the Mine",b="Kobolds dig deep in Echo Ridge Mine, hoarding what they steal and growing in number. Thin their ranks now, before they spread through Northshire Valley, its farms, and its spiritual retreat.",sp=0},{t="A Thin Defense",b="McBride has few soldiers to spare. The garrison guards the southern borders, while unrest is rumored across Elwynn. Prove reliable at Echo Ridge, and you earn the army’s respect and readiness for harder work elsewhere in the kingdom.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are kobolds infesting the Echo Ridge Mine?",a="Kobolds are drawn to mineral-rich tunnels and abandoned quarries. With Stormwind’s forces stretched thin, they enter unguarded places like Echo Ridge to dig burrows, hoard gold, and claim shelter underground.",al={"why kobolds in mine","echo ridge kobolds","what are kobolds doing"},it="target"},{q="Who orders the skirmish?",a="Marshal McBride orders the skirmish. He commands Stormwind Army forces at Northshire Abbey and oversees the valley’s defense with limited manpower.",al={"who gives skirmish quest","marshal mcbride orders"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is the strategic importance of Echo Ridge Mine?",a="Echo Ridge Mine holds stone and ore needed to maintain Northshire and help rebuild Stormwind. Kobolds on Northshire’s northern border threaten the abbey and nearby vineyards.",al={"why echo ridge matters","echo ridge mine importance"},it="place"},{q="Where does this mission lead next?",a="After the first kobold laborers are cleared from the mine, Marshal McBride sends you toward Goldshire to aid the region’s defense.",al={"what quest after skirmish","next step after echo ridge"},it="next_step"},{q="Why doesn't the Stormwind Army clear the mine themselves?",a="Stormwind’s forces are short on soldiers as they defend distant borders and answer bandit attacks across Elwynn. McBride relies on new recruits for local threats while seasoned guards hold the defensive lines.",al={"why recruits","where are stormwind soldiers"},it="why_me"},{q="Are kobolds intelligent enough to be an organized military threat?",a="Kobold laborers are cowardly and simple-minded alone, but territorial and aggressive in numbers. Left unchecked, they dig winding tunnels, set cavern traps, and draw larger, better-armed vermin.",al={"are kobolds smart","kobold danger level"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Marshal McBride want the kobolds in Echo Ridge Mine culled?",a="Marshal McBride knows that the longer the kobolds remain unchallenged in Echo Ridge Mine, the deeper their foothold in Northshire becomes. Leaving them unmolested invites them to entrench themselves further and threaten the valley, making their eventual removal far bloodier and risking the security of Northshire Abbey itself.",al={"why kill kobolds in echo ridge","mcbride motive echo ridge","why clear echo ridge mine"},it="motive",add="a391cdc3"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, clearing Echo Ridge is your first true test of arms in defense of your ancestral kingdom. You prove your mettle to Stormwind’s officers.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help reclaim mines holding stone and ore for rebuilding and fortifying human settlements after the war.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you face swarming kobold workers at close quarters among the first entrenched foes you meet.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you help make it possible to dig and smelt valuable mineral veins safely across Northshire Valley."},kw={"echo ridge","echo ridge mine","elwynn","kobold","laborer","marshal mcbride","mcbride","northshire","skirmish","stormwind army"},rel={"quest:15","subzone:echo-ridge-mine","npc:marshal-mcbride","subzone:northshire-abbey","topic:kobold","topic:stormwind-army","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={level="5",faction="Alliance",id=21},src={"Skirmish at Echo Ridge"}}
E["quest:2158"] = {t="quest",n="Rest and Relaxation",z="elwynn",s="From Northshire, new Alliance adventurers follow the road south to Goldshire for rest and welcome. At the Lion's Pride Inn, Innkeeper Farley offers food, drink, and a place by the hearth.",h="From Northshire, new Alliance adventurers follow the road south to Goldshire for rest and welcome.",sec={{t="A Haven on the Road",b="Weary travelers leave Northshire and follow the road south to Goldshire. It leads straight to the Lion's Pride Inn, where Innkeeper Farley welcomes those setting out into Elwynn Forest. For new adventurers, the inn is the first major outpost beyond the Abbey, with shelter and hot meals.",sp=0},{t="Farley's Hearth and Hospitality",b="Innkeeper Farley welcomes those who are tired and cold. Mention your referral, and you can settle by the open fire for a warm meal, sturdy ale, and a rest before continuing through Elwynn.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find the Lion's Pride Inn?",a="The Lion's Pride Inn is in Goldshire, south along the main road from Northshire Valley. Follow the road south to the tavern at the heart of town.",al={"where is lions pride inn","how to get to lion's pride inn","find lions pride"}},{q="Who is Innkeeper Farley?",a="Innkeeper Farley runs the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire. A close friend of contacts in Northshire, he welcomes weary adventurers with food, drink, and a warm hearth.",al={"who is innkeeper farley","farley lion's pride"}},{q="What is the purpose of Rest and Relaxation?",a="You travel from Northshire to Goldshire, where Innkeeper Farley offers food, drink, and lodging at the Lion's Pride Inn.",al={"what is the purpose of this quest","why go to lion's pride inn"}},{q="Does Innkeeper Farley really offer discounted food and drink?",a="Mention your referral to Innkeeper Farley, and you can ask about discounted food and drink while you recover from your travels.",al={"discount at lions pride","do i get cheaper food farley"}},{q="Why is rest important for traveling adventurers?",a="Travel across Elwynn is hard and dangerous. At an inn, you can shelter from the wilderness, warm yourself by the fire, recover, and replenish supplies before setting out again.",al={"why do adventurers need rest","rest and relaxation lore"}},{q="What is the motto of the Lion's Pride Inn?",a="Innkeeper Farley says the Lion's Pride Inn's motto is 'Rest and relaxation for the tired and cold.' Weary guests can find comfort by his hearth.",al={"what is lions pride inn motto","lions pride slogan"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The Lion's Pride Inn is a haven and gathering place for Alliance travelers in Elwynn Forest.",["race:Human"]="As a human recruit leaving Northshire Valley, you follow the southern road to Goldshire. There, Innkeeper Farley offers familiar hospitality near Stormwind."},kw={"alliance tavern","elwynn forest","goldshire","innkeeper farley","lion's pride inn","northshire","rest and relaxation"},rel={"npc:innkeeper-farley","subzone:lion-s-pride-inn"},m={faction="Alliance",id=2158},src={"In-game quest text: Rest and Relaxation"},fv=true}
E["quest:2205"] = {t="quest",n="Seek out SI: 7",z="elwynn",s="From Goldshire, Keryn Sylvius sends new rogues with a sealed package to Stormwind City. The delivery brings them before Master Mathias Shaw, who leads the crown's covert intelligence network.",h="From Goldshire, Keryn Sylvius sends new rogues with a sealed package to Stormwind City.",sec={{t="A Courier's Test",b="Rogue trainer Keryn Sylvius doubts that fresh initiates look like covert agents. She gives them a sealed delivery for the capital, testing their reliability as couriers. In doing so, she quietly judges whether they might serve the realm as scouts.",sp=0},{t="Behind Closed Doors in Old Town",b="SI: 7, or Stormwind Intelligence, Section 7, works from southeastern Old Town in Stormwind City. In this worn district, Master Mathias Shaw oversees the kingdom's covert operations. He receives the package with dry skepticism, then judges whether you have the grit for real espionage.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is SI:7?",a="SI: 7 means Stormwind Intelligence, Section 7. From its Old Town headquarters, Master Mathias Shaw leads its secret intelligence and covert operations for the Kingdom of Stormwind.",al={"what does si 7 mean","what is si7","si:7 lore"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Keryn Sylvius?",a="Keryn Sylvius trains rogues at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire. She works with SI: 7, evaluates local recruits and sends promising scouts to Master Mathias Shaw in Stormwind City.",al={"keryn sylvius","goldshire rogue trainer"},it="people"},{q="Where is Mathias Shaw located in Stormwind?",a="Master Mathias Shaw is on the upper floor of SI: 7 headquarters, in southeastern Old Town in Stormwind City, past the city's rogue trainers.",al={"where is shaw","find mathias shaw","mathias shaw location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after delivering the package to Shaw?",a="After you report to Mathias Shaw, he tests your rogue skills. He sends you to Jerod's Landing to steal a shipping schedule from a Defias dockmaster.",al={"next quest after seek out si 7","what does shaw want"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Keryn mock the player before handing over the delivery?",a="SI: 7 operatives prize competence and sharp instincts. Keryn Sylvius treats new recruits harshly to judge their temperament and see whether they have the resolve to approach Master Shaw.",al={"why does keryn insult me","cheese delivery insult"}},{q="Why does Keryn Sylvius want this package delivered to Mathias Shaw?",a="Keryn made a formal commitment to deliver the parcel to Master Mathias Shaw as part of an official assignment. While she clearly disdains running standard courier errands herself, sending you serves a dual purpose: it honors her obligation to the agency while putting your fledgling rogue talents to the test before her superiors in Stormwind.",al={"why deliver to mathias","keryn sylvius motive","why send package to si7"},it="motive",add="5aa3ad9f"},{q="Why does Keryn send an unproven rogue instead of delivering the package herself?",a="Keryn is stationed out in Goldshire scouting and mentoring new talent, leaving her little interest in walking minor deliveries back to Old Town. Handing the task off to an eager novice like you spares her the legwork while serving as a practical audition to see if you are sharp enough to locate the headquarters of Stormwind's secret service.",al={"why does keryn send me","why me seek out si7","why not deliver it herself"},it="why_me",add="6bd14f9c"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you enter Stormwind's foremost espionage agency, moving from back-alley tricks to royal reconnaissance.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you rely on SI: 7 to guard the realm against threats within and beyond its borders while King Varian Wrynn remains missing."},kw={"goldshire","keryn sylvius","mathias shaw","old town","rogue","seek out si: 7","si:7","stormwind"},rel={"quest:2206","npc:mathias-shaw","npc:keryn-sylvius","subzone:old-town","zone:stormwind","subzone:goldshire","quest:2300"},m={start="Keryn Sylvius",["end"]="Mathias Shaw",level="10",faction="Alliance",cl={"ROGUE"},id=2205},src={"Seek out SI: 7"}}
E["quest:2300"] = {t="quest",n="SI:7",z="elwynn",s="From Goldshire, promising young rogues are sent to report to Renzik \"The Shiv\" in Stormwind. There, you enter Master Mathias Shaw's service, where covert work awaits.",h="From Goldshire, promising young rogues are sent to report to Renzik \"The Shiv\" in Stormwind.",sec={{t="A Summons to Old Town",b="At the Lion's Pride Inn, Keryn Sylvius watches Goldshire's local recruits. You prove cunning and capable against the growing Defias threat, and Sylvius passes along a message from headquarters. Report to Renzik \"The Shiv\" without delay. You leave Elwynn's fields for Stormwind's covert ranks.",sp=0},{t="Stormwind's Hidden Eyes",b="Behind an unassuming barracks in Old Town, Stormwind's hidden agency keeps its headquarters. Master Mathias Shaw commands its work across the kingdom and beyond. The agency handles covert operations, reconnaissance, and assassination.\n\nRenzik \"The Shiv\" is Shaw's sharp-tongued second-in-command. He assesses promising agents, then sends them into dangerous work beyond the reach of the kingdom's formal military.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me to report to SI:7?",a="Keryn Sylvius, the rogue trainer at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, sends you to report to SI:7. After you prove your skill in the field, Sylvius gives you orders to report to Stormwind headquarters.",al={"who gives quest","quest giver","keryn sylvius"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Renzik \"The Shiv\"?",a="Renzik \"The Shiv\" is a goblin operative and SI:7's second-in-command under Master Mathias Shaw. He evaluates field agents and coordinates covert intelligence assignments from the headquarters in Old Town.",al={"renzik the shiv","who is renzik","renzik"},it="identity"},{q="What is SI:7?",a="SI:7, or Stormwind Intelligence, handles covert espionage, reconnaissance, and assassination for the Kingdom of Stormwind. Led by Mathias Shaw, its operatives gather intelligence on threats the kingdom's guards and soldiers cannot address.",al={"what is si7","what does si7 do","stormwind intelligence"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is the SI:7 headquarters located?",a="SI:7's headquarters is in eastern Old Town in Stormwind City. The agency works from a fortified guildhall and training barracks set away from the main streets.",al={"where is si7","si7 location","where is renzik"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after reporting to Renzik?",a="After you report to Renzik, he tests your readiness. Then he sends you beyond the city walls to meet an operative stationed in Redridge.",al={"next quest","what comes after","redridge rendezvous"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Keryn Sylvius call me 'fish'?",a="“Fish” is slang for an untested novice or new recruit. Agency operatives use colorful, abrasive nicknames to keep rookies grounded until they prove themselves on real assignments.",al={"why called fish","fish meaning"}},{q="Why does Keryn Sylvius send me to SI:7?",a="Keryn Sylvius is acting on orders from high above. Renzik \"The Shiv\" specifically sent word that he was looking for you, and Keryn knows better than to ignore a summons from Mathias Shaw's second-in-command. In the covert hierarchy of Stormwind's intelligence service, when Renzik calls for an operative, intermediaries like Keryn promptly pass along the command without keeping headquarters waiting.",al={"why does keryn send me","keryn sylvius motive","why report to si7"},it="motive",add="d2c94cb8"},{q="Why does SI:7 need me instead of their own agents?",a="Renzik \"The Shiv\" specifically asked for you by name. As an up-and-coming rogue working within the Alliance's network, you represent fresh talent outside the immediate gaze of local adversaries. Master Shaw and Renzik frequently rely on capable, newly proven field agents to take on discreet assignments across the kingdom where seasoned, well-known faces might draw unwanted attention.",al={"why me si7","why does renzik want me","why call on me"},it="why_me",add="fe886311"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, this summons takes you from local work into service as an operative for Stormwind's official intelligence branch.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can look to SI:7 for dangerous espionage beyond the reach of regular marshals and infantry."},kw={"keryn sylvius","mathias shaw","old town","renzik the shiv","rogue","sentinel hill","si:7","stormwind"},rel={"npc:renzik-the-shiv","npc:keryn-sylvius","quest:2281","quest:2282","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Keryn Sylvius",["end"]="Renzik \"The Shiv\"",level="16",faction="Alliance",cl={"ROGUE"},id=2300,xg=2260},src={"SI:7 (quest)"}}
E["quest:239"] = {t="quest",n="Westbrook Garrison Needs Help!",z="elwynn",s="At Westbrook Garrison, Deputy Rainer and his guards face growing pressure with few soldiers to spare. Marshal Dughan sends available adventurers west to the outpost on Elwynn Forest's border with Westfall. Stormwind's army is stretched thin across the kingdom, leaving the garrison to contend with Riverpaw gnolls and wandering thieves without regular reinforcements.",h="At Westbrook Garrison, Deputy Rainer and his guards face growing pressure with few soldiers to spare.",sec={{t="A Frontier Stretched Thin",b="Westbrook Garrison guards Elwynn Forest's western edge, where settled woodland meets Westfall's troubled plains. Gnoll warbands and bandits grow bolder along the waterways and western roads, so the small garrison has asked for more men. Marshal Dughan and Goldshire's administration have no Stormwind soldiers to spare. Local commanders must hire traveling mercenaries and wandering adventurers.",sp=0},{t="The Threat Across the Brook",b="Deputy Rainer and his men face Riverpaw gnolls who harass travelers and nearby homesteads. The pack ranges through the borderlands between Elwynn and Westfall. Stormwind is distracted by political and military troubles, and the gnolls press deeper into inhabited lands. Westbrook Garrison guards against their unchecked advance into the heart of the forest.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why can't Stormwind send regular soldiers to Westbrook Garrison?",a="Stormwind's standing military is stretched thin across several frontiers. With King Varian Wrynn missing and the realm beset by internal strife, high command has refused or been unable to send regular soldiers to rural outposts. Town marshals like Dughan must rely on freelance volunteers.",al={"why no stormwind troops","why send adventurers","where is stormwind army"},it="why_me"},{q="Where is Westbrook Garrison located?",a="Westbrook Garrison sits on Elwynn Forest's western edge. Follow the main road west from Goldshire, past the small brook. The fortified tower stands on your right, just before the Westfall border.",al={"westbrook garrison location","how to get to westbrook","where is deputy rainer"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What threats are troubling the garrison?",a="Deputy Rainer faces repeated raids by Riverpaw gnolls, along with growing thief and bandit activity in the border country between Westfall and Elwynn Forest.",al={"what attacks westbrook","why does rainer need help","who is attacking westbrook garrison"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Deputy Rainer?",a="Deputy Rainer is the Stormwind officer in command at Westbrook Garrison. He must hold the western border and rely on civilian volunteers and mercenaries because official military reinforcements are scarce.",al={"rainer lore","deputy rainer","who is rainer"},it="identity"},{q="What happens after reporting to Deputy Rainer?",a="Deputy Rainer enlists your help against the local Riverpaw gnolls. He places a bounty on their collars to thin their numbers and protect the border road.",al={"what comes next","westbrook quest chain","rainer quest"},it="next_step"},{q="Why are the gnolls pushing into Elwynn Forest?",a="The Riverpaw gnolls have camps along the rivers that separate Elwynn and Westfall. With fewer soldiers along the border, they have grown bold enough to raid trade routes and press toward Elwynn's interior farms.",al={"riverpaw gnolls elwynn","why are gnolls here","gnoll problem"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Marshal Dughan want you to go to Westbrook Garrison?",a="Marshal Dughan is responsible for maintaining order and security across Elwynn Forest from Goldshire, but his resources are stretched to the breaking point. Westbrook Garrison guards the kingdom's western boundary, and Deputy Rainer has sent urgent word of rising banditry and encroaching gnolls. Without regular troops to dispatch as reinforcements, Dughan must rely on independent adventurers to answer the outpost's plea for help before the western border collapses entirely.",al={"why send to westbrook garrison","marshal dughan motive","why westbrook garrison needs help"},it="motive",add="76645dec"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human of Stormwind, you see an unsettling sign of the kingdom's neglect. The crown's defenses have worn thin since the King's disappearance.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance volunteer, you take up the work of regular soldiers and help keep core territories from falling into complete chaos."},kw={"deputy rainer","elwynn forest","gnolls","goldshire","marshal dughan","riverpaw","westbrook garrison"},rel={"subzone:westbrook-garrison","npc:deputy-rainer","npc:marshal-dughan","quest:11","quest:76","zone:elwynn","topic:gnoll","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Marshal Dughan",["end"]="Deputy Rainer",faction="Alliance",id=239},src={"Westbrook Garrison Needs Help!"}}
E["quest:2998"] = {t="quest",n="Tome of Divinity",z="elwynn",s="A summons now calls promising paladins from Elwynn to Stormwind. Brother Wilhelm sends for them, and the Tome of Divinity begins the sacred trials that teach mastery of resurrection through the Holy Light.",h="A summons now calls promising paladins from Elwynn to Stormwind.",sec={{t="A Summons to the Capital",b="In Elwynn Forest, novice paladins spend their early days helping locals and testing their strength against wolves, Defias bandits, and kobolds. When an initiate shows discipline in battle and devotion to the Holy Light, mentors such as Brother Wilhelm send a personal summons. The paladin leaders mark promising students and direct them to leave the local chapels behind. Their report is due at the kingdom's spiritual heart.",sp=0},{t="The Cathedral of Light",b="In Cathedral Square, Stormwind's Cathedral of Light is the kingdom's foremost sanctuary for its priesthood and the Knights of the Silver Hand. Duthorian Rall lives there and oversees those sworn to the Order. Beneath its vaulted ceilings, high-ranking paladins set the formal trials of the Tome of Divinity before each initiate. The trials test compassion, fortitude, and willingness to sacrifice.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me to Stormwind for this quest?",a="Brother Wilhelm, the paladin trainer near the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, sends you to Stormwind after you have shown promise and strength in the field.",al={"quest giver","who gives quest","brother wilhelm"},gp=true},{q="Where can I find Duthorian Rall?",a="Duthorian Rall resides inside the Cathedral of Light in Cathedral Square, in northwestern Stormwind City. He spends most days training paladins beneath its grand halls.",al={"duthorian rall location","where is duthorian rall","paladin master location"},gp=true},{q="Why is this summons so important for paladins?",a="Reporting to Duthorian Rall marks the passage from basic martial training into deep communion with the Holy Light. The Tome of Divinity's trials begin there and ultimately grant the sacred power to call fallen allies back from death through the Light.",al={"why do this quest","quest importance","paladin trial"},it="purpose"},{q="Do non-human paladins receive this exact quest?",a="Brother Wilhelm's summons from Elwynn Forest is meant for human paladins. Dwarven paladins receive a parallel calling from their trainers in Dun Morogh to visit Ironforge.",al={"dwarf paladin","can dwarves do this","is this quest human only"},gp=true},{q="What happens after reporting to Duthorian Rall?",a="When you greet Duthorian Rall, he welcomes you to Stormwind and presents the Tome of Divinity's trials. They challenge your compassion and your dedication to defending the weak.",al={"next quest","what happens next","tome of divinity next step"},it="next_step"},{q="Who is Duthorian Rall?",a="Duthorian Rall is among the most influential paladins in Stormwind and the Knights of the Silver Hand. He instructs new generations of holy warriors in the capital.",al={"who is duthorian","duthorian rall lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Brother Wilhelm send you to Duthorian Rall?",a="Brother Wilhelm holds great respect for Duthorian Rall, one of the Order's most influential paladins. Having overheard Duthorian speak highly of your service and mention that you are ready to be put to the test, Wilhelm simply wants to ensure you seize the opportunity. Guiding promising initiates toward advanced instruction is his duty and pride as a mentor in Goldshire.",al={"why does wilhelm send me","brother wilhelm motive","why talk to duthorian rall"},it="motive",rc="Human",add="69ec335a"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, your mentors recognize your deeds and send you before the Silver Hand's high commanders. This marks a rite of passage for paladins.",["race:Human"]="As a human, your journey from rural Elwynn Forest to the grand Cathedral of Light binds you to the kingdom's deepest spiritual and martial institutions.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stormwind's recruitment and testing of holy warriors helps the Alliance keep dedicated frontline healers and combatants through troubled times."},kw={"brother wilhelm","cathedral of light","duthorian rall","goldshire","paladin","redemption","stormwind","tome of divinity"},rel={"npc:duthorian-rall","npc:brother-wilhelm","subzone:cathedral-of-light","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:light"},m={start="Brother Wilhelm",["end"]="Duthorian Rall",level="12",faction="Alliance",cl={"PALADIN"},ra={"Human"},id=2998,xg=2998},src={"Tome of Divinity (Brother Wilhelm)"}}
E["quest:3100"] = {t="quest",n="Simple Letter",z="elwynn",s="At Northshire Abbey, new warriors are sent to Llane Beshere for training. Their letter calls them to aid the valley's troubled residents.",h="At Northshire Abbey, new warriors are sent to Llane Beshere for training.",sec={{t="A Call to Arms",b="New warriors arriving in Northshire Valley are directed by letter to Llane Beshere, the trainer at Northshire Abbey. They are to meet their instructor and learn the lay of the surrounding land. Then they can prepare for the demands of martial life.",sp=0},{t="Securing the Valley",b="The Knights of the Silver Hand guard Northshire Abbey, yet trouble reaches people beyond its protection. Llane Beshere tells new warriors that valley residents need able protectors. He urges them to master their weapons and defend those who live there.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Simple Letter?",a="Warriors returning from the kobold camps receive the Simple Letter in Northshire Valley. It sends them to Llane Beshere, the local trainer, to begin martial instruction.",al={"what is simple letter","simple letter quest","starter letter human warrior"}},{q="Who is Llane Beshere?",a="Llane Beshere trains warriors at Northshire Abbey. He teaches novices combat and welcomes recruits sent to him with orders or recommendations.",al={"who is llane beshere","beshere location","where is warrior trainer northshire"}},{q="Where do I deliver the Simple Letter?",a="Bring the letter to Llane Beshere at Northshire Abbey in Northshire Valley. The holy order protects the abbey grounds.",al={"where to turn in simple letter","simple letter hand in","llane beshere location"}},{q="What role do the Knights of the Silver Hand play in Northshire?",a="The Knights of the Silver Hand guard Northshire Valley. Their protection keeps the abbey and its immediate grounds relatively secure while recruits, farmers, and clergy carry on amid growing local tensions.",al={"what are paladins doing in northshire","silver hand northshire abbey","paladins elwynn"}},{q="Why are the local citizens in need of assistance?",a="Local residents face encroachments and shortages, though the abbey itself is fairly well defended. Llane Beshere urges new arrivals to explore the surrounding land and lend strength to those in need.",al={"why does beshere want me to help citizens","northshire problems","who needs help northshire"}},{q="When should I return to Llane Beshere after delivering the letter?",a="Llane Beshere is at the abbey day and night, training warriors as they gain combat experience and need more advanced martial skills.",al={"when should i return to llane beshere","more warrior training northshire","beshere training"}}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="At Northshire Abbey, Llane Beshere trains warriors. The letter calls newly arrived fighters to begin martial training.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you receive your first guidance at Northshire Abbey before setting out into Elwynn Forest.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance recruit, you are called to aid troubled residents beyond the Silver Hand's shelter at Northshire Abbey."},kw={"elwynn forest","knights of the silver hand","llane beshere","northshire abbey","northshire valley","simple letter","warrior trainer"},rel={"subzone:northshire-abbey","topic:knights-of-the-silver-hand"},m={faction="Alliance",cl={"WARRIOR"},ra={"Human"},id=3100},src={"In-game quest text: Simple Letter"},fv=true}
E["quest:3101"] = {t="quest",n="Consecrated Letter",z="elwynn",s="At Northshire Abbey, the Consecrated Letter calls new initiates of the Holy Light to training. It sends each bearer to a class trainer and reminds them that their conduct reflects their faith.",h="At Northshire Abbey, the Consecrated Letter calls new initiates of the Holy Light to training.",sec={{t="A Sacred Calling",b="In Northshire Valley, the Consecrated Letter begins an initiate’s journey in the Holy Light. It calls those newly arrived to find their trainer at Northshire Abbey. There, they can formalize their instruction and take up their duties in the Kingdom of Stormwind.",sp=0},{t="Carrying the Light",b="The letter reminds each initiate of the weight of their calling. Those who channel the Holy Light shine before all, symbols of hope to allies and clear targets to adversaries. Their trainer teaches that such power demands discipline. Others will judge the faith by their conduct.",sp=0},{t="Guidance and Discipline",b="The letter begins a lasting bond between student and mentor. As the initiate tests their mettle against threats around Northshire, they are expected to return often to the abbey grounds. There, their trainer guides them toward deeper understanding of combat and divine grace.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Consecrated Letter?",a="The Consecrated Letter calls an initiate of the Holy Light in Northshire Valley to begin training. It directs the bearer to a class trainer at Northshire Abbey and recalls their sacred duties.",al={"what is consecrated letter","consecrated letter quest"}},{q="Where does the Consecrated Letter come from?",a="After a new paladin returns from the kobold camps, someone at Northshire Abbey hands over the letter. Sealed with Brother Sammuel’s insignia, it tells the paladin to come see him.",al={"who gives consecrated letter","who sends consecrated letter"}},{q="Who receives the Consecrated Letter?",a="Brother Sammuel, the paladin trainer near the entrance of Northshire Abbey in Elwynn Forest, receives the letter.",al={"who turns in consecrated letter","who reads consecrated letter"}},{q="What role does the trainer play after reading the letter?",a="The trainer mentors the initiate in the ways of the Holy Light. They teach martial techniques, defensive blessings, and sacred spells as the initiate gains practical combat experience in the valley.",al={"what does the trainer teach","why train with the trainer"}},{q="Why does the letter mention being a symbol?",a="Those who channel the Holy Light are visible paragons of faith and virtue. Friends and foes alike recognize its power, so their conduct reflects upon the faith itself.",al={"why am i a symbol","holy light symbol"}},{q="Where does this training take place?",a="Northshire Abbey lies in Elwynn Forest’s peaceful northern valley. It is a sanctuary of faith and the chief grounds for recruiting defenders of the Kingdom of Stormwind.",al={"where is northshire abbey","where do i take the letter"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you wield the Holy Light and embody its virtues. In Northshire and beyond, your allies look to you as a beacon of hope.",["race:Human"]="As a human beginning your service at Northshire Abbey, you are called to act as an honorable symbol in a Kingdom troubled by recent trials.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance representative of the Holy Light, you are expected to act with honor and uphold the Alliance’s moral standing and defense."},kw={"brother sammuel","consecrated letter","elwynn forest","holy light","northshire","northshire abbey","paladin","trainer"},rel={"topic:light"},m={faction="Alliance",cl={"PALADIN"},ra={"Human"},id=3101},src={"In-game quest text: Consecrated Letter"},fv=true}
E["quest:3102"] = {t="quest",n="Encrypted Letter",z="elwynn",s="At Northshire Abbey, Jorik Kerridan summons promising rogues to meet him in secret. His letter points them toward a quiet stable and counsel for the dangers ahead.",h="At Northshire Abbey, Jorik Kerridan summons promising rogues to meet him in secret.",sec={{t="A Discreet Summons",b="Northshire Abbey looks peaceful, yet covert talents are recruited within its walls. After dealing with the kobolds, promising novices receive a letter bearing Jorik Kerridan's seal. It is addressed discreetly, away from the priests and paladins. The bearer is sent to a secluded meeting in the stables behind the Abbey.",sp=0},{t="Shadows in Northshire",b="Jorik Kerridan keeps to the stables because they are quiet and draw little notice. When newcomers arrive unseen, he speaks plainly about the wider world. Stormwind's SI:7 and the Defias Brotherhood both seek stealthy operatives. Jorik urges each novice to keep their freedom and resist powerful groups that would push them around. A clever rogue holds the cards.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sent the Encrypted Letter?",a="Jorik Kerridan sent the letter, which bears his personal insignia. Promising novices receive it after scouting nearby kobold camps.",al={"who sent encrypted letter","who gave me encrypted letter","who wrote the encrypted letter"}},{q="Where is Jorik Kerridan located?",a="Jorik Kerridan stays in the quiet stable behind Northshire Abbey. He keeps out of sight while tending to his covert work.",al={"where is jorik","where to find jorik kerridan","jorik location"}},{q="What is the purpose of the Encrypted Letter?",a="The letter discreetly invites rising rogues to meet their local trainer. Its encrypted words keep training matters from prying eyes around the Abbey.",al={"why encrypted letter","what is encrypted letter for","why is letter encrypted"}},{q="Which organizations are looking to recruit rogues?",a="Jorik Kerridan says many factions seek skilled rogues, including Stormwind's covert agency SI:7 and the Defias Brotherhood. The Defias seek spies inside Stormwind.",al={"who wants rogues","factions interested in rogues","who covets rogue skills"}},{q="What advice does Jorik Kerridan give?",a="Jorik urges you to remain your own person and refuse to be bullied into work against your will. Rogues hold the cards before the game is done.",al={"jorik advice","what does jorik tell you","rogue advice jorik"}},{q="Why does Jorik Kerridan stay in the stable?",a="Jorik Kerridan stays in the quiet stable behind Northshire Abbey because it draws little attention. There, trainers and operatives can meet beyond the notice of the Abbey's clergy and guards.",al={"why hide in stables","why is jorik behind abbey","why quiet in stables"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you meet Jorik Kerridan and hear his counsel on dealing with SI:7 and the Defias Brotherhood while keeping your independence.",["faction:Alliance"]="Even within Northshire Abbey, Stormwind's shadow operatives recruit and train promising agents for the conflicts ahead."},kw={"defias brotherhood","encrypted letter","jorik kerridan","northshire abbey","northshire valley","rogue trainer","si:7"},rel={"subzone:northshire-abbey","quest:2300","topic:defias-brotherhood","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:kobold","quest:65"},m={faction="Alliance",cl={"ROGUE"},ra={"Human"},id=3102},src={"In-game quest text: Encrypted Letter"},fv=true}
E["quest:3103"] = {t="quest",n="Hallowed Letter",z="elwynn",s="In Northshire, Marshal McBride gives promising young priests a letter from Priestess Anetta. It calls them to begin formal training in the Holy Light at Northshire Abbey, while trouble still shadows the realm.",h="In Northshire, Marshal McBride gives promising young priests a letter from Priestess Anetta.",sec={{t="A Summons to the Cloth",b="After proving themselves against the kobold camps around Northshire, novice priests receive a letter sealed by Priestess Anetta. Marshal McBride delivers it as an invitation to study the Holy Light in the abbey's quiet halls.",sp=0},{t="A World in Need",b="When you bring the letter, Priestess Anetta tells you the realm remains troubled. The Burning Legion's lingering threats still shadow Azeroth, and the continents bear fresh wounds and unrest. To Anetta, becoming a priest means more than study. It is a duty to bring healing and comfort to a suffering world.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Hallowed Letter?",a="It is a sealed letter bearing Priestess Anetta's crest, delivered by Marshal McBride to newly arrived human priests in Northshire Valley. It directs the novice to continue formal training inside Northshire Abbey.",al={"hallowed letter","priest intro quest northshire","anetta letter"}},{q="Who sends the Hallowed Letter?",a="Priestess Anetta, the priest trainer in Northshire Abbey, writes and seals the letter. She asks Marshal McBride to hand it over when the initiate returns from scouting the kobold infestation.",al={"who wrote hallowed letter","who sent the letter"}},{q="Why does Priestess Anetta summon new priests?",a="Anetta recognizes your calling to the Holy Light and wants to guide your training. With dangers such as the Burning Legion's remnants still in the world, she says disciplined healers and guides are urgently needed.",al={"why does anetta want me","purpose of the letter"}},{q="Where can Priestess Anetta be found?",a="Priestess Anetta lives in the main hall of Northshire Abbey. There, she trains human priests in their first prayers and rituals.",al={"where is anetta","priestess anetta location"}},{q="What happens after presenting the letter to Priestess Anetta?",a="After reading the letter and greeting Anetta, she accepts you as her student. She shares basic wisdom and invites you to return for more training as you gain experience.",al={"next quest after hallowed letter","what follows hallowed letter"}},{q="Why is the Burning Legion mentioned in Northshire?",a="Though the Third War has ended, demonic remnants of the Burning Legion still haunt Azeroth. Anetta mentions this wider threat to show the dangers awaiting anyone who leaves the valley.",al={"burning legion northshire","why does anetta talk about demons"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you begin your formal study of the Holy Light under Priestess Anetta. Your magic carries a duty to heal a fractured world.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you find Northshire Abbey, a sanctuary of faith and recovery for the Kingdom of Stormwind. It keeps its traditions amid the troubles around Elwynn."},kw={"elwynn","hallowed letter","holy light","marshal mcbride","northshire abbey","priest","priestess anetta"},rel={"npc:priestess-anetta","subzone:northshire-abbey","npc:marshal-mcbride","topic:light","zone:elwynn","topic:burning-legion","topic:kobold"},m={start="Marshal McBride",["end"]="Priestess Anetta",level="3",faction="Alliance",cl={"PRIEST"},ra={"Human"},id=3103},src={"Hallowed Letter (quest)"}}
E["quest:3104"] = {t="quest",n="Glyphic Letter",z="elwynn",s="A summons reaches novice human mages in Northshire Valley from Marshal McBride. Khelden Bremen calls promising spellcasters to Northshire Abbey to begin their arcane tutelage.",h="A summons reaches novice human mages in Northshire Valley from Marshal McBride.",sec={{t="A Summons to the Arcane",b="Marshal McBride gives the rune-marked letter to an aspiring apprentice who has proved capable by helping him against local vermin. Khelden Bremen, the mage trainer at Northshire, wrote it. He watches new recruits arrive at the abbey, looking for magical discipline and talent.",sp=0},{t="The Weight of Wizardry",b="Northshire Abbey has long sheltered the Holy Light. Yet Stormwind's dangers call for practitioners of every discipline. The letter brings you upstairs to Khelden Bremen, who offers no easy praise. He warns that mastering arcane power means defying nature's limits. Such power earns profound respect and deep fear from ordinary folk.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who delivers the Glyphic Letter?",a="Marshal McBride gives the letter to newly arrived mages outside Northshire Abbey after they help clear nearby kobold vermin.",al={"who gives glyphic letter","glyphic letter quest giver"}},{q="Who wrote the Glyphic Letter?",a="Khelden Bremen, the mage trainer in Northshire Abbey's upper chambers, wrote and sealed the letter.",al={"author of glyphic letter","who sent glyphic letter"}},{q="Where do I find Khelden Bremen?",a="Enter Northshire Abbey behind Marshal McBride. Take the left hallway, then climb the stairs. Khelden waits in the rear chambers to teach.",al={"khelden bremen location","where is khelden"}},{q="Why is the mage trainer located in an abbey?",a="Northshire Abbey is a holy sanctuary, yet Stormwind uses the valley to train defenders in every discipline. Arcane tutors work there alongside clerics and marshals.",al={"why are mages in northshire abbey","mage trainer in holy abbey"}},{q="What happens after turning in the letter?",a="Khelden Bremen accepts you as his student. He welcomes your resolve to wield the arcane despite its dangers and offers direct access to basic spell training.",al={"what comes after glyphic letter","next quest after glyphic letter"}},{q="Why does Khelden warn that mages will be feared?",a="Arcane magic can bend reality and is volatile. Khelden warns that the pursuit of supreme knowledge crosses boundaries ordinary folk find deeply unsettling.",al={"why are mages feared","khelden bremen dialogue"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you begin your recognized apprenticeship in Stormwind's arcane arts under Khelden Bremen.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you carry Northshire's legacy of arcane magic. It reaches back to Dalaran's first human arcanists and the Kirin Tor, and continues in the Kingdom of Stormwind."},kw={"arcane","elwynn forest","glyphic letter","khelden bremen","mage","marshal mcbride","northshire abbey"},rel={"npc:khelden-bremen","npc:marshal-mcbride","subzone:northshire-abbey","zone:elwynn","topic:kobold"},m={start="Marshal McBride",["end"]="Khelden Bremen",level="3",faction="Alliance",cl={"MAGE"},ra={"Human"},id=3104},src={"Glyphic Letter (quest)"}}
E["quest:3105"] = {t="quest",n="Tainted Letter",z="elwynn",s="In Northshire, Tainted Letter draws novice human warlocks away from the Abbey guards to learn the fel arts. Drusilla La Salle gives it to Marshal McBride, who carries it to her recruits.",h="In Northshire, Tainted Letter draws novice human warlocks away from the Abbey guards to learn the fel arts.",sec={{t="A Discreet Summons",b="After proving themselves against the kobolds, novice warlocks receive a letter from Marshal McBride. Priests and paladins study openly in Northshire Abbey, but warlocks must keep to quieter paths. Drusilla La Salle's insignia marks the letter. It directs each fledgling spellcaster to her secluded post outside the abbey's main walls before taking on other duties.",sp=0},{t="Temptation and Ambition",b="Drusilla warns that Stormwind's guards watch warlocks closely. She calls them 'pathetic mundanes.' Drawing power from the Twisting Nether and communing with demons both risk corruption. So she urges patience, prudence, and firm self-control when handling those dark energies. Caution, she says, must not extinguish a warlock's ambition.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends the Tainted Letter?",a="Drusilla La Salle writes and seals the letter at her post just outside Northshire Abbey. She asks Marshal McBride to deliver it when you return from clearing the nearby kobold camps.",al={"who wrote tainted letter","tainted letter author","who gives the tainted letter"}},{q="Why does Marshal McBride deliver a warlock letter?",a="Marshal McBride carries messages to promising recruits in the valley. He recognizes Drusilla's seal and says her letter takes priority. His chief concern remains Northshire's defense and administration, not policing the defenders' magical practices.",al={"why does mcbride have it","does mcbride know what the letter is","mcbride warlock letter"}},{q="Where can I find Drusilla La Salle?",a="Drusilla La Salle waits outside Northshire Abbey's main entrance, near the outer walls and tents. She keeps away from the clerics inside.",al={"drusilla location","where is drusilla la salle","find drusilla"}},{q="Why are warlocks allowed in Northshire Abbey?",a="Warlocks in Alliance territory face heavy suspicion, so they keep a low profile. Drusilla trains recruits outdoors in Northshire, away from the sanctuary, to avoid direct confrontation with the Holy Order of Northshire clerics and paladins.",al={"warlocks in northshire","is fel magic legal in northshire","why allow warlocks"}},{q="What lesson does Drusilla teach upon receiving the letter?",a="Drusilla warns that drawing on the Twisting Nether risks corruption without discipline. She urges self-control and prudence, yet says fear of corruption must not crush a warlock's ambition.",al={"drusilla's advice","what does drusilla say","lesson from tainted letter"}},{q="What comes after delivering the Tainted Letter?",a="Speaking with Drusilla completes the summons and makes her your trainer. She invites you to return as you grow more powerful and learn more of the warlock's ways.",al={"next quest after tainted letter","tainted letter follow up"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you receive formal instruction in Northshire while staying beyond the guards' judgment. There, you learn to master dangerous nether magic.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you live in a culture that reveres the Holy Light and the Kirin Tor's disciplined arcane. Warlocks quietly practice their summoning on the fringes of settlements like Northshire."},kw={"corruption","drusilla la salle","elwynn forest","marshal mcbride","northshire abbey","tainted letter","twisting nether","warlock"},rel={"npc:drusilla-la-salle","npc:marshal-mcbride","subzone:northshire-abbey","zone:elwynn","topic:kobold"},m={start="Marshal McBride",["end"]="Drusilla La Salle",level="1",faction="Alliance",cl={"WARLOCK"},ra={"Human"},id=3105},src={"Tainted Letter (quest)"}}
E["quest:33"] = {t="quest",n="Wolves Across the Border",z="elwynn",s="In Northshire Valley, Eagan Peltskinner asks you to hunt wolves and bring him their meat. He waits outside Northshire Abbey, where daily needs remain even as guards focus on Defias bandits.",h="In Northshire Valley, Eagan Peltskinner asks you to hunt wolves and bring him their meat.",sec={{t="A Pragmatic Request",b="Eagan Peltskinner waits by Northshire Abbey’s walls, angry at the local timber wolves. Marshal McBride and the Stormwind guards have little strength to defend the abbey from Defias bandits. Tradesfolk still have daily needs, so Eagan asks you to thin the wolves’ numbers and bring back their tough meat for his cooking.",sp=0},{t="Wilds of Northshire",b="Wolves roam closer to Northshire Abbey as patrols weaken. The Kingdom of Stormwind has too few troops and lacks leadership. Young wolves and timber wolves prowl the abbey’s paths and orchards. Hunting them supplies Eagan’s pantry and makes nearby trails safer for novitiates, laborers, and newly arrived defenders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Eagan Peltskinner?",a="Eagan Peltskinner is a hunter and tradesman near the entrance to Northshire Abbey. He dislikes the local timber wolves and is glad to cook and eat their meat.",al={"who is eagan","peltskinner","eagan peltskinner"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Eagan want wolf meat?",a="Eagan enjoys eating wolf steaks. He offers useful starter gear and coin to recruits who bring him fresh meat.",al={"why wolf meat","eagan hungry","what does eagan do with meat"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the wolves located?",a="Timber wolves and young wolves roam Northshire Valley’s fields, hills, and riverbanks, especially south and east of the abbey.",al={"where are the wolves","wolf locations","find wolves"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are wolves a problem in Northshire?",a="Reduced patrols and Defias bandits have left Northshire’s roads and farms exposed to wildlife. Unescorted travel is dangerous for clergy and workers.",al={"why wolves attacking","northshire wolf problem"},it="threat"},{q="Do I need to talk to anyone before taking this quest?",a="No. Deputy Willem may send newcomers to Eagan through an introductory errand, but Eagan offers the hunt directly to anyone who approaches him outside the abbey.",al={"quest prereqs","prerequisites","who gives this quest"},gp=true},{q="Is tough wolf meat used for cooking recipes?",a="Eagan plans to cook the meat himself. Novitiate cooks often learn that wolf meat gathered in Elwynn Forest is a basic ingredient for outdoor cooking.",al={"tough wolf meat cooking","can players cook wolf meat"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What is the Tough Wolf Meat for?",a="Eagan Peltskinner intends to cook it up into wolf steaks for himself. Despite despising the beasts prowling the valley, he has developed a hearty appetite for their meat and gladly trades useful gear to anyone willing to supply his table.",al={"what is tough wolf meat for","why tough wolf meat","tough wolf meat use"},it="item",add="12d6ae41"},{q="Why are wolves roaming Northshire?",a="Young wolves and timber wolves naturally prowl the forested borders and open meadows of Northshire Valley. However, with local Stormwind guards preoccupied by the rising threat of the Defias Brotherhood, the predators roam closer to the abbey grounds unchecked.",al={"why are there wolves here","northshire timber wolves","wolves in northshire"},it="target",add="acd05579"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you learn a frontier truth from Eagan’s craving for wolf steak: what you hunt can often be cooked and eaten.",["race:Human"]="As a human recruit in Northshire, you find this among your first practical ways to help secure Stormwind’s nearby borders."},kw={"abbey","eagan","elwynn","meat","northshire","peltskinner","timber wolf","wolves"},rel={"quest:5261","subzone:northshire-abbey","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Eagan Peltskinner",level="2",faction="Alliance",id=33,ri={"Tough Wolf Meat"}},src={"Wolves Across the Border"}}
E["quest:345"] = {t="quest",n="Ink Supplies",z="elwynn",s="Brother Paxton at Northshire Abbey has run short of the ink his writings need. He sends you east to Lakeshire for Rethban ore.",h="Brother Paxton at Northshire Abbey has run short of the ink his writings need.",sec={{t="A Scribe's Formula",b="Brother Paxton uses his special ink for important writings, including The Stresses of Iron. The ink dries quickly and resists smearing. Yet its recipe has a flaw: left too long, it hardens in the pot. To make a fresh batch, Paxton needs raw Rethban iron ore from the rocky Redridge Mountains.",sp=0},{t="A Town Under Siege",b="Foreman Oslow has no workers to spare for mining. His laborers are strengthening Lakeshire’s barricades, rebuilding ruined structures, and defending the town from Blackrock orc raids. So you must brave the perilous Rethban Caverns yourself to find the ore Paxton needs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Brother Paxton need iron ore for ink?",a="Brother Paxton needs Rethban iron ore to make his special ink. Ground ore gives the ink its mineral pigment and setting qualities, so it dries quickly and resists smearing.",al={"why iron for ink","paxton ore ink","brother paxton ink recipe"},it="item"},{q="Who is Foreman Oslow?",a="Foreman Oslow oversees civic construction and repairs in Lakeshire. With Blackrock orcs pressing the town, he directs its rebuilding and fortification.",al={"foreman oslow","oslow lakeshire","who is oslow"},it="identity"},{q="Where does Brother Paxton send you?",a="Paxton sends you east from Elwynn Forest to Lakeshire in the Redridge Mountains. There, you are to find Foreman Oslow.",al={"ink supplies destination","where is oslow","where do i go for ink supplies"},it="place"},{q="Why won't Foreman Oslow just give you the ore?",a="Blackrock orc attacks keep Lakeshire under pressure. Oslow’s workers are busy repairing damaged buildings and strengthening the town, leaving no hands free to mine.",al={"why no ore","oslow refuses ore","why oslow mad"},it="conflict"},{q="What book is Brother Paxton attempting to copy?",a="Brother Paxton is copying The Stresses of Iron. His work stopped when his previous batch of quick-drying ink hardened in its container.",al={"paxton book","what is paxton copying","the stresses of iron"},it="purpose"},{q="What happens after speaking with Foreman Oslow?",a="Foreman Oslow tells you to gather Rethban iron ore yourself in the dangerous Rethban Caverns, north of Lake Everstill.",al={"next quest after ink supplies","what next after oslow","follow up ink supplies"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Brother Paxton want you to fetch Rethban ore?",a="Brother Paxton is dedicated to copying the scholarly treatise The Stresses of Iron for Northshire Abbey's library. He insists on brewing his own specialized ink, which relies on pulverized Rethban iron ore to ensure it dries rapidly and resists smudging. Unfortunately, his previous batch dried up completely before he could finish transcription, leaving his scholarly project stalled until fresh minerals arrive.",al={"why does brother paxton need ore","brother paxton motive","why ink supplies"},it="motive",add="3b01bf84"},{q="Why does Brother Paxton send you instead of getting the ore himself?",a="Brother Paxton is a devoted copyist confined to his duties within the cloistered walls of Northshire Abbey. Journeying all the way out to Lakeshire in the Redridge Mountains is far beyond his peaceful monastic routine, especially with travel routes growing increasingly perilous. As an able adventurer already traveling the realm, you can easily carry word to his usual contact.",al={"why cant paxton get the ore","why send an adventurer","why me ink supplies"},it="why_me",add="c7dba9bc"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you can help the clergy with scholarly work. Brother Paxton’s errand follows Brother Kristoff’s sermon on the Fortitude of the Spirit.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you can seek Rethban iron ore high in the crags of Redridge.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you see the contrast between Northshire Abbey’s quiet seclusion and the violence threatening Lakeshire."},kw={"brother paxton","foreman oslow","ink supplies","lakeshire","northshire abbey","redridge mountains","rethban ore","the stresses of iron"},rel={"npc:foreman-oslow","quest:344","quest:343","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge"},m={start="Brother Paxton",["end"]="Foreman Oslow",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=345},src={"Ink Supplies"}}
E["quest:346"] = {t="quest",n="Return to Kristoff",z="elwynn",s="In Cathedral Square, Brother Kristoff waits for the return of The Stresses of Iron. After a long search in Northshire, you bring the borrowed book back to the Cathedral of Light.",h="In Cathedral Square, Brother Kristoff waits for the return of The Stresses of Iron.",sec={{t="A Long-Delayed Return",b="Brother Kristoff waits in Cathedral Square for The Stresses of Iron, a book on metallurgy. Its path led from Stormwind Keep's Royal Library to Northshire Abbey, where Brother Paxton copied it by hand. The work stalled when Paxton ran short of Rethban ore for his ink. Now the ore has been found and the copy is complete. You bring the original book back to Stormwind.",sp=0},{t="The Labor of Scribes",b="Brother Paxton asks you to apologize to Librarian Milton Sheaf for the delay. Northshire's copyists preserve civic and spiritual lore, though their supplies are scarce. Valuable books must be copied stroke by stroke with mineral-rich ink. Only then can they leave the abbey and return to Stormwind's care.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the book The Stresses of Iron about?",a="The Stresses of Iron is a treatise on metallurgy and metalworking. Brother Kristoff sought it for study in Cathedral Square, and Northshire Abbey's scribes needed a copy to preserve its knowledge.",al={"what is stresses of iron","stresses of iron book","what book is kristoff looking for"},it="item"},{q="Why was the book at Northshire Abbey?",a="The Royal Library lent The Stresses of Iron to Brother Paxton so he could make an illuminated copy for Northshire Abbey's archives. His work stalled when he ran short of Rethban ore for specialized ink.",al={"why was paxton holding the book","why was it in northshire"},it="history"},{q="Who is Brother Kristoff?",a="Brother Kristoff belongs to the Clergy of the Holy Light and serves in Cathedral Square outside Stormwind's Cathedral of Light. He requested the book and offers spiritual blessings in gratitude.",al={"who is kristoff","kristoff stormwind"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Milton?",a="Milton Sheaf is the head librarian in Stormwind Keep's Royal Library. He permitted the loan of The Stresses of Iron and grew impatient over its long delay.",al={"who is librarian milton","milton sheaf"},it="people"},{q="Where does this quest chain begin?",a="The chain begins in Stormwind's Cathedral Square, where Brother Kristoff offers Speaking of Fortitude. It leads to Librarian Milton Sheaf, then Northshire Abbey and Redridge Mountains, before bringing you back to Kristoff.",al={"how to start speaking of fortitude","quest chain start"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Does this quest have any follow-ups?",a="Return to Kristoff ends the Speaking of Fortitude chain. When you deliver The Stresses of Iron, Brother Kristoff thanks you and offers a blessing of the Light.",al={"what comes after return to kristoff","is there a next quest"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Brother Paxton want the book returned to Brother Kristoff?",a="Brother Paxton only borrowed The Stresses of Iron so he could copy its contents at Northshire Abbey. Now that his transcription is complete, he has no further claim on the rare volume and owes its safe return to Stormwind's Cathedral of Light, hoping to mend any trouble caused by his lengthy delay.",al={"why return stresses of iron","brother paxton motive","why send book back to kristoff"},it="motive",add="46830297"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you see how the Church of the Holy Light preserves and shares important scholarship across the kingdom.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you rely on safe roads linking Stormwind Keep, Northshire, and the embattled Redridge Mountains."},kw={"brother kristoff","brother paxton","cathedral square","milton sheaf","northshire abbey","return to kristoff","stormwind","the stresses of iron"},rel={"npc:brother-kristoff","quest:344","quest:343","subzone:cathedral-square","topic:light"},m={start="Brother Paxton",["end"]="Brother Kristoff",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=346},src={"Return to Kristoff"}}
E["quest:35"] = {t="quest",n="Further Concerns",z="elwynn",s="East of Goldshire, Marshal Dughan sends you to check reports of danger. You cross Elwynn Forest to speak with Guard Thomas at the river crossing toward Redridge.",h="East of Goldshire, Marshal Dughan sends you to check reports of danger.",sec={{t="Eyes on the Eastern Crossing",b="Marshal Dughan commands Goldshire's garrison and takes reports of hostile creatures along Elwynn's riverbanks seriously. Bandits and vermin already trouble the forest's center, so he cannot spare guards from town. He sends you east to consult Guard Thomas, the sentry at the bridge toward Redridge.",sp=0},{t="A Frontier Stretched Thin",b="Guard Thomas has held the bridge outpost for more than a week and has seen the danger for himself. Hostile, semi-intelligent murlocs have made camps along eastern Elwynn's waterways. Stormwind's army is absent, and local garrisons guard town walls and supply lines. Rural bridge posts like Thomas's are left isolated as the danger grows.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Marshal Dughan send me to Guard Thomas?",a="Marshal Dughan sends you to Guard Thomas because reports speak of murlocs creeping into the eastern waterways. Thomas has been stationed at the eastern Elwynn bridge for a week, so Dughan trusts him to confirm the threat.",al={"why guard thomas","dughan purpose","talk to thomas"},it="motive"},{q="Where is Guard Thomas stationed?",a="Guard Thomas watches the wooden bridge over the river in far eastern Elwynn Forest, on the road toward the Redridge Mountains.",al={"guard thomas location","where is thomas","eastern bridge guard"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What threat does Guard Thomas confirm?",a="Guard Thomas confirms that hostile, semi-intelligent murlocs have settled along eastern Elwynn's streams and waterways. They threaten travelers and nearby farmsteads.",al={"murloc threat","what did thomas find","eastern river threat"},it="threat"},{q="How do you reach Guard Thomas?",a="Take the road east from Goldshire across Elwynn Forest to the bridge over the eastern river, where Guard Thomas keeps watch.",al={"fast travel to thomas","horse ride dughan","charger to bridge"},gp=true},{q="Why doesn't Stormwind send an army to help eastern Elwynn?",a="Stormwind's forces are stretched thin with King Varian Wrynn missing and resources diverted from the countryside. Sentries such as Guard Thomas are left to rely largely on passing adventurers.",al={"where are stormwind guards","why is elwynn undefended","stormwind military help"},it="conflict"},{q="What happens after reporting to Guard Thomas?",a="After confirming the murloc presence, Guard Thomas asks you to investigate what became of the other sentries who patrolled the riverbank and failed to return.",al={"next quest after further concerns","thomas follow up","lost guards quest"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Marshal Dughan send an adventurer instead of his own guards?",a="Marshal Dughan is stretched thin keeping Goldshire secure against Defias bandits and gnolls. With Stormwind denying additional troops and resources, the local garrison cannot spare soldiers for routine courier runs or distant scouting. Because you brought him the initial warning and showed concern for Elwynn's safety, he entrusts you with heading east to confer with Guard Thomas at the eastern bridge.",al={"why send me","why not use guards","why does dughan need me"},it="why_me",add="01d891f6"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, thin defenses near the capital reveal growing cracks in the Kingdom of Stormwind's strength.",["race:Human"]="As a human of Elwynn, you face murlocs whose spread threatens the breadbasket farms and trade routes connecting Goldshire to Lakeshire."},kw={"eastern bridge","elwynn forest","further concerns","goldshire","guard thomas","marshal dughan","murloc"},rel={"npc:marshal-dughan","npc:guard-thomas","quest:40","quest:37","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:murloc"},m={start="Marshal Dughan",["end"]="Guard Thomas",faction="Alliance",id=35},src={"Further Concerns"}}
E["quest:37"] = {t="quest",n="Find the Lost Guards",z="elwynn",s="Guard Thomas waits at Elwynn's eastern bridge, needing news of two missing Stormwind guards.",h="Guard Thomas waits at Elwynn's eastern bridge, needing news of two missing Stormwind guards.",sec={{t="A Patrol Vanished",b="At the crossing where the King's road nears Redridge, the riverbanks have grown more dangerous. Days ago, Thomas sent Rolf and Malakai north along the river to scout the murloc threat and clear their nests. Now he fears violence has stopped their patrol.",sp=0},{t="Grim Discovery",b="North along the river toward Stone Cairn Lake, swarming murlocs close around you. At the water's edge, you find a half-eaten corpse in the mud. An engraved medallion beside it bears the name Footman Malakai Stone. Malakai is dead, but Rolf is still missing.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gave this quest and where are they located?",a="Guard Thomas is waiting beside the bridge at Elwynn Forest's eastern border, where the road leads toward Redridge Mountains.",al={"quest giver","where is guard thomas","who starts find the lost guards"},gp=true},{q="Who are the missing guards?",a="Rolf and Malakai are two Stormwind city footmen. Guard Thomas sent them to scout the riverbanks and watch for aggressive murlocs.",al={"missing guards elwynn","who are rolf and malakai","lost guards names"},it="people"},{q="Where are the remains found?",a="Footman Malakai Stone's half-eaten remains lie on the river's eastern bank, just north of Guard Thomas's post and near the edge of a murloc settlement.",al={"where is malakai corpse","half-eaten body location","lost guards location"},sp=1,it="place",gp=true},{q="What killed Malakai?",a="Local river murlocs overran Malakai and ate him. They infest the shores of eastern Elwynn Forest.",al={"how did malakai die","who killed the guards"},sp=1,it="threat"},{q="What happened to Rolf?",a="You find Malakai's remains alone by the river. Rolf is still missing, and his fate remains unknown as you track deeper into the murloc camps.",al={"where is rolf","did rolf survive"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why were the guards sent out alone?",a="Stormwind's military is stretched thin across several territories. Small garrisons like Guard Thomas's rely on pairs of guards to patrol the wilderness borders.",al={"why were they sent","stormwind guard shortage"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Guard Thomas want you to find the lost guards?",a="Guard Thomas dispatched Rolf and Malakai north along the river days ago on an investigative patrol. They never reported back. As the officer overseeing this stretch of eastern Elwynn Forest, Thomas must account for his missing men to finish his official report for the Stormwind City Guard, whether that means bringing them home or confirming their deaths.",al={"why find lost guards","guard thomas motive","why look for rolf and malakai"},it="motive",add="5aa1fbbd"},{q="Why does Guard Thomas ask an adventurer instead of sending more guards?",a="Guard Thomas and his remaining men are stretched thin defending the bridges and borders of eastern Elwynn Forest from increasing murloc raids and gnoll incursions. With Stormwind's military spread across the kingdom and already missing two footmen, he cannot afford to pull more sentries off post to conduct a search party.",al={"why cant thomas find them","why ask me lost guards","why does thomas need help"},it="why_me",add="18be7cf7"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance soldier, you see how beast and murloc attacks threaten Elwynn's outer borders, even so close to Stormwind.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you can honor fallen defenders by recovering their insignia and bringing justice to those who guard the kingdom's frontier."},kw={"elwynn forest","find the lost guards","guard thomas","half-eaten body","malakai","malakai stone","murlocs","rolf"},rel={"npc:guard-thomas","quest:35","quest:45","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Guard Thomas",["end"]="A half-eaten body",faction="Alliance",id=37},src={"Find the Lost Guards"}}
E["quest:39"] = {t="quest",n="Deliver Thomas' Report",z="elwynn",s="In eastern Elwynn, Guard Thomas sends word of two dead guards and rising danger. He asks you to carry the report to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire, where few hands remain to defend the roads.",h="In eastern Elwynn, Guard Thomas sends word of two dead guards and rising danger.",sec={{t="Bad Tidings from the East",b="Guard Thomas watches the bridges into eastern Elwynn, where river traffic meets the wilderness. Aggressive murloc tribes have killed Guards Malakai and Rolf. Thomas has too few guards left to contain them, so he sends you down the road to Goldshire with an urgent report.",sp=0},{t="A Garrison Stretched to the Brink",b="Marshal Dughan receives Thomas' report in Goldshire, where he already struggles to keep patrols on the roads. Kobolds infest the area, Defias bandits threaten travelers, and Stormwind City has sent no reinforcements. The deaths of two experienced guards deepen his burden. Murlocs may soon threaten Goldshire itself, while the region's defenses grow ever thinner.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who are Malakai and Rolf?",a="Malakai and Rolf were Stormwind guards stationed in eastern Elwynn under Guard Thomas. Murloc tribes overwhelmed and killed them as they patrolled near the rivers and lakes.",al={"malakai and rolf","who died","dead guards"},it="people"},{q="Why is Guard Thomas asking an adventurer to deliver the report?",a="Guard Thomas has too few troops to spare. If he leaves his post or sends one of his few surviving sentries, the eastern bridges will stand undefended.",al={"why guard thomas needs help","why courier","cant thomas send a guard"},it="why_me"},{q="What threat do the murlocs pose to Goldshire?",a="Murloc tribes along the eastern rivers are spreading west. Marshal Dughan fears they may reach Goldshire's outskirts within the week, and he has too few guards to hold the perimeter.",al={"murloc threat","will murlocs attack goldshire","how bad are murlocs"},it="threat"},{q="Why doesn't Stormwind City send reinforcements to Elwynn?",a="Stormwind's military resources are stretched across several fronts. King Varian Wrynn's disappearance has left the capital politically paralyzed, so outlying settlements and frontier bridges are largely left to local town watches and hired adventurers.",al={"why no stormwind army","where are the troops","why are defenses thin"},it="conflict"},{q="What happens after Marshal Dughan reads the report?",a="Marshal Dughan knows his garrison lacks the strength to stop the murlocs directly. He turns to securing supplies and armor for those willing to hold the line.",al={"next quest","what does dughan do","chain after report"},it="next_step"},{q="Where is Guard Thomas stationed?",a="Guard Thomas is stationed in eastern Elwynn Forest, guarding bridges over the rivers between the heart of the forest and the wilder borders near the Redridge Mountains.",al={"guard thomas location","where is thomas","thomas location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Guard Thomas want his report delivered to Marshal Dughan?",a="Guard Thomas cannot contain the murlocs spreading across eastern Elwynn with the handful of men stationed at the river bridges. Having just confirmed the deaths of his guardsmen, Rolf and Malakai, he urgently needs Marshal Dughan to understand that the eastern border is collapsing. Without reinforcements or aid organized from Goldshire, the murloc incursions will sweep unchecked into the heart of the forest.",al={"why send the report","guard thomas report motive","why report to dughan"},it="motive",add="a496bd3c"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Carrying Thomas' report shows how vulnerable the Alliance's central kingdom has become. Even roads outside the capital are slipping from garrison control.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior serving the realm, you see the cost of frontier duty in the deaths of Malakai and Rolf, killed by relentless foes.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you feel these losses in your homeland, where too few defenders face more hostile incursions."},kw={"elwynn forest","goldshire","guard thomas","malakai","marshal dughan","murlocs","report","rolf"},rel={"npc:guard-thomas","npc:marshal-dughan","quest:71","quest:59","subzone:goldshire","topic:murloc","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Guard Thomas",["end"]="Marshal Dughan",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=39},src={"Deliver Thomas' Report"}}
E["quest:3903"] = {t="quest",n="Milly Osworth",z="elwynn",s="Deputy Willem sends you across Northshire Abbey to help his friend Milly Osworth. Her wagon and livelihood are in danger, and Willem's guards cannot leave the abbey grounds to help.",h="Deputy Willem sends you across Northshire Abbey to help his friend Milly Osworth.",sec={{t="A Dependable Pair of Hands",b="After you drive back the Defias thieves pressing into Northshire Valley, Deputy Willem trusts you with a personal favor. His friend Milly Osworth is a civilian caught in the valley's unrest, and helping her falls beyond his guard duties.",sp=0},{t="Trouble by the Stables",b="Milly waits beside her wagon near the stables on the far side of Northshire Abbey. Deputy Willem stays at his post to defend the abbey. With the guard garrison stretched thin, Milly's troubles in the valley go without help.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to speak with Milly Osworth?",a="Deputy Willem sends you to Milly after you prove reliable against the Defias bandits.",al={"who gives milly osworth","quest giver milly osworth","where to get milly osworth quest"}},{q="Where can Milly Osworth be found?",a="Milly waits beside her wagon on the far side of Northshire Abbey, near the stables and the vineyards to the southeast.",al={"milly osworth location","where is milly","where is milly osworth"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why can't Deputy Willem help Milly himself?",a="Willem's guard duties keep him at Northshire Abbey. Bandits and vermin press the valley, leaving the garrison too few hands for private civilian troubles.",al={"why doesnt willem help","willem duties","why help milly"},it="why_me"},{q="What prerequisites are needed for this quest?",a="You need to complete Brotherhood of Thieves for Deputy Willem before he trusts you to help Milly.",al={"milly osworth requirements","brotherhood of thieves follow up","how to unlock milly osworth quest"},gp=true},{q="What does Milly need help with?",a="Milly is struggling with her crop and wagon amid the local turmoil. Her harvest needs protection from the surrounding valley.",al={"what does milly want","milly problem","milly harvest troubles"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Milly Osworth to Deputy Willem?",a="Willem calls Milly a friend in need from the Northshire community. He looks out for her while bound to his post.",al={"willem and milly","is milly related to willem","how does willem know milly"},it="ties"},{q="Why does Deputy Willem want to help Milly Osworth?",a="Deputy Willem considers Milly a dear personal friend and knows she has run into trouble near the stables. While he cares deeply about her well-being, his official post as deputy keeps him tethered to Northshire Abbey. Sending a capable, trustworthy adventurer like you is his best way to ensure she gets the protection and help she desperately needs.",al={"why help milly osworth","willem motive milly","why does deputy willem care"},it="motive",add="c87a8d77"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="In Northshire, you see Alliance guards stretched thin and relying on passing adventurers to protect townspeople from emerging threats.",["race:Human"]="As a young human in Northshire, you can help Willem and show the community spirit that helps hold Elwynn together."},kw={"deputy willem","elwynn forest","harvest","milly osworth","northshire abbey","stables","wagon"},rel={"npc:willem","quest:18","subzone:northshire-abbey","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Deputy Willem",["end"]="Milly Osworth",level="4",faction="Alliance",id=3903},src={"Milly Osworth (quest)"}}
E["quest:3904"] = {t="quest",n="Milly's Harvest",z="elwynn",s="Defias brigands have driven Milly Osworth from the Northshire vineyards. Her gathered grapes remain in buckets and crates among the occupied rows, at risk of theft or ruin.",h="Defias brigands have driven Milly Osworth from the Northshire vineyards.",sec={{t="A Crop Left Behind",b="Milly Osworth fled the southeastern fields of Northshire Valley when Defias brigands swarmed the vines. The grapes she had gathered remain in buckets and crates among the occupied rows. Northshire's garrison is stretched thin, and Milly fears boots and fighting will crush any fruit the bandits leave behind.",sp=0},{t="Northshire Under Pressure",b="Defias bandits now occupy working vineyards, a sign of how little safety Northshire can offer. Stormwind's attention lies elsewhere, and the valley has too few guards. So farmers like Milly depend on recruits and wanderers to protect their property and secure the food and wine that supply the abbey.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Milly Osworth?",a="Milly Osworth farms the Northshire Vineyards. She tends and harvests the valley's grapes, but the arriving Defias Brotherhood drove her from her fields.",al={"milly osworth","who is milly","grape lady"},it="identity"},{q="Why can't the Northshire guards retrieve the harvest?",a="Northshire Valley's guards are too few and occupied with the widespread bandit threat and kobold infestations. Milly also fears a military sweep could trample her grapes into the mud.",al={"why don't guards help","northshire guards","lazy guards"},it="why_me"},{q="What are the Defias doing in the vineyards?",a="The Defias Brotherhood entered Northshire Valley to disrupt regional production, harass local people, and seize resources under Stormwind's guards' noses.",al={"why defias in vineyards","defias grapes","defias northshire"},it="target"},{q="Where are the crates located?",a="The harvest buckets and crates lie scattered across the ground in the Northshire Vineyards, just southeast of Northshire Abbey, among Defias brigands patrolling the rows.",al={"crate locations","where to find grapes","where is harvest"},gp=true},{q="What happens after Milly gets her grapes back?",a="Once her harvest is safe, Milly asks you to bring her Grape Manifest to Brother Neals inside Northshire Abbey. The yield can then be accounted for and processed into wine.",al={"next quest","after milly's harvest","what next"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why are grapes important to Northshire Abbey?",a="Northshire Valley produces famous wine and supplies the clerical community at the abbey. Milly's crop sustains local trade and the cellars maintained by the Brotherhood of Northshire.",al={"northshire wine","why grapes matter"},it="item"},{q="Why does Milly Osworth need you to retrieve her harvest?",a="Milly was in the middle of picking grapes when the Defias gang overran the vineyards. She fears that if the thieves do not make off with the fruit, the Abbey's guards will inevitably trample the crates in the chaos of battle. Her livelihood depends on recovering those buckets before they are ruined.",al={"why does milly need the harvest","why save the grapes","milly osworth motive"},it="motive",add="23083d02"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Recovering Milly's crop gives young Alliance recruits a first look at the Defias threat only miles from Stormwind City.",["race:Human"]="As a human beginning your journey in Northshire, protecting smallholder farmers like Milly is part of defending Elwynn's working folk."},kw={"crates","defias","elwynn forest","grapes","milly osworth","milly's harvest","northshire abbey","northshire vineyards"},rel={"quest:3903","subzone:northshire-vineyards","subzone:northshire-abbey","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Milly Osworth",level="4",faction="Alliance",id=3904,ri={"Milly's Harvest"}},src={"Milly's Harvest (quest)"}}
E["quest:3905"] = {t="quest",n="Grape Manifest",z="elwynn",s="Milly Osworth needs you to bring her manifest to Brother Neals at Northshire Abbey. It will help the brotherhood replenish its wine stores.",h="Milly Osworth needs you to bring her manifest to Brother Neals at Northshire Abbey.",sec={{t="The Valley's Vintage",b="Defias thieves and other brigands took the eastern fields. The abbey lost its food and its grapes. Milly has recovered the crop and recorded every bushel in her manifest, including what the occupied fields had yielded.",sp=0},{t="A Tipple in the Belfry",b="Brother Neals oversees food and drink at Northshire Abbey. In the quiet of the bell tower, he is known to sample Northshire's vintages. Brigands still threaten the gates, yet fresh grapes give the brotherhood a moment to toast the Light and take heart.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Grape Manifest?",a="Milly Osworth records her harvest recovered from Defias thieves in the Grape Manifest. The ledger helps the abbey's quartermaster restock its cellars.",al={"grape manifest item","what is manifest","millys manifest"},it="item"},{q="Who is Brother Neals?",a="Brother Neals is a monk at Northshire Abbey who oversees its food and drink. He often samples the vintages in the bell tower.",al={"brother neals","who is neals","monk in bell tower"},it="identity"},{q="Where do I find Brother Neals?",a="Brother Neals is inside Northshire Abbey, in the bell tower overlooking the grounds.",al={"neals location","where is brother neals","find brother neals"},gp=true},{q="Why is Northshire's grape crop so important?",a="Northshire's grapes provide celebrated wine and fresh food for the local clergy and soldiers. A lost harvest threatens daily stores and the abbey's sacramental wine across Elwynn.",al={"why grapes matter","northshire wine lore","milly harvest significance"},it="purpose"},{q="Who was threatening Milly's harvest?",a="Defias brigands occupied Northshire Valley's eastern fields, drove Milly Osworth out, and hid her boxed harvest throughout the vineyards. Adventurers drove them back.",al={"who stole the grapes","grape thieves","bandits in vineyards"},it="threat"},{q="What happens after giving Brother Neals the manifest?",a="Brother Neals gives his blessings in the name of the Light. He is overjoyed that the abbey's cellars will have fresh wine despite the bandit troubles across the valley.",al={"quest aftermath","does neals make wine","what follows grape manifest"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Milly Osworth want this done?",a="With her crop finally saved from the Defias bandits who overran her vineyards, Milly needs Northshire Abbey to know fresh supplies have survived. Brother Neals oversees all the food and drink for the valley, and this manifest officially documents that her grapes are ready for the abbey's wine cellars.",al={"milly osworth grape manifest motive","why send grape manifest","why does milly need this delivered"},it="motive",add="7b371529"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Securing Northshire's food stores helps Stormwind's main place of recruitment and recovery remain self-sufficient.",["race:Human"]="As a human beginning your journey, helping Milly and Brother Neals protects one of the kingdom's cherished pastoral traditions.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you know wine has a place in hospitality and sacramental rites at Northshire Abbey, where farming sustains the brotherhood's worship."},kw={"brother neals","defias","elwynn","grape manifest","harvest","milly osworth","northshire abbey","vineyard","wine"},rel={"npc:brother-neals","quest:3903","subzone:northshire-abbey","zone:elwynn","topic:light"},m={start="Milly Osworth",["end"]="Brother Neals",level="4",faction="Alliance",id=3905},src={"Grape Manifest (quest)"}}
E["quest:40"] = {t="quest",n="A Fishy Peril",z="elwynn",s="In eastern Elwynn, Remy \"Two Times\" fears a danger is spreading. Fishing has suffered and travelers face attacks, but he doubts the guard understands the trouble.",h="In eastern Elwynn, Remy \"Two Times\" fears a danger is spreading.",sec={{t="A Plea from the East",b="In Goldshire seeking business, Remy grows uneasy as murlocs swim up streams and into inland shallows. He asks passersby to warn the township before the threat spreads further.",sp=0},{t="A Strained Garrison",b="Marshal Dughan hears the report but doubts it. His garrison is stretched thin, and without confirmed intelligence, he will not send scarce men after rumors of fish-men in the eastern streams.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest A Fishy Peril?",a="Remy \"Two Times\", a merchant from Redridge, asks you to carry his warning in Goldshire, in Elwynn Forest.",al={"quest giver a fishy peril","who starts a fishy peril","remy quest"},it="people",gp=true},{q="Why is Remy \"Two Times\" worried about murlocs?",a="Remy has seen murlocs swim up the rivers of eastern Elwynn. They drive away local fish and attack travelers along the waterways.",al={"why remy scared","murloc problem elwynn","fishy peril lore"},it="motive"},{q="Why won't Marshal Dughan send troops immediately?",a="Marshal Dughan considers the reports unverified. His garrison is occupied by gnoll attacks and organized banditry, so he cannot commit soldiers without formal scout reports.",al={"why dughan ignores murlocs","marshal dughan response","why no troops east"},it="threat"},{q="Where does this quest lead next?",a="Marshal Dughan seeks reliable confirmation from scouts in Further Concerns before committing royal resources to the east.",al={"what comes after a fishy peril","next quest after fishy peril","further concerns quest"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Where does the player turn in A Fishy Peril?",a="You deliver the report to Marshal Dughan just outside the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire.",al={"where turn in fishy peril","fishy peril turn in","dughan location"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What larger threat are the murlocs part of in Elwynn?",a="Murlocs appear primitive and erratic, yet their spread into inland lakes such as Stonecairn Lake and Crystal Lake threatens rural trade and agriculture alongside gnoll and bandit attacks.",al={"murlocs in elwynn","are murlocs dangerous elwynn"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Remy send an adventurer instead of talking to Marshal Dughan himself?",a="Remy has already warned Marshal Dughan directly, but the marshal dismissed his warnings as merchant rumors. With Dughan focused entirely on the gnoll incursions and Defias bandits, Remy needs an outside voice—an independent adventurer—to emphasize the danger and convince the garrison to send troops east.",al={"why me a fishy peril","why cant remy talk to dughan","why does remy need me"},it="why_me",add="3afc8cff"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, this warning shows the strain on Stormwind's home guard and the township's reliance on independent adventurers to investigate rumors.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you see eastern waterways close to home become dangerous hunting grounds for aquatic beasts."},kw={"a fishy peril","elwynn forest","further concerns","goldshire","marshal dughan","murloc","remy two times"},rel={"npc:remy-two-times","npc:marshal-dughan","quest:35","topic:murloc","subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn","topic:gnoll"},m={start="Remy \"Two Times\"",["end"]="Marshal Dughan",faction="Alliance",id=40},src={"A Fishy Peril"}}
E["quest:45"] = {t="quest",n="Discover Rolf's Fate",z="elwynn",s="Guard Thomas waits for news of Rolf and Malakai, missing near Stone Cairn Lake. Malakai's half-eaten remains and webbed tracks point toward a murloc village.",h="Guard Thomas waits for news of Rolf and Malakai, missing near Stone Cairn Lake.",sec={{t="A Trail of Webbed Tracks",b="Malakai's half-eaten remains lie by the shore. Webbed footprints mark the mud and lead east along the water's edge. They run straight to a ramshackle murloc camp.",sp=0},{t="The End of Patrol",b="You follow the tracks into the heart of the coastal murloc settlement. Another corpse lies there, stripped by the creatures. An inscribed medallion around the dead soldier's neck names him Footman Rolf Hartford. Neither guard survived the ambush.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Rolf?",a="Rolf Hartford was a Stormwind footman assigned to patrol eastern Elwynn Forest under Guard Thomas, alongside Guard Malakai. Murlocs overwhelmed and killed both guards near Stone Cairn Lake.",al={"who is rolf","footman rolf","rolf hartford"},sp=1,it="identity"},{q="Where is Rolf's body located?",a="Rolf's corpse lies farther east along the southern shore of Stone Cairn Lake, inside a murloc village near the lake's border.",al={"rolf location","where is rolf","find rolf"},sp=1,gp=true},{q="Why were the guards out near Stone Cairn Lake?",a="Guard Thomas stationed guards along eastern Elwynn's rivers and lakes to watch for murloc and gnoll incursions. The patrols were understaffed and vulnerable to sudden, coordinated attacks.",al={"why were guards lost","what were guards doing","guard patrol elwynn"},it="why_here"},{q="How do you confirm the corpse belongs to Rolf?",a="A metal medallion hangs around the torn corpse's neck. The inscription names him Footman Rolf Hartford.",al={"rolf medallion","identifying rolf"},sp=1,gp=true},{q="What happens after finding Rolf?",a="With the fates of Malakai and Rolf confirmed, you are tasked with returning west to the bridge at Eastvale Logging Camp. There, you report the grim news to Guard Thomas.",al={"next quest after rolf","what to do after rolf"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Are the murlocs in Stone Cairn Lake an unusual threat?",a="Murlocs in Elwynn have grown unusually aggressive and coordinated. They are pushing inland into Stone Cairn Lake and the rivers, threatening local trade and lone patrols alike.",al={"murloc threat elwynn","why murlocs attacking"},it="threat"},{q="Why investigate the half-eaten body further?",a="The half-eaten body by the river belongs to Malakai Stone, but his patrol partner Rolf remains unaccounted for. Webbed tracks leading away from the carnage offer the only clue to Rolf's whereabouts, compelling you to press forward and determine whether he managed to escape or met a grim demise deeper within murloc territory.",al={"why search for rolf","half eaten body motive","why look for signs of rolf"},it="motive",add="51025c24"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Finding Rolf shows how exposed Stormwind's rural borders are. Garrison shortages leave even basic patrols open to deadly attacks from the wild.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you see in Rolf Hartford's body the bloody reality faced by footmen serving the realm."},kw={"elwynn forest","guard thomas","malakai","murlocs","rolf","rolf hartford","stone cairn lake"},rel={"quest:37","quest:71","subzone:stone-cairn-lake","topic:murloc","zone:elwynn"},m={start="A half-eaten body",["end"]="Rolf's corpse",faction="Alliance",id=45},src={"Discover Rolf's Fate"}}
E["quest:46"] = {t="quest",n="Bounty on Murlocs",z="elwynn",s="In eastern Elwynn, murlocs are spreading, and the Stormwind Army has set a bounty on them. With the garrison stretched thin, Guard Thomas turns to travelers to clear camps around Stone Cairn Lake and the southern waterways before murlocs overrun nearby farms and roads.",h="In eastern Elwynn, murlocs are spreading, and the Stormwind Army has set a bounty on them.",sec={{t="A Threat on the Waterways",b="Murlocs have made camps around Stone Cairn Lake and along the fork of the southern streams. Lurkers and foragers attack travelers and press toward human settlements. What began as a small nuisance now threatens eastern Elwynn, though the western roads remain comparatively secure.",sp=0},{t="Stretched Defenses",b="Guard Thomas is stationed at the eastern bridge beside the Redridge Mountains. Dangers beyond the bridge and disorder at home both call for his attention. King Varian Wrynn is missing, and bureaucracy weighs on Stormwind's military command. Town garrisons rarely receive the reinforcements they request. So Marshal Dughan and local officers offer public bounties, paying coin for murloc fins to slow the attacks along the waterways.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is there a bounty on murlocs in Elwynn?",a="Murlocs have growing camps around Stone Cairn Lake and the southern streams of eastern Elwynn. Their foraging parties threaten nearby farms, roads, and travelers, so the Stormwind Army pays travelers to cull their numbers.",al={"why kill murlocs","murloc bounty reason","why bounty on murlocs"},it="motive"},{q="Who is paying for the bounty?",a="The Stormwind Army funds the bounty through Goldshire's command under Marshal Dughan. Guard Thomas is the field contact at the eastern river crossing and pays travelers.",al={"who rewards this quest","who pays the bounty","stormwind army bounty"}},{q="Where are the murloc settlements located?",a="Murloc camps line the shores and islands of Stone Cairn Lake to the north. To the south, they follow the riverbanks where the eastern stream forks.",al={"murloc locations elwynn","where are elwynn murlocs","stone cairn lake murlocs"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why can't the Stormwind guards handle this themselves?",a="Stormwind's military is stretched thin across the kingdom by political strife, missing leadership, and banditry. Outposts like Guard Thomas's bridge have only a handful of men, too few to keep up attacks on the shoreline tribes.",al={"why guard thomas needs help","why aren't guards fighting murlocs","guard shortage elwynn"},it="why_me"},{q="What proof of the cull does Guard Thomas require?",a="Guard Thomas asks for torn fins taken from the lurkers and foragers in Elwynn's eastern waterways.",al={"what drops torn murloc fins","quest proof","murloc fins"},it="item"},{q="Does Marshal Dughan know about the severity of the murloc problem?",a="Yes. Guard Thomas says Marshal Dughan is anxious about the murloc threat across eastern Elwynn. Reports of cleared camps matter to local morale.",al={"marshal dughan murlocs","is goldshire aware","dughan reaction"}},{q="What are the murlocs doing in eastern Elwynn?",a="Murloc lurkers and foragers have pushed deep into eastern Elwynn Forest, setting up hostile settlements around Stone Cairn Lake to the north and along the southern river forks. These primitive, aggressive amphibians attack travelers and encroach on farmlands, turning eastern waterways into hazardous ground that the Stormwind Army must actively push back.",al={"why are murlocs in elwynn","murloc threat elwynn","murloc lurkers and foragers"},it="target",add="d8a52c2e"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Clearing the waterways protects supply lines and rural homes between Goldshire and the Redridge border.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you see how thin Stormwind's protection has grown beyond the capital's heartland.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you find marshy shores and reed-lined banks around Stone Cairn Lake suited to stalking nimble aquatic predators that move in swarms."},kw={"bounty","elwynn","fins","foragers","guard thomas","lurkers","marshal dughan","murlocs","stone cairn lake"},rel={"npc:guard-thomas","npc:marshal-dughan","subzone:stone-cairn-lake","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-army","topic:murloc","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Guard Thomas",["end"]="Guard Thomas",faction="Alliance",id=46,ri={"Torn Murloc Fin"}},src={"Bounty on Murlocs"}}
E["quest:47"] = {t="quest",n="Gold Dust Exchange",z="elwynn",s="At Goldshire's crossroads, Gold Dust Exchange brings Remy \"Two Times\" coin for gold dust from kobolds in Elwynn's mines. Travelers gather the dust and trade it to the nervous broker for pay.",h="At Goldshire's crossroads, Gold Dust Exchange brings Remy \"Two Times\" coin for gold dust from kobolds in...",sec={{t="A Town of Pockets and Picks",b="Goldshire sits where Elwynn Forest's roads meet. Travelers, merchants, and guards pass through town. Remy \"Two Times\" is a shady broker with a sharp eye for profit. He repeats his words, and instead of hiring mining crews to dig raw minerals, he offers coin to travelers passing through the Lion's Pride Inn for gold dust taken from kobolds in the region.",sp=0},{t="The Kobold Plunder",b="Kobolds have overrun Fargodeep Mine south of Goldshire and Jasperlode Mine to the northeast. These rat-like tunnelers chip through the dark for candles and shiny baubles, gathering flecks of unrefined ore in their pouches. Driving them back serves the kingdom. Their gold dust also turns the work into a trade for coin.",sp=0},{t="Shadows Behind the Counter",b="Remy says he pays well for ordinary trade, but each payment carries a warning. When he receives the dust, he gives his helpers a small token for his \"associates.\" Bandits, unpaid stonemasons, and hidden networks are active in Stormwind's shadows. Remy's quiet brokers may have plans for the gold beyond village commerce.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Remy \"Two Times\"?",a="Remy \"Two Times\" is a shady local broker outside the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire. He repeats the ends of his sentences, buys precious materials from travelers, and keeps ties with shadowy associates.",al={"remy two times","who gives gold dust exchange","remy in goldshire"},it="identity"},{q="Where do kobolds get gold dust?",a="Kobolds tunnel through Elwynn's mineral veins, including those in Fargodeep and Jasperlode. As they dig through rock for treasure and candle wax, raw gold flakes and dust gather in their pockets and pouches.",al={"why do kobolds have gold dust","where does gold dust come from"},it="origin"},{q="Where can I find the mines mentioned by Remy?",a="Kobolds carrying gold dust are found mainly within and around Fargodeep Mine, south of Goldshire, and Jasperlode Mine, northeast near the border toward the Eastvale Logging Camp.",al={"where are the mines","where to find kobolds elwynn"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Stormwind allow kobolds to control their mines?",a="With King Varian Wrynn missing and the House of Nobles refusing troops for the outskirts, the Stormwind City Guard is stretched thin. Local garrisons cannot clear the mines, leaving kobolds there while independent travelers fight them.",al={"why aren't the mines guarded","why did stormwind lose the mines"},it="conflict"},{q="Is gold dust used for blacksmithing or trade?",a="The particles in the kobolds' raw gold dust are too fine and impure for ordinary forge work. Brokers like Remy take it as a raw commodity, consolidate it, then refine it through their own private channels.",al={"what is gold dust used for","can you smelt gold dust"},it="power",gp=true},{q="Why does Remy \"Two Times\" want gold dust?",a="Remy operates as a shrewd local opportunist buying up valuable resources on the cheap. Rather than braving the dangerous kobold-infested tunnels himself, he relies on adventurous travelers to extract the raw gold dust from the vermin. He turns a quick profit trading in precious metals and uses the dealings to reward you with coin and connections to his associates.",al={"why does remy want gold dust","remy two times motive","why gold dust remy"},it="motive",add="9de6b9cb"},{q="Why does Remy need you instead of getting the gold dust himself?",a="Remy is a merchant and hustler, not a frontline fighter, and he clearly prefers staying safe within Goldshire rather than delving into dark mine shafts. Meanwhile, the local Stormwind garrison is already stretched thin dealing with rampant bandits, gnolls, and the broader kobold problem, leaving little interest or manpower for collecting scattered mineral dust. That makes independent mercenaries like you the ideal solution.",al={"why doesnt remy get gold dust","why does remy need me","why not the stormwind guards"},it="why_me",add="3c82823a"},{q="Why are kobolds in the Elwynn mines carrying gold dust?",a="Kobolds are natural burrowers who have overrun abandoned and lightly defended mines across Elwynn, including Fargodeep Mine and Jasperlode Mine. Driven by an obsessive urge to dig and hoard shiny trinkets, they chip away at the subterranean veins day and night. The loose gold dust accumulates on their paws, clothes, and pouches as they scramble through the shafts.",al={"why are kobolds in the mines","why do kobolds have gold dust","kobolds fargodeep mine"},it="target",add="27e84318"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Miners searching Fargodeep and Jasperlode find kobolds clinging to the richest copper veins. Clearing them out is necessary to harvest ore.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you may read Remy's hushed manner and the token from unnamed \"associates\" as signs of underground syndicates beneath Goldshire's placid surface.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see Elwynn's vital gold and mineral deposits in the hands of feral kobolds rather than royal excavators. The kingdom's military forces are depleted."},kw={"elwynn forest","fargodeep mine","gold dust","goldshire","jasperlode mine","kobold","remy two times"},rel={"npc:remy-two-times","topic:kobold","subzone:fargodeep-mine","subzone:jasperlode-mine","subzone:goldshire","quest:62","quest:76","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Remy \"Two Times\"",faction="Alliance",id=47,ri={"Gold Dust"}},src={"Gold Dust Exchange"}}
E["quest:52"] = {t="quest",n="Protect the Frontier",z="elwynn",s="At Elwynn's eastern bridge, Guard Thomas asks you to thin the wolves and bears threatening travelers and workers near Eastvale Logging Camp. The beasts have grown bold, putting roads and logging crews at risk.",h="At Elwynn's eastern bridge, Guard Thomas asks you to thin the wolves and bears threatening travelers and...",sec={{t="A Thinning Defense",b="Goldshire and Northshire Valley have visible Stormwind garrisons. The eastern frontier has far fewer guards. Guard Thomas watches the river crossing, one of the few sentries between the settled heartlands and the wilderness. Travelers help keep the supply roads open.",sp=0},{t="The Predatory Threat",b="Eastvale Logging Camp sends timber to Stormwind City. Woodsmen cutting trees at the forest's edge face prowlers, gray forest wolves, and young forest bears near the roads and lumber yards. Culling the beasts eases the danger to local workers for a time. Thomas suspects something deeper in the woods is driving them toward settlements.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Protect the Frontier?",a="Guard Thomas gives the order. He watches the eastern bridge on Elwynn Forest's main road, between the forest interior and the Eastvale region.",al={"quest giver protect the frontier","who starts protect the frontier","guard thomas quest"},it="identity"},{q="Why are wolves and bears attacking the frontier?",a="Wolves and bears press near roads and work sites around Eastvale Logging Camp. Thomas suspects something deeper in the wilderness is agitating them and driving them toward settled ground.",al={"why are bears aggressive","why are wolves attacking eastvale","animal attacks elwynn"},it="threat"},{q="Where is the Eastvale Logging Camp?",a="Eastvale Logging Camp lies in eastern Elwynn Forest, just east of Guard Thomas's bridge. It supplies vital lumber to Stormwind and border settlements.",al={"eastvale location","where is logging camp elwynn","eastvale camp"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Guard Thomas watching the bridge alone?",a="Stormwind's army and city guard are stretched thin across the kingdom. River and crossroads outposts often have only one or two guards watching the highways, so they rely on travelers to handle large wildlife threats.",al={"why is guard thomas alone","guard thomas post","stormwind guards eastvale"},it="why_me"},{q="What animals need to be culled for this task?",a="You need to slay eight wolves, either prowlers or gray forest wolves, and five young forest bears roaming eastern Elwynn Forest.",al={"protect the frontier targets","wolves and bears to kill","what mobs for protect the frontier"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What happens once the wildlife is culled?",a="When you report back, Guard Thomas thanks you, and logging caravans can travel more safely. He remains wary that the dark influence stirring the beasts may bring further trouble to the forest.",al={"protect the frontier follow up","turn in protect the frontier"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Guard Thomas want the wild beasts culled?",a="The Eastvale Logging Camp is under constant assault from increasingly aggressive wolves and bears prowling eastern Elwynn Forest. Guard Thomas is stationed at the eastern bridge to protect workers and travelers along the road, but the predators are bold enough to disrupt vital logging operations and threaten anyone stepping beyond the camp perimeter.",al={"why cull wolves guard thomas","protect the frontier why","why protect eastvale"},it="motive",add="ad29ae35"},{q="What animals are you sent against in Protect the Frontier?",a="You are sent to cull the prowlers, gray forest wolves, and young forest bears roaming the woods surrounding the Eastvale Logging Camp. Typically timid wildlife in western Elwynn has turned unusually vicious and bold here on the frontier, making everyday travel and lumber work perilous.",al={"what wolves and bears protect the frontier","protect the frontier beasts","which animals guard thomas"},it="target",add="ce43057a"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Keeping the eastern roads secure helps Eastvale's lumber reach Alliance lands, where it supports reconstruction and defense.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can test your tracking and marksmanship against the wolves and bears stalking eastern Elwynn Forest."},kw={"eastvale logging camp","elwynn forest","gray forest wolf","guard thomas","protect the frontier","prowler","young forest bear"},rel={"npc:guard-thomas","subzone:eastvale-logging-camp","zone:elwynn","subzone:goldshire"},m={start="Guard Thomas",faction="Alliance",id=52},src={"Protect the Frontier"}}
E["quest:5261"] = {t="quest",n="Eagan Peltskinner",z="elwynn",s="Timber wolves threaten Northshire Valley, and Eagan Peltskinner has work for recruits outside the abbey. The local furrier needs hunters to thin the packs and bring back pelts.",h="Timber wolves threaten Northshire Valley, and Eagan Peltskinner has work for recruits outside the abbey.",sec={{t="A Word with the Furrier",b="Deputy Willem often sends abbey recruits to find Eagan Peltskinner on the nearby grounds. Northshire Valley's orchards and fields meet wild woods where timber wolves prowl. Eagan asks newcomers to hunt the aggressive packs and gather pelts for his craft.",sp=0},{t="Trouble on the Perimeter",b="Timber wolves threaten workers, acolytes, and supplies traveling to and from Northshire. Sending young champions to Eagan helps keep nearby paths safe and leaves Stormwind's few remaining guards free for other duties. Those guards are already occupied by rising tensions across Elwynn Forest.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to speak with Eagan Peltskinner?",a="Deputy Willem sends promising recruits to Eagan after telling them about the valley's security concerns. He waits outside Northshire Abbey's entrance.",al={"who gives this quest","who starts eagan peltskinner quest"},it="origin"},{q="Where is Eagan Peltskinner located?",a="Eagan Peltskinner works near Northshire Abbey's outer walls, around the left side of the main building, among his drying racks and gear.",al={"where is eagan","eagan peltskinner location","find eagan"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Eagan Peltskinner need help with?",a="Eagan needs a hunter to kill aggressive timber wolves in the surrounding woods and bring back their pelts. This helps clear Northshire's perimeter.",al={"what does eagan want","why hunt wolves","eagan purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Can you skip this quest and talk to Eagan directly?",a="Yes. Eagan offers hunting work to anyone who approaches him. Speaking with him first means you miss Deputy Willem's introduction.",al={"can i skip eagan quest","wolves across the border directly"},gp=true},{q="Why are there so many wolves in Northshire Valley?",a="Northshire Valley borders dense, untamed woodlands where timber wolves roam freely. Local guards are stretched thin by other threats across the kingdom, leaving the predators unchecked.",al={"why wolves in northshire","wolf problem elwynn"},it="threat"},{q="What task follows speaking with Eagan Peltskinner?",a="After speaking with Eagan, you are asked to hunt timber wolves beyond the abbey grounds and collect their tough pelts.",al={"next quest after eagan","what does eagan offer next"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Deputy Willem send you to Eagan Peltskinner?",a="Deputy Willem is tasked with maintaining security around Northshire Abbey. With wolf sightings surging across the valley, a hunter requesting help culling the pack is a welcome opportunity. Willem directs willing recruits to Eagan so the abbey's limited guards can focus on larger concerns while still curbing the predators encroaching on the settlement.",al={"why willem sends you to eagan","willem motive eagan peltskinner","why visit eagan"},it="motive",add="b90d340a"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Every small task in Northshire helps secure Stormwind's home territory while the kingdom's core army remains stretched thin elsewhere.",["race:Human"]="As a young human leaving Northshire Abbey, you first learn to defend your homeland by helping local tradesfolk like Eagan."},kw={"deputy willem","eagan peltskinner","northshire abbey","northshire valley","timber wolves","wolves across the border"},rel={"quest:783","quest:33","subzone:northshire-valley","zone:elwynn"},m={level="2",faction="Alliance",id=5261},src={"Eagan Peltskinner (quest)"}}
E["quest:54"] = {t="quest",n="Report to Goldshire",z="elwynn",s="Marshal McBride sends you south to Goldshire with dispatches for Marshal Dughan. Beyond Northshire's sheltered valley, Stormwind's nobles give Elwynn Forest less and less thought.",h="Marshal McBride sends you south to Goldshire with dispatches for Marshal Dughan.",sec={{t="From Northshire to the Greater Forest",b="You've proved yourself against Northshire's troubles, and McBride releases you from the valley's guard. His transfer papers send you past the border gates and down the road to Goldshire. From there, your duty reaches across the wider forest.",sp=0},{t="The Burden of the Marshals",b="Marshal Dughan waits in Goldshire to receive McBride's dispatches and make you an Acting Deputy of the Stormwind Marshals. His welcome carries a grim warning: beside the dangers roaming Elwynn, Northshire is a peaceful garden. Stormwind's royal army is bound up in distant nobles' politics, instead of guarding home ground.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Marshal Dughan?",a="Marshal Dughan commands the Stormwind Marshals in Goldshire. He oversees Elwynn Forest's defenses and patrols.",al={"who is marshal dughan","where is dughan","dughan role"}},{q="Why are recruits sent to Goldshire?",a="When recruits have dealt with trouble in Northshire Valley, Marshal McBride sends those who prove capable south to Goldshire. The dangers there stretch across all of Elwynn Forest.",al={"why go to goldshire","leaving northshire","next step after northshire"}},{q="What does Acting Deputy Status mean?",a="Acting Deputy is a field rank granted with Marshal McBride's papers. It brings promising recruits into the Stormwind Marshals to help keep the law.",al={"acting deputy","what is acting deputy status","deputy status meaning"}},{q="Where is the Stormwind army?",a="Marshal Dughan says most of Stormwind's standing army is away. The court nobles keep it busy with their duties instead of patrolling the towns and farms at home.",al={"where is stormwind army","stormwind army missing","why is elwynn unprotected"}},{q="Who is Marshal McBride?",a="Marshal McBride commands the garrison at Northshire Abbey. He trains new defenders and sends those who prove themselves to the front line at Goldshire.",al={"who is mcbride","mcbride role"}},{q="How do you find Goldshire from Northshire?",a="Follow the main road south out of Northshire Valley, past the border gates and into Elwynn Forest's heart. Goldshire lies along the road.",al={"goldshire road","how to get to goldshire","direction to goldshire"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, your move from Northshire to Goldshire is your first real recognition from Stormwind's military.",["faction:Alliance"]="With Stormwind's army sent elsewhere, Elwynn's defense rests more and more on newly deputized recruits and volunteers like you."},kw={"acting deputy","elwynn forest","goldshire","marshal dughan","marshal mcbride","northshire","report to goldshire","stormwind marshals"},rel={"npc:marshal-dughan","npc:marshal-mcbride","subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={faction="Alliance",id=54},src={"In-game quest text: Report to Goldshire"},fv=true}
E["quest:5545"] = {t="quest",n="A Bundle of Trouble",z="elwynn",s="At Eastvale Logging Camp, Supervisor Raelen races to meet a timber shipment deadline for Stormwind. Wolves and bears have driven her woodcutters from the northern woods, leaving the cut bundles behind.",h="At Eastvale Logging Camp, Supervisor Raelen races to meet a timber shipment deadline for Stormwind.",sec={{t="A Looming Deadline",b="Eastvale's timber rebuilds towns and strengthens bridges across the kingdom, yet this vital shipment has fallen behind. The delivery deadline is drawing near, and Supervisor Raelen has little time to spare.",sp=0},{t="Predators in the Timber",b="North of the camp, wolves and bears drove the woodcutters from the bundles they cut and tied. Raelen cannot wait for guards to clear the woods, so she asks you to bring the timber back before the contract is lost.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Supervisor Raelen?",a="Supervisor Raelen manages Eastvale Logging Camp in eastern Elwynn Forest. She oversees the woodcutters and timber shipments bound for Stormwind and nearby settlements.",al={"supervisor raelen","raelen","eastvale supervisor"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the wood abandoned in the woods?",a="The laborers had cut and bundled the logs before bears and wolves drove them from the clearing. They fled to camp without the wood.",al={"why wood left","abandoned lumber","forest wood"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Raelen mention Deputy Rainer?",a="Raelen says she contacted Deputy Rainer about the predators. He is stationed at Westbrook Garrison, far across Elwynn Forest. The message may have passed through the guards, or local authority may be stretched thin.",al={"deputy rainer raelen","why deputy rainer","rainer connection"},it="ties"},{q="Where is the lumber needed?",a="Eastvale Logging Camp sends timber throughout the kingdom to rebuild towns and strengthen palisades and bridges. A missed deadline can hurt Elwynn's economy and delay construction.",al={"who needs the wood","lumber delivery","timber purpose"},it="item"},{q="Why can't the loggers collect the wood themselves?",a="The woodcutters are laborers who fell trees, not fighters trained to face predators. Wolves and bears drove them away, and they will not return to the thicket unarmed.",al={"why loggers scared","why not loggers","loggers wolves"},it="why_me"},{q="Where can the bundles of wood be found?",a="The bundles lie in the woods just north of Eastvale Logging Camp, where the laborers were working before local beasts drove them away.",al={"wood location","where are bundles","find bundles"},gp=true},{q="Why does Supervisor Raelen need this lumber so quickly?",a="Supervisor Raelen is facing a strict delivery deadline for an order of timber. If she fails to supply the promised wood on time, Eastvale's logging operations and her reputation suffer. The wood is already chopped, but the camp's laborers were forced to flee when wild predators moved in, putting the entire shipment at risk.",al={"why does raelen need wood","raelen deadline","why rush lumber order"},it="motive",add="d8093908"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can help keep Stormwind's rebuilding and regional outposts supplied with lumber from Eastvale.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can track through predator-filled groves and face the local beasts while recovering the supplies."},kw={"bears","bundle of wood","deputy rainer","eastvale","elwynn forest","logging camp","supervisor raelen","timber","wolves"},rel={"npc:supervisor-raelen","subzone:eastvale-logging-camp","npc:deputy-rainer","zone:elwynn","subzone:westbrook-garrison"},m={start="Supervisor Raelen",faction="Alliance",id=5545,ri={"Bundle of Wood"}},src={"A Bundle of Trouble"}}
E["quest:5623"] = {t="quest",n="In Favor of the Light",z="elwynn",s="At Northshire Abbey, Priestess Anetta sends you south to continue your training in Goldshire. Priestess Josetta waits at the Lion's Pride Inn to guide your next steps in the Holy Light.",h="At Northshire Abbey, Priestess Anetta sends you south to continue your training in Goldshire.",sec={{t="Stepping Beyond Northshire",b="Your training carries you beyond Northshire Abbey's cloistered halls and into the lives of Elwynn's people. You leave secluded study for active ministry, where the Holy Light must answer everyday needs beyond the abbey's walls.",sp=0},{t="Tutelage in Goldshire",b="At the Lion's Pride Inn, Priestess Josetta tends to Goldshire's spiritual needs and guides rising acolytes. She builds on your lessons and teaches you to offer comfort, protect the faithful, and heal the injured. Under her guidance, you learn the duties of the Church's servants across the kingdom, including caring for a wounded guard and receiving ceremonial clerical vestments.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who starts this quest and who do I report to?",a="Priestess Anetta gives you instructions inside Northshire Abbey and sends you down the road to meet Priestess Josetta in Goldshire.",al={"who gives in favor of the light","quest turn in","where to turn in in favor of the light"},it="identity",gp=true},{q="Why is a priest sent away from Northshire so early?",a="Northshire teaches you the foundations of the Holy Light, while Goldshire lets you serve a real community. Under Josetta's direction, you can help townspeople and town guards.",al={"why go to goldshire","why leave northshire abbey"},it="motive"},{q="Where can Priestess Josetta be found in Goldshire?",a="Priestess Josetta is inside the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, where she trains priests.",al={"where is priestess josetta","find josetta","josetta location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after meeting Priestess Josetta?",a="After you meet Priestess Josetta, she tests your training by asking you to care for a wounded guard and receive ceremonial clerical vestments.",al={"next quest after in favor of the light","what follows in favor of the light"},it="next_step"},{q="Is this quest restricted to priests?",a="Yes. These teachings are for priest initiates learning to serve the Church of the Holy Light.",al={"can any class do in favor of the light","is this priest only"},it="for_you",gp=true},{q="What role does the Church of the Holy Light play in Elwynn?",a="The Church of the Holy Light offers comfort, spiritual guidance, and healing to townspeople and defenders facing bandits and dangerous wildlife in Elwynn.",al={"church of the holy light role","priests in elwynn"},it="history"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you leave your sheltered studies in Northshire to serve the people and garrisons of Elwynn Forest.",["race:Human"]="As a human of Stormwind, you can seek the priesthood's guidance in Goldshire as you help uphold your kingdom's moral and spiritual life.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can look to the Church of the Holy Light for healers who tend to those defending the Alliance."},kw={"anetta","church","elwynn forest","goldshire","holy light","josetta","northshire","priest quest"},rel={"quest:5624","npc:priestess-josetta","npc:priestess-anetta","topic:light","subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Priestess Anetta",["end"]="Priestess Josetta",level="4",faction="Alliance",cl={"PRIEST"},ra={"Human"},id=5623},src={"In Favor of the Light (Elwynn Forest)"}}
E["quest:5624"] = {t="quest",n="Garments of the Light",z="elwynn",s="Priestess Josetta sends you east of Goldshire to Crystal Lake, where Guard Roberts lies wounded. His recovery matters to the town, and the Church of the Holy Light will recognize your service.",h="Priestess Josetta sends you east of Goldshire to Crystal Lake, where Guard Roberts lies wounded.",sec={{t="A Practical Test of Faith",b="Josetta asks you to put divine power to use before the Church recognizes a novice priest. Guard Roberts needs healing, giving you a chance to serve someone in need. Tending him is your first step toward formal standing in the Church of the Holy Light.",sp=0},{t="Sustaining the Realm",b="Close Roberts's wounds with restorative prayers, then strengthen him with a blessing of fortitude. He needs healing and resilience to return to his duties. Your care helps a town guard withstand danger, and supports the township. Josetta expects a priest to sustain defenders as well as mend them.",sp=0},{t="Vestments of the Order",b="Once Roberts has been treated, return to the Lion’s Pride Inn for your first formal robes. They mark the approval and fellowship of Stormwind's priesthood, though further training does not require them. The Church recognizes you as a servant of the Holy Light.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Guard Roberts?",a="Guard Roberts is just east of Goldshire, near Crystal Lake. He rests by the roadside at the water’s edge while he recovers from wounds suffered on watch.",al={"guard roberts location","where is guard roberts","find guard roberts"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What spells are required to complete this quest?",a="Use Lesser Heal Rank 2 to restore Guard Roberts’s health, then cast Power Word: Fortitude to strengthen him. Return to Priestess Josetta afterward.",al={"spells needed","what spells do i cast on roberts","how to heal guard roberts"},it="power",gp=true},{q="Who is Priestess Josetta?",a="Priestess Josetta trains priests for the Church of the Holy Light at the Lion’s Pride Inn in Goldshire. She guides young acolytes from Northshire Abbey in practical service and divine magic.",al={"josetta lore","priestess josetta goldshire","who gives garments of the light"},it="identity"},{q="Why does the Church give out robes for this task?",a="The robes show the Church of the Holy Light approves of the acolyte and supports their ministry. Caring for Guard Roberts demonstrates the skill and discipline needed to wear the church’s vestments.",al={"why garments of the light","priest robe reward lore","church robes meaning"},it="purpose"},{q="Can other classes complete this quest?",a="No. Only Alliance priests can complete this trial in their introductory training, after learning fundamental healing and warding prayers.",al={"is garments of the light priest only","can paladins do garments of the light","priest class quest"},it="why_me",gp=true},{q="What happens after completing Garments of the Light?",a="After your early priest training in Goldshire, there is no immediate follow-up. Priestess Josetta and other trainers throughout the kingdom offer further training and trials as you gain experience.",al={"next quest after garments of the light","garments of the light followup"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Priestess Josetta want this done?",a="Priestess Josetta usually sets a minor challenge to test novice priests before the Church of the Holy Light officially recognizes them with their vestments. Hearing word that a town guard lies wounded near the lake east of Goldshire, she sees an opportunity to test your healing and protective magic in the field while helping secure the safety of the town.",al={"why does josetta send you","priestess josetta motive","why heal guard roberts"},it="motive",add="45956511"},{q="Who is Guard Roberts?",a="Guard Roberts is a Stormwind guard stationed around Goldshire who was wounded near the lake east of town. With threats pressing in on Elwynn Forest, every able defender counts, making his recovery vital to the township's protection.",al={"guard roberts","who is the injured guard","injured guard roberts"},it="target",add="010a8804"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you carry what you learned in Northshire into service in the field. Healing and fortifying allies helps keep those on the front line alive.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see local church disciples helping town guards hold their ground while Stormwind’s army is stretched thin and absent from hamlets.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you belong to a culture that honors the Church of the Holy Light. Earning vestments from a township priestess marks an important civic and spiritual milestone."},kw={"crystal lake","elwynn forest","garments of the light","goldshire","guard roberts","lesser heal","power word fortitude","priest robe","priestess josetta"},rel={"npc:priestess-josetta","subzone:goldshire","quest:5623","zone:elwynn","topic:light"},m={start="Priestess Josetta",level="4",faction="Alliance",cl={"PRIEST"},ra={"Human"},id=5624},src={"Garments of the Light (Elwynn Forest)"}}
E["quest:5628"] = {t="quest",n="Returning Home",z="elwynn",s="In Goldshire, a novice night elf priest hears an urgent call from Darnassus. Priestess Josetta carries the message: return to the Temple of the Moon and continue training under Priestess Alathea.",h="In Goldshire, a novice night elf priest hears an urgent call from Darnassus.",sec={{t="A Word in Goldshire",b="Night elves are rare in Elwynn Forest, and a young acolyte among its human settlements draws attention. When you reach Goldshire, Priestess Josetta greets you with news. A Sister of Elune has traveled across continents seeking you, bearing an urgent command from the Temple of the Moon. Your calling now leads back to Kalimdor, where your training can advance.",sp=0},{t="The Call of the Temple",b="Darnassus looks to the Temple of the Moon for night elf faith and leadership. Priestess Alathea and High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind oversee the Sisterhood’s instruction, keeping watch over disciples even when curiosity carries them overseas. When you return, the priestesses welcome you with motherly concern. Then they begin your deeper studies of the Moon Goddess’s celestial mysteries.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is a night elf priest being summoned from human lands?",a="Young night elf priests who travel to the Eastern Kingdoms remain bound to their sacred order in Teldrassil. Priestess Alathea follows their progress and calls them back to the Temple of the Moon when they are ready to learn higher rites of Elune.",al={"why am i called back","why returning home","priest quest goldshire"},it="why_me"},{q="Who is Priestess Josetta?",a="Priestess Josetta is the human priest trainer at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire. She serves the Holy Light and respects visiting kaldorei acolytes, helping emissaries from Darnassus reach their wayward kin.",al={"who gives returning home","goldshire priest trainer","priestess josetta"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Priestess Alathea?",a="Priestess Alathea is a senior Sister of Elune who trains acolytes at the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus. She works with High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind to watch novice night elf priests’ growth and spiritual dedication.",al={"who is alathea","temple priest trainer","priestess alathea"},it="identity"},{q="What happens after returning to Darnassus?",a="When you report to Priestess Alathea at the Temple of the Moon, she welcomes you home and gives you your next task, Stars of Elune. There, you explore the sacred power granted by the goddess.",al={"what comes next","next quest after returning home","followup quest"},it="next_step"},{q="How does this differ from the normal training path?",a="This alternate path guides night elf priests who choose to train in human lands such as Elwynn Forest back to their racial trainers in Darnassus. There, they can learn their race-specific priestly abilities.",al={"do all priests do this","is this quest mandatory","elwynn priest quest"}},{q="How did the messenger find an acolyte all the way in Elwynn Forest?",a="A Sister of Elune travels from Darnassus to the Eastern Kingdoms and leaves word with Alliance trainers such as Priestess Josetta in Goldshire. Josetta watches for the traveling novice and directs them home.",al={"how did they know i was here","who tracked me to goldshire"}},{q="Why does Priestess Josetta want you to return to Darnassus?",a="Priestess Josetta is not directing your training herself; she is passing along an urgent summons from your own people. A priestess from Darnassus came searching specifically for you in Goldshire, asking that you report back to Priestess Alathea at the Temple of the Moon. Josetta recognizes how far you have journeyed from home at an early age, but as a fellow servant of the divine, she knows that advanced spiritual instruction from your mentors takes precedence over wandering foreign lands.",al={"why does josetta send you back","priestess josetta motive","why return to darnassus"},it="motive",add="50552740"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="Every priest order has deep roots in tradition. As a kaldorei acolyte, you advance in the lunar rites only with senior priestesses’ approval at the Temple of the Moon.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you may travel far across the sea to the lands of the younger races, but Teldrassil and Elune’s blessings draw you back to your sacred sanctuaries.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see growing cooperation between the Church of the Holy Light in Elwynn and the Sisterhood of Elune in Darnassus. Their hospitality strengthens the bonds between Alliance races."},kw={"darnassus","elune","goldshire","priestess alathea","priestess josetta","returning home","stars of elune","temple of the moon"},rel={"quest:5627","npc:priestess-alathea","npc:priestess-josetta","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","zone:darnassus","topic:elune","quest:2519"},m={start="Priestess Josetta",["end"]="Priestess Alathea",level="10",faction="Alliance",cl={"PRIEST"},ra={"NightElf"},id=5628,xg=5631},src={"Returning Home (Elwynn Forest)"}}
E["quest:5635"] = {t="quest",n="Desperate Prayer",z="elwynn",s="In Stormwind, promising priests from Elwynn Forest come for deeper training in the Church of the Holy Light. After proving their devotion and discipline, they present themselves to High Priestess Laurena at the Cathedral of Light.",h="In Stormwind, promising priests from Elwynn Forest come for deeper training in the Church of the Holy Light.",sec={{t="A Summons to the Capital",b="Priestess Josetta guides novice priests in Goldshire, while local mentors serve Elwynn Forest's outlying settlements. When a disciple proves capable in spirit and deeds, word reaches Stormwind's senior priesthood. A summons to the Cathedral of Light marks a move to deeper duties in the faith and formal training at the spiritual heart of the Kingdom of Stormwind.",sp=0},{t="Guidance from the High Priestess",b="At the Cathedral, acolytes come before High Priestess Laurena, a senior leader of the Church in Stormwind. She oversees their spiritual grounding and practical training as newly elevated priests. Her instruction prepares them for the Alliance's harsh trials and teaches the Light's miracles, including Desperate Prayer, a plea for salvation known among human practitioners.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the quest Desperate Prayer?",a="Desperate Prayer sends promising priests from Goldshire to Stormwind's Cathedral of Light for further training under High Priestess Laurena.",al={"desperate prayer quest","what is desperate prayer quest","why do desperate prayer"},it="purpose"},{q="Who gives the quest Desperate Prayer?",a="Priestess Josetta, the priest trainer at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, gives you the summons after you prove your devotion.",al={"who starts desperate prayer","desperate prayer quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Who is High Priestess Laurena?",a="High Priestess Laurena is a senior leader of the Church of the Holy Light who trains acolytes inside Stormwind's Cathedral of Light.",al={"who is laurena","high priestess laurena lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the Cathedral of Light located?",a="The Cathedral of Light is in Cathedral Square, in Stormwind City's northern district. It is the kingdom's spiritual center for priests and paladins.",al={"where is cathedral of light","cathedral location stormwind"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the quest named Desperate Prayer?",a="Human priests learn Desperate Prayer in Stormwind as a plea to the Light for immediate, self-preserving deliverance.",al={"why called desperate prayer","desperate prayer name meaning"},it="name"},{q="Do other races or classes get this quest?",a="This instruction is for priests advancing from Elwynn Forest to begin higher training in Stormwind.",al={"can dwarves do desperate prayer quest","is desperate prayer priest only"},gp=true},{q="Why does Priestess Josetta want you to visit the Cathedral of Light?",a="Priestess Josetta is acting on orders from the Church hierarchy. You have proven your devotion and capability in the field, drawing the attention of the church superiors in Stormwind. Josetta's role is to direct promising young acolytes toward higher mentorship, and she sends you to the Cathedral of Light so you can receive more advanced instruction in the ways of the Light.",al={"why does josetta send you","priestess josetta motive","why visit stormwind priest"},it="motive",add="24d97f9e"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you move from novice service in Goldshire to training under the Cathedral of Light's senior leadership.",["race:Human"]="As a human who follows the Holy Light, entering the Cathedral of Light affirms your duty to the kingdom's spiritual heart.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you belong to a people bound in part by the Church of the Holy Light, one of its strongest cultural and moral pillars amid looming threats."},kw={"cathedral of light","desperate prayer","goldshire","high priestess laurena","holy light","priest","priestess josetta","stormwind"},rel={"npc:high-priestess-laurena","npc:priestess-josetta","subzone:cathedral-of-light","topic:light","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Priestess Josetta",["end"]="High Priestess Laurena",level="10",faction="Alliance",cl={"PRIEST"},ra={"Dwarf","Human"},id=5635,xg=5634},src={"Desperate Prayer (Goldshire)"}}
E["quest:59"] = {t="quest",n="Cloth and Leather Armor",z="elwynn",s="In Goldshire, Cloth and Leather Armor sends a trusted traveler east for gear. Marshal Dughan issues an armor marker for Sara Timberlain at Eastvale Logging Camp. Beyond Guard Thomas's bridge, recruits seek armor for the realm's defense.",h="In Goldshire, Cloth and Leather Armor sends a trusted traveler east for gear.",sec={{t="The Marshal's Token",b="Guard Thomas watches Elwynn's eastern river crossing, where murlocs and gnolls threaten the border. You carry his report to Goldshire, and Marshal Dughan marks your service with an official Stormwind Armor Marker. Goldshire's garrison has few stores, so Dughan gives you a marker instead of equipment. It is a military voucher recording your service to the crown.",sp=0},{t="The Weaver of Eastvale",b="East of Guard Thomas's bridge lies Eastvale Logging Camp, Elwynn's main timber operation. Sara Timberlain works there under commission from the Stormwind Army, making cloth and leather gear. The kingdom's central armories are strained, so local artisans like Sara outfit troops and auxiliary scouts on the frontier.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a Stormwind Armor Marker?",a="A Stormwind Armor Marker is an official military requisition slip issued by officers such as Marshal Dughan. Trusted recruits can claim custom-fitted armor from civilian artisans commissioned by the army, rather than having officers keep bulky armor sets at their posts.",al={"armor marker","stormwind voucher","what is the marker"},it="item"},{q="Who is Sara Timberlain?",a="Sara Timberlain is a tailor and crafter who lives at Eastvale Logging Camp. Under contract with the Stormwind Army, she makes cloth and leather equipment for kingdom personnel and authorized auxiliary fighters.",al={"sara timberlain","eastvale tailor","who makes the armor"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the Eastvale Logging Camp?",a="Eastvale Logging Camp lies in far eastern Elwynn Forest. From Guard Thomas's river bridge post, take the road east into the wooded valley, where woodcutters harvest timber for the kingdom.",al={"eastvale location","where is eastvale","how to get to timberlain"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Marshal Dughan send adventurers to Eastvale?",a="Marshal Dughan directs recruits to Sara Timberlain at Eastvale because he does not hand out finished gear from his Goldshire post. After brave deeds, he sends travelers east to obtain proper protection for Elwynn's defense.",al={"why marshal dughan marker","dughan purpose","why eastvale"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is the army relying on local tailors for supplies?",a="King Varian Wrynn is missing, and Stormwind's military is spread thin responding to Defias activity and wild beasts. Local defense posts depend on contracted regional workers to keep supplies moving.",al={"stormwind supply problems","why local artisan","army logistics"},it="history"},{q="Who is Guard Thomas defending against?",a="Guard Thomas watches Elwynn Forest's eastern border and the bridge against river murlocs, prowling beasts, and the dangerous wilderness by the Redridge Mountains.",al={"guard thomas enemies","threats at bridge","eastern elwynn threats"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Marshal Dughan want this done?",a="Marshal Dughan wants to reward your valor and shrewdness after you carried Guard Thomas's report from the eastern border. By handing you an official requisition marker for Sara Timberlain, he ensures you are properly outfitted in sturdy cloth or leather to continue defending Elwynn Forest against mounting threats.",al={"marshal dughan motive","why send to sara timberlain","why give armor marker"},it="motive",add="ebb61187"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance defender, you see how local contracts help Elwynn's rural communities keep the Alliance functioning while the capital is politically paralyzed.",["race:Human"]="As a human, your service to Marshal Dughan and dealings with Sara Timberlain reflect the civic bonds that hold Elwynn's small homesteads together.",["profession:Tailoring"]="As a tailor, you can see in Sara Timberlain's army commission that cloth crafting is an officially sponsored military trade in the kingdom."},kw={"armor marker","cloth and leather armor","eastvale","elwynn forest","guard thomas","logging camp","marshal dughan","sara timberlain","stormwind army"},rel={"npc:guard-thomas","npc:marshal-dughan","npc:sara-timberlain","subzone:eastvale-logging-camp","quest:39","topic:stormwind-army","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Marshal Dughan",["end"]="Sara Timberlain",faction="Alliance",id=59},src={"Cloth and Leather Armor"}}
E["quest:6"] = {t="quest",n="Bounty on Garrick Padfoot",z="elwynn",s="Near Northshire Abbey, an Alliance bounty calls recruits to hunt Garrick Padfoot by the vineyards. The notorious thief and his gang threaten the valley's farmers and merchants.",h="Near Northshire Abbey, an Alliance bounty calls recruits to hunt Garrick Padfoot by the vineyards.",sec={{t="A Plague on the Valley",b="Northshire Valley offered a safe place to train recruits and tend its sacred vineyards. But as order falters across Elwynn, thieves have reached the valley. Garrick Padfoot, a cutthroat, quickly rose to lead them. For weeks, he and his gang have plundered shipments, robbed merchants on the roads, and threatened local farmers.",sp=0},{t="Deputy Willem's Justice",b="Stormwind's guards are stretched thin, protecting the capital and its outer borders. So local marshals and deputies rely on volunteers to keep Northshire peaceful. Deputy Willem posts a public bounty on Garrick's head, hoping to rid the valley of his gang. Padfoot's rundown shack lies east of the river. Bringing him down there strikes at the lawlessness spreading through the human heartland.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Garrick Padfoot?",a="Garrick Padfoot is a bandit and cutthroat in Northshire Valley. For weeks, he has harassed local farmers and ambushed merchants, gathering a small ring of thugs near the vineyards.",al={"garrick padfoot","who is garrick","padfoot"},it="target"},{q="Where can Garrick Padfoot be found?",a="Garrick Padfoot hides in a small wooden shack east of Northshire Abbey, across the river bridge and near the vineyards. Fellow thugs guard him.",al={"where is garrick padfoot","garrick location","garrick shack"},gp=true},{q="Who issues the bounty on Garrick?",a="Deputy Willem, stationed outside Northshire Abbey, posts the bounty. With too few city guards to police the valley, he calls on wandering recruits to bring the outlaw to justice.",al={"who gives bounty on garrick padfoot","willem bounty"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why is Stormwind not sending regular soldiers to deal with him?",a="Stormwind's military is stretched too thin. With King Varian Wrynn missing and tensions rising across Elwynn Forest and beyond, the capital cannot spare veteran garrisons for every small-time thug. Local deputies must call on recruits.",al={"why don't guards kill garrick","where are stormwind guards"},it="why_me"},{q="Is Garrick Padfoot working alone?",a="No. Garrick has gathered a small gang of outlaws and bandits who camp around his shack near the Northshire vineyards to protect him.",al={"is garrick solo","padfoot gang"},it="allies"},{q="What proof does Deputy Willem require?",a="Deputy Willem requires physical proof before paying the coin: bring Garrick Padfoot's severed head back to Northshire Abbey.",al={"proof of garrick death","garricks head"},it="item"},{q="Why does Deputy Willem want Garrick Padfoot killed?",a="Garrick Padfoot has spent weeks terrorizing Northshire Valley. As a cutthroat leading a gang of thieves, he actively preys upon the local farmers and traveling merchants who sustain the valley. Deputy Willem wants him dead to put an end to his raids, restore safety to the vineyards and roads, and protect the abbey's community from further violence.",al={"why kill garrick padfoot","deputy willem motive","why does willem want garrick dead"},it="motive",add="38d5a8ce"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Bringing down Garrick Padfoot is an early service for an aspiring Alliance adventurer, helping restore stability to the Kingdom of Stormwind.",["race:Human"]="As a human raised in the kingdom, you have reason to protect your homeland's sacred ground and local farmers from cutthroats like Padfoot.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you see how outlaws operate in Elwynn's shadows. A poorly hidden hideout invites a swift blade."},kw={"bounty","cutthroat","elwynn","garrick","northshire","padfoot","thieves","vineyard","willem"},rel={"subzone:northshire-abbey","quest:18","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Deputy Willem",level="5",faction="Alliance",id=6,ri={"Garrick's Head"}},src={"Bounty on Garrick Padfoot"}}
E["quest:60"] = {t="quest",n="Kobold Candles",z="elwynn",s="At the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, William Pestle seeks candles from kobolds crowding Elwynn's mines. The alchemist has come from his Stormwind shop for their thick wax. His errand brings adventurers face to face with the creatures encroaching on the kingdom's gold veins.",h="At the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, William Pestle seeks candles from kobolds crowding Elwynn's mines.",sec={{t="Apothecary's Errands",b="William Pestle runs Pestle's Apothecary with his brother in Stormwind City's Trade District. He needs wax for the remedies, ointments, and concoctions he brews. So he turns to Elwynn's kobolds instead of buying polished candles from city merchants. They carry hefty lumps of tallow and wax on their brows, ready for an adventurer to pry loose.",sp=0},{t="The Mines of Elwynn",b="Kobolds have overrun Fargodeep Mine south of Goldshire and Jasperlode Mine to the northeast. They prize their candles above almost everything. The flames guide them through dark shafts as they dig for gold and shiny trinkets. Taking the candles replenishes Pestle's alchemy stocks and weakens the vermin choking off the kingdom's precious mining claims.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does William Pestle need kobold candles?",a="William Pestle and his brother run an apothecary in Stormwind's Trade District. They use tallow and wax from large candles in sealing, salves, and other alchemical preparations.",al={"why pestle wants candles","what are candles used for","candle wax use"},it="motive"},{q="Where do you find the large candles?",a="Kobold workers, vermin, and diggers carry the candles in Elwynn Forest's mines. Look especially in Fargodeep Mine south of Goldshire and Jasperlode Mine to the east.",al={"where are kobold candles","candle locations","how to get large candles"},gp=true},{q="Why are kobolds so obsessed with candles?",a="Kobolds live in pitch-black tunnels underground and rely on the flames strapped to their heads to see as they dig. Their fear of the dark is superstitious and almost frantic, so they fiercely defend their candles from anyone who tries to take them.",al={"why do kobolds have candles","you no take candle meaning","kobold candle lore"}},{q="Who is William Pestle?",a="William Pestle is a human merchant and alchemist from Stormwind. Away from his shop in the city's Trade District, he travels to Goldshire to secure cheap materials from adventurers.",al={"who is william pestle","william pestle lore","goldshire pestle"},it="identity"},{q="Does this quest connect to other troubles in Elwynn?",a="Yes. The kobolds in Fargodeep and Jasperlode Mines threaten Goldshire and Stormwind's economy. Human miners have been driven out, and securing the tunnels is one of Marshal Dughan's top priorities.",al={"elwynn mine problems","why are kobolds in mines","goldshire kobold threat"},it="ties"},{q="Are there any other mines infested by kobolds in Elwynn?",a="Fargodeep Mine and Jasperlode Mine are the two main kobold sites near Goldshire. Their activity also reaches the forest's riverbanks and extends east toward the borders of Redridge.",al={"other kobold mines","elwynn mines list"}},{q="What is the Large Candle used for?",a="William Pestle needs the large candles for their wax. He and his brother run Pestle's Apothecary in the Trade District of Stormwind. The quests do not specify the particular preparations for which they use that wax.",al={"large candle use","why large candles","what are the candles for"},it="item",add="13eaf00c"},{q="Why are kobolds in the Elwynn mines?",a="Kobolds are subterranean scavengers drawn to dark, mineral-rich tunnels where they can dig for gold and precious ore. With Stormwind's military stretched thin and King Varian Wrynn missing, Elwynn's local mines like Fargodeep and Jasperlode were left poorly defended, allowing the kobolds to overrun the shafts and drive out human miners.",al={"why are kobolds here","fargodeep kobolds why","kobold infestation elwynn"},it="target",add="decb568d"},{q="Why does William Pestle ask you instead of the Stormwind guards?",a="William Pestle is an alchemist, not a soldier. With kobolds aggressively guarding the tunnels of Fargodeep and Jasperlode, venturing into the mines himself would be lethal. Meanwhile, the local Stormwind guards and Elwynn Marshals are completely overwhelmed dealing with Defias bandits and gnolls, leaving trivial errands like gathering wax to passing adventurers.",al={"why doesn't william get candles himself","why hire adventurers for candles","why not stormwind guards"},it="why_me",add="27573e3c"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Clearing kobolds for their candles brings prospectors to Elwynn's richest copper and gold veins, abandoned by human miners.",["race:Human"]="As a human, reclaiming Elwynn's stolen mines and supplying Stormwind's artisans are early duties for a young subject of the kingdom.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help secure local infrastructure while the royal army is stretched thin by internal political strife and missing crown forces."},kw={"apothecary","candle","elwynn","fargodeep","goldshire","jasperlode","kobold","wax","william pestle"},rel={"npc:william-pestle","subzone:fargodeep-mine","subzone:jasperlode-mine","subzone:goldshire","topic:kobold","quest:62","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="William Pestle",faction="Alliance",id=60,ri={"Large Candle"}},src={"Kobold Candles"}}
E["quest:61"] = {t="quest",n="Shipment to Stormwind",z="elwynn",s="William Pestle sends a parcel from Goldshire to his brother in Stormwind. Its candles carry wax gathered from kobolds in Elwynn Forest to Morgan at Pestle's Apothecary.",h="William Pestle sends a parcel from Goldshire to his brother in Stormwind.",sec={{t="A Family Trade",b="William Pestle gathers herbs, reagents, and raw goods in Goldshire. His brother Morgan runs Pestle's Apothecary in Stormwind's Trade District. William cannot easily leave the Lion's Pride Inn, so he trusts travelers bound for the city to carry his goods.",sp=0},{t="From Kobold Wax to Capital Potions",b="William's parcel holds large candles gathered from kobolds in Elwynn's mines. He collects them for their wax, but does not say how the brothers use it. You carry the shipment to Morgan at Pestle's Apothecary in the Trade District.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside William's shipment?",a="The shipment contains candles gathered from kobolds in Elwynn Forest. William collected them for their wax and packed them for Morgan at Pestle's Apothecary.",al={"shipment contents","what is in the package","what did william send"},it="item"},{q="Where do I find Morgan Pestle?",a="Morgan Pestle works inside Pestle's Apothecary in Stormwind City's Trade District, a short walk past the main gates.",al={"morgan pestle location","where is morgan","find morgan pestle"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How are William and Morgan Pestle related?",a="William and Morgan Pestle are brothers who run an alchemical enterprise together. William gathers materials in Elwynn Forest, while Morgan runs their shop in Stormwind.",al={"pestle brothers","who is william pestle brother"},it="ties"},{q="Why doesn't William deliver the package himself?",a="William is occupied with his trade and gathering alchemical ingredients in Goldshire. He relies on travelers already heading toward the capital to carry the package.",al={"why doesn't william go to stormwind","why hire a courier"},it="why_me"},{q="Do kobold candles have an actual alchemical use?",a="William says he and his brother need the candles for their wax. He does not explain how they use it at the apothecary.",al={"why kobold candles","kobold wax alchemy"},it="power"},{q="What comes after delivering the shipment?",a="Delivering the shipment ends the short chain that began with gathering kobold candles in Elwynn Forest. Morgan pays you for carrying the parcel and welcomes your business in his shop.",al={"what next after shipment to stormwind","follow up quest shipment to stormwind"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does William Pestle want this shipment delivered?",a="Morgan is waiting at the brothers' apothecary in Stormwind for the shipment of candles. William gathered them for their wax but lacks time to make the journey, so he asks a traveler to carry the supplies.",al={"why send the shipment","william pestle motive","why deliver the candles"},it="motive",add="e0018b76"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="The Pestle family trade depends on local reagents from Elwynn. Their Stormwind shop is a familiar stop for gatherers and potion-makers.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion, you carry supplies along the king's road into Stormwind, traveling from countryside skirmishes toward the capital."},kw={"elwynn forest","goldshire","kobold candles","morgan pestle","pestle's apothecary","shipment to stormwind","trade district","william pestle"},rel={"quest:60","npc:william-pestle","npc:morgan-pestle","subzone:trade-district","zone:elwynn","topic:kobold","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="William Pestle",["end"]="Morgan Pestle",level="7",faction="Alliance",id=61},src={"Shipment to Stormwind"}}
E["quest:62"] = {t="quest",n="The Fargodeep Mine",z="elwynn",s="South of Goldshire, Marshal Dughan sends you to scout the kobold-held Fargodeep Mine. It lies between the Stonefield and Maclure farms, and its fall points to trouble beyond its tunnels.",h="South of Goldshire, Marshal Dughan sends you to scout the kobold-held Fargodeep Mine.",sec={{t="Trouble South of Goldshire",b="Kobolds have taken the Fargodeep Mine south of Goldshire, between the feuding Stonefield and Maclure homesteads. It once supplied stone and ore for the realm. Now shrill chattering echoes through its damp tunnels, where tallow candles burn. Marshal Dughan sends you to scout the depths and learn how bad the trouble is.",sp=0},{t="A Strained Guard",b="When Dughan hears your report, he worries about other mineral sites, including the Jasperlode Mine to the northeast. The news adds to the Stormwind Guard's strain. Its troops are already stretched thin defending against Defias bandits and gnoll incursions, leaving too few to clear the tunnels.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Fargodeep Mine located?",a="The Fargodeep Mine lies almost due south of Goldshire in Elwynn Forest, between the Stonefield and Maclure homesteads.",al={"fargodeep location","where is fargodeep mine","fargodeep mine map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who sends you to scout the Fargodeep Mine?",a="Marshal Dughan, the Stormwind Guard's commanding officer in Goldshire, sends you to scout the tunnels.",al={"who gives fargodeep quest","marshal dughan quest"}},{q="What creatures have taken over the mine?",a="Kobolds have overrun the mine, lit their candles, and driven out the human workers.",al={"who is in fargodeep","what monsters in fargodeep"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Marshal Dughan need adventurers to check the mine?",a="The Stormwind Guard is stretched thin by local banditry, orc remnants, and gnoll raids, leaving Dughan without spare soldiers even to confirm scout reports.",al={"why send scouts","why doesn't the guard go"},it="why_me"},{q="What happens after scouting the Fargodeep Mine?",a="After you report the trouble to Marshal Dughan, he fears it is widespread and sends you northeast to investigate the Jasperlode Mine.",al={"next quest after fargodeep","what comes next"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why is the infestation of Fargodeep Mine significant?",a="The fall of the Fargodeep Mine shows that the kobold infestation in Northshire was not isolated. Wild threats are pressing rapidly into settled farmland just outside Stormwind's gates.",al={"why does fargodeep matter","lore of fargodeep mine"},it="motive"},{q="Why have kobolds taken over Fargodeep Mine?",a="Kobolds are natural tunnel-dwellers constantly seeking gold and precious minerals beneath the earth. With Stormwind's guards spread thin protecting the region from Defias bandits and wild beasts, the local mines have been left largely undefended. Drawn to rich deposits of ore and gold, the vermin swarmed into Fargodeep Mine, digging in deep and driving out any workers.",al={"why are kobolds in fargodeep mine","kobolds fargodeep mine why","who is in fargodeep mine"},it="target",add="88321243"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you can find rich copper veins inside the Fargodeep Mine, though territorial kobolds stand in your way.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see the overrun mine as another sign that Stormwind struggles to protect Elwynn's essential sites."},kw={"dughan","elwynn","fargodeep","goldshire","jasperlode","kobold","maclure","stonefield"},rel={"npc:marshal-dughan","subzone:fargodeep-mine","quest:76","subzone:goldshire","topic:kobold","subzone:jasperlode-mine","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Marshal Dughan",faction="Alliance",id=62},src={"The Fargodeep Mine"}}
E["quest:7"] = {t="quest",n="Kobold Camp Cleanup",z="elwynn",s="In Northshire's northern woods, kobold numbers threaten the abbey grounds. Marshal McBride needs the camps cleared, and the valley's defense depends on fresh volunteers.",h="In Northshire's northern woods, kobold numbers threaten the abbey grounds.",sec={{t="A Valley Under Pressure",b="Marshal McBride directs the valley's defense from Northshire Abbey, but he has too few soldiers. So he depends on fresh volunteers like you. Each threat he cannot answer could disrupt the abbey's work or spread into the vineyards nearby. The kobold camps cannot wait.",sp=0},{t="The Vermin in the Woods",b="Kobolds are timid, candle-obsessed cave-dwellers who usually pick at underground seams, away from direct sunlight. Now an entire clan has reached the northern timberline. Left alone, their numbers could turn scavenging into open raids. McBride sends you to thin their vanguard and test your resolve to defend the realm.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who orders the culling of the kobold camp?",a="Marshal McBride orders the culling. From Northshire Abbey, he oversees recruit intake and the valley's security for Stormwind.",al={"who gives this quest","quest giver","marshal mcbride role"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why are kobolds in the northern woods instead of a mine?",a="Northshire's growing population has spilled into the open forest, where kobolds have made primitive camps among the northern trees near the edge of civilized land. They usually live in burrows and mines.",al={"why are kobolds outside","kobolds above ground","why woods"},it="why_here"},{q="Why are these kobolds considered a threat to Stormwind?",a="Kobold vermin are timid and weak alone. In packs, they can ambush travelers, raid supplies, and overwhelm unguarded outposts. Stormwind can ill afford this threat while its forces are stretched thin.",al={"are kobolds dangerous","why kill vermin"},it="threat"},{q="Where does this mission lead next?",a="After thinning the kobolds on the surface, recruits are sent deeper into Echo Ridge Mine to investigate, where the heart of the infestation lies.",al={"what quest is next","next step","after camp cleanup"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Is Northshire receiving regular royal army backup?",a="No. Political tension and troop shortages after King Varian's disappearance leave commanders like McBride relying on civilian volunteers, adventurers, and trainees for border security.",al={"where are stormwind guards","why volunteers"},it="allies"},{q="What makes kobolds so attached to their candles?",a="Kobolds revere candles as their main defense against the smothering darkness of underground tunnels. Their flames give them safety, sight, and a sense of ownership.",al={"why candles","candle obsession"}},{q="Why does Marshal McBride want the kobold camp cleaned up?",a="A clan of kobolds has begun infesting the woods north of the abbey, and Marshal McBride wants their numbers reduced before they overrun the valley. Stormwind is already strained by threats elsewhere, leaving Northshire to protect itself. While individually cowardly, the kobolds grow bold in packs. Culling them now keeps the settlement safe and begins the effort to drive them out of Northshire entirely.",al={"why cull kobolds","mcbride kobold motive","why clean kobold camp"},it="motive",add="afae4267"},{q="What are the kobold vermin you are sent to hunt?",a="Kobold vermin are the scouts and scavengers of a clan that has crept into the northern forest. Naturally subterranean rat-like humanoids, they are cowardly thieves on their own, but they have gathered in the woods outside Northshire in alarming numbers. Left unchecked, their encroaching camps threaten travelers, orchards, and the abbey itself.",al={"who are the kobold vermin","what are kobold vermin","kobold vermin target"},it="target",add="35967b57"},{q="Why does Marshal McBride send you instead of the Stormwind guards?",a="Stormwind's royal army has stretched its forces thin dealing with crises across the kingdom, leaving Northshire Valley garrisoned by only a handful of guards. McBride must keep his soldiers stationed around the abbey and primary roads to maintain defensive perimeters. With no spare troops to patrol the wilderness, he relies on capable new recruits and passing volunteers to root out emerging dangers.",al={"why not send guards","why does mcbride need me","why recruit adventurers kobolds"},it="why_me",add="921e514b"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human of Northshire, driving back kobold vermin helps protect the abbey and farmland from being overrun. It is a civic duty.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see the strain on Stormwind's home territories. Even scavenger infestations call for urgent help from volunteer militia."},kw={"echo ridge","elwynn forest","kobold","marshal mcbride","northshire","northshire abbey","vermin"},rel={"npc:marshal-mcbride","quest:783","quest:15","topic:kobold","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:human"},m={start="Marshal McBride",level="2",faction="Alliance",id=7},src={"Kobold Camp Cleanup"}}
E["quest:70"] = {t="quest",n="The Legend of Stalvan",z="elwynn",s="In Goldshire, an old letter renews the search for Stalvan Mistmantle. Its trail runs from Elwynn Forest to Stormwind's Canal District.",h="In Goldshire, an old letter renews the search for Stalvan Mistmantle.",sec={{t="A Midnight Terror",b="At the Lion's Pride Inn, Innkeeper Farley recalls a stormy night years ago. A traveling courier came in from the rain to find shelter. Around midnight, he rushed downstairs in a panic, wearing only his sleepwear. He vanished into the storm, and no one saw him again.",sp=0},{t="The Leftover Parcel",b="The courier left his satchel and personal chest in the upstairs room. Among the forgotten cargo was an unsent letter bearing the name Stalvan, addressed to someone in Stormwind City's Canal District. The chest remained untouched at the foot of the bed until Farley allowed it to be opened.",sp=0},{t="A Chilly Welcome",b="Caretaker Folsom watches over property along Stormwind's canals near the Park. When you bring him the long-overdue letter, he meets Stalvan's name and handwriting with disgust and hostility, not gratitude. His reaction points to old scandals tied to the sender.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the undelivered letter kept?",a="The undelivered letter is in a storage chest upstairs at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire. Climb the stairs, turn right, and enter the bedroom with the bed. The chest rests at the foot of the bed frame.",al={"find letter","stalvan chest location","where is the chest"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Why was the letter never delivered originally?",a="Years ago, the courier took shelter from a downpour at the Lion's Pride Inn. Near midnight, something terrified him, and he fled into the storm in his nightclothes, leaving his chest and deliveries behind.",al={"why abandoned letter","what scared the courier","why did messenger run"},it="history"},{q="Where do I find Caretaker Folsom in Stormwind?",a="Caretaker Folsom is along the Canals in Stormwind City, near the edge of the Park district.",al={"folsom location","where is caretaker folsom","canal district turn in"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why is Caretaker Folsom angry about receiving the letter?",a="Folsom recognizes Stalvan's name and handwriting, and reacts with indignation. Stalvan Mistmantle left bitter memories and outrage among the people connected to his past in Stormwind.",al={"why is folsom mad","folsom reaction","you have some nerve"},it="motive"},{q="How does this connect to the trouble in Duskwood?",a="The town council in Darkshire is investigating a lingering evil tied to Stalvan Mistmantle. To learn who he was, you retrace his earlier travels and associations through Elwynn Forest and Stormwind.",al={"why duskwood quest in goldshire","how does this relate to duskwood"},it="threat"},{q="What happens after giving the letter to Caretaker Folsom?",a="Caretaker Folsom's sharp response opens the Stormwind chapter of the investigation. You must uncover Stalvan's former employment and the grim events involving the noble family he served.",al={"next step","what follows this quest"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Innkeeper Farley want Stalvan's letter delivered?",a="Innkeeper Farley has no personal stake in Stalvan's affairs or the old letter; he is merely helping you piece together the mystery you are investigating. When you ask about Stalvan Mistmantle, Farley recalls a terrified courier who fled the Lion's Pride Inn years ago during a storm, abandoning his dispatch chest upstairs. Remembering that an undelivered letter from Stalvan was left behind and addressed to Stormwind's Canal District, Farley offers it up so you can track down your elusive lead.",al={"why does farley help","innkeeper farley motive","why deliver the letter"},it="motive",add="1a6ccbd1"},{q="What is the Undelivered Letter?",a="The letter is an old piece of correspondence written by Stalvan Mistmantle years ago, intended for an address in Stormwind's Canal District. It was left behind at the Lion's Pride Inn when a messenger fled into the night in sheer terror, leaving his belongings locked in a chest upstairs. For your investigation, the letter serves as a crucial physical clue, directing you to Caretaker Folsom in Stormwind to discover who Stalvan was contacting and what became of him.",al={"what is an undelivered letter","stalvan undelivered letter","what does the letter say"},it="item",add="b7fa74bd"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="To unravel Stalvan's mystery, you travel through the heartlands of the Alliance. An old trail leads from Goldshire to the capital's grand canals.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you see the darker undercurrents of the Kingdom of Stormwind. The evils haunting Duskwood reach to the capital's doorstep."},kw={"canals","caretaker folsom","goldshire","innkeeper farley","lion's pride inn","mistmantle","stalvan","stormwind","undelivered letter"},rel={"npc:innkeeper-farley","npc:caretaker-folsom","subzone:lion-s-pride-inn","subzone:canals-stormwind-city","subzone:park","zone:duskwood","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Innkeeper Farley",["end"]="Caretaker Folsom",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=70,ri={"An Undelivered Letter"}},src={"The Legend of Stalvan (5)"}}
E["quest:71"] = {t="quest",n="Report to Thomas",z="elwynn",s="Guard Thomas waits at the eastern bridge between Goldshire and the Eastvale Logging Camp. The fate of his missing men may show whether the river murlocs threaten more than scouts.",h="Guard Thomas waits at the eastern bridge between Goldshire and the Eastvale Logging Camp.",sec={{t="A Grim Confirmation",b="With few men to spare at the crossing, Thomas had hoped Malakai and Rolf were only cut off or delayed in the riverlands. Their recovered service medallions leave no such hope. Both guards were slain near the waterways.",sp=0},{t="The Threat Along the Water",b="For months, Stormwind's leaders have treated murlocs as nuisance river-dwellers, focusing instead on bandits and the kingdom's wider borders. Now two armed Stormwind guards have been slaughtered along the inland streams. The medallions show Thomas that Elwynn's eastern frontier faces an active assault, and he calls for a response before the logging routes and settlements are overwhelmed.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does Guard Thomas stand?",a="Guard Thomas is posted at the stone bridge over the river in eastern Elwynn Forest, on the road between Goldshire and the Eastvale Logging Camp.",al={"thomas location","guard thomas bridge","where is guard thomas"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who were Rolf and Malakai?",a="Rolf and Malakai were Stormwind guards sent to patrol eastern Elwynn Forest. Murlocs along the riverbanks and Stonecairn Lake overwhelmed and killed them.",al={"missing guards elwynn","who was rolf","who was malakai"},sp=1,it="people"},{q="Why were their medallions necessary?",a="The medallions identify Stormwind city guards. Returning them gives Guard Thomas proof that his missing men died in the line of duty.",al={"why medallions","guard medallions purpose"},sp=1,it="item"},{q="Why is the murloc attack such a big deal?",a="Murlocs are commonly dismissed as primitive, cowardly pests. The deaths of two armed guards show that river tribes can carry out coordinated ambushes and threaten trained soldiers.",al={"why murlocs threat","are murlocs dangerous elwynn"},sp=1,it="threat"},{q="What happens after reporting back to Thomas?",a="Thomas asks you to carry a report of the guards' deaths and the growing murloc threat to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire. Dughan warns that the region's defenses are already stretched thin.",al={"next quest after report to thomas","what does thomas do next"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why is Guard Thomas posted alone at the bridge?",a="Stormwind's military is stretched thin across the realm, with King Varian Wrynn missing and resources strained. The eastern bridge and other outlying posts have few guards to protect vital routes.",al={"why is thomas alone","stormwind bridge guard alone"},it="why_here"},{q="Why deliver the medallions to Guard Thomas?",a="Guard Thomas sent patrols out toward the river, only for them to vanish without word. Finding Rolf and Malakai fallen among the reeds provides grim certainty of their end. Delivering their recovered medallions back to Thomas proves beyond doubt what happened to his men and warns him of the lethal murloc presence along the eastern water.",al={"why report to thomas","why bring medallions to thomas","purpose of report to thomas"},it="motive",add="d4d51b05"},{q="Why are you the one returning the medallions to Thomas?",a="Rolf and Malakai are dead, slain by the murlocs deep within the hostile riverbank village. Guard Thomas is stationed alone guarding the eastern bridge and cannot leave his post unguarded. As the traveler who found the fallen guards and braved the murlocs to recover their insignia, the task falls on you to bring the grim news back.",al={"why me report to thomas","why do i bring the medallions"},it="why_me",add="3744e02c"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Rolf and Malakai's deaths show how exposed Elwynn Forest's borders are. Even routine river patrols can be overwhelmed when guards are scarce.",["race:Human"]="As a human, recovering the fallen guards' medallions gives Stormwind soldiers who died defending the kingdom's interior roads a measure of honor and finality."},kw={"bridge","elwynn forest","goldshire","guard thomas","malakai","medallions","murlocs","rolf"},rel={"quest:45","npc:guard-thomas","quest:39","quest:59","topic:murloc","zone:elwynn","subzone:eastvale-logging-camp","subzone:goldshire"},m={start="Rolf's corpse",["end"]="Guard Thomas",faction="Alliance",id=71},src={"Report to Thomas"}}
E["quest:75"] = {t="quest",n="The Legend of Stalvan",z="elwynn",s="In Elwynn, your search for The Legend of Stalvan leads you to Marshal Haggard's home. The veteran's failing eyesight left an upstairs chest of papers unread.",h="In Elwynn, your search for The Legend of Stalvan leads you to Marshal Haggard's home.",sec={{t="A Veteran's Attic",b="Marshal Haggard lives near Elwynn Forest's southeastern edge, close to Duskwood and Redridge. Upstairs, an old chest holds parchments he found when he moved into his secluded home. His failing eyesight kept him from reading them, and they have remained untouched until you ask about Stalvan.",sp=0},{t="Lingering Shadows",b="The papers in Haggard's upstairs chest stir a restless force tied to Stalvan's past. When you disturb his belongings, a Forlorn Spirit appears. Among the papers, a journal page bears Stalvan's own words and shows that the reclusive scholar left his mark in Elwynn before he vanished.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Marshal Haggard?",a="Marshal Haggard is an aging veteran who lives in a secluded cabin in southeastern Elwynn Forest. His home holds old papers that belonged to Stalvan Mistmantle.",al={"marshal haggard","haggard elwynn","who is haggard"},it="identity"},{q="Why did the trail lead back to Elwynn Forest?",a="Clues from Darkshire and Moonbrook trace Stalvan's travels across southern Stormwind territory. Haggard's home holds papers Stalvan left behind.",al={"why elwynn forest","stalvan elwynn","why go to haggard"},it="history"},{q="What is inside the chest upstairs?",a="The upstairs chest holds a faded journal page written by Stalvan Mistmantle, among parchments Haggard never managed to examine properly.",al={"upstairs chest","faded journal page","what is in the chest"},it="item"},{q="Why does a spirit attack when the chest is opened?",a="A Forlorn Spirit haunts relics from Stalvan's past. It attacks when an outsider disturbs his writings and memories.",al={"forlorn spirit","why ghost attacks","ghost in haggard house"},it="target"},{q="How does this advance the Stalvan investigation?",a="The faded page offers firsthand evidence in Stalvan's own hand, helping you piece together his past.",al={"stalvan mystery","what does the page reveal","stalvan questline step"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why couldn't Marshal Haggard read the papers himself?",a="Age has left Haggard's eyesight weak and clouded. He could not read the small, weathered writing on the faded papers.",al={"haggard blind","why haggard needs help"},it="why_me"},{q="Why does Marshal Haggard want this done?",a="Marshal Haggard is an old soldier living in quiet retirement, but he still carries the instincts of an officer of the realm. When you come seeking the truth about Stalvan Mistmantle, he remembers the discarded parchments left in the chest when he took over the home. Though he has no personal stake in the dark mystery, he wants to aid your investigation as best he can—even if his failing eyesight prevents him from examining the papers himself.",al={"why help haggard","marshal haggard motive","why does haggard want journal"},it="motive",add="7284e072"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Tracing Stalvan's past brings you into the darker history hidden within Elwynn's peaceful farmlands.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you follow Stalvan through familiar settlements and see how isolation and malice can hide in plain sight."},kw={"duskwood","elwynn forest","faded journal page","forlorn spirit","marshal haggard","stalvan"},rel={"zone:elwynn","zone:duskwood","quest:1666"},m={start="Marshal Haggard",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=75,ri={"A Faded Journal Page"}},src={"The Legend of Stalvan (8)"}}
E["quest:76"] = {t="quest",n="The Jasperlode Mine",z="elwynn",s="Scouts are bound for The Jasperlode Mine in eastern Elwynn, where kobolds may have spread. Marshal Dughan needs to know how far they have reached.",h="Scouts are bound for The Jasperlode Mine in eastern Elwynn, where kobolds may have spread.",sec={{t="A Second Incursion",b="After kobolds swarmed the Fargodeep tunnels south of Goldshire, Marshal Dughan feared they had reached other mines. Jasperlode lies in the rocky foothills northeast of the Tower of Azora. Its stone and metal supply the kingdom. With Stormwind guards needed on town patrols, Dughan sends independent adventurers east to learn whether kobolds have taken this mine too.",sp=0},{t="Overextended Defenses",b="Scouts reaching Jasperlode's chambers find kobolds have driven out the human miners and fortified the dark passages. Marshal Dughan faces another blow as the crisis grows. King Varian Wrynn is missing, and royal troops remain withheld from outlying lands. The local garrison has too few soldiers to clear the mine. The kingdom's heart is left short of minerals and hemmed in by threats.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Jasperlode Mine located?",a="Jasperlode Mine lies in the northern foothills of eastern Elwynn Forest. Travel east from Goldshire along the main road, pass the Tower of Azora, then head north into the hills.",al={"where is jasperlode","jasperlode mine location","how to find jasperlode"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Marshal Dughan need a scout instead of sending guards?",a="Marshal Dughan has too few guards to spare. King Varian Wrynn is missing, and political gridlock in the capital has left local forces stretched thin protecting farms and towns from bandits and gnolls. So Dughan relies on civilian scouts.",al={"why send adventurers","why no stormwind guard","where are the guards"},it="why_me"},{q="Why are kobolds taking over Elwynn's mines?",a="Kobolds tunnel toward mineral veins and damp caves. As Stormwind's military presence thinned, they grew bolder and pushed into human mines like Fargodeep and Jasperlode to claim gold, ore, and territory.",al={"why kobolds in jasperlode","what do kobolds want","kobold infestation reason"},it="threat"},{q="What happens after scouting the Jasperlode Mine?",a="After you report Jasperlode's fall, Marshal Dughan faces the loss of mines in the east and threats on several fronts. He turns his attention to western Elwynn, where Riverpaw gnolls are putting heavy pressure on the Westbrook Garrison.",al={"what next after jasperlode","jasperlode follow up"},it="next_step"},{q="Why is the loss of Jasperlode Mine significant to Stormwind?",a="Elwynn's mines supply the ore and stone Stormwind needs for its economy and to forge weapons and armor. Losing Fargodeep and Jasperlode halts mineral extraction and weakens the kingdom's recovery.",al={"why jasperlode matters","jasperlode importance"},it="ruin"},{q="Who owns the Tower of Azora nearby?",a="The Tower of Azora is a small mage tower along Elwynn Forest's eastern road. Theocritus, the Archmage of Azora, presides there, and Azora's servants run the tower. Travelers use it as a landmark on the way to the eastern foothills.",al={"what is tower of azora","who lives in azora tower"}},{q="Why does Marshal Dughan want Jasperlode Mine scouted?",a="Having already confirmed that kobolds have overrun the Fargodeep Mine, Marshal Dughan fears the infestation is not an isolated incident. He needs to know whether the threat has spread east to Jasperlode Mine as well. Securing Elwynn's resource supply and understanding the full scale of the encroaching danger are vital to defending the township of Goldshire and protecting Stormwind's vital trade routes.",al={"dughan motive jasperlode","why scout jasperlode","why does dughan need jasperlode investigated"},it="motive",add="a973508b"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you see valuable deposits in Jasperlode's tunnels, but territorial kobolds stand between you and the ore.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see how fragile Stormwind's home territories have become without centralized royal support, with both Fargodeep and Jasperlode lost.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you witness Elwynn's rural infrastructure faltering as frontier resources fall close to the capital."},kw={"azora","dughan","elwynn","fargodeep","goldshire","jasperlode","kobold","mine","scout"},rel={"subzone:jasperlode-mine","quest:62","subzone:fargodeep-mine","npc:marshal-dughan","subzone:tower-of-azora","quest:239","subzone:goldshire","topic:kobold"},m={start="Marshal Dughan",faction="Alliance",id=76},src={"The Jasperlode Mine"}}
E["quest:78"] = {t="quest",n="The Legend of Stalvan",z="elwynn",s="Marshal Haggard sends you to find Tavernkeep Smitts, who may know the hand behind a page from Stalvan's journal.",h="Marshal Haggard sends you to find Tavernkeep Smitts, who may know the hand behind a page from Stalvan's...",sec={{t="A Lead from the Marshal",b="Marshal Haggard cannot read the faded writing on the torn journal page you recovered from his chest in Elwynn Forest. His failing eyesight leaves the words beyond him. He recalls serving with the Stormwind Guard and spending evenings at the Scarlet Raven Tavern in Darkshire. So he sends you across the river to Tavernkeep Smitts, whose years behind the bar have made him a keeper of local history and rumors.",sp=0},{t="Return to the Scarlet Raven",b="You cross Duskwood's gloomy woods and show the faded page to Smitts behind the counter. He is glad to hear of his old acquaintance Haggard, though he grieves for the veteran's failing health. Then Smitts sees the parchment, and alarm overtakes his easy manner. He knows the distinctive handwriting without doubt, bringing the search closer to the truth of Stalvan's madness.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Marshal Haggard send me back to Darkshire?",a="Marshal Haggard is aging and nearly blind, so he cannot examine the recovered journal page. He remembers Tavernkeep Smitts as a keeper of local lore from his Stormwind Guard days, and sends you to ask him about the writing.",al={"why go to darkshire","haggard to darkshire","why smitts"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is Tavernkeep Smitts located?",a="Tavernkeep Smitts tends the bar inside the Scarlet Raven Tavern, on the eastern side of Darkshire in Duskwood.",al={"where is smitts","smitts location","scarlet raven tavern location"},gp=true},{q="What item do you carry to Tavernkeep Smitts?",a="You carry a Faded Journal Page, an excerpt from Stalvan Mistmantle's lost journal, found secured inside Marshal Haggard's footlocker.",al={"what item","faded journal page","stalvan journal page"},it="item"},{q="Does Tavernkeep Smitts recognize the handwriting?",a="Yes. Smitts recognizes the handwriting as soon as he sees the faded page, and his alarm gives the search for Stalvan its next lead.",al={"does smitts know the writing","smitts reaction to journal"}},{q="How does Smitts know Marshal Haggard?",a="Smitts hosted Haggard years ago, when Haggard led Stormwind Guard patrols into Duskwood and visited the Scarlet Raven Tavern for drinks.",al={"smitts haggard relationship","how smitts knows haggard"},it="ties"},{q="What comes next in the search for Stalvan?",a="Take the faded journal page to Smitts at the Scarlet Raven Tavern and follow the lead he gives you.",al={"what is next","next step stalvan","stalvan chain continue"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Marshal Haggard want this done?",a="Marshal Haggard cannot read the faded journal page because his eyesight is failing. He remembers Tavernkeep Smitts as an old acquaintance with a strong knowledge of local history, and asks you to bring the page to him in Darkshire.",al={"why does haggard want this done","marshal haggard motive","why help find stalvan"},it="motive",add="bf062962"},{q="Why does Marshal Haggard send you instead of going himself?",a="Haggard is an old, retired marshal living in isolation, rapidly losing his eyesight. The roads through the woods are dangerous, and he simply lacks the youth and physical stamina to trek back across the border to Duskwood. He relies on an capable traveler like you to run his errand and show the journal page to his old acquaintance.",al={"why can't haggard go","why does haggard need me","why doesn't haggard visit smitts"},it="why_me",add="c297959a"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance defender, you see bonds between former Stormwind guardsmen and keepers of local history across the Kingdom of Stormwind.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you see how tragedies in Elwynn and Darkshire remain part of the settlements' memories."},kw={"darkshire","duskwood","elwynn","journal","marshal haggard","mistmantle","scarlet raven tavern","stalvan","tavernkeep smitts"},rel={"quest:1666","npc:tavernkeep-smitts","subzone:scarlet-raven-tavern","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-guard","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Marshal Haggard",["end"]="Tavernkeep Smitts",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=78},src={"The Legend of Stalvan (9)"}}
E["quest:783"] = {t="quest",n="A Threat Within",z="elwynn",s="In Northshire Valley, volunteers answer Stormwind's call as local defenses falter. At Northshire Abbey, Marshal McBride directs the response, and you begin serving on the threatened grounds.",h="In Northshire Valley, volunteers answer Stormwind's call as local defenses falter.",sec={{t="A Kingdom Stretched Thin",b="Northshire Valley once gave people quiet for prayer, farming, and monastic study. Now it is Elwynn Forest's first defense against unrest at home. Few guards remain nearby, so the Stormwind Guard calls on each willing volunteer who reaches the abbey. Trouble spreads across the surrounding countryside.",sp=0},{t="The Marshal's Call",b="From Northshire Abbey, Marshal McBride directs the valley's defenses as danger grows. Bandits, vermin, and pests from below ground threaten the people nearby. You begin by clearing the ground around the abbey, where these threats press close to the valley's defenders and the place they protect.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="Marshal McBride is calling new arrivals to Northshire Valley to help defend it. You go inside Northshire Abbey and report to him.",al={"threat within quest","what is this quest","northshire intro quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Marshal McBride?",a="Marshal McBride is the senior Stormwind Guard officer at Northshire Abbey. He directs the valley's defense and assigns recruits to face threats in the nearby countryside.",al={"marshal mcbride","who is mcbride","abbey commander"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Stormwind recruiting volunteers instead of sending regular soldiers?",a="Stormwind's regular forces serve abroad to protect the Alliance. With heartland garrisons short of soldiers, local commanders rely on volunteers to defend their homes.",al={"why volunteers","where are the guards","why is stormwind understaffed"},it="why_me"},{q="What threats are currently plaguing Northshire Valley?",a="Kobolds infest the nearby mines and hills, while diseased or predatory pests trouble the vineyards. Brigands and outlaws also take advantage of the valley's depleted garrison.",al={"valley threats","what is attacking northshire","northshire problems"},it="threat"},{q="Where does this assignment lead next?",a="After you report to Marshal McBride, you are sent to clear kobolds from the hills, help local farmers and workers, and look into the growing presence of organized bandits.",al={"next quest","what comes after threat within","mcbride follow up"},it="next_step"},{q="Why is Northshire Abbey being used as a military command post?",a="Northshire Abbey is a holy place of study and faith, but its stone walls and central position make it a practical base for the valley. With local authority under strain, the Stormwind Guard has set up its command within the abbey.",al={"why military in abbey","northshire church military","holy abbey soldiers"},it="place"},{q="Why does Deputy Willem send you to Marshal McBride?",a="Deputy Willem is stationed outside Northshire Abbey to vet able-bodied arrivals as quickly as possible. With the kingdom's military stretched thin and multiple crises closing in on Northshire's borders, he needs every capable volunteer properly mustered into service. Rather than assigning missions himself, Willem directs you straight to his commanding officer, Marshal McBride, so you can be formally briefed and deployed wherever the valley's defenses are faltering most.",al={"why talk to mcbride","willem motive","why speak with mcbride"},it="motive",add="2039075b"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human defender from Northshire, answering Marshal McBride's call is your first official pledge to protect your homeland and the Kingdom of Stormwind.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see how duties across distant lands leave even its heartlands exposed to trouble within."},kw={"a threat within","abbey","elwynn forest","marshal mcbride","northshire","recruitment","stormwind guard","volunteers"},rel={"npc:marshal-mcbride","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-guard","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:alliance"},m={level="1",faction="Alliance",id=783},src={"A Threat Within"}}
E["quest:7881"] = {t="quest",n="Carnival Boots",z="elwynn",s="Workers at the Darkmoon Faire seek sturdy footwear from skilled crafters. In exchange for top notch boots, carnival hands hand over prized faire tickets.",h="Workers at the Darkmoon Faire seek sturdy footwear from skilled crafters.",sec={{t="Footwear for the Faire",b="Gatherers and craftspeople bring sturdy carnival boots to the Darkmoon Faire, where carnival workers trade prized tickets for top notch work. Every pair helps keep the traveling carnival on its feet.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does the Darkmoon Faire need boots?",a="The Darkmoon Faire accepts sturdy, well-crafted footwear to support its workers and carnival grounds, offering prize tickets in trade.",al={"carnival boots purpose","why boots darkmoon faire"}},{q="What are Darkmoon Faire tickets used for?",a="Tickets earned from the carnival can be gathered and traded for various Darkmoon Faire prizes and curiosities.",al={"what do darkmoon faire tickets buy","faire tickets purpose"}},{q="What kind of boots does the carnival accept?",a="Carnival workers inspect the boots for top notch craftsmanship and durability before handing over tickets.",al={"darkmoon faire boots trade","carnival boots requirements"}}},kw={"carnival","carnival boots","craftsmanship","darkmoon faire","darkmoon faire ticket"},m={id=7881},src={"In-game quest text: Carnival Boots"},fv=true}
E["quest:7890"] = {t="quest",n="Heavy Grinding Stone",z="elwynn",s="A faire attendant asks you to bring Heavy Grinding Stones. Your delivery earns tickets for the faire.",h="A faire attendant asks you to bring Heavy Grinding Stones.",sec={{t="At the Faire",b="The faire attendant thanks you and says the stones are already making their muscles grow. In return, you receive tickets and a warning not to eat too many sweets. The attendant wants you to stay strong and ready to fight.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the attendant want?",a="The attendant wants Heavy Grinding Stones.",al={"heavy grinding stone what","stones for faire"}},{q="What do I get for bringing the stones?",a="The attendant gives you tickets for the faire.",al={"stone tickets","faire tickets"}},{q="Why does the attendant mention sweets?",a="The attendant warns you not to eat too many sweets and says you need to stay in fighting shape.",al={"too many sweets","faire sweets"}}},kw={"faire","grinding stones","heavy grinding stone","sweets","tickets"},m={id=7890},src={"In-game quest text: Heavy Grinding Stone"},fv=true}
E["quest:7900"] = {t="quest",n="Torn Bear Pelts",z="elwynn",s="You bring torn bear pelts to someone who plans to have them sewn into plush toys. Tickets are offered as payment.",h="You bring torn bear pelts to someone who plans to have them sewn into plush toys.",sec={{t="A New Use",b="The recipient plans to have the bear pelts sewn into plush toys, with stuffing and paint. They offer you tickets as payment.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are the bear pelts for?",a="They are intended to be sewn into plush toys with stuffing and paint.",al={"torn bear pelts purpose","what do pelts make"}},{q="What do I get for the pelts?",a="The recipient offers you tickets as payment.",al={"payment for pelts","pelts tickets"}},{q="Who will sew the toys?",a="The recipient says someone will sew the pelts into plush toys.",al={"who makes plush toys","who sews the bears"}}},kw={"bear pelts","paint","plush toys","stuffing","tickets","torn bear pelts"},m={id=7900},src={"In-game quest text: Torn Bear Pelts"},fv=true}
E["quest:7901"] = {t="quest",n="Soft Bushy Tails",z="elwynn",s="At the Darkmoon Faire, a request for bushy tails helps provide prizes for its visitors. The Faire hopes happy visitors will bring others along.",h="At the Darkmoon Faire, a request for bushy tails helps provide prizes for its visitors.",sec={{t="Faire Prizes",b="Happy visitors mean more to the Darkmoon Faire. The tails you bring make prizes for those who come, and pleased visitors may tell their friends to visit too. The Faire gives you tickets and welcomes you to enjoy your time there.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are the bushy tails for?",a="The Darkmoon Faire will use them as prizes for its visitors.",al={"why tails","bushy tails use","tails for faire"}},{q="Why does the Faire want happy visitors?",a="Happy visitors may tell their friends about the Faire and bring more visitors.",al={"why happy visitors","faire visitors","more people at faire"}},{q="What does the Faire give you?",a="The Faire gives you tickets.",al={"faire tickets","what do i get","tickets for tails"}}},kw={"darkmoon faire","prizes","soft bushy tails","tails","tickets","visitors"},rel={"quest:7905"},m={id=7901},src={"In-game quest text: Soft Bushy Tails"},fv=true}
E["quest:83"] = {t="quest",n="Red Linen Goods",z="elwynn",s="At Eastvale Logging Camp, Sara Timberlain needs linen for her tailoring. She asks you to recover bandanas from Defias bandits so she can keep making goods for travelers.",h="At Eastvale Logging Camp, Sara Timberlain needs linen for her tailoring.",sec={{t="Bandits and Burlap",b="Across Elwynn, Defias bandits wear red linen bandanas. Their less organized kin in Northshire make do with cheap burlap masks. The linen gives Sara workable cloth for her tailoring.",sp=0},{t="Salvage at the Camp",b="At Eastvale Logging Camp, Sara Timberlain needs textiles for her trade. Taking bandanas from Defias camps scattered through the woods supplies her with cloth and helps check the bandits' encroachment.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers the Red Linen Goods quest?",a="Sara Timberlain, a seamstress at Eastvale Logging Camp in eastern Elwynn Forest, asks you to bring her cloth.",al={"who gives red linen goods","red linen goods questgiver","sara timberlain quest"},it="identity",gp=true},{q="What items are needed for Red Linen Goods?",a="You need six Red Linen Bandanas from Defias gang members scattered throughout Elwynn Forest.",al={"what do i collect for red linen goods","items for red linen goods","bandanas needed"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Where can I find Defias bandits in Elwynn Forest?",a="Defias outlaws camp across Elwynn Forest, including around Brackwell Pumpkin Patch, Stonefield Farm, and the woods around Jerod's Landing.",al={"defias locations elwynn","where are defias camps","where to get red bandanas"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do the Elwynn Defias wear linen instead of burlap?",a="Low-ranking Defias in Northshire wear burlap masks, while better-equipped members across Elwynn wear red linen. The bandanas mark the Brotherhood's greater organization and supply.",al={"why red linen","burlap vs linen defias","defias mask material"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Sara Timberlain want bandit bandanas?",a="Sara Timberlain needs fabric for her tailoring. She reuses linen from Defias masks to sew practical goods for woodsmen and travelers at the logging camp.",al={"why collect bandanas","what does sara do with masks"},it="motive"},{q="Where is the Eastvale Logging Camp located?",a="Eastvale Logging Camp lies in far eastern Elwynn Forest, just north of the main road toward the bridge into Redridge Mountains.",al={"eastvale location","where is eastvale","how to find sara timberlain"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Red Linen Bandana used for?",a="The red linen bandanas are worn as masks by Defias Brotherhood bandits prowling throughout Elwynn Forest. While the scoundrels in Northshire make do with rough burlap, the thieves in the broader forest carry better-grade cloth. Sara Timberlain unravels and reweaves these captured masks to craft serviceable linen garments.",al={"what is red linen bandana for","red linen bandana use","why red linen bandana"},it="item",add="18a4a024"},{q="Why are Defias bandits in Elwynn Forest?",a="The Defias Brotherhood has established camps scattered across Elwynn Forest to harass travellers, rob supply lines, and undermine Stormwind's authority. Their growing presence threatens local settlements like the Eastvale Logging Camp, taking advantage of the kingdom's stretched guard forces to expand their outlaw operations right outside the capital.",al={"defias in elwynn","why are defias here","defias brotherhood elwynn forest"},it="target",add="8ac6c8ef"},{q="Why does Sara Timberlain need you instead of the guards?",a="Sara Timberlain is a tailor at the Eastvale Logging Camp, not a soldier, and she lacks the means to fight outlaws herself. Stormwind's guards and the local garrison are already overburdened trying to contain widespread Defias incursions and gnoll raids, leaving humble artisans to rely on passing adventurers for materials and protection.",al={"why ask me sara","why not elwynn guards","why timberlain need help"},it="why_me",add="fea06053"}},ang={["profession:Tailoring"]="As a tailor, you know how scarce fabric can lead a seamstress to salvage cloth from bandits' clothing.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can weaken the Defias Brotherhood in Elwynn while bringing useful cloth to Eastvale."},kw={"burlap","defias brotherhood","eastvale logging camp","elwynn forest","red linen bandana","red linen goods","sara timberlain","tailoring"},rel={"npc:sara-timberlain","subzone:eastvale-logging-camp","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Sara Timberlain",level="9",faction="Alliance",id=83,ri={"Red Linen Bandana"}},src={"Red Linen Goods"}}
E["quest:84"] = {t="quest",n="Back to Billy",z="elwynn",s="Bernice Stonefield sends you across the road with a pork belly pie for Billy Maclure. He has information about her missing necklace, and the delivery carries on the feud between their families in central Elwynn Forest.",h="Bernice Stonefield sends you across the road with a pork belly pie for Billy Maclure.",sec={{t="A Bitter Pie",b="The feud between the Stonefields and Maclures leaves little room for kindness. Auntie Bernice Stonefield baked a pork belly pie because Billy Maclure would not share what he knew about her family heirloom without one. She hands you the pie with plain irritation. Bernice hopes Billy chokes on every bite.",sp=0},{t="A Boy's Bribe",b="At the Maclure Vineyards, across the road, Billy Maclure waits hungry and cannot remember what happened to the necklace. The rivalry between the two homesteads reaches their children too. They barter gossip and stolen trinkets for farm treats. With the pie delivered, Billy remembers, and the search for the necklace's true location can begin.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this delivery?",a="Billy Maclure says he knows where Auntie Bernice Stonefield's lost necklace is, but he will not talk until you bring him a home-cooked pork belly pie. The delivery meets his demand, so he will reveal where the heirloom went.",al={"why deliver pie","what does billy want","back to billy goal"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is Auntie Bernice so upset with Billy?",a="The Stonefield and Maclure families have been locked in a bitter rural feud for years. Bernice resents cooking a treat for a troublesome Maclure child to recover an heirloom that went missing on their borders.",al={"why does bernice hate billy","stonefield maclure fight","why tell him to choke"},it="motive"},{q="Where does Billy say the necklace actually is?",a="After eating the pie, Billy reveals that he did not keep the necklace. Goldtooth, a notorious kobold in the Fargodeep Mine, got it.",al={"where is the necklace","who took the necklace","goldtooth connection"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Where is Billy Maclure located?",a="Billy Maclure is at the Maclure Vineyards, just south of the road in central Elwynn Forest and opposite the Stonefield Farm.",al={"billy maclure location","where is billy","find billy"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who baked the Pork Belly Pie?",a="Auntie Bernice Stonefield baked the pie at the Stonefield Farm after you gathered fresh chunks of boar meat from the nearby wilderness.",al={"who made the pie","pie cook"},it="origin"},{q="Does this quest resolve the feud between the families?",a="No. The pie satisfies Billy's personal bribe, while the deep animosity between the adult Stonefields and Maclures remains.",al={"does the feud end","stonefield maclure peace"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Auntie Bernice send an outsider to deal with Billy?",a="The bitter feud between the Stonefields and the Maclures makes direct contact between the families nearly impossible. Auntie Bernice cannot bear to step foot on Maclure land herself—let alone cater in person to an obnoxious child demanding food in exchange for stolen property. A passing traveler offers a neutral courier who can walk across the road, deliver the pie, and pry the truth out of young Billy without sparking an outright brawl between the neighboring clans.",al={"why send me back to billy","why not bernice herself","why does auntie bernice need an adventurer"},it="why_me",add="6d42dc77"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you find disputes between human farmsteads even in peaceful Elwynn Forest. Helping local folk often means dealing with these quarrels.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you know pork belly pie as a comforting Elwynn farmhouse dish made from meat of the forest's roaming wild boars."},kw={"back to billy","bernice stonefield","billy maclure","elwynn forest","maclure vineyards","pork belly pie","stonefield farm","stonefield necklace"},rel={"npc:billy-maclure","npc:auntie-bernice-stonefield","quest:86","subzone:maclure-vineyards","zone:elwynn"},m={start="\"Auntie\" Bernice Stonefield",["end"]="Billy Maclure",faction="Alliance",id=84},src={"Back to Billy"}}
E["quest:85"] = {t="quest",n="Lost Necklace",z="elwynn",s="In southern Elwynn, Bernice Stonefield looks for her missing necklace. She suspects Billy Maclure, the young son of the family across the road, and asks you to find him.",h="In southern Elwynn, Bernice Stonefield looks for her missing necklace.",sec={{t="A Neighborly Accusation",b="The Stonefields and Maclures live on adjoining land in southern Elwynn Forest, but goodwill between them is scarce. When “Auntie” Bernice Stonefield finds her cherished necklace missing, she blames the youngest Maclure. Certain Billy Maclure came onto her farm and took it, the bitter widow asks you to cross the road to the vineyards, find the boy, and demand its return.",sp=0},{t="A Boy with an Appetite",b="At the neighboring vineyard, Billy Maclure denies taking the necklace and says he is no thief. With a knowing grin, he hints that he may know where it went. First, he wants someone to satisfy his hunger with a fresh pork pie.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Auntie Bernice Stonefield?",a="Auntie Bernice Stonefield is an elderly widow who lives on Stonefield Farm in southern Elwynn Forest. She distrusts the neighboring Maclure family, especially their troublemaking young son, Billy.",al={"who is auntie bernice","bernice stonefield","who gives lost necklace"},it="identity"},{q="Did Billy Maclure actually steal the necklace?",a="Billy Maclure firmly denies stealing the necklace. He hints that he knows who took it, but will not share what he knows until someone feeds him.",al={"is billy a thief","did billy steal it","did billy take the necklace"},sp=1,it="target"},{q="Where can I find Billy Maclure?",a="You can find Billy Maclure among the grapevines at Maclure Vineyards, just east across the road from Stonefield Farm.",al={"billy maclure location","where is billy","find billy maclure"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do the Stonefields and Maclures dislike each other?",a="The neighboring Stonefield and Maclure families have been caught in a bitter rural feud for years. Property, pride, and old personal grudges keep tensions high, so each side suspects the worst of the other.",al={"family feud","stonefield maclure feud","why do they hate each other"},it="conflict"},{q="What happens after talking to Billy Maclure?",a="Billy says he is too hungry to remember where the necklace went. He sends you back to Auntie Bernice to bake him a pork pie in exchange for the information.",al={"what next","after lost necklace","next quest"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="You travel through southern Elwynn Forest between Stonefield Farm and the adjoining Maclure Vineyards.",al={"quest zone","where is lost necklace"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Auntie Bernice want her necklace back?",a="Auntie Bernice is an elderly widow, and the necklace is a deeply cherished personal possession. Losing it distresses her, and she immediately suspects the rival family next door—specifically young Billy Maclure—of snatching it. Recovering the heirloom would bring peace of mind and warm an old widow's heart.",al={"why does bernice want the necklace","bernice necklace motive","stonefield necklace importance"},it="motive",add="b7900c48"},{q="Why doesn't Auntie Bernice confront Billy Maclure herself?",a="The bitter feud between the Stonefields and the Maclures makes it nearly impossible for either side to speak civilly without igniting a brawl. Bernice cannot simply walk over to the Maclure Vineyards herself, and Stormwind's guards are far too stretched dealing with gnolls and Defias bandits to arbitrate petty squabbles between neighboring farmers. A passing adventurer offers a neutral party who can question the boy directly.",al={"why does bernice need me","why send an adventurer to billy","why not ask stormwind guards"},it="why_me",add="27b02d6f"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance novice in Elwynn Forest, you get a taste of frontier life by settling a petty dispute between the squabbling Stonefield and Maclure families.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you see that strife in the Kingdom of Stormwind comes not only from Defias outlaws and gnoll warbands. Old quarrels between rural neighbors run deep, too."},kw={"bernice","billy","elwynn","farm","maclure","necklace","stonefield","vineyards"},rel={"npc:auntie-bernice-stonefield","npc:billy-maclure","quest:86","subzone:maclure-vineyards","zone:elwynn"},m={start="\"Auntie\" Bernice Stonefield",["end"]="Billy Maclure",faction="Alliance",id=85},src={"Lost Necklace"}}
E["quest:86"] = {t="quest",n="Pie for Billy",z="elwynn",s="In Elwynn, you gather meat for Bernice's pie while Billy holds back what he knows about her necklace. Bernice agrees to bake, though she believes Billy stole her family's jewelry.",h="In Elwynn, you gather meat for Bernice's pie while Billy holds back what he knows about her necklace.",sec={{t="A Boy's Bribe",b="Billy Maclure gives no apology when you ask about the necklace. He will neither return it nor name who has it until he gets a freshly baked pork belly pie. He knows Bernice is the finest cook in the valley, and means to enjoy the bargain.",sp=0},{t="Baking Through Bad Blood",b="Bernice is furious at the thought of feeding the boy she believes stole her family's jewelry. Still, she agrees to bake before you gather the meat. You bring her meat from wild boars roaming nearby pastures. She sets aside her pride, hoping to get her prized necklace back.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Billy want a pie before talking?",a="Billy Maclure knows where Auntie Bernice's necklace is, and uses that knowledge to bargain for food. He will not say who has it until he gets one of Bernice's pork belly pies.",al={"why billy wants pie","billy bribe pie","billy pork belly pie"},it="motive"},{q="Why does Auntie Bernice agree to bake for a thief?",a="Auntie Bernice is furious at the boy she believes stole her necklace, but sees no other way to recover it. She agrees to bake when you bring her boar meat, putting the return of her property before her pride.",al={"why does bernice bake","bernice stonefield pie reason","stonefield baking for maclure"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where does the meat for the pie come from?",a="The meat comes from wild boars foraging in Elwynn Forest, in the meadows and along the edges of the Stonefield and Maclure farms.",al={"where to get meat","tender boar meat source"},it="item"},{q="What is the history between the Stonefields and Maclures?",a="The Stonefield and Maclure families are neighboring farmers with a bitter rivalry that has lasted for years. They suspect each other of theft, vandalism, and bad-faith squabbling across their property lines.",al={"stonefield maclure feud","farm rivalry","maclure vs stonefield"},it="conflict"},{q="Did Billy actually steal the necklace?",a="Auntie Bernice accuses Billy directly. He avoids a straight confession, but clearly knows where the necklace ended up and uses that knowledge to bargain for food.",al={"did billy steal necklace","who took necklace","billy necklace thief"},it="identity"},{q="What happens after Bernice gets the meat?",a="When you bring her tender boar meat, Auntie Bernice bakes a pork belly pie for you to take to Billy. She hopes he will then reveal who has her necklace.",al={"next step after pie","what follows pie for billy"},it="next_step"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Auntie Bernice says wild boar meat can be tough and bland. With proper spices and a slow simmer, it makes exceptional savory pie filling.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you see the stubborn, insular rivalries of Elwynn's rural homesteaders, just south of Stormwind's gates."},kw={"bernice stonefield","billy maclure","elwynn forest","lost necklace","maclure vineyards","pork belly pie","stonefield farm","tender boar meat"},rel={"quest:85","quest:84","npc:billy-maclure","npc:auntie-bernice-stonefield","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Billy Maclure",["end"]="\"Auntie\" Bernice Stonefield",faction="Alliance",id=86,ri={"Tender Boar Meat"}},src={"Pie for Billy"}}
E["quest:8649"] = {t="quest",n="Stormbrow the Elder",z="elwynn",s="Near Goldshire, Stormbrow the Elder greets travelers during the Lunar Festival. They honor Azeroth’s ancient traditions and olden races, and receive a commemorative coin in return.",h="Near Goldshire, Stormbrow the Elder greets travelers during the Lunar Festival.",sec={{t="A Spirit in Goldshire",b="Behind Goldshire’s smithy, a quiet pond lies beneath the forest canopy. There Stormbrow the Elder appears as an honored spirit. Guards, tradesfolk, and travelers pass through the town as visitors come to honor the realm’s long history.",sp=0},{t="Honoring the Olden Races",b="During the Lunar Festival, the spirits of great ancestors return to walk among the living. Stormbrow commends travelers who remember those who came before. For honoring the elder peoples’ wisdom and legacy, visitors receive a blessing and a commemorative coin.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Elder Stormbrow?",a="Find Stormbrow the Elder beside the pond behind the blacksmith’s forge in Goldshire, in Elwynn Forest.",al={"stormbrow location","where is elder stormbrow","goldshire elder"}},{q="Who is Elder Stormbrow?",a="Stormbrow the Elder is an ancestral spirit who appears during the Lunar Festival. The spirit represents the revered elders of Azeroth’s olden races.",al={"who is stormbrow","stormbrow lore","elder stormbrow identity"}},{q="What is the purpose of visiting Elder Stormbrow?",a="Travelers visit Stormbrow the Elder to honor ancient ancestors during the festival. The spirit offers greetings and a token of appreciation in return.",al={"why visit stormbrow","elder stormbrow quest","stormbrow the elder purpose"}},{q="Can Horde players speak to Elder Stormbrow?",a="The Lunar Festival elders honor all who seek them in peace. Goldshire is heavily guarded Alliance territory, so a visit is perilous for Horde travelers.",al={"horde stormbrow","can horde visit stormbrow"}},{q="What token does the Elder offer?",a="Stormbrow the Elder offers a Coin of Ancestry, a traditional token of respect and remembrance shared by elders throughout the festival.",al={"stormbrow reward","what token","lunar coin stormbrow"}},{q="Why does Stormbrow mention the 'olden races'?",a="Stormbrow commends travelers who remember that present civilizations walk lands shaped by ancient peoples and enduring customs. Those peoples and customs came long before the modern kingdoms.",al={"olden races meaning","why olden races","stormbrow dialogue"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human living in Elwynn, you can look to Stormbrow the Elder as a reminder of ancient history beyond Stormwind’s walls and its recent wars.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler passing through Goldshire, you can find Stormbrow the Elder in the heart of Elwynn Forest, among the most accessible ancestral spirits for young adventurers."},kw={"ancestor","elder stormbrow","elwynn forest","forge","goldshire","lunar festival","token"},rel={"zone:elwynn","subzone:goldshire"},m={start="Elder Stormbrow",id=8649},src={"Stormbrow the Elder"}}
E["quest:87"] = {t="quest",n="Goldtooth",z="elwynn",s="Near Fargodeep Mine, Billy Maclure's careless play has set the Stonefield and Maclure families against each other. His trail leads you to the kobold Goldtooth.",h="Near Fargodeep Mine, Billy Maclure's careless play has set the Stonefield and Maclure families against each...",sec={{t="A Boy's Mischief",b="Auntie Bernice Stonefield's missing necklace has stirred trouble between the Stonefield and Maclure families. Bernice suspects her rivals, but Billy Maclure lost the trinket while playing near Fargodeep Mine. He tries to hide his guilt. He says he found the necklace before a creature snatched it away.",sp=0},{t="The Den Above the Mine",b="Billy says a large kobold with gleaming fangs took the shiny necklace and fled to a den above Fargodeep Mine. Yet Goldtooth lurks on the mine's lower level. Slaying the kobold returns Bernice's necklace and settles the families' dispute. Bernice also gives you an old campaign keepsake left by her late husband.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who stole Auntie Bernice's necklace?",a="Billy Maclure most likely took Auntie Bernice's necklace. He lets slip that he lost it while playing near Fargodeep Mine, then claims he only found it there. Before he could retrieve it, Goldtooth the kobold grabbed the shiny trinket.",al={"who stole necklace","who took the necklace","did maclures steal necklace"},sp=1},{q="Where can Goldtooth be found?",a="Goldtooth lurks on the lower level inside Fargodeep Mine, though Billy says the kobold's den is above the mine.",al={"goldtooth location","where is goldtooth","find goldtooth"},gp=true},{q="What kind of creature is Goldtooth?",a="Goldtooth is an oversized kobold with a gleaming golden fang. Like other kobolds, he is drawn to bright, shiny trinkets.",al={"what is goldtooth","is goldtooth a kobold"},it="target"},{q="How does this quest tie into the Maclure and Stonefield feud?",a="The Stonefields and Maclures are bitter rivals who blame each other for petty thefts and misfortunes. Auntie Bernice suspects the Maclures took her necklace out of spite, but Billy lost it through carelessness.",al={"stonefield maclure drama","why does bernice blame billy"},sp=1,it="ties"},{q="What is the reward from Auntie Bernice?",a="Auntie Bernice gives you an old keepsake that belonged to her late husband. She says it was lucky, but he forgot to take it on his final military campaign.",al={"bernice reward","what do you get"},gp=true},{q="What quest leads directly into Goldtooth?",a="Back to Billy leads directly to Goldtooth. You bribe Billy Maclure with pork, and he finally confesses what happened to the necklace.",al={"goldtooth prereq","quest before goldtooth"},gp=true},{q="Why does Billy Maclure want Bernice's necklace back?",a="Billy accidentally dropped Auntie Bernice's necklace while playing near the Fargodeep Mine, though he is desperate to deny stealing it. He knows he is in serious trouble if it remains lost, especially given the fierce feud between the Maclures and the Stonefields. Having you recover it from the kobold lets him set things right without directly facing Bernice's wrath.",al={"billy maclure motive","why does billy want the necklace","why help billy maclure"},it="motive",add="36c74007"},{q="What is Bernice's Necklace?",a="Bernice's Necklace is a cherished family heirloom belonging to \"Auntie\" Bernice Stonefield. After going missing amidst the bitter rivalry between the Stonefield and Maclure families, it ended up snatched away by a greedy kobold. Its value is largely sentimental to Bernice, who desperately wants it returned home to the Stonefield Farm.",al={"bernices necklace","what is auntie bernices necklace","bernice necklace use"},it="item",add="b7400482"},{q="Why does Billy ask you instead of the guards?",a="Billy is just a frightened child hiding his guilt, and calling upon the Stormwind guards would expose that he took or mishandled Bernice Stonefield's jewelry in the first place. Furthermore, the local guards are already stretched thin dealing with Defias bandits and gnolls throughout Elwynn Forest, making them unlikely to hunt down an aggressive kobold over an old lady's lost necklace.",al={"why me billy","why not stormwind guards","why does billy need help"},it="why_me",add="4539d353"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, you help ease friction between two of Elwynn's oldest farming families and face the kobolds that plague the realm."},kw={"bernice","billy","fargodeep","goldtooth","kobold","maclure","necklace","stonefield"},rel={"quest:84","npc:billy-maclure","npc:auntie-bernice-stonefield","subzone:fargodeep-mine","subzone:stonefield-farm","topic:kobold","quest:62","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Billy Maclure",["end"]="\"Auntie\" Bernice Stonefield",faction="Alliance",id=87,ri={"Bernice's Necklace"}},src={"Goldtooth (quest)"}}
E["quest:88"] = {t="quest",n="Princess Must Die!",z="elwynn",s="At Stonefield Farm, Ma Stonefield asks you to kill Princess before the sow ruins the harvest. The enormous prize-winning pig from Brackwell Pumpkin Patch keeps raiding the Stonefields’ vegetables, putting the family’s crops at risk.",h="At Stonefield Farm, Ma Stonefield asks you to kill Princess before the sow ruins the harvest.",sec={{t="A Menace to the Harvest",b="The sow belongs to the Brackwells. She grew enormous by crossing onto the Stonefield plots. Ma has had enough of Princess eating the crops she worked to grow. She wants the pig put down before the season’s yield is lost.",sp=0},{t="The Porcine Entourage",b="Princess stays at Brackwell Pumpkin Patch, east beyond the Maclure homestead. Protective boars surround her. Get past her guards and bring Ma the distinctive brass collar from Princess’s neck. It will prove the sow can trouble the Stonefield fields no more.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Princess?",a="Princess is an enormous, prize-winning sow belonging to the Brackwell family. She grew so large by sneaking onto Stonefield Farm and gorging on Ma Stonefield’s vegetables.",al={"what is princess","princess elwynn","who is the pig princess"},it="target"},{q="Why does Ma Stonefield want Princess killed?",a="Princess keeps wandering into Ma Stonefield’s fields and devouring the vegetables. Ma fears the sow will eat the family’s entire harvest, so she hires travelers to slay Princess and bring back her brass collar as proof.",al={"why kill princess","ma stonefield pig quest","why does princess must die"},it="motive"},{q="Where can Princess be found?",a="Princess can be found at Brackwell Pumpkin Patch in southeastern Elwynn Forest, east beyond the Maclure Vineyards. She roams among the ruined pumpkins with boars guarding her.",al={"princess location","where is princess","princess spawn"},gp=true},{q="Who owns the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch?",a="The Brackwell family owns Brackwell Pumpkin Patch. Bandits and wild beasts have brought hard times to the local farmers and their lands in southern Elwynn Forest. Though the family has neglected the patch, Princess stayed behind to gorge on what remained.",al={"who are the brackwells","brackwell farm lore","brackwell owners"}},{q="How do you prove Princess is dead?",a="Bring the Brass Collar from around Princess’s neck to Ma Stonefield at Stonefield Farm to prove she is dead.",al={"princess proof","what item for princess","brass collar"},gp=true},{q="Does Princess fight alone?",a="No. Defensive boars called the Porcine Entourage accompany Princess and attack anyone who tries to slay the prize sow.",al={"princess adds","princess entourage","princess guards"},gp=true},{q="What is the Brass Collar for?",a="Princess is a prized domestic sow, marked by the brass collar fastened around her thick neck. Ma Stonefield asks you to tear it off her carcass and bring it back as undeniable proof that the gluttonous beast has been put down before she can ravage the Stonefield vegetable patches again.",al={"brass collar purpose","why take princess collar","princess collar"},it="item",add="f51dd6ea"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Princess’s great size has become a tale among local cooks. Elwynn’s oversized boars yield plenty of hearty meat for roasting over an open fire.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you help farmers like Ma Stonefield keep rogue beasts from threatening Stormwind’s southern breadbasket, even while the kingdom’s formal army is absent."},kw={"boar","brackwell pumpkin patch","brass collar","elwynn","ma stonefield","princess","sow","stonefield farm"},rel={"npc:ma-stonefield","subzone:stonefield-farm","subzone:brackwell-pumpkin-patch","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Ma Stonefield",level="9",faction="Alliance",id=88,ri={"Brass Collar"}},src={"Princess Must Die! (Classic)"}}
E["quest:91723"] = {t="quest",n="Delicate Instruments",z="elwynn",s="Hamish Bergwort's instruments at the Tower of Azora falter as surges of magic rise from the north. Their source is Jasperlode Mine, where kobold geomancers stir the earth.",h="Hamish Bergwort's instruments at the Tower of Azora falter as surges of magic rise from the north.",sec={{t="Disrupted Calibrations",b="At the Tower of Azora, Hamish Bergwort's arcane apparatus needs careful calibration. Uncontrolled surges keep unsettling his measurements. He cannot make precise adjustments while the interference continues.",sp=0},{t="The Interference from Jasperlode",b="The magical pulses lead north to Jasperlode Mine. Kobolds have taken its tunnels, where their geomancers work crude earth magic. Their frequent rituals send ripples through the stone. Those tremors unsettle the Tower of Azora's sensitive instruments.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Hamish Bergwort?",a="Hamish Bergwort is an arcane researcher at the Tower of Azora in Elwynn Forest. His sensitive instruments need precise calibration and are easily disturbed by magical fluctuations.",al={"who is hamish bergwort","quest giver delicate instruments","hamish bergwort tower of azora"}},{q="Why are the arcane instruments malfunctioning?",a="Magical surges from Jasperlode Mine to the north disrupt the instruments. Kobolds there create the surges with crude earth magic.",al={"why are instruments disrupted","cause of arcane surges","what is interfering with azora"}},{q="What is Jasperlode Mine?",a="Jasperlode Mine lies north of the Tower of Azora in Elwynn Forest. Kobolds occupy its tunnels, where geomantic rituals send ripples through the surrounding woods.",al={"what is jasperlode mine","where are the geomancers","jasperlode kobolds"}},{q="What are Kobold Geomancers?",a="Kobold geomancers are spellcasters among the kobold packs who wield crude elemental earth magic. Their rituals together create disturbances that interfere with sensitive arcane equipment.",al={"what are kobold geomancers","kobold magic users","geomancy kobold"}},{q="How does eliminating the geomancers resolve the issue?",a="Stopping the geomancers' rituals in Jasperlode Mine ends the elemental surges. Then researchers at the Tower of Azora can calibrate their devices without interference.",al={"why kill geomancers","delicate instruments purpose","stopping the surges"}},{q="What is the Tower of Azora?",a="The Tower of Azora is an arcane study spire in eastern Elwynn Forest. Scholars and mages there observe regional phenomena and maintain finely tuned magical apparatus.",al={"what is tower of azora","azora tower lore","elwynn mage tower"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you know the Tower of Azora's delicate apparatus needs steady surroundings. Crude geomantic magic can disrupt careful arcane study.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can help protect Elwynn Forest's scholarly enclaves by aiding the researchers at the Tower of Azora against the kobolds' disruptive magic."},kw={"arcane","delicate instruments","elwynn forest","geomancy","hamish bergwort","jasperlode mine","kobold","kobold geomancer","tower of azora"},rel={"subzone:tower-of-azora","subzone:jasperlode-mine","topic:kobold"},m={faction="Alliance",id=91723},src={"In-game quest text: Delicate Instruments"},fv=true}
E["quest:91724"] = {t="quest",n="Delicate Instruments",z="elwynn",s="At the Tower of Azora, Defias magic troubles Delicate Instruments. Hamish Bergwort's equipment suffers from erratic spellcasting near Stone Cairn Lake. The disturbance must end before his instruments can work properly.",h="At the Tower of Azora, Defias magic troubles Delicate Instruments.",sec={{t="Interference at the Tower",b="Hamish Bergwort studies arcane questions in the Tower of Azora. His work depends on precise readings, and even a slight change in local magic can ruin hours of careful study. He suspects crude spells nearby are causing the interruptions.",sp=0},{t="Banditry and the Arcane",b="Defias rogue wizards practice magic near Stone Cairn Lake, and their casting causes the interference. Their unchecked spellcraft brings unstable magic into Elwynn. End their casting, and the disturbance will cease, allowing Bergwort's instruments to give clean readings.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers the quest Delicate Instruments?",a="Hamish Bergwort offers Delicate Instruments from the Tower of Azora in eastern Elwynn Forest. He needs stable magical conditions for his research.",al={"who gives delicate instruments","delicate instruments questgiver","where is hamish bergwort"}},{q="What is disrupting Hamish Bergwort's instruments?",a="Crude spells from Defias bandits near Stone Cairn Lake interfere with the instruments in the Tower of Azora.",al={"what is disrupting the instruments","why are instruments disrupted","delicate instruments interference"}},{q="Where can the Defias Rogue Wizards be found?",a="The Defias rogue wizards gather along the shores and surrounding grounds of Stone Cairn Lake, just north of the Tower of Azora in Elwynn Forest.",al={"where are the rogue wizards","stone cairn lake rogue wizards","where to find defias rogue wizards"}},{q="Why are Defias bandits practicing magic?",a="The Defias Brotherhood has recruited renegade dabblers in the arcane. These rogue wizards practice magic without sanction and cause erratic disturbances in the region.",al={"why do defias have wizards","defias spellcasters","rogue wizards lore"}},{q="What is the Tower of Azora?",a="The Tower of Azora is an arcane spire in eastern Elwynn Forest. Human magi and scholars study ley lines, magical anomalies, and regional security there.",al={"what is tower of azora","azora tower elwynn","who runs tower of azora"}},{q="Does eliminating the rogue wizards fix the problem?",a="Yes. Once you cull the Defias rogue wizards casting at Stone Cairn Lake, the magical resonance calms and Hamish Bergwort's apparatus works properly again.",al={"does stopping the wizards work","delicate instruments outcome","hamish bergwort instruments fixed"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you know careless spells from amateurs like the Defias rogue wizards can send wild fluctuations across Elwynn and disrupt sensitive magical research.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help keep eastern Elwynn Forest secure from Defias encroachment by maintaining order around the Tower of Azora."},kw={"defias brotherhood","defias rogue wizard","delicate instruments","elwynn forest","hamish bergwort","stone cairn lake","tower of azora"},rel={"subzone:tower-of-azora","subzone:stone-cairn-lake"},m={faction="Alliance",id=91724},src={"In-game quest text: Delicate Instruments"},fv=true}
E["quest:91725"] = {t="quest",n="Stolen Enchanting Supplies",z="elwynn",s="Near the Tower of Azora, Blixie Fitzwink has lost the supplies she was carrying after a gnoll ambush. The enchanting reagents are scattered among camps around Stone Cairn Lake. Their return could spare her weeks of chore duty and keep Master Theocritus's arcane studies supplied.",h="Near the Tower of Azora, Blixie Fitzwink has lost the supplies she was carrying after a gnoll ambush.",sec={{t="An Ambush on the Road",b="Blixie Fitzwink was carrying supplies from a trading post to the Tower of Azora when gnolls ambushed her on the road. She fled, leaving the cargo scattered among their camps along Stone Cairn Lake. The valuable reagents were meant for Master Theocritus, whom Blixie assists. Now she asks travelers to recover them, fearing weeks of cleanup duty after her arcane polymorph experiments.",sp=0},{t="Arcane Errands and Local Hazards",b="Master Theocritus conducts sensitive magical research at the Tower of Azora in eastern Elwynn Forest. His work depends on delicate reagents brought from local trading posts. Gnoll packs around Stone Cairn Lake have grown bolder, making the route dangerous. The lost supplies could interrupt his studies, while their return may spare his beleaguered assistant further trouble.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Stolen Enchanting Supplies?",a="Blixie Fitzwink asks for help near the Tower of Azora. She assists Master Theocritus and was ambushed by gnolls while carrying supplies back from a local trading post.",al={"who gives stolen enchanting supplies","who is blixie fitzwink","quest giver blixie"}},{q="Who is Master Theocritus?",a="Master Theocritus is a senior human wizard who lives at the Tower of Azora in eastern Elwynn Forest. He oversees arcane investigations in the region and relies on assistants to bring him enchanting reagents and research materials.",al={"who is master theocritus","theocritus role","tower of azora mage"}},{q="What supplies were taken by the gnolls?",a="The gnolls took enchanting reagents gathered at a trading post for Master Theocritus's arcane work. The ambush scattered the cargo, and the items ended up in gnoll camps around Stone Cairn Lake.",al={"what are the supplies","what did gnolls steal","enchanting reagents"}},{q="Where did the gnolls take the supplies?",a="Stone Cairn Lake lies in eastern Elwynn Forest, north of the Tower of Azora. Gnoll packs camp along its shores and on surrounding islands, threatening travelers on nearby roads.",al={"where is stone cairn lake","where are gnolls holding supplies","lake gnolls elwynn"}},{q="Why is Blixie Fitzwink worried about losing the package?",a="Blixie fears Master Theocritus will give her weeks of cleaning duty after his polymorph experiments. Apprentices at the tower face mundane or messy chores when errands or magical duties go wrong.",al={"what happens if blixie fails","blixie punishment","polymorph cleanup"}},{q="Why are gnolls attacking travelers in eastern Elwynn?",a="Gnoll packs prowl eastern Elwynn Forest, with hostile camps around Stone Cairn Lake and raids on nearby roads. They disrupt trade and ambush travelers moving between settlements and arcane outposts.",al={"why are gnolls near tower of azora","gnoll threat elwynn","riverpaw stone cairn lake"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Keeping the supply route to the Tower of Azora secure helps Stormwind's frontline mages stay equipped against threats in Elwynn Forest and beyond.",["class:Mage"]="The Tower of Azora's arcane research depends on delicate materials. Recovered enchanting reagents matter to mages studying under Master Theocritus.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome apprentice, you may find yourself doing menial work for human archmages. A mistake can bring humiliating chore duty."},kw={"blixie fitzwink","elwynn forest","enchanting supplies","gnolls","master theocritus","polymorph","stone cairn lake","tower of azora"},rel={"subzone:tower-of-azora","subzone:stone-cairn-lake","npc:theocritus","topic:gnoll"},m={faction="Alliance",id=91725},src={"In-game quest text: Stolen Enchanting Supplies"},fv=true}
E["quest:91732"] = {t="quest",n="Good Steel",z="elwynn",s="At Eastvale Logging Camp, Hagar Lowe seeks good steel for the tools worn by its woodcutters. With fine metal scarce after the wars, he sends adventurers to Jasperlode Mine for picks whose steel can be reused.",h="At Eastvale Logging Camp, Hagar Lowe seeks good steel for the tools worn by its woodcutters.",sec={{t="A Kingdom's Scarcity",b="After the wars that battered the human kingdoms, good steel grows scarce in Elwynn Forest. At Eastvale Logging Camp, woodcutters rely on sturdy axes, saws, and other tools. Constant use and poor metal have worn them down. Without steady shipments from Stormwind's foundries, craftsman Hagar Lowe must keep the camp working with what he can find.",sp=0},{t="Salvaging the Past",b="North of Eastvale Logging Camp, Jasperlode Mine lies abandoned after its fall. Miners once worked its rich veins with finely made picks, forged when steel was plentiful and expertly tempered. Hagar sends adventurers into the infested tunnels to bring those picks back to Eastvale. Their sound metal can be melted down and made into tools for the camp's lumberjacks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Good Steel?",a="Hagar Lowe, a craftsman at Eastvale Logging Camp in eastern Elwynn Forest, asks adventurers to salvage good steel equipment from abandoned workings. The camp needs reliable tools.",al={"who gives good steel","where do i turn in good steel","who is hagar lowe"}},{q="Why does Hagar Lowe need mining tools from Jasperlode Mine?",a="Wars have left quality steel scarce, and the camp's tools badly worn. Hagar wants the finely made picks abandoned in Jasperlode Mine so he can reuse their steel for tools used in lumbering.",al={"why get picks","why does hagar want mining tools","purpose of mining tools"}},{q="What is Jasperlode Mine?",a="Jasperlode Mine is an old mining site in north-eastern Elwynn Forest, north of Eastvale Logging Camp. It was overrun and abandoned, leaving finely made mining equipment in its depths.",al={"what is jasperlode mine","where are the tools","jasperlode lore"}},{q="Why is good steel in short supply?",a="The Third War and prolonged conflicts disrupted production, supply lines, and trade across the human kingdoms. Resources are stretched thin as the realm is defended and rebuilt, so outlying places like Eastvale salvage durable metal from old tools.",al={"why is steel scarce","steel shortage elwynn","after the war metal shortage"}},{q="What is Eastvale Logging Camp?",a="Eastvale Logging Camp is Stormwind's main timber settlement, on Elwynn Forest's eastern border near the Redridge Mountains. Its woodcutters supply raw lumber to Stormwind and nearby communities, so reliable tools matter to their work.",al={"where is eastvale logging camp","eastvale camp purpose","eastvale lumber camp"}},{q="What makes the tools in Jasperlode Mine so special?",a="The picks left in Jasperlode Mine were forged when craftsmanship was higher and steel was more plentiful. Their lasting shine and durability show Hagar they were made with better steel than is available today.",al={"who makes the picks","why are the picks good","mining tools quality"}}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="With high-grade steel scarce in post-war Elwynn, smiths and craftsmen must scrounge for metal and reuse it from old, abandoned tools.",["profession:Mining"]="The picks left behind in Jasperlode Mine show an older, finer standard of metalworking that workers in Elwynn struggle to match today.",["faction:Alliance"]="Strained supplies across Stormwind's outlying lands leave settlements like Eastvale Logging Camp salvaging abandoned tools to keep working."},kw={"eastvale logging camp","elwynn forest","good steel","hagar lowe","jasperlode mine","mining tools","post-war shortages","repurposing steel"},rel={"subzone:jasperlode-mine","subzone:eastvale-logging-camp"},m={faction="Alliance",id=91732},src={"In-game quest text: Good Steel"},fv=true}
E["quest:91733"] = {t="quest",n="Downstream",z="elwynn",s="Near Eastvale Logging Camp, Ormin Pelford's wagon has overturned, and the river has carried his woodworking tools downstream. Murlocs and wolves guard the banks where they lie.",h="Near Eastvale Logging Camp, Ormin Pelford's wagon has overturned, and the river has carried his woodworking...",sec={{t="A Mishap on the Road",b="Laborer Ormin Pelford was bringing a shipment back from a local trading post when his wagon tipped near Eastvale Logging Camp. Its gear spilled into the river, and the current swept it downstream before he could secure it. Without the woodworking tools, the loggers face delays in their timber work.",sp=0},{t="Perils Along the Riverbank",b="Ormin Pelford's lost cargo lies along banks where murlocs and wolves roam. Aggressive murlocs claim the muddy shoals downstream, while predatory wolves prowl the surrounding woods. Ormin cannot face those dangers alone. He needs hardy travelers to search the riverbanks, recover the submerged saw, axe, and toolbox, and bring them back safely.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Downstream?",a="Ormin Pelford asks for help near Eastvale Logging Camp. He is a laborer whose supply wagon overturned in the river while he was hauling goods from a trading post.",al={"who gives downstream","downstream quest giver","who is ormin pelford"}},{q="What supplies were lost in the water?",a="Ormin Pelford lost a Waterlogged Axe, a Waterlogged Saw, and a Waterlogged Toolbox. They fell into the river when his wagon tipped over.",al={"what fell in the river","lost supplies downstream","what items downstream"}},{q="Where did the supplies wash up?",a="The crates and tools drifted downstream along the river south of Eastvale Logging Camp in eastern Elwynn Forest.",al={"where are the tools","where do supplies wash up","downstream location"}},{q="Why can't Ormin Pelford retrieve the supplies himself?",a="Ormin Pelford cannot face the riverbanks alone, where river murlocs and forest wolves prowl near the cargo.",al={"why can't ormin get supplies","why ormin pelford needs help"}},{q="What dangers lurk along the riverbanks?",a="Aggressive murlocs claim the downstream riverbanks, and wolves prowl nearby. Salvage is dangerous there.",al={"downstream river hazards","threats downstream"}},{q="Why are these tools important to Eastvale?",a="The axes, saws, and toolboxes are essential to the woodsmen at Eastvale Logging Camp. They provide raw timber for Elwynn Forest and Stormwind.",al={"why are tools important eastvale","logging camp timber tools"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Keeping Eastvale Logging Camp supplied with tools helps its timber reach Stormwind and Elwynn's settlements."},kw={"downstream","eastvale logging camp","elwynn forest","murloc","ormin pelford","waterlogged axe","waterlogged saw","waterlogged toolbox"},rel={"subzone:eastvale-logging-camp","topic:murloc"},m={faction="Alliance",id=91733},src={"In-game quest text: Downstream"},fv=true}
E["quest:91736"] = {t="quest",n="Applejack Still",z="elwynn",s="At the Applejack Still, cider becomes a clear, potent spirit. Apple vapor rises as the coils turn it into liquor.",h="At the Applejack Still, cider becomes a clear, potent spirit.",sec={{t="The Distillation Device",b="Fermented cider passes through the still and emerges as strong spirit. Near the apparatus, apple vapor stings the nostrils. Pipes and coils draw the fruit's essence and condense it into liquor.",sp=0},{t="A Clear Pour",b="Alcohol vapor condenses inside the still and becomes a clear spirit. Applejack flows from the outlet into a waiting bottle, ready to drink or store. Even in rough field conditions, the apparatus produces a clear, potent brew.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Applejack Still?",a="The Applejack Still distills fermented apples into applejack, a potent spirit. Coils condense the vapor into clear liquor that pours into a bottle.",al={"what is applejack still","what is this device","what does the still do"}},{q="Why is the apple scent so strong around the still?",a="Concentrated apple vapor gives the still its sharp scent, strong enough to sting the nostrils. The vapor rises as alcohol evaporates and condenses inside the metal coils.",al={"what does it smell like","why does it burn","still scent"}},{q="What kind of liquid does the machine dispense?",a="The still pours a clear spirit into a bottle. This applejack is a potent fruit brandy made by distilling fermented apples.",al={"what liquid comes out","clear liquid still","what does it dispense"}},{q="How does the distillation device operate?",a="The still heats fermented apple cider or wash, separating alcohol vapor from water and fruit solids. Coils condense the vapor, and the spirit collects at the spout before filling a waiting bottle.",al={"how does applejack still work","distillation process"}},{q="What exactly is applejack?",a="Applejack is a strong alcoholic drink made by distilling fermented apple cider. It is clear and aromatic, with more alcohol than ordinary cider or ale.",al={"what is applejack","applejack drink"}},{q="Is operating the still hazardous?",a="The still gives off alcoholic vapors strong enough to sting the nose. It dispenses clear liquor, but high-proof vapor and pressure call for caution.",al={"is the still safe","is it dangerous"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can distill and brew strong spirits from orchard fruit, a craft known among rustic cooks and tavern keepers across Azeroth.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can see how mechanical condensation and plumbing turn fermented cider into concentrated liquor automatically."},kw={"alcohol","apparatus","applejack","brewing","cider","distillery","liquor","still"},m={faction="Alliance",id=91736},src={"In-game quest text: Applejack Still"},fv=true}
E["quest:91738"] = {t="quest",n="An Apple Treat",z="elwynn",s="A sergeant welcomes a bottle of Thunder Applejack after months without any. He says it should cheer the troops.",h="A sergeant welcomes a bottle of Thunder Applejack after months without any.",sec={{t="A Welcome Bottle",b="A sergeant recognizes your Thunder Applejack and says the troops will be glad of it. He thanks you for bringing it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the sergeant want?",a="The sergeant welcomes a bottle of Thunder Applejack, which he says should bring the troops some cheer.",al={"what does he need","sergeant applejack","apple treat"}},{q="How long has it been since he saw Thunder Applejack?",a="The sergeant says he has not seen Thunder Applejack in months.",al={"applejack how long","months without it","when last applejack"}},{q="Who is the bottle for?",a="The sergeant says the bottle should put a smile on the troops' faces.",al={"who gets the applejack","applejack for troops","who wants the bottle"}}},kw={"an apple treat","bottle","sergeant","thunder applejack","troops"},m={faction="Alliance",id=91738},src={"In-game quest text: An Apple Treat"},fv=true}
E["quest:91740"] = {t="quest",n="Croaky's Head",z="elwynn",s="At Ridgepoint Tower, Croaky's death brings grim relief to a grieving Stormwind garrison. The murloc leader terrorized eastern Elwynn's roads. Proof of his death gives the guards hope as they struggle to secure the waterways.",h="At Ridgepoint Tower, Croaky's death brings grim relief to a grieving Stormwind garrison.",sec={{t="Terror on the Eastvale Roads",b="Murlocs along Elwynn Forest's rivers and streams have grown bolder. They ambush travelers and threaten trade routes. Croaky was a particularly aggressive chieftain who rallied other murlocs to attack near local roads. Merchants, farmers, and travelers between Elwynn and Redridge now face deadly roads. Croaky's death ends his ambushes and removes a threat to Stormwind's hold on the eastern woodland outskirts.",sp=0},{t="The Watch at Ridgepoint Tower",b="Ridgepoint Tower guards Elwynn Forest's eastern edge and the strategic crossing into the Redridge Mountains. Officer Merell Ross leads the guards, though dangers around the outpost have stretched them thin. Murloc attacks recently killed two watchmen on patrol.\n\nThe deaths shook the garrison and exposed the vulnerable border. Bringing Croaky's severed head to Ross proves the chieftain is dead. Now the guards have reason to hope they can drive the raiders back from Elwynn's borders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Croaky?",a="Croaky was a notorious murloc leader who terrorized travelers and patrols along eastern Elwynn Forest's waterways. His particularly aggressive ambushes near roads threatened regional peace until an adventurer hunted him down.",al={"who is croaky","croaky lore","what kind of murloc is croaky"}},{q="Who is Merell Ross?",a="Merell Ross is a member of the Stormwind city watch stationed at Ridgepoint Tower on Elwynn Forest's eastern border. Ross oversees border security and seeks to rally the garrison after murloc raids killed guards. The watch protects the high road into the Redridge Mountains.",al={"merell ross","who is officer ross","ridgepoint tower commander"}},{q="Where is Ridgepoint Tower located?",a="Ridgepoint Tower guards the far eastern edge of Elwynn Forest and the road into the Redridge Mountains. East of the Eastvale Logging Camp, the stone garrison houses Stormwind guards facing hostile creatures and highway bandits.",al={"where is ridgepoint tower","ridgepoint tower location","how to find ridgepoint tower"}},{q="Why did the guards at Ridgepoint Tower want Croaky dead?",a="Murlocs recently killed two Ridgepoint Tower patrol members in the surrounding woods and waters. The guards want Croaky dead to stop the road ambushes and begin a concerted effort to drive the murlocs out of Elwynn.",al={"why kill croaky","why do guards want croakys head","murloc attack on ridgepoint watch"}},{q="What does turning in Croaky's Head accomplish for Elwynn Forest?",a="Bringing Croaky's Head to Ridgepoint Tower proves a dangerous organizer of roadside raids is dead. The guards hope to regain the offensive, secure eastern trade paths, and gradually push murloc tribes from Elwynn's riverbanks.",al={"croakys head purpose","what happens when you kill croaky","turn in croakys head"}},{q="Why are murlocs such a threat along Elwynn's roads?",a="Murlocs commonly nest along Elwynn Forest's rivers, lakes, and streams, and key roads run beside those waterways. Their tribes ambush travelers, trade caravans, and isolated patrols, overwhelming defenders with unpredictable numbers and fierce raids.",al={"why are murlocs attacking roads","elwynn murloc problem","murloc threat in elwynn"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion, you aid Stormwind's overextended forces by eliminating dangerous leaders who prey on travelers. Securing the eastern border road reinforces Alliance authority between Elwynn and Redridge.",["race:Human"]="As a human of Elwynn, you face murloc incursions that threaten homesteads and claim the lives of local town guardsmen. Slaying Croaky brings justice for two fallen watchmen and defends the realm's heartland.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you know the brutal reality of frontline combat and the cost paid by fallen watchmen. Felling an aggressive chieftain relieves a hard-pressed defensive line."},kw={"croaky","croaky's head","eastvale","elwynn forest","merell ross","murloc","ridgepoint tower","stormwind guard"},rel={"subzone:ridgepoint-tower","topic:murloc"},m={faction="Alliance",id=91740},src={"In-game quest text: Croaky's Head"},fv=true}
E["quest:91741"] = {t="quest",n="Nibbled-On Book",z="elwynn",s="In Northshire Valley, Nibbled-On Book has been chewed by kobolds. Brother Paxton hopes to see it returned to Northshire Abbey's modest collection.",h="In Northshire Valley, Nibbled-On Book has been chewed by kobolds.",sec={{t="A Chewed Tome",b="Kobolds in Northshire Valley scavenge what they find left unguarded. You recover a chewed tome from a slain kobold, its cover torn and its parchment marked by teeth. The book came from the library shelves of nearby Northshire Abbey. Valley kobolds have been taking volumes from there.",sp=0},{t="Brother Paxton's Plight",b="Brother Paxton tends the small library inside Northshire Abbey, where the Brotherhood of Northshire reads and studies. Kobolds from the valley slip inside and snatch books from the shelves. Paxton is grateful to have this nibbled volume back. Yet he worries about the rest of his collection still missing in kobold hands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Nibbled-On Book?",a="Kobolds stole the volume from Northshire Abbey. Its cover bears tooth marks, as though the scavengers mistook its parchment and leather binding for food.",al={"what is this book","nibbled book lore","what book did the kobold drop"}},{q="Why did the kobolds try to eat the book?",a="The tooth marks suggest the kobolds tried to chew or eat the book. They scavenge what they find, and Brother Paxton says they steal his books to gnaw on them.",al={"why do kobolds want books","why are kobolds eating books","kobold diet books"}},{q="Who is Brother Paxton?",a="Brother Paxton is a cleric at Northshire Abbey who cares for its modest library. Kobolds sneaking into the abbey and taking books from his shelves distress him.",al={"who is brother paxton","paxton northshire","abbey librarian"}},{q="Where did the book originally come from?",a="The book came from the small library Brother Paxton keeps inside Northshire Abbey, in Northshire Valley of Elwynn Forest.",al={"where did the book come from","where does paxton keep books","northshire library"}},{q="Are there other missing books from the abbey's library?",a="Yes. Brother Paxton worries that kobolds have repeatedly stolen from his shelves. He wonders what to do about the rest of his missing collection.",al={"are more books missing","rest of the collection","did kobolds steal more books"}},{q="Who should the book be returned to?",a="Return the recovered book to Brother Paxton inside Northshire Abbey. He inspects its tooth-marked cover and takes it back into his care.",al={"how to get the book back","who wants the nibbled book","return book to paxton"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance recruit in Elwynn Forest, you help secure Northshire Valley by recovering property stolen from Northshire Abbey.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you share an interest in Northshire Abbey's library, which preserves clerical and historical knowledge for the kingdom of Stormwind."},kw={"abbey library","brother paxton","elwynn forest","kobold","nibbled-on book","northshire abbey","stolen book"},rel={"topic:kobold","quest:344"},m={faction="Alliance",id=91741},src={"In-game quest text: Nibbled-On Book"},fv=true}
E["quest:91743"] = {t="quest",n="Rascally Rodents",z="elwynn",s="Kobolds are carrying books away from Brother Paxton’s library in Northshire Valley. He fears they are devouring the abbey’s collection.",h="Kobolds are carrying books away from Brother Paxton’s library in Northshire Valley.",sec={{t="A Threat to the Library",b="Brother Paxton fears the kobolds that have spread from the hills and mines into Northshire Valley’s sacred grounds. He believes they are devouring books from his collection. With the library at risk, he asks young adventurers to hunt the kobolds and recover whatever volumes they can.",sp=0},{t="An Unexplained Appetite",b="Brother Paxton finds that the eight recovered volumes have not been eaten. The kobolds took and hoarded the books for reasons he cannot explain. Many volumes are still missing from the valley, and their strange interest in the books leaves him unsettled.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Rascally Rodents?",a="Brother Paxton, a resident of the abbey in Northshire Valley, asks for help protecting its library from the kobolds.",al={"who gives rascally rodents","quest giver rascally rodents","paxton book quest"}},{q="Why are the kobolds stealing books?",a="Brother Paxton thinks the kobolds are eating his books, but the recovered volumes are untouched. Why the kobolds take and hoard them remains unknown.",al={"why kobolds taking books","do kobolds eat books","why do kobolds want books"}},{q="Where do you find the Stolen Books?",a="You find the Stolen Books among the kobolds in Northshire Valley, in their camps and mine workings.",al={"where to find stolen books","stolen books location","kobold books northshire"}},{q="Who is Brother Paxton?",a="Brother Paxton belongs to the Northshire brotherhood and cares deeply for the abbey’s books. He relies on passing initiates to recover them from scavengers.",al={"who is brother paxton","brother paxton lore"}},{q="What does Brother Paxton give you as a reward?",a="When you return eight stolen volumes, Brother Paxton gives you one of his how-to books, which he says he does not need. Many volumes remain missing.",al={"what reward paxton gives","how to book reward"}},{q="Are all the stolen books recovered?",a="No. Brother Paxton says many volumes are still missing from the valley, and the kobolds’ interest in them remains unexplained.",al={"are all books recovered","are all books saved"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human initiate training in Northshire Valley, you help defend the abbey’s treasures and books from pests and invaders.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest aiding the Abbey of Northshire, you help protect the Holy Light’s scholars and their books from destruction.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you know written knowledge is precious, even when kobolds threaten it."},kw={"brother paxton","kobolds","library","northshire abbey","northshire valley","rascally rodents","stolen books"},rel={"quest:344","subzone:northshire-valley","topic:kobold"},m={faction="Alliance",id=91743},src={"In-game quest text: Rascally Rodents"},fv=true}
E["quest:91745"] = {t="quest",n="Mining Consultant",z="elwynn",s="At Echo Ridge Mine, Kelsey Fargo watches the kobolds from her post outside the entrance. Their strange movements have drawn local attention.",h="At Echo Ridge Mine, Kelsey Fargo watches the kobolds from her post outside the entrance.",sec={{t="Trouble at the Mine",b="Kobold trouble at Echo Ridge Mine has taken an odd turn. The creatures defend their underground claims and gather candles, but now their coordinated disturbances have caught the authorities’ attention. You are sent to Kelsey Fargo, a mining apprentice stationed near the entrance. From her post outside the tunnels, she has watched the kobolds closely.",sp=0},{t="Scholarly Scavengers",b="Kelsey Fargo has seen kobolds scampering back and forth with heavy books and arguing as they go. She believes they stole the volumes from the library inside Northshire Abbey. What the tunnel dwellers want with books they cannot read remains unclear.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Kelsey Fargo?",a="Kelsey Fargo is a mining apprentice stationed just outside Echo Ridge Mine in Northshire Valley. From her post, she can watch the local kobolds’ movements and habits.",al={"who is kelsey fargo","kelsey fargo role","mining apprentice northshire"}},{q="Why are kobolds carrying books?",a="Kelsey Fargo has seen kobolds running back and forth with books while arguing. She suspects they stole the volumes from the library inside Northshire Abbey, but their purpose is unknown.",al={"why are kobolds stealing books","kobolds reading","books in echo ridge mine"}},{q="Where is Echo Ridge Mine?",a="Echo Ridge Mine lies in the hills northwest of Northshire Abbey, in northwestern Northshire Valley. Kobolds have heavily infested it and disrupted mining operations.",al={"where is echo ridge mine","echo ridge mine location"}},{q="Where are the kobolds getting these books?",a="The books are believed to have come from the library inside Northshire Abbey. Local human clergy and scholars keep records, scriptures, and historical volumes there.",al={"where do the books come from","abbey library kobolds"}},{q="What is the purpose of consulting the mining apprentice?",a="You are sent to speak with Kelsey Fargo outside the mine about the strange kobold activity. From her post, she can tell you what she has witnessed.",al={"mining consultant quest purpose","why talk to kelsey"}},{q="What strange behavior have the kobolds exhibited?",a="Kobolds around Echo Ridge Mine have been seen yelling at one another and carrying off written texts. Their behavior is unusually erratic compared with their usual digging and defense of their territory.",al={"what are the kobolds doing","kobold behavior northshire"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you can speak with Kelsey Fargo, an apprentice stationed just outside Echo Ridge Mine. She is a local contact for learning about mineral work and conditions nearby.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you begin in Northshire Valley, a training ground for new adventurers. The abbey’s archives and nearby mines matter to the region, and kobolds threaten them both."},kw={"echo ridge mine","kelsey fargo","kobold","library","mining","mining consultant","northshire abbey","northshire valley"},rel={"subzone:echo-ridge-mine","subzone:northshire-valley","topic:kobold"},m={faction="Alliance",id=91745},src={"In-game quest text: Mining Consultant"},fv=true}
E["quest:91746"] = {t="quest",n="Elmpaw's Head",z="elwynn",s="At Elmpaw's Head, the hunt is over, and a wealthy collector awaits its prize. The beast’s head goes to a handler who prepares and mounts trophies for affluent patrons.",h="At Elmpaw's Head, the hunt is over, and a wealthy collector awaits its prize.",sec={{t="The Fallen Beast",b="Elmpaw has fallen, and hunters prize the beast’s head as proof of victory. Trackers regard the hunt as an impressive feat, a hard-won end to the chase.",sp=0},{t="A Collector's Prize",b="A handler rewards you for Elmpaw’s severed head. Then the handler prepares and mounts it for wealthy patrons who want fierce wild trophies on their mantles.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who or what is Elmpaw?",a="Elmpaw is a formidable creature, and hunters regard bringing it down as an impressive feat. Its head proves the victory.",al={"who is elmpaw","what is elmpaw","elmpaw boss"}},{q="Why does the quest giver want Elmpaw's head?",a="The handler wants Elmpaw’s head to prepare and mount as a trophy for wealthy collectors who display such prizes on their mantles.",al={"why want head","elmpaw head turn in","what is trophy for"}},{q="Who are the collectors interested in the trophy?",a="The collectors are wealthy patrons who value exotic beast trophies for their homes. Once mounted, Elmpaw’s head can fetch a high price.",al={"who buys trophy","elmpaw buyers","who wants elmpaw head"}},{q="Is Elmpaw a dangerous target?",a="Elmpaw is a notable challenge, and hunters regard bringing the beast down as an impressive feat.",al={"how hard is elmpaw","is elmpaw tough"}},{q="What kind of task is Elmpaw's Head?",a="You hunt Elmpaw in the wild and bring its head to an interested handler. The handler rewards you and prepares the trophy for sale.",al={"is elmpaw head a bounty","who posted elmpaw quest"}},{q="Where can Elmpaw be found?",a="Elmpaw roams wilderness where hunters encounter dangerous beasts. After the hunt, bring its head back to the handler.",al={"elmpaw location","where to find elmpaw"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you know the skill it takes to bring down a formidable beast like Elmpaw and claim its trophy."},kw={"beast","collector","elmpaw","head","hunter","mantle","trophy"},m={faction="Alliance",id=91746},src={"In-game quest text: Elmpaw's Head"},fv=true}
E["quest:91751"] = {t="quest",n="Rough Wolf Pelts",z="elwynn",s="Near Goldshire, Rough Wolf Pelts are needed for Helene Peltskinner's leather orders. Her husband is occupied near Northshire Abbey, so she asks for help skinning local wolves.",h="Near Goldshire, Rough Wolf Pelts are needed for Helene Peltskinner's leather orders.",sec={{t="A Skinner's Need",b="Just outside Goldshire, Helene Peltskinner supplies travelers and residents with cured leather and furs. Her husband usually hunts Elwynn Forest's timber wolves for her. Now his duties near Northshire Abbey keep him away, while customer orders wait. So Helene asks passing apprentices to skin the local wolves.",sp=0},{t="Prowlers of the Forest",b="Timber wolves prowl Elwynn Forest's woodlands, farmlands, and roads. Skinning them gives novice skinners practice harvesting hides. Their pelts help Helene continue her leatherwork and keep trade moving through Goldshire. Hunters, too, sharpen their woodcraft.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Helene Peltskinner?",a="Helene Peltskinner is a skinner and leatherworker based just outside Goldshire in Elwynn Forest. She prepares hides and fills craft orders for travelers and locals. Her husband is occupied near Northshire Abbey, so she needs help gathering wolf hides for her work.",al={"who is helene peltskinner","helene peltskinner","who gives rough wolf pelts"}},{q="Why does Helene need wolf pelts?",a="Helene needs wolf pelts to fill her backlog of leather orders near Goldshire. Her husband usually hunts wolves for her work, but his duties elsewhere in Elwynn leave her short on hides. Passing travelers can help by skinning local wolves.",al={"why need rough wolf pelts","why collect pelts","what does helene do with pelts"}},{q="Where is Helene's husband?",a="Helene's husband is occupied near Northshire Abbey. He usually hunts wolves and gathers skins for her, so his absence leaves Helene needing help to keep up with her orders.",al={"where is helene husband","helene husband","who is helene husband"}},{q="Where are the wolves found in Elwynn Forest?",a="Timber wolves roam Elwynn Forest's woodlands around Goldshire and Northshire. Skinners harvest their pelts and bring them to Helene's leatherworking post.",al={"where to find rough wolf pelts","which wolves drop pelts","wolf locations elwynn"}},{q="Is skinning required to harvest these pelts?",a="Yes. Helene offers travelers practice in skinning, and the pelts come from skinning slain wolves. Hunting them alone does not provide the hides she needs.",al={"do i need skinning for rough wolf pelts","rough wolf pelts skinning requirement","skinning quest goldshire"}},{q="Where can Helene Peltskinner be found?",a="Helene Peltskinner works near Goldshire, the central settlement of Elwynn Forest. Her work is close to the township, where hunters and travelers on the King's Road can bring her hides from the forest.",al={"where is helene peltskinner located","helene peltskinner location","where to find helene"}}},kw={"elwynn forest","goldshire","helene peltskinner","leatherworking","pelts","rough wolf pelts","skinning","timber wolves"},rel={"subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn"},m={faction="Alliance",id=91751},src={"In-game quest text: Rough Wolf Pelts"},fv=true}
E["quest:91752"] = {t="quest",n="The Big Picture",z="elwynn",s="In Northshire Valley, kobolds carry stolen illustrated books into the mine for Shinyfinder Narf. The volumes are to be returned to Marshal McBride at Northshire Abbey.",h="In Northshire Valley, kobolds carry stolen illustrated books into the mine for Shinyfinder Narf.",sec={{t="The Kobold Book Thief",b="Kobolds in Northshire Valley have been seen fleeing with books and crying, “Picture for Narf!” Most gather candles and shiny trinkets, but Shinyfinder Narf seeks illustrated tomes. He has collected a sack of them in his hideout beneath the mine.",sp=0},{t="Recovering the Abbey's Tomes",b="The deeper shafts hold tougher, meaner kobolds who guard Narf and his strange hoard. To recover the stolen books, you face those darker tunnels and confront him. Then the sack goes to Marshal McBride at Northshire Abbey, who sees that the valuable volumes return to Brother Paxton.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Shinyfinder Narf?",a="Shinyfinder Narf leads kobolds deep in the mine near Northshire Valley. He hoards stolen books and calls for picture books, so local authorities have ordered his cache recovered.",al={"who is narf","shinyfinder narf lore","narf kobold"}},{q="Why are the kobolds stealing books?",a="Kobolds from the mine have been seen shouting, “Picture for Narf!” as they snatch books. Narf seeks illustrated works and keeps them in a sack deep in the tunnels.",al={"why do kobolds want picture books","what is picture for narf","why books stolen"}},{q="Whose books were stolen?",a="The stolen books belong to Brother Paxton, who lives at Northshire Abbey. Marshal McBride receives the recovered sack and arranges for the books to return to Brother Paxton's collection.",al={"who is brother paxton","paxton books"}},{q="Who is Marshal McBride?",a="Marshal McBride is the law enforcement officer stationed just inside Northshire Abbey. He keeps order, protects the abbey grounds and organizes defense against the local kobolds.",al={"who is marshal mcbride","where is mcbride"}},{q="Where can Shinyfinder Narf be found?",a="Shinyfinder Narf lives in the deeper, more dangerous reaches of the mine in Northshire Valley. Meaner kobolds surround him and guard his hoard.",al={"where is narf","where to find narf","mine location"}},{q="How dangerous is the mine where Narf lives?",a="The kobolds deeper in the mine with Narf are meaner and more hostile than the common scavengers outside. Narf and his den are dangerous for anyone traveling alone.",al={"is narf dangerous","can you solo narf"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion, you help keep Northshire Valley peaceful and recover stolen goods from the encroaching vermin.",["race:Human"]="As a human adventurer, you begin your service at Northshire Abbey, protecting Stormwind's outlying territories."},kw={"brother paxton","kobold","marshal mcbride","narf","northshire abbey","picture books","shinyfinder narf","the big picture"},rel={"npc:marshal-mcbride","quest:344","topic:kobold"},m={faction="Alliance",id=91752},src={"In-game quest text: The Big Picture"},fv=true}
E["quest:91753"] = {t="quest",n="An Enchanting Lesson",z="elwynn",s="At the Tower of Azora in Elwynn Forest, Kitta Firewind gives An Enchanting Lesson to apprentice enchanters. Kobold geomancers bind simple magic into crude wax effigies, showing why practice matters alongside arcane theory.",h="At the Tower of Azora in Elwynn Forest, Kitta Firewind gives An Enchanting Lesson to apprentice enchanters.",sec={{t="Theory and Practice",b="Kitta Firewind, an enchanter at the Tower of Azora, challenges apprentice enchanters to look beyond polished libraries. She asks them to examine magic where it appears naturally. Even the uneducated kobolds beneath Elwynn Forest channel cantrips into everyday talismans, proof that magical instinct can thrive without formal schooling.",sp=0},{t="Primitive Cantrips",b="Kobold geomancers shape Crude Wax Effigies with simple folk enchantments. Students obtain the effigies and carefully unravel their bound magic through disenchantment, extracting Luminous Residue. By taking these primitive charms apart, they learn how raw magic behaves in the field. Enchantment's fundamental threads are found through observation as well as in grimoires.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest An Enchanting Lesson?",a="Kitta Firewind, an enchanter at the Tower of Azora in Elwynn Forest, offers this lesson to adventurers. She teaches that scholarly theory and hands-on practice belong together.",al={"who gives an enchanting lesson","quest giver enchanting lesson","kitta firewind quest"}},{q="Where is the Tower of Azora located?",a="The Tower of Azora stands in eastern Elwynn Forest. It is a bastion of magical study and wizardry amid the farmlands and woods of the human kingdom.",al={"where is tower of azora","tower of azora location"}},{q="How do kobolds know how to use magic?",a="Kobolds have no formal schooling or scholarly traditions, yet geomancers have an instinctive knack for binding basic cantrips and enchantments into crude wax effigies.",al={"can kobolds do magic","kobold geomancers magic","do kobolds have enchantments"}},{q="What are the wax effigies used for?",a="Crude Wax Effigies are primitive items fashioned by kobold geomancers. Though unsophisticated, they hold bound magic that can be unraveled and studied through disenchanting.",al={"what are wax effigies","crude wax effigies","kobold wax magic"}},{q="What is Luminous Residue?",a="Luminous Residue is the essence obtained by deconstructing and disenchanting the crude wax effigies carried by kobold geomancers. It is tangible proof of their innate cantrips.",al={"what is luminous residue","how to get luminous residue"}},{q="What is the main takeaway of Kitta Firewind's lesson?",a="Kitta Firewind teaches that theoretical knowledge and practical experimentation are inseparable. She urges students to study practical magic wherever it appears.",al={"lesson of the quest","what does kitta firewind teach"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Scholarly mages often scoff at subterranean vermin, yet Kitta Firewind reminds them that even primitive creatures can reveal unexpected truths about raw magical currents.",["faction:Alliance"]="Studying at the Tower of Azora in Elwynn Forest gives Alliance adventurers insight into academic wizardry and the surprisingly magical pests infesting their lands."},kw={"an enchanting lesson","disenchanting","elwynn forest","kitta firewind","kobold geomancer","luminous residue","tower of azora","wax effigy"},rel={"subzone:tower-of-azora","topic:kobold"},m={faction="Alliance",id=91753},src={"In-game quest text: An Enchanting Lesson"},fv=true}
E["quest:91758"] = {t="quest",n="Follow That Kobold!",z="elwynn",s="A kobold has fled Northshire's mines with Brother Paxton's books, and the abbey calls on Tordrin Sternblade to track it. Follow That Kobold! begins with a theft from the local mines.",h="A kobold has fled Northshire's mines with Brother Paxton's books, and the abbey calls on Tordrin Sternblade...",sec={{t="The Book Thief of Northshire",b="Kelsey saw a kobold flee the Northshire Abbey mine tunnels with a heavy sack of books. The workers and clerics thought the vermin in the mines were under control. The books belong to Brother Paxton, who needs them back in the abbey's collection.",sp=0},{t="Calling in the Mountaineer",b="The kobold is a nimble scavenger from below ground. Tracking it through Northshire Abbey's wooded grounds calls for special skill. You are sent behind the abbey to the stables, where Tordrin Sternblade can be found. The dwarven Hunter trainer has newly arrived from Ironforge, and his wilderness knowledge can help pick up the kobold's scent.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Follow That Kobold! about?",a="A kobold fled Northshire Valley's mine with a heavy sack of Brother Paxton's stolen books. The abbey wants them returned.",al={"what is follow that kobold","quest follow that kobold"}},{q="Who is Tordrin Sternblade?",a="Tordrin Sternblade is a dwarven Hunter trainer newly arrived from Ironforge. He is behind Northshire Abbey near the stables, where his tracking skill can help recover the books.",al={"who is tordrin sternblade","where is tordrin","hunter trainer northshire"}},{q="What did the kobold steal?",a="Kelsey reports that a kobold slipped out of the Northshire mine tunnels with a large sack of books. The human tomes belong to Brother Paxton, and the abbey needs them returned.",al={"why did kobold steal books","what did kobold take","sack of books"}},{q="Who reported the theft?",a="Kelsey Fargo, the new mining apprentice who works right outside the Northshire mine, reported the theft. She noticed a kobold leaving the tunnels with a sack stuffed with books.",al={"who is kelsey","kelsey northshire"}},{q="Who is Brother Paxton?",a="Brother Paxton is a cleric at Northshire Abbey. The stolen library materials belong to him or his sacred duties, so the abbey calls for an experienced tracker to recover them.",al={"who is brother paxton","paxton books"}},{q="How do you track the thieving kobold?",a="You are warned against charging blindly into the woods and sent to consult Tordrin Sternblade behind the abbey. His wilderness knowledge can help you track the thief.",al={"how do i track the kobold","tracking the thief"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a Hunter, you meet Tordrin Sternblade, a veteran Hunter trainer newly arrived from Ironforge to assist Northshire Abbey.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you bring traditional dwarven tracking expertise from Ironforge to help the humans of Northshire.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see Stormwind's holy abbey and an Ironforge mountaineer support one another."},kw={"brother paxton","follow that kobold","hunter trainer","ironforge","kelsey","kobold","northshire","tordrin sternblade"},rel={"topic:hunter","topic:kobold","zone:ironforge","quest:344"},m={faction="Alliance",id=91758},src={"In-game quest text: Follow That Kobold!"},fv=true}
E["quest:91772"] = {t="quest",n="Shhh! We're Hunting Kobolds",z="elwynn",s="Kobolds are moving from Northshire Valley toward Elwynn Forest. You follow their trail with a tracking kit and report what you find to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire.",h="Kobolds are moving from Northshire Valley toward Elwynn Forest.",sec={{t="Tracking the Vermin",b="Kobolds have spread beyond Northshire Valley and the abbey grounds. With a tracking kit, you follow their trail to learn where they gather. Your report will help Goldshire prepare for threats across Elwynn Forest.",sp=0},{t="The Fargodeep Connection",b="The tracks run southwest from Northshire and across Elwynn Forest toward Fargodeep Mine. Marshal Dughan commands Goldshire's garrison and already knows the mine is heavily infested with kobolds. Your report confirms the threat, and the mine remains overrun.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the goal of this task?",a="You follow kobolds moving beyond Northshire Valley with a tracking kit. Find where they are gathering, then report what you find to the Stormwind authorities in Goldshire.",al={"quest purpose","what is this quest","why hunt kobolds"}},{q="Who is concerned about the kobold movements?",a="Marshal McBride, commander of Northshire Valley, is concerned about the kobolds' movements. A local guide gives you a tracking kit so you can follow their trail out of the valley and into Elwynn Forest.",al={"who gives tracking kit","who is concerned about kobolds"}},{q="Where do the kobold tracks lead?",a="The tracks lead out of Northshire toward Fargodeep Mine in central Elwynn Forest. Kobolds have gathered there in force.",al={"where do tracks go","kobold destination","where are kobolds heading"}},{q="Who is Marshal Dughan?",a="Marshal Dughan commands the Stormwind guard garrison in Goldshire. He coordinates Elwynn Forest's local defenses and receives reports of threats moving into the region.",al={"who is marshal dughan","where is dughan","report to dughan"}},{q="Why are the kobolds heading to Fargodeep Mine?",a="Fargodeep Mine is already infested with kobolds. More of them heading there means greater danger for local workers and nearby settlements.",al={"why fargodeep mine","fargodeep kobolds"}},{q="What happens once you reach Goldshire?",a="When you report to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire, he confirms that kobolds infest Fargodeep Mine. He is not surprised and prepares to recruit fighters to confront them.",al={"what happens after reporting","dughan reaction"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer leaving Northshire, you help protect Elwynn's supply lines and settlements. Goldshire's garrison needs to know when threats gather.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you know a tracking kit can help you follow vermin trails through the woods."},kw={"elwynn forest","fargodeep mine","goldshire","kobold tracking kit","kobolds","marshal dughan","marshal mcbride","northshire","shhh we're hunting kobolds"},rel={"subzone:fargodeep-mine","quest:62","npc:marshal-dughan","subzone:goldshire","npc:marshal-mcbride","topic:kobold"},m={faction="Alliance",id=91772},src={"In-game quest text: Shhh! We're Hunting Kobolds"},fv=true}
E["quest:91775"] = {t="quest",n="Book Return",z="elwynn",s="In Elwynn, Marshal Dughan sends you to Fargodeep Mine for Brother Paxton’s lost books. One volume, “Fun with Elementals,” could place dangerous instructions in kobold hands.",h="In Elwynn, Marshal Dughan sends you to Fargodeep Mine for Brother Paxton’s lost books.",sec={{t="Lost Pages in the Dark",b="Marshal Dughan sends you into Fargodeep Mine for books belonging to Brother Paxton of Northshire Abbey. Kobolds have overrun the mine, and Paxton fears they might read “Fun with Elementals.” Its simple instructions could teach them to summon an elemental in the tunnels.",sp=0},{t="Knowledge in Peril",b="Fargodeep Mine once brought gold to the kingdom of Stormwind. Now kobolds overrun its lower levels, while Elwynn’s defenders are stretched thin. The damp, dangerous caverns threaten the books. You carry the recovered volumes in a protective book bag, keeping Paxton’s records safe and arcane lessons beyond the kobolds’ reach.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest Book Return?",a="Marshal Dughan in Goldshire sends you into Fargodeep Mine for books belonging to Brother Paxton. One is “Fun with Elementals,” a magical primer Paxton is especially anxious to recover.",al={"what is book return","book return quest","who gives book return"}},{q="Why are Brother Paxton's books inside Fargodeep Mine?",a="Kobolds who stole Brother Paxton’s books from Northshire were tracked to Fargodeep Mine. Kobolds now overrun its tunnels, and Paxton wants the books gathered before they are ruined or misused.",al={"why paxton books in mine","how did books get into fargodeep","why are books in fargodeep mine"}},{q="What is the book 'Fun with Elementals'?",a="“Fun with Elementals” is an introductory book about conjuring that Brother Paxton is desperate to recover. He fears its simple instructions could let even a kobold summon an elemental servant deep in the mine.",al={"fun with elementals","what is fun with elementals","paxton elemental book"}},{q="Who is Brother Paxton?",a="Brother Paxton is a cleric at Northshire Abbey devoted to study, records, and literature. Some books he has lost contain potent, basic magic.",al={"who is brother paxton","paxton lore","librarian paxton"}},{q="Why is Marshal Dughan involved in retrieving books?",a="Marshal Dughan oversees Elwynn Forest’s defense from Goldshire. As he sends you to investigate kobolds in Fargodeep Mine, he also seeks to help Brother Paxton recover his books before the kobolds become a greater magical threat.",al={"why dughan care about books","marshal dughan books"}},{q="Could a kobold really summon an elemental?",a="Brother Paxton fears a simple guide could teach the kobolds to conjure elemental forces. Their growing presence in the mine already threatens Elwynn.",al={"can kobolds use magic","can kobolds summon elementals"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you know careless handling of arcane books like “Fun with Elementals” can put dangerous knowledge within reach of kobolds.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see Northshire Abbey and Goldshire’s garrison working together to protect books and dangerous magical texts from Elwynn’s pests."},kw={"book return","brother paxton","elwynn forest","fargodeep mine","fun with elementals","goldshire","kobold","marshal dughan"},rel={"quest:62","quest:344","subzone:fargodeep-mine","npc:marshal-dughan","topic:kobold"},m={faction="Alliance",id=91775},src={"In-game quest text: Book Return"},fv=true}
E["quest:91777"] = {t="quest",n="Rare Books",z="elwynn",s="In Northshire Valley, Rare Books sends you after two primers taken by kobolds. Brother Paxton needs them back at Northshire Abbey.",h="In Northshire Valley, Rare Books sends you after two primers taken by kobolds.",sec={{t="Missing from the Abbey",b="Brother Paxton has lost two books from the library at Northshire Abbey. Kobolds carrying books and other things have taken them into Jasperlode Mine. The missing volumes are Geomancy for Curious Young Wizards and Arcane Explainer: Magical Stuff in Simple Words. Both are primers on magic.",sp=0},{t="Arcane Kobolds in Jasperlode",b="Kobolds in Jasperlode Mine are studying the stolen books. An apprentice has already tried to summon an elemental. No one knows what a more practiced geomancer might call forth from those lessons.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the quest Rare Books?",a="You are asked to recover the last two books missing from Brother Paxton's catalog. Kobolds have taken them into Jasperlode Mine.",al={"rare books quest","what is rare books","what is this quest"}},{q="Who is Brother Paxton?",a="Brother Paxton is a cleric at Northshire Abbey who cares for its books and documents. Kobolds have taken volumes from the library, and he needs them returned.",al={"who is paxton","brother paxton lore","abbey librarian"}},{q="Which books need to be recovered?",a="The missing books are Geomancy for Curious Young Wizards and Arcane Explainer: Magical Stuff in Simple Words. Both introduce arcane and magical theory.",al={"which books are missing","stolen book titles","missing library books"}},{q="Where are the missing books located?",a="The missing books are in Jasperlode Mine in Northshire Valley. Kobold diggers and geomancers occupy the gold mine.",al={"where are the books","book locations","where to find the books"}},{q="Why did the kobolds take books on magic?",a="Kobolds in Jasperlode Mine appear to be using the books to study geomancy and spellcasting. An apprentice has tried to summon an elemental.",al={"why do kobolds have books","can kobolds read","kobold wizards"}},{q="Why does Brother Paxton reward weapons intended for the militia?",a="Brother Paxton gives helpers spare weapons set aside for the Northshire militia. He believes adventurers facing threats in the valley can put them to better use.",al={"paxton reward weapons","why militia weapons","abbey weapons"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you may recognize the basic principles in these primers. Their lessons have reached kobolds beneath the earth.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help recover books stolen from Northshire Abbey and aid the local militia."},kw={"arcane explainer","brother paxton","geomancy","jasperlode mine","kobold","northshire abbey","northshire valley","rare books"},rel={"subzone:jasperlode-mine","quest:344","quest:76","topic:kobold"},m={faction="Alliance",id=91777},src={"In-game quest text: Rare Books"},fv=true}
E["quest:92124"] = {t="quest",n="Book Inventory",z="elwynn",s="At Northshire Abbey, Brother Paxton needs help finding missing books. He sends young adventurers to Daniel, his daydreaming assistant, to count the library's archives. But Daniel's thoughts turn to local tradeskills, making a clear answer hard to get.",h="At Northshire Abbey, Brother Paxton needs help finding missing books.",sec={{t="A Librarian's Frustration",b="Northshire Abbey keeps scholarly works, spiritual writings, and records of Stormwind's history that survived the First War. Brother Paxton, a careful monk, takes pride in the collection. Now books are missing from the shelves, and he needs a clear count to learn how many are gone. He has little patience for chasing his daydreaming helper.",sp=0},{t="Daniel's Straying Interests",b="Daniel assists Brother Paxton in the abbey library, but his thoughts stray from parchment and catalog numbers. He is fascinated by the practical trades and professions of Elwynn Forest, including smithing, leatherworking, tailoring, and herbal craft. So when Paxton asks him to count the books, Daniel rambles about local crafters instead of looking for lost scriptures.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Brother Paxton?",a="Brother Paxton is a monk of Northshire Abbey who tends its extensive collection of books, scriptures, and historical scrolls. He takes pride in the collection and quickly loses his temper when books go missing or his helpers neglect their duties.",al={"brother paxton","who gives book inventory","paxton elwynn"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Daniel?",a="Daniel is Brother Paxton's young assistant in the Northshire Abbey library. He is meant to organize books and count the collection, though his thoughts often turn to tradeskills and professions across Elwynn Forest.",al={"who is daniel","paxton assistant","daniel northshire"},it="identity"},{q="Why are books missing from Northshire Abbey?",a="Brother Paxton says books have gone missing but gives no reason. He asks Daniel to count the collection and find out how many are gone.",al={"why are books missing","missing books northshire","lost books abbey"},it="conflict"},{q="Where can Daniel be found?",a="Daniel can be found inside Northshire Abbey, among the shelves and desks of the abbey library.",al={"where is daniel","daniel location","find daniel"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Paxton call Daniel useless?",a="Paxton considers Daniel useless because he neglects his library duties. Instead of cataloging and shelving books, Daniel spends his hours daydreaming and talking about practical tradeskills.",al={"why does paxton hate daniel","daniel useless"},it="ties"},{q="What tradeskills is Daniel interested in?",a="Daniel is fascinated by crafts practiced throughout Elwynn Forest, including blacksmithing, leatherworking, tailoring, and herbal craft. He prefers hands-on work to dusty tomes.",al={"daniel tradeskills","what professions does daniel like"}},{q="Why does Brother Paxton want a book inventory done?",a="Northshire Abbey has noticed books disappearing from its shelves, and Brother Paxton needs to determine the full scale of the loss before the abbey's collection suffers further. His assistant, Daniel, is supposed to keep the library in order, but his constant daydreaming about local trades has left Paxton frustrated and completely in the dark about how many volumes have actually gone missing.",al={"why book inventory","why does paxton want an inventory","paxton motive"},it="motive",add="deb80ab5"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a young human beginning service at Northshire Abbey, you may know the struggle to balance monastic study with practical village life.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest studying Northshire's sacred archives, you rely on order in the library to preserve holy scriptures and Church traditions."},kw={"book inventory","brother paxton","daniel","elwynn forest","library","northshire abbey","professions","tradeskills"},rel={"zone:elwynn","quest:344"},m={start="Brother Paxton",["end"]="Daniel",level="2",faction="Alliance",id=92124},src={"Book Inventory"},fv=true}
E["quest:92479"] = {t="quest",n="A Scribbled Letter",z="elwynn",s="At Northshire Abbey, adventurers receive a summons from Tordrin Stemblade after clashes with nearby kobolds. It calls promising recruits to seek his training as Stormwind faces growing dangers.",h="At Northshire Abbey, adventurers receive a summons from Tordrin Stemblade after clashes with nearby kobolds.",sec={{t="A Summons in Northshire",b="After clashes with kobold camps in the valley, adventurers at Northshire Abbey receive a hasty letter sealed by Tordrin Stemblade. It asks them to give it prompt attention before taking up other business. The summons brings budding champions to formal mentorship within the abbey’s protective grounds.",sp=0},{t="Guidance in Perilous Times",b="Tordrin Stemblade says times have changed. Unfamiliar folk now take up weapons to defend the realm. As the wilderness around Northshire grows more dangerous by the day, he offers travelers counsel day or night. He guides them as they master their skills and help Stormwind’s beleaguered people.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is A Scribbled Letter?",a="After clashes with kobold camps, adventurers at Northshire Abbey receive a letter sealed by Tordrin Stemblade. It directs them to seek his mentorship and training in the valley.",al={"what is the scribbled letter","scribbled letter quest","letter from tordrin"}},{q="Who sent the letter?",a="Tordrin Stemblade sent the letter. He is a local trainer at Northshire Abbey, where he instructs fledgling adventurers learning their craft.",al={"who sent the letter","who wrote the letter","author scribbled letter"}},{q="Where can Tordrin Stemblade be found?",a="Tordrin Stemblade can be found at Northshire Abbey in Northshire Valley. He remains there day and night, ready to offer travelers instruction and advice.",al={"where is tordrin stemblade","tordrin location","find tordrin stemblade"}},{q="Why did Tordrin Stemblade send the letter?",a="After an adventurer proves capable against local kobolds, Tordrin sends word so they can receive proper training. He aims to prepare them for the growing dangers threatening Northshire’s residents and the wider realm of Stormwind.",al={"why did tordrin send a letter","tordrin stemblade purpose","why summons"}},{q="What threats are currently affecting Northshire?",a="Northshire Valley faces incursions from aggressive kobold camps and dangerous man-eating beasts roaming the surrounding woods. Local mentors muster and drill capable fighters in response.",al={"what threats are in northshire","dangers in northshire abbey","kobolds northshire"}},{q="What does Tordrin Stemblade offer after receiving the letter?",a="Tordrin offers continuous training and guidance. He urges adventurers to learn the lay of the land and assist local folk with the kingdom’s many troubles.",al={"what does tordrin offer","tordrin training","what happens after meeting tordrin"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="Tordrin Stemblade mentors hunters at Northshire Abbey. He notes how times have changed as new races take up the bow to defend Stormwind from beasts and vermin.",["faction:Alliance"]="Training skilled defenders at Northshire Abbey helps secure Elwynn Forest against encroaching kobolds and other growing threats to Stormwind."},kw={"a scribbled letter","hunter trainer","kobold camps","northshire abbey","northshire valley","scribbled letter","tordrin stemblade"},rel={"subzone:northshire-abbey","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:kobold"},m={faction="Alliance",cl={"WARRIOR"},id=92479},src={"In-game quest text: A Scribbled Letter"},fv=true}
E["quest:94"] = {t="quest",n="A Watchful Eye",z="elwynn",s="At the Tower of Azora, Theocritus watches Morganth from afar. He sends travelers east into Redridge Mountains to place an enchanted glyph at an old lion statue near the Tower of Ilgalar.",h="At the Tower of Azora, Theocritus watches Morganth from afar.",sec={{t="A Rivalry Across the Border",b="From his tower in eastern Elwynn Forest, Theocritus watches the hills. His rival, Morganth, is a powerful sorcerer who has claimed the Tower of Ilgalar in Redridge Mountains. Fearing Morganth's dark magic may cross the border, Theocritus made the Eye of Azora to watch the rogue wizard from afar.",sp=0},{t="The Lion's Vigil",b="A distant view cannot show Theocritus what Morganth plans. So he gives travelers the Glyph of Azora and sends them to the Old Lion Statue near the Tower of Ilgalar. The statue has kept watch there for decades.\n\nSet the glyph into the worn hollow at its base. An arcane link then reaches back to Azora, letting Theocritus look into his rival's mind.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Theocritus?",a="Theocritus is an Alliance wizard who lives in the Tower of Azora in eastern Elwynn Forest. He studies magic to guard the region from rogue spellcasters, especially Morganth.",al={"theocritus","tower of azora mage","who gives a watchful eye"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Morganth?",a="Morganth is a rogue human wizard who has made the Tower of Ilgalar in Redridge Mountains his stronghold. He is Theocritus's bitter rival, and Theocritus fears his schemes against the surrounding lands.",al={"morganth","who is morganth","rival mage"},it="target"},{q="Where is the Old Lion Statue located?",a="The Old Lion Statue stands on the ridges overlooking the Tower of Ilgalar in the eastern hills of Redridge Mountains. A shallow hollow at its base can hold the Glyph of Azora.",al={"lion statue location","where is the statue","where to put glyph of azora"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does the Glyph of Azora do?",a="The Glyph of Azora is an enchanted stone made by Theocritus. Set in the lion statue near the Tower of Ilgalar, it carries his arcane listening spell and lets him study Morganth's thoughts.",al={"glyph of azora","what is the glyph"},it="item"},{q="What is the Tower of Ilgalar?",a="The Tower of Ilgalar is an isolated stone tower high in the crags of eastern Redridge Mountains. Morganth and his servants occupy and defend it.",al={"tower of ilgalar","ilgalar"},it="threat"},{q="What comes after placing the glyph?",a="After you set the Glyph of Azora in the statue, Theocritus speaks through the stone and offers Looking Further. He begins to uncover Morganth's plans.",al={"next quest","what after a watchful eye"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Theocritus want this done?",a="Morganth is a ruthless mage of formidable power holed up in the Tower of Ilgalar. While Theocritus can view his rival using the scrying magic of the Eye of Azora, seeing him is no longer enough. By affixing the Glyph of Azora to the nearby lion statue, Theocritus hopes to penetrate Morganth's mind and discover what the dark wizard is plotting before he unleashes it upon the region.",al={"theocritus motive","why place the glyph of azora","why spy on morganth"},it="motive",add="0c307b8a"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you see how arcane divination can reach across a great distance. Theocritus uses methods from Elwynn, while Morganth practices rogue sorcery.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help guard the border between Elwynn Forest and the embattled settlements of Redridge Mountains from rogue human spellcasters like Morganth."},kw={"elwynn","glyph of azora","morganth","old lion statue","redridge","theocritus","tower of azora","tower of ilgalar"},rel={"quest:178","quest:248","quest:249","npc:theocritus","subzone:tower-of-ilgalar","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Theocritus",["end"]="Old Lion Statue",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=94},src={"A Watchful Eye"}}
E["quest:94774"] = {t="quest",n="Divine Grace",z="elwynn",s="High Priestess Laurena calls you to Stormwind’s Cathedral of Light because your superiors have approved further training. Your lessons in the ways of the Light are ready to begin.",h="High Priestess Laurena calls you to Stormwind’s Cathedral of Light because your superiors have approved...",sec={{t="A Call to Stormwind",b="Your superiors send you to the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind after judging that you have proven yourself. There, High Priestess Laurena is ready to guide your further training. She says there are lessons every servant of the Light must learn, and she is prepared to discuss them with you.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why am I being sent to Stormwind?",a="Your superiors believe you have proven yourself and have approved further training in the ways of the Light.",al={"why Stormwind","sent to Cathedral","why go there"}},{q="Who is High Priestess Laurena?",a="High Priestess Laurena is in the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind and is ready to guide your training.",al={"Laurena who","who is Laurena","high priestess"}},{q="Where do I find High Priestess Laurena?",a="High Priestess Laurena is at the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind.",al={"Laurena location","where is Laurena","cathedral location"}},{q="What training is Laurena offering?",a="Laurena is prepared to discuss lessons that all servants of the Light must learn.",al={"Light training","what lessons","learn the Light"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, your superiors have approved further training in the ways of the Light."},kw={"cathedral of light","divine grace","high priestess laurena","light","servant of the light","stormwind","training"},rel={"subzone:cathedral-of-light","npc:high-priestess-laurena","topic:light","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={faction="Alliance",id=94774},src={"In-game quest text: Divine Grace"},fv=true}
E["quest:94792"] = {t="quest",n="Taming the Beast",z="elwynn",s="Josephine Carson is teaching aspiring hunters in Taming the Beast how to care for a wild companion. The trial uses a Rockhide Boar and a Taming Rod, with nature’s balance in mind.",h="Josephine Carson is teaching aspiring hunters in Taming the Beast how to care for a wild companion.",sec={{t="Bonding with Beasts",b="Traveling alone in the wild can be dangerous. An animal companion offers protection in battle and company on long journeys. For aspiring hunters and trackers, forming that bond is a vital step. Josephine Carson guides novices through a trial with a Rockhide Boar and a Taming Rod. To calm and direct the beast, they must stay composed and focused without giving in to fear or causing needless bloodshed.",sp=0},{t="The Balance of Nature",b="Josephine Carson warns her pupils not to exploit beasts recklessly. Taming calls for patience and discipline, never cruelty or dominance, and nature’s balance must be kept. The enchanted rod lets novices practice handling a formidable Rockhide Boar without permanently depleting local wildlife. Once they learn to command and soothe the beast, they return the rod. Respect for nature comes before pride.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the quest Taming the Beast?",a="Taming the Beast teaches aspiring hunters how to bond with wild creatures. Josephine Carson shows them how to approach and pacify a Rockhide Boar with a Taming Rod. The trial teaches survival skills and respect for nature’s balance.",al={"taming the beast quest","what is taming the beast","hunter pet quest"}},{q="Who is Josephine Carson?",a="Josephine Carson mentors adventurers in caring for animal companions. She lends students a Taming Rod so they can practice patience and skill with beasts. She teaches that the work takes practice and respect for nature’s balance.",al={"josephine carson","who gives taming the beast","taming rod quest giver"}},{q="What is the Taming Rod used for?",a="The Taming Rod is an enchanted tool for safely handling a formidable beast. It lets novices practice commanding and soothing a Rockhide Boar without permanently depleting local wildlife. They return the rod once they learn the fundamentals.",al={"taming rod","what does the taming rod do","how to use taming rod"}},{q="Why do hunters need animal companions?",a="An animal companion offers protection, watchfulness, and aid in combat. A loyal beast can guard the front line and keep a traveler company on long, hazardous journeys through wild lands.",al={"why get a pet","beast companion benefits","why tame beasts"}},{q="What creature must be tamed during this trial?",a="The trial calls for a Rockhide Boar, a sturdy beast suited to testing basic animal handling. The exercise teaches composure and discipline when facing aggressive wildlife. Afterward, adventurers report their progress to Josephine Carson.",al={"which boar do i tame","rockhide boar target","taming the beast mob"}},{q="Why does Josephine Carson emphasize the balance of nature?",a="Josephine Carson warns against greed and force when handling wild beasts. Reckless use disrupts nature’s balance, and beasts are not disposable tools. True mastery means respecting their place in nature.",al={"balance of nature meaning","nature balance taming","why respect nature"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, taming wild beasts is a defining rite of passage. A loyal companion offers protection and watchfulness in battle, forging an enduring partnership between tracker and beast.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know that care and restraint help preserve nature’s balance. Treating forest wildlife with respect honors the natural order you are sworn to protect."},kw={"animal companion","balance of nature","beast taming","hunter pet","josephine carson","rockhide boar","taming rod","taming the beast"},rel={"item:taming-rod","quest:456"},m={faction="Alliance",cl={"HUNTER"},ra={"Human"},id=94792},src={"In-game quest text: Taming the Beast"},fv=true}
E["quest:94793"] = {t="quest",n="Training the Beast",z="elwynn",s="In Goldshire, Training the Beast shows young hunters how to care for a tamed companion. Isaac Chan teaches them to feed and revive their beasts, then train them for life at their side.",h="In Goldshire, Training the Beast shows young hunters how to care for a tamed companion.",sec={{t="The Responsibilities of the Hunt",b="You seek Isaac Chan, an experienced woodsman in Goldshire, to learn how to train your beast. A tamed creature needs care and discipline before it can become a steady ally. Without Chan's guidance, your companion may remain unruly in the wilderness.",sp=0},{t="A Woodsman's Guidance",b="Isaac Chan teaches you to care for your animal companion. You learn to feed it and revive it if it falls in battle. He also teaches commands that help it fight, and reminds you that power over wildlife calls for respect. Honor nature's balance and live in awe of the world around you.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Isaac Chan?",a="Isaac Chan is a lifelong woodsman who lives in Goldshire, in Elwynn Forest. He knows wildlife and wilderness survival, and teaches novice hunters to guide, feed, revive, and teach abilities to their animal companions.",al={"who is isaac chan","goldshire beast trainer","isaac chan lore"}},{q="What is the purpose of Training the Beast?",a="Hunters learn to care for a tamed beast and maintain their bond. Isaac Chan teaches them to feed their companion, revive it if it falls in battle, and teach it new combat abilities.",al={"what does this quest do","why train beast","purpose of training the beast"}},{q="Where can Isaac Chan be found?",a="Isaac Chan lives in Goldshire, the central township of Elwynn Forest, south of Northshire Valley and southwest of Stormwind City.",al={"where is isaac chan","where do i turn this in","isaac chan location"}},{q="What skills does Isaac Chan teach?",a="Isaac Chan teaches the basics of caring for and training an animal companion. You learn to feed your beast, revive it if it falls in combat, and teach it new abilities as it grows alongside you.",al={"what skills do you get","pet abilities learned","what does isaac chan teach"}},{q="Why does Isaac Chan remind hunters to respect nature?",a="Isaac Chan teaches hunters humility before the wild. He asks them to honor nature's balance and live in awe of the world around them, so their bond with a beast rests on stewardship rather than exploitation.",al={"why respect nature","respect the balance hunter"}},{q="Who undertakes this quest?",a="Hunters who can already tame beasts seek Isaac Chan's woodland discipline to sustain and train an animal companion.",al={"who can do this quest","is training the beast hunter only"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you move beyond capturing beasts to build a lasting, disciplined bond. Feed, revive, and train your companion.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance hunter in Elwynn Forest, you can learn the basics of beast handling from veteran woodsmen like Isaac Chan in Goldshire."},kw={"elwynn forest","feed pet","goldshire","hunter pet","isaac chan","pet training","revive pet","training the beast","woodsman"},rel={"subzone:goldshire"},m={faction="Alliance",cl={"HUNTER"},ra={"Human"},id=94793},src={"In-game quest text: Training the Beast"},fv=true}
E["quest:94863"] = {t="quest",n="Taming the Beast",z="elwynn",s="Josephine Carson guides you through Taming the Beast as you learn to handle a boar before facing a Gray Forest Wolf. With a Taming Rod, you seek the fiercer creature's trust.",h="Josephine Carson guides you through Taming the Beast as you learn to handle a boar before facing a Gray...",sec={{t="The Path of the Hunter",b="Josephine Carson watches as you take another step in learning to handle beasts. You have practiced with simple boars; now you enter the forest to tame a Gray Forest Wolf. The enchanted rod she gives you helps calm the predator. Patience and respect matter as much as tracking and marksmanship when you seek a wild creature's trust.",sp=0},{t="A Test of Instinct and Trust",b="Josephine Carson gives you a specialized Taming Rod to calm dangerous wildlife. Approach the wolf with patience and precision, and overcome its aggression without lethal force. After practicing your bond with the beast, return the rod to Josephine as proof of your growing skill.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest Taming the Beast?",a="Taming the Beast is a hunter's training trial, where you use an enchanted Taming Rod to tame a Gray Forest Wolf.",al={"taming the beast quest","gray forest wolf quest","tame wolf lesson"}},{q="Who gives and completes this quest?",a="Josephine Carson instructs you and gives you the Taming Rod. After the trial, you return it to her.",al={"who gives taming the beast","who is josephine carson","where to turn in taming the beast"}},{q="What creature do you have to tame?",a="You are instructed to tame a Gray Forest Wolf, a fiercer forest predator than the boars you handled before.",al={"what do i tame","which beast","target of taming the beast"}},{q="What is the Taming Rod used for?",a="Josephine Carson gives you the Taming Rod to soothe a wild Gray Forest Wolf and form a temporary bond without causing permanent harm.",al={"what does taming rod do","why use taming rod","taming rod lore"}},{q="What did the hunter tame before this trial?",a="Before facing the Gray Forest Wolf, you practiced handling a forest boar.",al={"taming previous lesson","what was tamed before wolf"}},{q="Do you keep the Gray Forest Wolf as a permanent companion?",a="No. After practicing your beast-bonding skills, you return the Taming Rod to Josephine Carson.",al={"do you keep wolf","is wolf permanent pet"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you learn the patience and respect needed to bond with fierce wild predators."},kw={"beast taming","gray forest wolf","hunter","hunter training","josephine carson","taming rod","taming the beast"},rel={"item:taming-rod"},m={faction="Alliance",cl={"HUNTER"},ra={"Human"},id=94863},src={"In-game quest text: Taming the Beast"},fv=true}
E["quest:94864"] = {t="quest",n="Taming the Beast",z="elwynn",s="In Elwynn Forest, hunters face Taming the Beast, the final trial Josephine Carson oversees. After taming a boar and a wolf, each hunter uses a Taming Rod to earn a Young Forest Bear’s trust. The test deepens the hunter’s bond with beasts and teaches respect for the woodland’s balance.",h="In Elwynn Forest, hunters face Taming the Beast, the final trial Josephine Carson oversees.",sec={{t="The Final Trial of the Hunt",b="Hunters in Elwynn Forest learn to live among the wild creatures around them. After taming a wolf and a boar, they face one last test of courage and patience. Josephine Carson sends each hunter to a Young Forest Bear, the strongest of the forest’s common predators. The hunter must endure the bear’s strength and earn its trust, rather than force it to submit.",sp=0},{t="Respect and Balance in Elwynn",b="Taming wildlife in Elwynn calls for respect, not dominion. Forest bears embody the woodland’s strength and vitality, and help keep its natural order. With a Taming Rod, hunters learn to calm a bear’s aggression and form a bond through understanding. Earning the trust of such a powerful animal deepens a hunter’s bond with the wild and completes the first lessons Josephine Carson oversees.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who assigns this trial to hunters?",a="Josephine Carson assigns the trial to hunters training in Elwynn Forest. After they tame lesser beasts, she gives them guidance and the Taming Rod for the forest bear. When the trial is done, they return the rod to her.",al={"who gives taming the beast","taming the beast quest giver","josephine carson quest"}},{q="Which beasts must be tamed before this challenge?",a="Hunters first tame a boar and a wolf before facing a Young Forest Bear. Those trials show they can handle resilient and pack-oriented beasts before attempting to earn a bear’s trust.",al={"prerequisite beasts for taming","what did i tame before bear","beasts tamed before this"}},{q="Why are hunters sent after a Young Forest Bear?",a="A Young Forest Bear tests a hunter against the brawn and might of Elwynn Forest’s wildlife. After handling the quick wolf and resilient boar, the hunter must show endurance, respect, and courage to earn the bear’s trust.",al={"why tame young forest bear","young forest bear purpose","why bears in elwynn"}},{q="What is the purpose of the Taming Rod?",a="Josephine Carson gives hunters a Taming Rod to help calm wild animals. It helps soothe an aggressive Young Forest Bear without killing it and lets the hunter form a peaceful bond. Hunters return the rod to Carson when the trial is complete.",al={"taming rod purpose","what does taming rod do","why use taming rod"}},{q="How does taming beasts help Elwynn Forest?",a="Hunters learn to preserve Elwynn Forest’s natural balance by treating wildlife with respect and restraint. They guide dangerous beasts peacefully instead of hunting them down, preserving harmony between local wildlife and humanoid settlements.",al={"why does elwynn balance matter","elwynn forest balance","taming and forest balance"}},{q="What does completing this lesson signify for a hunter?",a="Completing the final trial deepens a hunter’s bond with wild beasts. Earning the trust of Elwynn’s mightiest creature teaches the understanding needed for lifelong partnerships with animal companions across Azeroth.",al={"what happens after taming the bear","hunter training completion","attunement to beasts meaning"}},{q="Where are Young Forest Bears found?",a="Young Forest Bears roam the wooded areas of Elwynn Forest, among dense trees and alongside wolves and spiders. Hunters leave nearby settlements and track the bears through the undergrowth, following Carson’s final direction with the Taming Rod.",al={"young forest bear location","where to find bears in elwynn","forest bear elwynn"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you move beyond tracking and toward a deeper, more understanding bond with wild beasts.",["race:Human"]="As a human hunter training in Elwynn Forest, you learn to live alongside the kingdom’s natural predators instead of trying to destroy them.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance beast master, you can give wilderness scouts disciplined companions to defend homesteads and patrol trade roads across Stormwind’s territories."},kw={"attunement to beasts","beast training","elwynn forest","hunter quest","josephine carson","taming rod","taming the beast","young forest bear"},rel={"item:taming-rod"},m={faction="Alliance",cl={"HUNTER"},ra={"Human"},id=94864},src={"In-game quest text: Taming the Beast"},fv=true}
E["quest:95998"] = {t="quest",n="The Great Outdoors",z="elwynn",s="At Sam’s fire, travelers learn to rest and endure the road. Then they can turn to tradeskills and work in the wild.",h="At Sam’s fire, travelers learn to rest and endure the road.",sec={{t="Lessons by the Fire",b="Sam welcomes restless travelers who cross Azeroth in search of fortune, danger, and renown. Ambition alone cannot keep a newcomer warm or ease the miles. By his fire, you learn when to rest, how to build a fire, and how to gather strength for the open road.",sp=0},{t="Fieldcraft and Trade",b="A campfire offers warmth against the night chill and a chance for boosted rest. Those who know the wild understand that endurance comes from resting between journeys. Once you have learned these basics, you can turn to tradeskills. Craftsmen and gatherers can learn to make camp fixtures suited to their work in the field.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sam?",a="Sam is an experienced outdoorsman and traveler who teaches newcomers to endure the wild. He welcomes them to share his fire and learn practical ways to face the road.",al={"who is sam","sam campfire quest","quest giver"}},{q="What is the purpose of sitting by the campfire?",a="Boosted Rest is the renewal that comes from resting beside a proper campfire in the wild. Its warmth and comfort help weary travelers recover and continue their journey.",al={"what is boosted rest","boosted rest buff","resting by fire"}},{q="Why are wilderness skills important for adventurers?",a="Wilderness skills help travelers endure the dangers and long miles beyond settlement walls. Fieldcraft lets them sustain themselves without succumbing to fatigue.",al={"why learn outdoorsman skills","why thrive in wilds","survival skills"}},{q="How do tradeskills relate to wilderness camping?",a="After you learn to make a basic camp, profession trainers can teach you to craft camp fixtures suited to your work in the field.",al={"tradeskills camping","camp fixtures","professions after this"}},{q="What should an adventurer do after completing this lesson?",a="After resting by Sam’s fire and learning basic campcraft, you can seek out profession trainers. A practical craft lets you build field stations suited to your trade.",al={"next steps","what after great outdoors","after campfire quest"}},{q="Who can undertake The Great Outdoors?",a="Any traveler setting out into the wider world can learn these lessons, whatever their background or allegiance.",al={"can anyone do this","who can take great outdoors","is this quest general"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, learning to make camp gives you a foundation for preparing meals in the open air.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, living off the land and resting by an open flame may feel familiar. Even seasoned scouts benefit from learning campcraft."},kw={"basic campfire","boosted rest","camp fixture","campcraft","outdoorsman","sam","the great outdoors","tradeskill"},m={faction="Alliance",id=95998},src={"In-game quest text: The Great Outdoors"},fv=true}
E["quest:96626"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Cooking",z="elwynn",s="In Goldshire, Cook Tomas shows new travelers how cooking kindles a campfire. With that fire, they can make a simple camp in the wild.",h="In Goldshire, Cook Tomas shows new travelers how cooking kindles a campfire.",sec={{t="The Hearth in the Wild",b="A campfire gives you a place to prepare food and begin a camp in Azeroth's wilds. Learn to cook, and you learn to build that fire. Then an open stretch of wilderness can become a place to camp.",sp=0},{t="Instruction in Goldshire",b="In Elwynn Forest, new travelers find Cook Tomas in Goldshire and learn the craft. His instruction gives you the skill to make a basic camp in the wild. At first, your camp holds few furnishings. Greater cooking skill lets you build larger fires, while other crafting trades give you more ways to furnish and shape your campsite.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest Camping 101: Cooking?",a="Cooking teaches you to build a basic campfire for a campsite in the wild.",al={"what is camping 101 cooking","what does camping 101 teach","purpose of camping 101"}},{q="Who is Tomas and where can he be found?",a="Tomas teaches cooking in Goldshire, in Elwynn Forest. Find him at the Lion's Pride Inn, where he teaches the basics of cooking and lighting a campfire.",al={"who is tomas","where is tomas","tomas goldshire"}},{q="Why is cooking required to establish a campsite?",a="Cooking teaches you to build the campfire at the heart of a wilderness camp, where you can rest and arrange furnishings.",al={"why do i need cooking for camping","is cooking required to camp","cooking campfire relationship"}},{q="Can you make larger campfires as your skill improves?",a="Greater cooking skill lets you build larger, sturdier fires for your camp in the wild.",al={"how to upgrade campfire","can i build bigger campfires","bigger fires cooking"}},{q="How do you acquire furnishings for your campsite?",a="Other tradeskill trainers teach you ways to make campsite furnishings. Different crafting trades let you create items to decorate and improve a camp in the wild.",al={"how to add camp furnishings","where do camp furnishings come from","crafting camp items"}},{q="Where can an adventurer set up camp?",a="Once you know how to cook and build a campfire, you can make camp in the open wilderness. Your first campsites are modest and hold only a few furnishings until you expand your skills.",al={"can i camp anywhere","wilderness camping rules","camp placement limits"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Cooking teaches you to build basic campfires at the heart of your camps in the wild.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer new to Elwynn Forest, you are directed to Cook Tomas at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire to learn cooking and campfire building."},kw={"campfire","camping","camping 101: cooking","campsite","cooking","furnishings","goldshire","tomas"},rel={"subzone:goldshire"},m={faction="Alliance",id=96626},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Cooking"},fv=true}
E["quest:96627"] = {t="quest",n="The Adventurer",z="elwynn",s="From Northshire Valley, Marshal McBride sends you toward Goldshire to find Sam Sarsaparilla. You have proved your skill defending the abbey, and now he wants you to look into a newcomer.",h="From Northshire Valley, Marshal McBride sends you toward Goldshire to find Sam Sarsaparilla.",sec={{t="Leaving the Valley",b="With the Defias and vermin threats easing, McBride turns his attention to the road beyond the valley. His garrison needs promising fighters to watch travelers and wanderers in the surrounding woods.",sp=0},{t="A Curious Newcomer",b="Marshal McBride asks you to check on Sam Sarsaparilla, who was spotted near Goldshire. This is neither a military order nor a hunt for a bounty. The newcomer draws you from Northshire’s secluded valley into Elwynn’s wider wilds.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me on this task?",a="Marshal McBride, commander of Stormwind's garrison in Northshire Valley, sends you after you prove your mettle defending the abbey.",al={"quest giver","who gives the adventurer","marshal mcbride quest"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Sam Sarsaparilla?",a="Sam Sarsaparilla is an adventurer near the road by Goldshire. Marshal McBride hears he is there and asks you to find out what he is doing.",al={"sam sarsaparilla","who is sam","goldshire adventurer"},it="target"},{q="Where do I find Sam Sarsaparilla?",a="Sam Sarsaparilla is along the main road south from Northshire toward Goldshire in Elwynn Forest.",al={"sam sarsaparilla location","where is sam","find sam sarsaparilla"},gp=true},{q="Why does Marshal McBride care about a random adventurer?",a="Northshire remains on alert for bandits and intruders. McBride keeps watch on unfamiliar sellswords and wanderers passing through, and trusts dependable locals to make first contact.",al={"why send me","mcbride motives","why look for sam"},it="motive"},{q="Do I need to leave Northshire Valley to finish this?",a="Yes. Leave Northshire Valley through its southern gates and follow the forest road toward Goldshire.",al={"outside northshire","does this leave northshire","go to goldshire"},gp=true},{q="Is this part of the normal Stormwind military chain of command?",a="Marshal McBride is a Stormwind officer, but he calls this an unusual assignment rather than standard guard duty. He relies on your judgment as an independent protector, outside formal military protocol.",al={"stormwind military","is this standard duty","official business"}},{q="Why does Marshal McBride choose me to investigate Sam?",a="Marshal McBride considers this an unusual task rather than standard garrison duty. Having watched you deal with Northshire's local threats, he views you as a capable protector who can operate discreetly beyond the abbey gates. With his own garrison stretched thin dealing with local troubles, sending a trusted recruit to look into rumors down the road makes far more sense than dispatching regular guards.",al={"why me marshal mcbride","why does mcbride send me","why not send a guard to sam"},it="why_me",add="dd262048"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For new Alliance recruits finishing their service in Northshire, this is your first official step into the wider realm of Elwynn Forest.",["race:Human"]="As a human defender leaving Northshire Abbey, you take your first steps toward Goldshire, the heart of Elwynn."},kw={"elwynn forest","goldshire","marshal mcbride","northshire","sam sarsaparilla","the adventurer"},rel={"npc:marshal-mcbride","subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Marshal McBride",["end"]="Sam Sarsaparilla",level="6",faction="Alliance",id=96627},src={"The Adventurer (Elwynn Forest)"},fv=true}
E["quest:97170"] = {t="quest",n="Learning to Ride",z="elwynn",s="Randal Hunter offers to teach you horseback riding once you have enough coin. Train with him, and Katie will provide a free mount.",h="Randal Hunter offers to teach you horseback riding once you have enough coin.",sec={{t="Randal's Offer",b="Randal Hunter can teach you to ride a horse for a fee. Once you have enough coin, speak with him to learn Apprentice Riding. Katie will provide a free mount after your training, and you can purchase additional mounts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who teaches me to ride a horse?",a="Randal Hunter offers to teach you horseback riding for a fee.",al={"horse riding trainer","who is Randal","ride trainer"}},{q="What do I need to learn riding?",a="You need enough coin to pay Randal Hunter for training.",al={"how learn riding","riding cost","need coin"}},{q="Who gives me a free mount?",a="Katie provides a free mount after you train with Randal Hunter.",al={"free horse","Katie mount","where mount"}},{q="Can I buy more mounts?",a="After training, you can purchase additional mounts.",al={"additional mounts","buy horse","more mount"}},{q="Do other creatures need different riding skills?",a="Different creatures require their own riding skill, and you will need to find trainers for each.",al={"other riding skills","creature riding","mount training"}}},kw={"apprentice riding","coin","horse","katie","learning to ride","mount","randal hunter","riding"},m={faction="Alliance",id=97170},src={"In-game quest text: Learning to Ride"},fv=true}
E["quest:97915"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Alchemy",z="elwynn",s="An Alchemist can learn to craft a Mana Well from Alchemist Mallory near Stormwind. It gives healers and spellcasters a refreshing taste at camp.",h="An Alchemist can learn to craft a Mana Well from Alchemist Mallory near Stormwind.",sec={{t="A Camp for Brews",b="An Alchemist can ask Alchemist Mallory near Stormwind in Elwynn Forest to teach a camping craft. You need to show proficiency in your skill before learning to make a Mana Well. Healers and spellcasters can come to the camp for a refreshing taste.",sp=0},{t="Setting Up Camp",b="Once you know the craft, you can make your own Mana Well. Camps belong in the wilderness, and a campfire is needed before you start one. Someone who trains cooks can teach you the basics of making a fire.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who teaches Alchemists to make a Mana Well?",a="Alchemist Mallory teaches the craft near Stormwind in Elwynn Forest, once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",al={"mana well trainer","alchemy camp craft","mallory alchemy"}},{q="What is a Mana Well for?",a="A Mana Well gives healers and spellcasters a refreshing taste at camp.",al={"mana well use","what does mana well do","alchemy camp item"}},{q="Where can I find Alchemist Mallory?",a="Alchemist Mallory is near Stormwind in Elwynn Forest.",al={"mallory location","where is mallory","alchemy trainer elwynn"}},{q="What do I need before starting a camp?",a="You need a campfire before starting your camp. Someone who trains cooks can teach you how to make a fire.",al={"campfire needed","how start camp","camp basics"}},{q="Where should I try out my Mana Well?",a="Try it in the wilderness, since most folk do not care for camps in the center of town.",al={"mana well camping","camp in town","where test mana well"}}},kw={"alchemist","alchemist mallory","alchemy","camp","campfire","camping","elwynn forest","healers","mana well","spellcasters","stormwind"},rel={"zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={faction="Alliance",id=97915},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Alchemy"},fv=true}
E["quest:97916"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Blacksmithing",z="elwynn",s="In Goldshire, Smith Argus teaches skilled metalworkers to prepare for work in the wild. They learn to forge a portable Sharpening Wheel and to make camp in open country with a proper fire.",h="In Goldshire, Smith Argus teaches skilled metalworkers to prepare for work in the wild.",sec={{t="Forging for the Trail",b="Smith Argus of Goldshire shows skilled metalworkers how to carry their craft beyond the town anvils. Those ready for the work can learn to forge a Sharpening Wheel, keeping blades keen on long travels.",sp=0},{t="Life in the Field",b="Field gear alone does not make a proper camp. Goldshire townsfolk frown on camps within settlements, so crafters must head into the open frontier to use their equipment. A wilderness camp also needs a warm fire. Visit a local cook to learn the basics of making one.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Camping 101: Blacksmithing?",a="Smith Argus teaches skilled blacksmiths to forge a portable Sharpening Wheel for use in the wilderness.",al={"what does this quest do","camping 101 blacksmithing purpose","what do i learn"}},{q="Who is Smith Argus?",a="Smith Argus is the blacksmith and trainer in Goldshire, within Elwynn Forest. He teaches promising smiths basic metalworking and camping craft.",al={"who is smith argus","goldshire blacksmith trainer","argus goldshire"}},{q="What is a Sharpening Wheel?",a="A Sharpening Wheel is camping equipment that blacksmiths can forge to hone tools and weapons away from town forges.",al={"what is a sharpening wheel","camping sharpening wheel","blacksmith camp item"}},{q="Can you set up camp inside town?",a="Townsfolk frown on camps in settled places like Goldshire. Smiths need to head into the wilderness to set up their gear.",al={"can i camp in goldshire","pitch tent in town","where can i camp"}},{q="Why do you need a campfire to make camp?",a="A campfire completes a wilderness camp. Blacksmiths can visit a cooking trainer to learn basic fire-making before heading out.",al={"do i need cooking for camping","campfire for camp","how to make a camp"}},{q="When can you learn this camping craft?",a="Smith Argus teaches this camping craft to blacksmiths with sufficient skill.",al={"camping 101 requirements","blacksmith proficiency requirement"}}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Blacksmiths learning their trade in Elwynn Forest can forge a Sharpening Wheel to maintain equipment and hone blades in the field.",["profession:Cooking"]="A proper campsite needs a reliable fire, so basic cooking training pairs well with metalworking in the wilderness.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance artisans starting out in Goldshire can ask Smith Argus how to prepare for long journeys beyond town."},kw={"blacksmithing","campfire","camping","camping 101","elwynn forest","goldshire","sharpening wheel","smith argus"},rel={"npc:smith-argus","subzone:goldshire"},m={faction="Alliance",id=97916},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Blacksmithing"},fv=true}
E["quest:97917"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Enchanting",z="elwynn",s="In Stormwind, Betty Quin teaches enchanters to bring a little magic to the campfire. With an Enchanted Lute, they can lift spirits and help travelers rest along the trail.",h="In Stormwind, Betty Quin teaches enchanters to bring a little magic to the campfire.",sec={{t="Magic on the Trail",b="Long roads across Azeroth call for more than steel and rations. Comfort and good spirits matter in the wild, too. Enchanters put their craft to work at camp, turning quiet hours into music and rest before the next stretch of trail.",sp=0},{t="Seeking Betty Quin",b="Betty Quin in Stormwind teaches enchanters to make special items for the campsite. Once they have shown skill in enchanting, she can teach them to craft an Enchanted Lute. Its charms lift spirits around the campfire.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Camping 101: Enchanting?",a="Enchanters can learn to make magical supplies for camp from Betty Quin in Stormwind. She teaches those who have honed their craft.",al={"what is camping 101 enchanting","camping 101 enchanters","enchanting camp quest"}},{q="Who is Betty Quin?",a="Betty Quin teaches skilled enchanters in Stormwind how to make magical items for the road and for leisure.",al={"who is betty quin","stormwind enchanting trainer betty","where is betty quin"}},{q="What is an Enchanted Lute?",a="An Enchanted Lute is a magical instrument that brings music and lifts spirits during camp. It helps travelers face the hardships of the trail.",al={"what does enchanted lute do","why craft enchanted lute","enchanted lute purpose"}},{q="Why are enchanters valued at a campsite?",a="Enchanters bring magic to camp, making downtime a chance to rest, prepare, and enjoy some music before a hard journey.",al={"why enchanters in camp","enchanter camp usefulness"}},{q="Where do I go to complete this task?",a="Find Betty Quin in Stormwind, the capital of the kingdom of Stormwind.",al={"where do i turn in camping 101 enchanting","betty quin location"}},{q="What skill is needed to learn camping enchanting recipes?",a="Betty Quin teaches campcraft to enchanters who have shown solid skill in enchanting, including how to make an Enchanted Lute.",al={"camping 101 enchanting requirements","when can i learn enchanted lute"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance enchanters traveling through their lands can find Betty Quin in Stormwind for lessons in campcraft."},kw={"betty quin","camp","camping 101","camping 101: enchanting","enchanted lute","enchanting","stormwind"},rel={"topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={faction="Alliance",id=97917},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Enchanting"},fv=true}
E["quest:97919"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: First Aid",z="elwynn",s="At the Lion's Pride Inn, Michelle Belle shows you how to prepare First Aid Kits for camping. You need enough First Aid skill to learn how to ready these supplies for the road ahead.",h="At the Lion's Pride Inn, Michelle Belle shows you how to prepare First Aid Kits for camping.",sec={{t="Field Medicine on the Road",b="Travel through Elwynn can leave you wounded, far from a town healer or inn. First Aid lets you tend your own injuries without relying on anyone else. Bandages help with bleeding and trauma, without arcane rites or holy prayers.",sp=0},{t="Supplies for the Campsite",b="At Goldshire's Lion's Pride Inn, Michelle Belle teaches skilled practitioners to assemble First Aid Kits. Keep medical supplies at camp so a weary party can treat injuries and regain strength before facing the dangers ahead.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="Adventurers with basic First Aid seek Michelle Belle in Goldshire. She teaches them to make a First Aid Kit and stock a wilderness camp with medical supplies.",al={"camping first aid purpose","what does this quest do","why camping 101 first aid"}},{q="Who do I need to speak with in Goldshire?",a="Speak with Michelle Belle, a First Aid trainer in Goldshire. Once you show enough skill, she teaches you how to make camping supplies for field medicine.",al={"who is michelle belle","camping trainer goldshire","first aid camp trainer"}},{q="Why is First Aid important for travelers?",a="First Aid helps travelers tend injuries from beasts, bandits, and harsh weather. Anyone can bandage wounds and recover between skirmishes, with or without divine or arcane magic.",al={"why learn first aid","is first aid useful","first aid lore"}},{q="Where is Goldshire located?",a="Goldshire is Elwynn Forest's main hamlet, just south of Stormwind City along the main trade road. It is a central hub for supplies and local trainers, with rest at the Lion's Pride Inn.",al={"where is goldshire","goldshire location","how to find michelle belle"}},{q="Do I need prior training to complete this task?",a="Yes. Michelle Belle asks you to show your First Aid skill before she teaches you to make camp kits.",al={"requirements camping 101","first aid skill needed","prerequisites"}},{q="How does a First Aid Kit fit into camping?",a="A wilderness campsite offers a safe place to recover. A First Aid Kit keeps bandages and remedies close at hand, ready to save lives far from town healers.",al={"camp first aid kit use","camping item first aid","why make a first aid kit"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Goldshire is a crossroads for Alliance travelers heading from Northshire into Elwynn.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you have no healing spells of your own, so you rely on bandages and field kits to endure long campaigns in the wild.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue working in the shadows far from help, you depend on field medicine to bandage bleeding wounds before moving on to your next mark."},kw={"bandages","camp kit","camping 101","elwynn forest","first aid","goldshire","michelle belle","survival"},rel={"subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn"},m={level="6",faction="Alliance",id=97919},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: First Aid"},fv=true}
E["quest:97920"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Fishing",z="elwynn",s="Lee Brown teaches novice anglers near Goldshire how to use their fishing skill around camp. With simple catches and basic materials, they can make useful additions for a campsite.",h="Lee Brown teaches novice anglers near Goldshire how to use their fishing skill around camp.",sec={{t="Campcraft for Anglers",b="Fishing can feed you on the road and add comfort to camp. A fish bowl lifts the spirits of weary travelers between excursions. A sound mind and high spirits help make formidable fighters.",sp=0},{t="Lee Brown's Expertise",b="Lee Brown waits beside the waters outside Goldshire for fishermen ready to broaden their craft. Show him your skill with rod and line, and he can teach you to make useful additions for camp.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="Lee Brown near Goldshire directs aspiring fishermen. After you show basic skill at fishing, he teaches you to make camp items such as a fish bowl for roadside campsites.",al={"why do camping fishing","what does camping 101 do","purpose of quest"}},{q="Who is Lee Brown?",a="Lee Brown is a fishing trainer beside Crystal Lake, just outside Goldshire in Elwynn Forest. He teaches angling and how fishermen can make items for camp.",al={"where is lee brown","who teaches fishing camping","lee brown"}},{q="What does a Fish Bowl do for a campsite?",a="A fish bowl brings comfort and joy to a campsite. Pleasant surroundings lift morale and help adventurers feel ready and capable when facing the wilderness.",al={"fish bowl effect","what does fish bowl do","why make a fish bowl"}},{q="Where does this training take place?",a="The training takes place in Elwynn Forest, beside the waters around Goldshire where local anglers gather.",al={"quest location","where do i go","elwynn camping trainer"}},{q="Do I need prior skill in fishing to complete this?",a="Yes. Lee Brown teaches travelers who have practiced casting and shown basic skill at fishing.",al={"fishing skill requirement","do i need fishing","proficiency requirement"}},{q="Is camping useful for combat?",a="Yes. A well-kept camp offers comfort that improves an adventurer's physical and mental preparedness, resilience, and effectiveness in combat in the field.",al={"does camping help combat","camping buffs","why camp"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As a human traveler starting out in Elwynn Forest, you can learn wilderness self-sufficiency beside the familiar waters of Goldshire."},kw={"campcraft","camping 101: fishing","crystal lake","elwynn forest","fish bowl","goldshire","lee brown"},rel={"subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn"},m={level="6",faction="Alliance",id=97920},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Fishing"},fv=true}
E["quest:97921"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Herbalism",z="elwynn",s="In Elwynn Forest, Herbalist Pomeroy teaches skilled gatherers a new comfort for camp. They learn to make Incense Candles, whose fragrance lifts the spirits of spellcasters resting in the wild.",h="In Elwynn Forest, Herbalist Pomeroy teaches skilled gatherers a new comfort for camp.",sec={{t="Botanical Utilities for the Road",b="A herbalist's craft can help a traveling party in more ways than brewing restorative draughts or selling flowers. With skill in gathering, you can help your companions endure the wilds. A camp needs more than a fire and dry bedroll. Weary travelers also need comforts that keep their minds keen. Some plants give off aromas that refresh tired minds, so herbalists can support a party far from civilization.",sp=0},{t="The Guidance of Herbalist Pomeroy",b="In Elwynn Forest, Herbalist Pomeroy teaches skilled gatherers to make campsite supplies from local plants. She shows them how to shape an Incense Candle, putting herbs to use beyond alchemy flasks. Burned at camp, its fragrance soothes tired travelers and lifts the spirits of companions who rely on mana. With Pomeroy's teaching, herbalists can bring comfort to parties traveling in the wild.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Camping 101: Herbalism?",a="Skilled herbalists can learn to make Incense Candles for campsites. Herbalist Pomeroy teaches this craft in Elwynn Forest.",al={"camping 101 herbalism quest","herbalism camping quest","what is camping 101 herbalism"}},{q="Who teaches the camping recipe for herbalists?",a="Herbalist Pomeroy teaches skilled gatherers in Elwynn Forest to make Incense Candles from local plants.",al={"who teaches herbalism camping","camping 101 trainer","where is herbalist pomeroy","herbalist pomeroy location"}},{q="What item do herbalists learn to craft from this quest?",a="Herbalists learn to make an Incense Candle. Its fragrance soothes travelers and lifts the spirits of companions who rely on mana while resting in the wild.",al={"what do herbalists make for camping","herbalism camp item","incense candle herbalism","what does camping 101 teach"}},{q="What are the requirements to start Camping 101: Herbalism?",a="You need skill in Herbalism and gathering before Herbalist Pomeroy will teach you camp craft.",al={"camping 101 herbalism requirements","when can i get camping 101 herbalism","herbalism skill needed for camping 101"}},{q="Why are Incense Candles useful for adventuring parties?",a="Incense Candles soothe travelers and lift the spirits of companions who rely on mana while resting in the wild.",al={"what does incense candle do","why make incense candle","incense candle benefits","herbalism incense candle use"}},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="You travel to Elwynn Forest to meet Herbalist Pomeroy and learn to make campsite supplies.",al={"camping 101 herbalism zone","where to turn in camping 101 herbalism","elwynn forest herbalism quest"}},{q="Can non-herbalists craft the Incense Candle?",a="No. Making an Incense Candle requires Herbalism and knowledge of wild plants and aromatic materials, which Herbalist Pomeroy teaches.",al={"can anyone make incense candle","is incense candle herbalism only","do i need herbalism for incense candle"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist, you can use your knowledge of plants to make Incense Candles that comfort your traveling companions at camp.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you can rest near an Incense Candle and take heart from its fragrance during wilderness travel.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can benefit from an herbalist companion who makes Incense Candles for camp.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, you can seek Herbalist Pomeroy's instruction in Elwynn Forest."},kw={"camp","camping 101","campsite","elwynn forest","healers","herbalism","herbalist pomeroy","incense candle","spellcasters"},rel={"zone:elwynn"},m={faction="Alliance",id=97921},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Herbalism"},fv=true}
E["quest:97922"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Leatherworking",z="elwynn",s="In Goldshire, Adele Fielder teaches leatherworkers to make a tent for journeys beyond town. It shelters travelers from harsh weather and gives them a place to rest while camping in the wilderness.",h="In Goldshire, Adele Fielder teaches leatherworkers to make a tent for journeys beyond town.",sec={{t="Shelter for the Open Road",b="Beyond the gates of Goldshire, shelter matters as much as armor. In Elwynn Forest, leatherworkers can visit Adele Fielder to learn more than simple belts and tunics. After they show skill with hide and needle, Adele teaches them to make a durable tent for long journeys overland. It is built to withstand harsh weather.",sp=0},{t="The Essentials of Campcraft",b="A finished tent covers a campsite and guards against the elements. It keeps travelers cool under scorching suns, dry in driving rain, and rested between dangerous encounters.\n\nGoldshire locals and city guards will not allow campsites in the town streets, so you need to head into the open wilderness to camp. Adele also reminds wanderers that a proper camp needs a campfire. A culinary trainer can teach you to make one.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who teaches leatherworkers how to craft tents?",a="Adele Fielder teaches leatherworkers in Goldshire, in Elwynn Forest, to make sturdy tents after they show skill in their craft.",al={"who gives tent training","adele fielder location","leatherworking tent teacher"}},{q="What purpose does a crafted tent serve?",a="A crafted tent shelters travelers from harsh weather, keeping them cool on sweltering days and dry in heavy rain. It also gives adventurers rest in the wilderness.",al={"why make tent","what does tent do","tent benefits"}},{q="Can you pitch a tent inside a town?",a="You cannot pitch a tent in town streets or town centers. Take your gear into the wilderness to set up camp.",al={"can i pitch tent in town","where can i use tent","tent in stormwind or goldshire"}},{q="What else is needed alongside a tent to complete a camp?",a="Adele Fielder says a camp needs a campfire as well as a tent, for warmth and practical use in the wild.",al={"what else do i need for camp","tent campfire requirement","how to complete campsite"}},{q="Where can a traveler learn to build a campfire?",a="Culinary trainers and local cooks teach the basics of lighting a campfire. Learn from them so you can build a reliable fire wherever you roam.",al={"who teaches campfire","how to learn campfire","fire for camp"}},{q="When can a leatherworker learn to craft a camping tent?",a="A leatherworker must first show skill in the craft before Adele Fielder teaches tentmaking.",al={"tent skill requirements","how to get tent recipe","when can i craft tent"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Adele Fielder says a wilderness campsite needs a campfire and urges you to learn cooking so you can kindle one.",["faction:Alliance"]="In Goldshire, this training guides Alliance leatherworkers toward practical survival crafts for journeys across Azeroth."},kw={"adele fielder","campfire","camping","elwynn forest","goldshire","leatherworking","tent","wilderness survival"},rel={"subzone:goldshire"},m={faction="Alliance",id=97922},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Leatherworking"},fv=true}
E["quest:97923"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Mining",z="elwynn",s="In Stormwind, Gelman Stonehand teaches miners to shape a lodestone for camps in the wild. Set by a campfire, it strengthens the fighters gathered there.",h="In Stormwind, Gelman Stonehand teaches miners to shape a lodestone for camps in the wild.",sec={{t="The Earth's Resonant Power",b="Miners in Stormwind can shape the earth’s natural magnetism into a lodestone. At an expedition’s campsite, it bolsters the fighting strength of those gathered there. Gelman Stonehand, Stormwind’s mining instructor, teaches the craft to prospectors who prove their skill with a pickaxe.",sp=0},{t="Wilderness Camps and Campfires",b="A lodestone belongs in the wild, far from Cathedral Square and the Trade District. Townsfolk disapprove of travelers camping within city limits, so pioneers must head into the wild to make camp. The stone also needs a campfire. Cooks across the realm teach this basic wilderness skill.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Camping 101: Mining?",a="Gelman Stonehand teaches miners in Stormwind to craft a lodestone for a wilderness campsite. You must prove your mining skill to learn the craft.",al={"what is camping 101 mining","quest objective","what do i do"}},{q="Who teaches the Lodestone schematic?",a="Gelman Stonehand is a mining trainer in Stormwind City. He teaches qualified miners to make a lodestone for expeditions in the wild.",al={"who teaches lodestone","where is gelman stonehand","stonehand location"}},{q="What does a Lodestone do?",a="A lodestone set at a wilderness campsite strengthens warriors and other fighters gathered around its campfire.",al={"what does lodestone do","lodestone buff","why make lodestone"}},{q="Can I set up camp inside Stormwind?",a="Stormwind's townsfolk disapprove of camps in city squares and streets. Go beyond the settlement gates to make camp and set your lodestone in the wilderness.",al={"can i camp in town","where can i place camp","camping restrictions"}},{q="Why do I need a campfire to set up camp?",a="A campfire is the foundation of a campsite, and specialized gear like a lodestone is useless without one. Cooks teach travelers to start fires with wood and flint.",al={"do i need cooking for camping","how to make camp","campfire requirement"}},{q="Who benefits most from gathering around a Lodestone?",a="Anyone who fights with a blade, axe, or hammer can benefit from a lodestone. Fighters seek its added strength while resting by the flames before a dangerous battle.",al={"who benefits from lodestone","is lodestone for melee","lodestone classes"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you can shape a lodestone to strengthen your wilderness campsite and aid allies resting beside you.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can learn to tend a campfire, the foundation for specialized camp equipment.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance tradesfolk, you can learn from Gelman Stonehand in Stormwind to turn earthcraft into practical field tools."},kw={"campfire","camping 101: mining","campsite","gelman stonehand","lodestone","mining","stormwind","wilderness"},rel={"topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={faction="Alliance",id=97923},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Mining"},fv=true}
E["quest:97924"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Skinning",z="elwynn",s="In Elwynn Forest, skinners learn Camping 101: Skinning from Helene Peltskinner in Goldshire. She teaches them to shape harvested hides into a Camp Chair for rests beyond settled towns.",h="In Elwynn Forest, skinners learn Camping 101: Skinning from Helene Peltskinner in Goldshire.",sec={{t="Creature Comforts in the Wild",b="You can shape hides taken from beasts into a Camp Chair for rest in the wild. In Goldshire, Helene Peltskinner teaches proficient skinners to make this seat for travelers on long journeys through dangerous lands.",sp=0},{t="Rules of the Campsite",b="Take your gear into the wilderness before making camp, for townspeople often object to camps in the town square. A field camp also needs a campfire. Many skinners learn basic culinary arts to master fire-building.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Camping 101: Skinning?",a="In Goldshire, Helene Peltskinner teaches proficient skinners to make a Camp Chair from harvested hides.",al={"what is camping 101 skinning","what does this quest do","skinning camp chair quest"}},{q="Who teaches skinners how to craft a Camp Chair?",a="Helene Peltskinner teaches proficient skinners to make a Camp Chair in Goldshire.",al={"who teaches camp chair","helene peltskinner location","where to turn in camping 101 skinning"}},{q="What is the purpose of crafting a Camp Chair?",a="A Camp Chair gives travelers a seat where they can rest during wilderness journeys.",al={"what does a camp chair do","why make a camp chair","camp chair purpose"}},{q="Where can adventurers set up camp?",a="Town residents generally dislike camps in the middle of settlements, so set up your camp in the wilderness.",al={"can i camp in town","where can i place camp chair","camping in goldshire"}},{q="What else is required to build a complete campsite?",a="A campsite needs a basic campfire. If you do not know how to build one, learn culinary arts from a local cook.",al={"what do i need for a camp","do i need a fire to camp","campfire requirement"}},{q="Who is eligible to learn this camping craft?",a="Skinners proficient at harvesting hides from beasts can learn this craft and put those hides to practical use in the wild.",al={"who can learn camp chair","can non skinners do this","skinning requirement camping"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a skinner learning to make a field camp, consult a cook. A campsite needs a basic campfire for warmth and meal preparation.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance skinner visiting Elwynn Forest, find Helene Peltskinner in Goldshire to learn this wilderness craft."},kw={"camp chair","campfire","camping 101: skinning","goldshire","helene peltskinner","skinning","wilderness camping"},rel={"subzone:goldshire"},m={faction="Alliance",id=97924},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Skinning"},fv=true}
E["quest:97925"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Tailoring",z="elwynn",s="In Elwynn Forest, skilled clothworkers are sent to Eldrin at the Eastvale Logging Camp. He teaches them to weave a Faction Banner that inspires travelers and raises morale at wilderness camps.",h="In Elwynn Forest, skilled clothworkers are sent to Eldrin at the Eastvale Logging Camp.",sec={{t="A Weaver's Purpose in the Wild",b="Eldrin, an artisan at the Eastvale Logging Camp in eastern Elwynn Forest, guides skilled needleworkers. Tailoring makes garments and bags, but it can also sustain a journey. Those who have proven their skill with thread and loom can learn to make camp accessories for travel through the wilderness.",sp=0},{t="Banners of Morale",b="The Faction Banner is the chief craft Eldrin teaches. It stands beside a traveler's fire, where its emblem can hearten those on dangerous journeys and in battle. A banner at camp gives weary travelers a familiar sign of resolve and helps them press on through hostile lands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of Camping 101: Tailoring?",a="Eldrin at the Eastvale Logging Camp in Elwynn Forest teaches skilled tailors to make a Faction Banner. The banner inspires travelers and raises morale at camp.",al={"what is camping 101 tailoring","tailoring camp item quest","how to get camp banner"}},{q="Who is Eldrin and where can he be found?",a="Eldrin is an artisan at the Eastvale Logging Camp in eastern Elwynn Forest. He teaches skilled tailors to craft faction banners for camps.",al={"who is eldrin","where is eldrin","eldrin location"}},{q="What does the Faction Banner do for a camp?",a="A Faction Banner inspires travelers and raises morale at camp. Its emblem offers weary travelers resolve as they journey through hostile lands.",al={"what does the tailoring banner do","faction banner camp","why craft a faction banner"}},{q="What requirements are needed to learn the craft from Eldrin?",a="Tailors must first prove their skill before Eldrin teaches them the craft. They need honed needlework to weave and assemble the banner.",al={"what skill do i need","camping banner requirements","can any tailor make a banner"}},{q="Where is the Eastvale Logging Camp located?",a="The Eastvale Logging Camp lies in the eastern woods of Elwynn Forest, along the road toward Redridge Mountains. Local craftspeople and workers gather at this logging hub.",al={"where is eastvale logging camp","eastvale logging camp elwynn"}},{q="Is this task exclusive to Alliance tailors?",a="Eldrin is in the heart of Elwynn Forest, within Alliance territory. The instruction there is for Alliance-aligned craftsmen from the eastern settlements.",al={"can horde do this quest","is this alliance only"}}},ang={["profession:Tailoring"]="Tailors can weave a Faction Banner to inspire travelers and raise morale at camp during long expeditions.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance adventurers are directed to Eldrin at the Eastvale Logging Camp in Elwynn Forest to learn to stitch a faction banner."},kw={"banner","camping","camping 101","eastvale logging camp","eldrin","elwynn forest","faction banner","tailoring"},rel={"subzone:eastvale-logging-camp","zone:elwynn"},m={faction="Alliance",id=97925},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Tailoring"},fv=true}
E["quest:99127"] = {t="quest",n="A Net Disaster",z="elwynn",s="At Crystal Lake, A Net Disaster starts with fishermen finding no fish on their hooks and no minnows in the shallows. They set traps overnight to protect their stock.",h="At Crystal Lake, A Net Disaster starts with fishermen finding no fish on their hooks and no minnows in the...",sec={{t="Troubled Waters at Crystal Lake",b="Fishermen at Crystal Lake in Elwynn Forest come up empty. Hooks bring in no fish, and even the minnows have vanished from the shallows. So they set traps overnight, hoping to catch enough to keep their stock.",sp=0},{t="Wrecked Traps and Neighboring Nuisances",b="Lee's traps beneath Crystal Lake lie ruined. Hostile neighbors along the shore have wrecked the fishing gear. If the damage continues, local fishermen risk losing their livelihoods.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is A Net Disaster?",a="At Crystal Lake in Elwynn Forest, fishermen find no fish on their hooks and no minnows in the shallows. They set traps overnight to protect their stock.",al={"what is a net disaster","net disaster quest","crystal lake net disaster"}},{q="Where do you inspect the fishing traps?",a="Lee's overnight fishing traps lie beneath the waters of Crystal Lake. Lee set them to preserve the fish stock after hook-and-line fishing failed.",al={"where are the traps","net disaster location","crystal lake traps"}},{q="Who is Lee?",a="Lee is a fisherman at Crystal Lake. After hook-and-line fishing brought in nothing, Lee set traps overnight to secure the fish stock.",al={"who is lee","lee fisherman"}},{q="What happened to the fish in Crystal Lake?",a="No fish are biting, and not even minnows appear in Crystal Lake's shallows. Hostile neighbors have ruined the overnight traps.",al={"what happened to crystal lake fish","why no fish crystal lake","crystal lake empty"}},{q="Who are the neighboring nuisances mentioned at the end?",a="The neighboring nuisances are aggressive murlocs. They have made camps in Crystal Lake's waters and along its shores, disrupting local wildlife and fishing gear.",al={"who are the neighboring nuisances","net disaster nuisances","who broke the traps"}},{q="Why is the lack of fish such a big problem for the fishermen?",a="The fishermen rely on Crystal Lake's fish for their livelihoods. With the catch gone and the traps ruined, their work and income are at risk.",al={"why does the quest giver care","crystal lake fishing business"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you find Crystal Lake in Elwynn Forest. Disruptions there threaten local livelihoods and the supplies that support Alliance territory."},kw={"a net disaster","crystal lake","elwynn forest","fish stock","fishing traps","lee","murlocs","nuisances"},rel={"subzone:crystal-lake"},m={faction="Alliance",id=99127},src={"In-game quest text: A Net Disaster"},fv=true}
E["quest:99128"] = {t="quest",n="Slimy Menace",z="elwynn",s="At Crystal Lake in Elwynn Forest, murlocs threaten the fish and people along the shore. Their growing numbers endanger the lake's supply and nearby locals.",h="At Crystal Lake in Elwynn Forest, murlocs threaten the fish and people along the shore.",sec={{t="Trouble at Crystal Lake",b="Aggressive murlocs have settled along Crystal Lake's eastern shore. Sharp teeth and fierce tempers make the water dangerous for anyone who fishes or comes near. Local residents depend on the lake for their livelihoods, and the murlocs threaten them at the water's edge.",sp=0},{t="An Endless Infestation",b="If their numbers grow unchecked, murlocs may devour every fish in the lake. Thinning them gives the waters respite, though their eerie, echoing warbles warn that they persist. Even when scattered, they replenish their ranks swiftly, so the shoreline needs constant watch.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest Slimy Menace about?",a="Murlocs along Crystal Lake's far shores threaten the fish and anyone working or traveling nearby. Left unchecked, they can devour the local fish supply.",al={"what is slimy menace","slimy menace quest info","slimy menace summary"}},{q="Where do the events of this quest take place?",a="The disturbance is at Crystal Lake in Elwynn Forest, where murlocs have gathered on the opposite shoreline. They disrupt the lake's wildlife and endanger local residents.",al={"where are murlocs crystal lake","crystal lake location","where does this happen"}},{q="Why must the murlocs at Crystal Lake be culled?",a="Murlocs rapidly deplete the lake's fish and terrorize the surrounding area with fierce tempers and sharp teeth. Thinning their ranks helps protect the fishery and slows their aggressive expansion for a time.",al={"why kill crystal lake murlocs","murlocs eating fish","what is the problem with murlocs"}},{q="Does clearing the murlocs permanently resolve the problem?",a="No. Thinning the murlocs offers only a temporary reprieve. They reproduce and regroup swiftly, so their numbers recover despite initial losses.",al={"are murlocs gone forever","did we wipe out murlocs","will crystal lake murlocs return"}},{q="Who asks for help with the slimy menace?",a="An Elwynn local concerned about Crystal Lake asks for help. Distressed by the murlocs' unsettling warbling and voracious appetite, they want the murlocs thinned to protect the fishery.",al={"who gives slimy menace","slimy menace quest giver"}},{q="What makes the murlocs such a threat?",a="Murlocs are vicious, temperamental amphibious creatures with sharp teeth and a guttural warble. They gather along shores, aggressively defend their territory, and attack anything that ventures too close to their feeding grounds.",al={"what are murlocs like","murloc behavior crystal lake"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Protecting Crystal Lake's shores helps keep local Elwynn fishermen and travelers near Goldshire safe from aggressive murloc raids.",["race:Human"]="As a human, your people in Elwynn Forest face murloc encroachment that threatens their waterways, food supply, and nearby settlements."},kw={"crystal lake","elwynn forest","fish","goldshire","murloc","murlocs","slimy menace"},rel={"subzone:crystal-lake","topic:murloc"},m={faction="Alliance",id=99128},src={"In-game quest text: Slimy Menace"},fv=true}
E["quest:99129"] = {t="quest",n="A Man About a Murloc",z="elwynn",s="Jason's fishing is in danger, and he turns to Remy \"Two Times\" for help. Remy shares his hatred of murlocs and has plans of his own.",h="Jason's fishing is in danger, and he turns to Remy \"Two Times\" for help.",sec={{t="Trouble on the Water",b="Jason is a local fisherman, and murlocs keep raiding his catches. He knows Remy \"Two Times\" hates them as much as he does. So Jason sends you to ask whether Remy has found a way to drive the creatures from the waters.",sp=0},{t="Remy's Retaliation",b="Remy says the local guards have ignored his repeated warnings about the murloc threat. He will not wait for their help. Instead, he prepares to strike back and asks you to aid his plans.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest A Man About a Murloc?",a="Jason, a local fisherman, asks how to stop murlocs from raiding his catches.",al={"who gives a man about a murloc","who starts a man about a murloc","jason murloc quest"}},{q="Who is Remy \"Two Times\"?",a="Remy \"Two Times\" is a local resident who has repeatedly warned the guards about murlocs. Jason hopes Remy can find a way to drive them away.",al={"who is remy two times","remy two times elwynn","where is remy"}},{q="Why does Jason want to consult Remy?",a="Murlocs raid Jason's catches, so he turns to Remy for help protecting his fishing.",al={"why does jason need help","jason fish murlocs","murloc problem jason"}},{q="What does Remy plan to do about the murlocs?",a="Remy says the town guards ignore his warnings. He plans to strike back at the murlocs and asks you to gather materials.",al={"remy two times ideas","what is remy plan","remy murlocs plan"}},{q="Why haven't the guards dealt with the murlocs?",a="Remy says he has repeatedly warned the local guards about the murlocs, but they have not heeded him.",al={"guards murlocs elwynn","why dont guards help remy","remy guards warning"}},{q="What happens after speaking to Remy?",a="After you speak with Remy, he shares his plans to strike back at the local murlocs and sets you to further work for him.",al={"where does a man about a murloc lead","after a man about a murloc","next quest after remy"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you may find murlocs troubling settlements along lakeshores and docks. Their incursions strain residents and guards across Elwynn and nearby Alliance territories."},kw={"a man about a murloc","elwynn","fish","jason","murloc","remy two times"},rel={"npc:remy-two-times","topic:murloc"},m={faction="Alliance",id=99129},src={"In-game quest text: A Man About a Murloc"},fv=true}
E["quest:99130"] = {t="quest",n="An Enticing Offer",z="elwynn",s="Remy asks you to gather duskweed for bait against nearby murlocs. Clearing it may also help local farmers.",h="Remy asks you to gather duskweed for bait against nearby murlocs.",sec={{t="A Twofold Solution",b="Remy has a plan for two local troubles. You gather duskweed from nearby fields, where it troubles the growers, then use it to make bait meant to keep murlocs from settled lands. The plan is to teach the murlocs to avoid the weed.",sp=0},{t="The Nature of Duskweed",b="Duskweed is both the heart of the bait and a persistent weed in nearby farm plots. Its petals harm most beasts when gathered in substantial quantities. Gathering it from troubled farmers clears an aggressive plant from their fields and supplies the base for bait meant to steer murloc packs away.",sp=0},{t="Baiting the Waters",b="Duskweed makes the bait hazardous to handle because its toxins harm other creatures too. Keep domestic animals and pets away from the mixture. Remy also warns you to make sure Jason does not mistake the pungent bait for a meal.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest An Enticing Offer?",a="Remy asks you to gather duskweed and make toxic bait to deter nearby murlocs. The gathering also helps farmers clear the weed from their fields.",al={"what is an enticing offer","what is this quest"}},{q="What is duskweed?",a="Duskweed is a persistent weed in local farm fields. Its petals are toxic to most beasts in substantial quantities, making them useful in bait meant to deter murlocs.",al={"what is duskweed","duskweed plant","duskweed effects"}},{q="How is the murloc bait intended to work?",a="The plan uses bait made with toxic duskweed petals to teach local murlocs to avoid the area instead of trying to exterminate them.",al={"how does the bait work","murloc poison bait","why make bait"}},{q="Who is Jason?",a="Jason is the fisherman who sent you to Remy about his murloc trouble. Remy says to warn Jason not to eat the duskweed bait.",al={"who is jason","dont let jason eat it","jason bait warning"}},{q="Is the murloc bait dangerous to other creatures?",a="Yes. Duskweed petals are toxic to most animals in substantial quantities. Keep domestic animals and pets away from the mixture.",al={"is duskweed bait dangerous","pet poison bait"}},{q="Why is gathering duskweed considered a win-win?",a="Duskweed aggressively invades cultivated fields and troubles local growers. Gathering it clears the fields and provides the ingredient for bait against murlocs.",al={"why help farmers","win win situation"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist, you know duskweed as a troublesome local plant with toxic petals. Handle it carefully when gathering it for bait.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you know the bait can harm domestic beasts and hunting companions if they eat it."},kw={"an enticing offer","duskweed","jason","murloc bait","murlocs","toxic bait"},rel={"topic:murloc"},m={faction="Alliance",id=99130},src={"In-game quest text: An Enticing Offer"},fv=true}
E["quest:99131"] = {t="quest",n="Baited for Success",z="elwynn",s="Jason Mathers asks Remy for help as murlocs disrupt his fishing waters. He hopes poisoned bait will drive them off without harming the fish he sells.",h="Jason Mathers asks Remy for help as murlocs disrupt his fishing waters.",sec={{t="A Fisherman's Dilemma",b="Aggressive murlocs disrupt the waters where Jason Mathers fishes. He asks how to clear them so he can sell his catch again. Remy prepares poisoned bait meant to target the murlocs and let ordinary fishing resume.",sp=0},{t="A Targeted Solution",b="Remy prepares poison and promises to explain how to use it against murlocs without contaminating the fish. Mathers plans to collect it from Remy later that day. He hopes the waters will be clear and his livelihood restored.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who prepared the bait for Jason Mathers?",a="Remy prepares poisoned bait for Jason Mathers and promises to explain how to use it when Mathers comes by later that day.",al={"who gives baited for success","remy bait quest","who made the bait"}},{q="Why does Jason Mathers need this bait?",a="Local murlocs disrupt Jason Mathers's fishing, making it hard to sell his catch. The bait is meant to reduce their numbers without harming the fish he hopes to catch and sell.",al={"why does jason mathers need bait","mathers fish business","why poisoned bait"}},{q="Will the poisoned bait harm the fish?",a="Mathers worries that fish might consume the poison. Remy plans for it to target murlocs while leaving the fish unharmed, so Mathers can return to fishing.",al={"is the bait safe for fish","does poisoned bait kill fish"}},{q="Where is this task completed?",a="You report directly to Jason Mathers that Remy is preparing the bait.",al={"where do i turn in baited for success","baited for success quest end"}},{q="What threat do the murlocs pose to Mathers?",a="Murlocs disrupt the fishing waters, making it dangerous or impossible for Mathers and other fishermen to earn a living until their numbers fall.",al={"why kill murlocs here","murloc problem mathers"}},{q="What are Mathers's plans once he hears from Remy?",a="After hearing from Remy, Mathers plans to collect the poisoned bait from him later that day and learn how to use it safely.",al={"what happens after delivering the message","does mathers get the bait"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help secure the waters for local fishing and reduce the aggressive murloc population.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can appreciate poison tailored to control troublesome murlocs."},kw={"baited for success","fishing","jason mathers","murloc","poisoned bait","remy"},rel={"topic:murloc"},m={faction="Alliance",id=99131},src={"In-game quest text: Baited for Success"},fv=true}
E["quest:99143"] = {t="quest",n="Bottles and Baubles",z="elwynn",s="An angler wants to try a curious theory with murloc trinkets. Their shine may draw fish to the hook.",h="An angler wants to try a curious theory with murloc trinkets.",sec={{t="Fish Logic and Shoreline Scavenging",b="An eccentric angler has a theory about murlocs and fish. Murlocs look like fish, so the angler reasons that their minds work alike. Whatever catches a murloc's eye may tempt a hungry fish on a hook. You search a nearby murloc camp, sifting through its hoards for shiny discarded junk to test the idea.",sp=0},{t="Gleaming Baubles as Bait",b="Along coasts and riverbanks, murlocs gather bright stones, shells, polished glass, and metal scraps in messy piles around their huts. Sifting through the muddy heaps turns up glittering refuse that an angler can shape into crude lures and flashers. The finds satisfy the angler enough to earn you starter fishing supplies.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why do you need to collect junk from murlocs?",a="The angler believes that whatever attracts a murloc may also attract fish beneath the water. Since murlocs look like fish, the angler reasons that their minds work alike, and shiny trinkets from their camps could make bait.",al={"why collect junk","what are bottles and baubles for","shiny junk murloc"}},{q="Where is the shiny junk found?",a="The shiny junk lies in a nearby murloc camp. Murlocs hoard glittering debris, discarded trinkets, and glass along shorelines and waterways.",al={"where find junk","murloc camp location","how to get shiny junk"}},{q="Who gives this task and what do they want?",a="A local angler asks for the work, hoping to stock up on lures and bait. The angler offers surplus fishing gear to helpful scavengers and beginners.",al={"who gives bottles and baubles","who is the questgiver","quest turn in"}},{q="Do murlocs actually think like fish?",a="The angler believes murlocs think like fish, but murlocs are amphibious tribal humanoids. They are drawn to gleaming items, polished shells, and bright trinkets, while their hoard piles happen to hold glittering materials.",al={"do murlocs think like fish","murloc intellect","are murlocs actually fish"}},{q="How will the murloc junk be used as bait?",a="The angler plans to fashion reflective glass, metal bits, and polished odds and ends into lures and improvised bait. Their sheen may mimic small minnows or catch the curiosity of feeding fish.",al={"what is shiny junk used for","is shiny junk bait","does murloc junk work as bait"}},{q="What does the questgiver offer as a reward?",a="After you bring back enough suitable shiny scraps, the angler gives you older personal angling supplies. The basic tools and provisions help aspiring fishermen try their hand at the waters.",al={"what reward bottles and baubles","what do you get","fishing supplies reward"}}},kw={"bait","bottles and baubles","fishing","lures","murloc","murloc camp","shiny junk"},rel={"topic:murloc"},m={faction="Alliance",id=99143},src={"In-game quest text: Bottles and Baubles"},fv=true}
E["subzone:brackwell-pumpkin-patch"] = {t="subzone",n="Brackwell Pumpkin Patch",z="elwynn",s="Defias brigands hold Brackwell Pumpkin Patch in southeastern Elwynn Forest. The farm belonged to the Brackwell family, but now conspirators meet in its cottage and fields, where stolen mine gold arrives.",h="Defias brigands hold Brackwell Pumpkin Patch in southeastern Elwynn Forest.",sec={{t="A Bandit Haven",b="Southeast of the Stonefield homestead, Brackwell's fields lie untended. The family vanished as crime spread through the area, driven away or worse. The Defias Brotherhood now occupies the sturdy cottage and overgrown fields. Beyond the reach of Goldshire's patrols, brigands regroup here. Morgan the Collector and other prominent conspirators use the isolated farm to receive illicit gold from the forest's mines.",sp=0},{t="Pigs and Dark Magic",b="A giant sow named Princess still roams among the pumpkin vines. The Brackwells left her behind, and she terrorizes the neighboring fields. The farmhouse attic and outbuildings shelter other dangerous dealings. Erlan Drudgemoor, a bandit, seduced Surena Caledon, a rogue warlock apprentice who fled her master in Stormwind with a stolen bloodstone artifact. Her presence has drawn dark practitioners to the hideout.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What happened to the Brackwell family?",a="No one knows the Brackwell family's exact fate. As the Defias Brotherhood spread across southeastern Elwynn Forest, the family either fled or was killed. Their pumpkin fields and farmhouse fell to the bandits.",al={"where are the brackwells","who lived at brackwell farm","brackwell family fate"},it="ruin"},{q="Why is the Defias Brotherhood using this farm?",a="The farm gives the Defias an isolated base near the forest's borders. They store plundered goods and arrange smuggling there, including stolen mine gold brought by couriers such as Morgan the Collector. This keeps their dealings away from the Stormwind Guard.",al={"why are defias here","what are bandits doing at the pumpkin patch","defias at brackwell"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Princess?",a="Princess is an enormous, prize-winning sow raised by the Brackwells. Left behind when the farm fell, she grew larger by repeatedly breaking into nearby Stonefield Farm to eat its prized crops.",al={"giant pig","princess pig","why is there a huge boar here"}},{q="Why do warlocks come to the pumpkin patch?",a="Surena Caledon, apprentice to Stormwind warlock trainer Gakin the Darkbinder, stole a powerful bloodstone choker and fled to the farm with her lover, Defias bandit Erlan Drudgemoor. Gakin sends novice warlocks to kill her and recover the relic.",al={"warlock quest brackwell","surena caledon","gakin voidwalker quest"}},{q="What is the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch?",a="The Brackwell Pumpkin Patch is a Stormwindian farmstead nestled in southeastern Elwynn Forest. Once a peaceful agrarian homestead cultivating ripe pumpkins and raising livestock, it has recently fallen into chaos and outlaw hands.",al={"brackwell pumpkin patch","what is this farm","brackwell farm"},it="place",add="f38a2be0"},{q="What happened at the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch?",a="Formerly a productive family farm, the patch was overrun by the Defias Brotherhood when bandits seized the territory. The Brackwells vanished, and the farm quickly became an outpost for Defias activities, including gold drop-offs and illicit hideouts.",al={"brackwell farm history","what happened here","brackwell lore"},it="history",add="0e932b65"},{q="Who lives in or runs the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch?",a="The farm's original owners are gone, and Defias bandits currently occupy the grounds. Among them, figures like Erlan Drudgemoor and his runaway lover Surena Caledon hide out here, while Morgan the Collector utilizes the farm to receive gold shipments from local mines.",al={"who runs brackwell patch","who lives at brackwell","brackwell inhabitants"},it="residents",add="ae1356ee"},{q="Is the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch dangerous?",a="Yes, you should tread carefully. Armed Defias cutpurses patrol the pumpkin fields, alongside the notorious and voracious prize-winning pig, Princess, who aggressively protects her foraging grounds with her porcine escorts.",al={"is brackwell safe","brackwell dangers","is this farm dangerous"},it="danger",add="90becbea"},{q="Why is it called the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch?",a="It is named after the Brackwell family, the human farmers who settled the land and cultivated its distinctive pumpkin fields before bandit raids forced them from their home.",al={"brackwell name origin","why brackwell","who were the brackwells"},it="name",add="43009602"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="Surena Caledon, a fugitive apprentice, hides in the farm's shack. Her stolen bloodstone choker is needed to bind a voidwalker.",["faction:Alliance"]="The overrun patch is one of the Defias Brotherhood's easternmost bases in Elwynn. It threatens nearby farms and trade routes."},kw={"brackwell","defias","elwynn","erlan drudgemoor","morgan the collector","princess","pumpkin patch","surena caledon"},rel={"topic:defias-brotherhood","zone:elwynn","quest:123","quest:88","quest:1688","subzone:stonefield-farm","npc:marshal-dughan","npc:gakin-the-darkbinder"},src={"Brackwell Pumpkin Patch"}}
E["subzone:crystal-lake"] = {t="subzone",n="Crystal Lake",z="elwynn",s="At Crystal Lake, murlocs claim the shore east of Goldshire. Their attacks endanger villagers and travelers passing by.",h="At Crystal Lake, murlocs claim the shore east of Goldshire.",sec={{t="A Troubled Shore",b="East of Goldshire, Crystal Lake lies within walking distance of the Lion's Pride Inn. Freshwater murlocs claim its shore and shallow shoals, attacking anyone who comes too close. William Pestle, an alchemist at the inn, hires travelers to drive them back and gather the crystal kelp they carry for his experiments.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Crystal Lake located?",a="Crystal Lake lies east of Goldshire in central Elwynn Forest, just past the village outskirts.",al={"crystal lake location","where is crystal lake","find crystal lake"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are murlocs gathered at Crystal Lake?",a="Freshwater murlocs nest and forage at Crystal Lake. Their numbers near Goldshire have grown as Stormwind's local guard struggles to protect the area.",al={"why murlocs crystal lake","murloc problem goldshire","crystal lake murlocs"},it="threat"},{q="What do adventurers need from Crystal Lake?",a="William Pestle, an apothecary at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, hires travelers to slay murlocs along the shore and gather crystal kelp for an invisibility potion.",al={"william pestle crystal lake","kelp quest crystal lake","invisibility potion elwynn"},it="why_me"},{q="What is Crystal Lake?",a="Crystal Lake is a freshwater lake lying directly east of Goldshire in the heart of Elwynn Forest. While it might once have been a peaceful watering hole, its tranquil waters have lately become a hotbed of trouble for nearby travelers and townsfolk.",al={"what is crystal lake","crystal lake elwynn","crystal lake lore"},it="place",add="18711dcc"},{q="Is Crystal Lake dangerous?",a="Yes, it can prove deadly to an unwary or inexperienced traveler. The lake's shores and shallows are heavily infested with aggressive murlocs that will attack anyone wandering too close to the water's edge.",al={"how dangerous is crystal lake","is crystal lake safe","crystal lake threats"},it="danger",add="c07536f5"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Crystal Kelp grows in the lake's freshwater shallows. Most of it comes from resident murlocs, who gather it from the lake bed.",["faction:Alliance"]="The murlocs near Goldshire show how stretched the kingdom's military is in protecting its core territories."},kw={"crystal kelp","crystal lake","elwynn","goldshire","murloc","william pestle"},rel={"zone:elwynn","subzone:goldshire","npc:william-pestle","topic:murloc","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Crystal Lake"}}
E["subzone:eastvale-logging-camp"] = {t="subzone",n="Eastvale Logging Camp",z="elwynn",s="Timber orders from Stormwind reach Eastvale Logging Camp, where danger keeps the work from going smoothly. Wolves and bears drive lumberjacks from the eastern woods, but the camp still sends timber to Stormwind and nearby settlements.",h="Timber orders from Stormwind reach Eastvale Logging Camp, where danger keeps the work from going smoothly.",sec={{t="A Vital Operation Under Siege",b="Timber buyers across the Kingdom of Stormwind send Eastvale Logging Camp orders with strict deadlines. Wolves and bears prowl the woods around the work sites. They drive lumberjacks away and leave cut timber behind.\n\nSupervisor Raelen directs the camp’s work. Travelers help drive off the beasts and recover the abandoned wood before deliveries fall behind schedule.",sp=0},{t="Life on the Eastern Frontier",b="Eastvale Logging Camp has homes and horse stables where travelers can buy fine mounts. On a nearby hill above the work site, retired Marshal Haggard lives in a quiet manor.\n\nHe once led the Stormwind Guard. Then he left its service to retire far from the capital’s politics.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the main purpose of Eastvale Logging Camp?",a="Eastvale Logging Camp supplies timber to the Kingdom of Stormwind from eastern Elwynn Forest. Its lumberjacks work long hours to meet strict deadlines and supply builders and nobles across the realm.",al={"why is eastvale here","what is eastvale","eastvale lumber role"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is the logging camp always hiring adventurers?",a="Wolves and bears menace workers in the dense woods around Eastvale Logging Camp. Their attacks drive lumberjacks away from cut timber and put orders at risk of missing shipment deadlines.",al={"eastvale problems","why do loggers need help","wolves at eastvale"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Marshal Haggard?",a="Marshal Haggard is the retired former leader of the Stormwind Guard. He left the service a few years ago and now lives in a peaceful estate on the bluffs above Eastvale Logging Camp.",al={"haggard","old man near eastvale","marshal haggard elwynn"},it="identity"},{q="Can you buy mounts at Eastvale Logging Camp?",a="Yes. The horse stable at Eastvale Logging Camp sells riding horses and offers riding training.",al={"horse vendor eastvale","eastvale horses","buy mount elwynn"},gp=true},{q="What is Eastvale Logging Camp?",a="Eastvale Logging Camp is a sprawling network of lumber mills, stables, and worker dwellings tucked into the eastern reaches of Elwynn Forest. It serves as a vital economic lifeline for the Kingdom of Stormwind, constantly processing timber to meet strict orders and construction deadlines across the realm.",al={"what is eastvale","eastvale lumber camp","about eastvale logging camp"},it="place",add="ba9b781f"},{q="What happened at Eastvale Logging Camp?",a="The camp was developed to harvest Elwynn's thick timberlands. Over time, retired veterans such as former Stormwind Guard commander Marshal Haggard settled here for quiet seclusion. Despite steady operations, the camp has found itself increasingly beleaguered as local wildlife surges out of control, threatening timber shipments and worker safety.",al={"eastvale history","history of eastvale logging camp","past of eastvale"},it="history",add="c2c2b618"},{q="Who lives in or runs Eastvale Logging Camp?",a="Day-to-day lumber operations fall under Supervisor Raelen, who manages the workers and strives to keep wood shipments moving on schedule. The camp also houses numerous lumberjacks, local stable hands, and retired figures like Marshal Haggard, who keeps to his manor just beyond the busy sawmills.",al={"who runs eastvale","who leads eastvale logging camp","eastvale overseer"},it="residents",add="85f79eeb"},{q="Is Eastvale Logging Camp dangerous?",a="While the camp itself is guarded, the surrounding woods are rife with predatory wolves and aggressive bears that routinely stalk the lumberjacks. Workers have been driven from their work sites and left abandoned timber scattered in the undergrowth, making venturing past the mill buildings perilous for the unwary.",al={"how dangerous is eastvale","is eastvale safe","threats at eastvale"},it="danger",add="6b46ecbb"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human of Stormwind, you rely on Eastvale’s timber to rebuild and maintain the kingdom’s settlements.",["faction:Alliance"]="At Eastvale Logging Camp, you can buy dependable Stormwind steeds."},kw={"eastvale","elwynn","haggard","horses","logging camp","lumber","raelen","timber"},rel={"npc:supervisor-raelen","quest:1666","quest:52","quest:5545","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom","zone:redridge","subzone:goldshire"},src={"Eastvale Logging Camp"}}
E["subzone:echo-ridge-mine"] = {t="subzone",n="Echo Ridge Mine",z="elwynn",s="Kobolds hold Echo Ridge Mine in the northwestern cliffs of Northshire Valley, where stone and ore once fed the valley.",h="Kobolds hold Echo Ridge Mine in the northwestern cliffs of Northshire Valley, where stone and ore once fed...",sec={{t="A Foothold for Vermin",b="Echo Ridge Mine was cut into the hills above Northshire Abbey to supply the valley with stone and metal. Kobolds poured through its tunnels and drove out the workers. Marshal McBride fears they endanger Northshire's safety and its recruits. So he sends new recruits into the mine to thin their numbers and take it back.",sp=0},{t="The Threat Beneath Northshire",b="Kobolds have pushed beyond Echo Ridge Mine into Elwynn Forest. From the northwestern ridge, they threaten Northshire's training grounds and the flow of resources to the abbey.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are kobolds in Echo Ridge Mine?",a="Kobolds burrow into dark tunnels rich in minerals. Echo Ridge Mine's defenses were weak, so they overran it and now dig for treasure while claiming the tunnels as their own.",al={"why kobolds here","echo ridge kobolds","who took the mine"},it="residents"},{q="Who is trying to reclaim Echo Ridge Mine?",a="Marshal McBride at Northshire Abbey leads the effort to clear Echo Ridge Mine. He sends newly arrived adventurers to scout its tunnels and thin the kobold numbers before they spread farther into the valley.",al={"who wants echo ridge back","echo ridge quests","mcbride echo ridge"},it="in_charge"},{q="Where is Echo Ridge Mine located?",a="Echo Ridge Mine's entrance lies in Northshire Valley's northwestern corner, cut into the rocky hillside just north of the abbey vineyards.",al={"echo ridge location","where is echo ridge","find echo ridge mine"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Echo Ridge Mine?",a="Echo Ridge Mine is a mining cavern tucked into the northwestern ridges of Northshire Valley. Established to supply stone and ore to the valley and the abbey, the site has recently fallen into disarray after being overrun by scavenging kobolds.",al={"what is echo ridge","echo ridge mine info","tell me about echo ridge mine"},it="place",add="7d0021d3"},{q="What happened at Echo Ridge Mine?",a="The mine was actively worked by local human miners until an infestation of kobolds swarmed the shafts. The intruders drove out the workers and took over the tunnels, forcing Northshire authorities to pull back their workforce and seek martial aid to clear the infestation.",al={"echo ridge history","what happened here","why did the mine shut down"},it="history",add="d8e2171b"},{q="Why is Echo Ridge Mine abandoned?",a="Human operations came to an abrupt halt when the kobolds overwhelmed the workers. Lacking the immediate guard numbers to maintain safety underground, the abbey suspended normal mining duties while relying on newly arrived recruits to drive out the pests.",al={"why is echo ridge abandoned","is echo ridge ruined","why is the mine closed"},it="ruin",add="9fd09044"},{q="Is Echo Ridge Mine dangerous?",a="The tunnels are thick with defensive kobolds digging for resources and guarding their candlelit claims. While individual vermin are relatively weak, an inattentive traveler can quickly get cornered inside the winding, enclosed shafts.",al={"is echo ridge mine dangerous","echo ridge danger","how dangerous is echo ridge"},it="danger",add="df055836"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Echo Ridge Mine's shafts hold mineral deposits, but prospectors must fight through the candle-bearing kobolds to reach the ore.",["race:Human"]="As a human answering Stormwind's call, you help clear Echo Ridge Mine and defend Northshire Abbey."},kw={"echo ridge","echo ridge mine","kobold","marshal mcbride","mine","northshire","northshire valley"},rel={"subzone:northshire-valley","npc:marshal-mcbride","quest:15","quest:21","topic:kobold","zone:elwynn"},src={"Echo Ridge Mine"}}
E["subzone:fargodeep-mine"] = {t="subzone",n="Fargodeep Mine",z="elwynn",s="Kobolds now swarm through Fargodeep Mine, south of Goldshire in central Elwynn Forest. Its gold once filled Stormwind's treasury, but now kobolds make their home in its tunnels.",h="Kobolds now swarm through Fargodeep Mine, south of Goldshire in central Elwynn Forest.",sec={{t="A Lost Vein",b="Gold once flowed from Fargodeep Mine into Stormwind's treasury. As the Kingdom's military presence in Elwynn dwindled, the outlying mine grew vulnerable. Kobolds filled its dark tunnels and made a warren beneath the hills. Now Marshal Dughan and Goldshire's authorities fear the lost ore and the danger to nearby farms, including the Stonefield and Maclure holdings.",sp=0},{t="Depths of the Warren",b="Fargodeep Mine runs through several levels, with lower shafts reaching deep beneath the forest floor. Kobold laborers and vermin hurry along wooden scaffolds, guarding the wax and gold dust they have scavenged. Goldtooth, a cunning kobold leader, lurks in a den above the main tunnels. He hoards trinkets stolen from travelers and nearby residents.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why did Stormwind abandon Fargodeep Mine?",a="Stormwind neglected Fargodeep Mine as its military stretched thin across the southern lands. Town guards focused on Goldshire and the main roads, leaving the underground mine unguarded. Kobolds moved in and fortified its tunnels.",al={"why abandoned","why did humans leave fargodeep","who owned fargodeep mine"},it="ruin"},{q="Why are the kobolds here so dangerous to local farmers?",a="Fargodeep Mine lies between the Stonefield and Maclure family farms. Kobolds come out of its tunnels to steal livestock, tools, and personal belongings. They also harass anyone near the entrance.",al={"why are kobolds a problem","kobold threat","stonefield kobolds"},it="danger"},{q="Who is Goldtooth?",a="Goldtooth is a prominent kobold who nests in a den in Fargodeep Mine's upper reaches. He is known for stealing Auntie Bernice Stonefield's prized family necklace.",al={"goldtooth","who is goldtooth","goldtooth location"},it="residents"},{q="Why do people in Goldshire want items from the mine?",a="People in Goldshire see a reason to clear the pests from Fargodeep Mine. Remy 'Two Times' buys salvaged gold dust, while the alchemist William Pestle uses kobold candle wax for reagents. Marshal Dughan needs the infestation monitored to protect Elwynn.",al={"fargodeep quests","why gather candles","gold dust"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Fargodeep Mine?",a="Fargodeep Mine is an abandoned gold mine in central Elwynn Forest, south of Goldshire. Once an active excavation site supplying the Kingdom of Stormwind, it has fallen into disuse and is now completely overrun by subterranean kobolds tunneling through its upper chambers and lower shafts.",al={"what is fargodeep","fargodeep mine overview","about fargodeep mine"},it="place",add="7f063a4c",nx={6}},{q="What happened at Fargodeep Mine?",a="Originally operated by Stormwind miners extracting Elwynn's rich gold veins, the site was eventually abandoned as miners withdrew. In their absence, a clan of aggressive kobolds moved in, carving out tunnels, establishing their warrens, and turning the old shafts into a fortified den that threatens neighboring settlements.",al={"fargodeep history","what happened here","fargodeep lore"},it="history",add="e2f4f077"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Though pests infest Fargodeep Mine, its rocky tunnels still hold accessible copper veins for new miners.",["faction:Alliance"]="Clearing the vermin from Fargodeep Mine helps secure the supply lines and farmlands around Goldshire."},kw={"candles","elwynn","fargodeep","fargodeep mine","goldshire","goldtooth","kobold","marshal dughan","remy two times"},rel={"zone:elwynn","npc:marshal-dughan","quest:62","quest:87","quest:47","quest:60","topic:kobold"},src={"Fargodeep Mine"}}
E["subzone:forest-s-edge"] = {t="subzone",n="Forest's Edge",z="elwynn",s="At Forest's Edge, Riverpaw gnolls under Hogger threaten travelers on Elwynn's southwestern frontier.",h="At Forest's Edge, Riverpaw gnolls under Hogger threaten travelers on Elwynn's southwestern frontier.",sec={{t="A Contested Frontier",b="At Forest's Edge, the woods run southwest from Stormwind City, between Mirror Lake Orchard and the rivers that border Westfall. Westbrook Garrison is nearby, yet Stormwind has too few soldiers to keep the woods clear of wild beasts and raiding parties. Boars roam among the trees and along the banks. Riverpaw gnolls gather in force, using the woods as a staging ground.",sp=0},{t="Hogger's Stronghold",b="Hogger and his pack hunt through the woods of Forest's Edge. He is a massive, brutal gnoll chieftain who leads raids on nearby farms and harasses travelers. The Stormwind Army has placed a bounty on his head. His pack makes the timberland dangerous for anyone crossing it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where exactly is Forest's Edge?",a="Forest's Edge lies in southwestern Elwynn Forest, south of Westbrook Garrison. Mirror Lake Orchard and the waterways leading toward Westfall border the area.",al={"forests edge location","where is forests edge","forest edge map"},it="place"},{q="Why is this area so dangerous?",a="Riverpaw gnolls have claimed the woods and threaten travel along Elwynn's southwestern border. Their chieftain, Hogger, is the fiercest threat, prowling the same woods.",al={"why dangerous forests edge","what is at forest edge","forests edge threats"},it="danger"},{q="Who is Hogger?",a="Hogger is a powerful gnoll leader who directs violent attacks along Elwynn's borders. The Stormwind Army offers a bounty for proof of his death and warns against facing him alone.",al={"hogger lore","who is hogger","hogger info"},it="leader"},{q="Why hasn't Westbrook Garrison cleared the area?",a="Stormwind's military is stretched thin across the kingdom. Unrest in Westfall and threats on all sides leave Westbrook Garrison without enough soldiers to clear the gnoll camps, so volunteers must confront them.",al={"why westbrook garrison not clearing","why stormwind guards not help","westbrook guards"},it="conflict"},{q="Who lives in Forest's Edge?",a="Forest's Edge has fallen entirely into the hands of aggressive gnolls. Under the brutal dominance of the monstrous gnoll Hogger, these raiders have claimed the woodlands and riverbanks for themselves. The local wildlife, mostly wandering boars, now shares the clearing with these prowling gnoll packs.",al={"who lives here","forests edge residents","who is in forests edge"},it="residents",add="898568c8"},{q="Why is it called Forest's Edge?",a="The area forms the southwestern border of Elwynn Forest, where the dense woodland gives way to the Nazferiti River and the open plains toward Westfall. Tucked beside the riverbanks and orchard, it naturally represents the outer rim of the forest before travelers cross into harsher lands.",al={"why is it called forests edge","forests edge name meaning","why forests edge"},it="name",add="61fe669f"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance recruit in Elwynn Forest, clearing Forest's Edge and defeating Hogger is an early trial of your readiness to serve the crown.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Forest's Edge has common woodland herbs along its riverbanks and in its shaded groves. Watch for aggressive gnoll patrols while gathering them."},kw={"elwynn forest","forest's edge","forests edge","gnolls","hogger","nazferiti river","riverpaw","westbrook garrison"},rel={"subzone:westbrook-garrison","topic:gnoll","zone:elwynn","subzone:mirror-lake-orchard","zone:westfall","topic:stormwind-kingdom","zone:stormwind","quest:1861"},src={"Forest's Edge"}}
E["subzone:goldshire"] = {t="subzone",n="Goldshire",z="elwynn",s="Goldshire stands where Elwynn’s roads meet, between Stormwind City, Westfall, Redridge, and the southern frontier. Rebuilt after the First War, it offers travelers the Lion’s Pride Inn, while a hard-pressed Stormwind Guard defends the town.",h="Goldshire stands where Elwynn’s roads meet, between Stormwind City, Westfall, Redridge, and the southern...",sec={{t="A Crossroads Under Strain",b="Goldshire holds the crossroads in rural Elwynn, where the king’s highways meet. Threats press closer as Stormwind’s forces thin and King Varian Wrynn remains mysteriously absent. Marshal Dughan must rely on passing adventurers instead of regular troops to guard the borders. Riverpaw gnolls push in from the west, while hostile murlocs claim the shores of Stone Cairn Lake and Crystal Lake. Their attacks have killed royal guards and brought danger close to town.",sp=0},{t="Scars of the Great Wars",b="Goldshire and Moonbrook were the last strongholds to fall in the First War. Warchief Blackhand cut King Llane Wrynn I off from his realm before sacking Stormwind Keep, and the Orcish Horde overwhelmed both towns. Goldshire was reduced to ash and lay barren until it was rebuilt after the Second War.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is in charge of defending Goldshire?",a="Marshal Dughan of the Stormwind Guard commands Goldshire’s defenses. He coordinates the garrison from the town center, but a lack of reinforcements leaves him hiring freelance adventurers to face border threats and monster bounties.",al={"who leads goldshire","goldshire marshal","who protects goldshire"},it="in_charge"},{q="What threats are currently menacing the town?",a="Riverpaw gnolls raid east toward Westbrook Garrison, while hostile murlocs infest Stone Cairn Lake and Crystal Lake. Local scouts warn that the skirmishes could reach Goldshire’s streets without intervention.",al={"goldshire problems","why is goldshire in danger","enemies near goldshire"},it="threat"},{q="What happened to Goldshire during the First War?",a="Goldshire was one of the last two human towns to fall before Stormwind was sacked. Warchief Blackhand destroyed it alongside Moonbrook to sever King Llane’s supply lines, leaving it in ruins until its rebuilding after the Second War.",al={"goldshire first war","did goldshire fall to orcs","goldshire destruction"},it="history"},{q="Why is the Lion's Pride Inn so notable?",a="The Lion’s Pride Inn is one of Azeroth’s most respected and frequented alehouses. At the junction of several regional highways, it is a meeting hall, resting place, and training ground for travelers crossing the kingdom.",al={"lions pride inn","goldshire inn","tavern in goldshire"},it="fame"},{q="What is Goldshire?",a="Goldshire is a bustling human town centrally located in Elwynn Forest, resting at the crossroads between Stormwind City, Northshire Valley, Westfall, and Redridge. Serving as a vital waystation for trade and travelers, it is often the first major settlement visited by fledgling heroes departing the abbey.",al={"what is goldshire","about goldshire","goldshire town"},it="place",add="510017eb"},{q="Who lives in Goldshire?",a="Goldshire is home to human merchants, tradesfolk, and craft trainers catering to local travelers and farmers. Security and governance fall under Marshal Dughan and his Stormwind Guards, who garrison the outpost, maintain order along the crossroads, and direct arriving adventurers to where defense is most needed.",al={"who lives here","who lives in goldshire","goldshire residents"},it="residents",add="c15b14b9"},{q="Is Goldshire dangerous?",a="Within town borders, the Stormwind Guard keeps you relatively safe, but danger creeps dangerously close to the perimeter. Aggressive Riverpaw gnolls prowl the western borderlands, while deadly murlocs have overrun nearby lakes and rivers, threatening to push directly into the village if left unchecked.",al={"is goldshire safe","danger in goldshire","is it dangerous here"},it="danger",add="d3dbe578"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human fresh from Northshire Abbey, you find Goldshire offers your first real taste of the kingdom beyond the monastery walls and a sobering view of Stormwind’s strained borders.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you pass through Goldshire on the way from the capital to the frontier lands of Westfall, Redridge, and Duskwood."},kw={"crystal lake","elwynn","goldshire","lion's pride inn","marshal dughan","murloc","riverpaw","stone cairn lake"},rel={"subzone:lion-s-pride-inn","npc:marshal-dughan","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-guard","quest:46","quest:11","subzone:crystal-lake","topic:first-war"},src={"Goldshire"}}
E["subzone:hall-of-arms-northshire"] = {t="subzone",n="Hall of Arms",z="elwynn",s="Recruits train with the Stormwind Army in Northshire Abbey’s Hall of Arms, south of the Main Hall.",h="Recruits train with the Stormwind Army in Northshire Abbey’s Hall of Arms, south of the Main Hall.",sec={{t="Groundwork of the Guard",b="Blunted steel rings through the Hall of Arms, and instruction keeps a measured cadence. South of Northshire Abbey’s Main Hall, human fighters and devout aspirants train for the Stormwind Army. Veteran battle instructors and paladin mentors teach the postures and disciplines needed to defend Elwynn Forest from kobolds, Defias bandits, and gnoll raiders. Across the courtyard, clerics and scholars study ancient tomes in the Library Wing.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Hall of Arms?",a="The Hall of Arms trains new soldiers, mercenaries, and paladins in weapons and combat inside Northshire Abbey, before they venture into the wider kingdom.",al={"what is this room","hall of arms purpose","what happens here"},it="purpose"},{q="Who can be found inside this wing?",a="Veteran warrior and paladin trainers instruct Stormwind Army recruits in martial disciplines, shield work, and basic combat maneuvers.",al={"who is in hall of arms","trainers hall of arms","who teaches here"},it="residents"},{q="Where is the Hall of Arms located within Northshire Abbey?",a="The Hall of Arms lies south of Northshire Abbey’s Main Hall. Across the courtyard stands the Library Wing.",al={"hall of arms location","where is hall of arms","abbey layout"},it="place"},{q="Is the Hall of Arms dangerous?",a="Not at all. The Hall of Arms is a secure sanctuary within Northshire Abbey, shielded from the Defias cutpurses and kobolds prowling the valley outside. Inside its quiet stone chambers, experienced paladins and seasoned soldiers watch over the recruits. Unless trouble somehow breaches the abbey gates, you can rest and train here without any threat.",al={"hall of arms danger","is hall of arms safe","enemies in hall of arms"},it="danger",add="1c4cb7f4"},{q="Why is it called the Hall of Arms?",a="The wing earns its name from its role as Northshire Abbey's center of martial discipline. While the opposite wing is devoted to study and holy texts in the library, this hall is dedicated to the profession of arms, housing the weapon instructors, armaments, and martial trainers who ready new warriors and paladins for the Stormwind Army.",al={"why hall of arms","hall of arms name meaning","meaning of hall of arms"},it="name",add="c5e01713"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a human warrior entering service, you receive your first lessons here in stance, weapon handling, and the Stormwind Army’s martial discipline.",["class:Paladin"]="As a fledgling paladin, you learn to wield the Light alongside martial arms, joining holy devotion with martial training."},kw={"elwynn forest","hall of arms","northshire abbey","northshire valley","paladin trainer","stormwind army","warrior trainer"},rel={"subzone:northshire-abbey","subzone:main-hall-northshire","subzone:library-wing-northshire","subzone:northshire-valley","topic:stormwind-army","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Hall of Arms (Northshire)"}}
E["subzone:heroes-vigil"] = {t="subzone",n="Heroes' Vigil",z="elwynn",s="On Stone Cairn Lake's island, Heroes' Vigil lies neglected and overrun by renegade wizards. The Stone of Remembrance honors those who fell in the First War.",h="On Stone Cairn Lake's island, Heroes' Vigil lies neglected and overrun by renegade wizards.",sec={{t="A Forgotten Memorial",b="Heroes' Vigil gathers around the Stone of Remembrance on an island in Stone Cairn Lake. Erected after the First War, its inscribed circle honors the soldiers and citizens slain when the Old Horde sacked Goldshire and the surrounding valleys. Once a sacred place of faith and sacrifice, the memorial has slipped from Stormwind's attention. Its grounds are overgrown, and no soldiers tend them.",sp=0},{t="Claimed by Renegades",b="Without a kingdom garrison, outcasts have claimed the island. Rogue wizards control Stone Cairn Lake and the memorial grounds. They practice wild, undisciplined magic beyond the oversight of the Kirin Tor and the Academy of Arcane Sciences. Near the stones lies Henze Faulk's body among other tragic casualties. Travelers can only wonder whether the shrine will know peace again.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Heroes' Vigil?",a="Heroes' Vigil stands on an island in Stone Cairn Lake in eastern Elwynn Forest. Its stone ring and memorial honor those who fell in the First War.",al={"heroes vigil","what is heroes vigil","island shrine elwynn"},it="place"},{q="What does the Stone of Remembrance commemorate?",a="The Stone of Remembrance honors the citizens and defenders who died when the orcish Horde sacked Goldshire and ravaged eastern Elwynn Forest during the First War.",al={"stone of remembrance","monument meaning","what is the stone of remembrance"},it="history"},{q="Who controls Heroes' Vigil today?",a="Hostile rogue wizards occupy the island and Heroes' Vigil. They act beyond Stormwind's law and the oversight of established magical institutions.",al={"who is at heroes vigil","heroes vigil enemies","wizards on lake"},it="residents"},{q="Why has Stormwind neglected the vigil?",a="Stormwind has left the vigil undefended and largely forgotten because King Varian Wrynn is missing and the realm is stretched thin by internal dissent, brigands, and monster incursions. Remote shrines have been left without protection.",al={"why is it abandoned","why did stormwind forget it","forgotten shrine"},it="ruin"},{q="Who is Henze Faulk?",a="Henze Faulk is a dwarf whose body lies near the monument. Defias Brotherhood forces struck him down while he was saving his friend, Gazin Tenorm.",al={"henze faulk body","who is the dead guy on the island"},it="identity"},{q="Is Heroes' Vigil dangerous?",a="Yes, deeply so for the unwary. The island in Stone Cairn Lake has fallen entirely under the control of Rogue Wizards and conjurers who practice forbidden arts in exile. They attack anyone who approaches the monument on sight, making what should be a peaceful sanctuary of remembrance into a deadly trap for travelers.",al={"is heroes vigil safe","heroes vigil danger","heroes vigil hostile"},it="danger",add="e301b338"},{q="Why is it called Heroes' Vigil?",a="The site was established as an enduring watch and memorial for the fallen defenders of the First War. At its heart stands the Stone of Remembrance, raised to honor the soldiers and civilians slaughtered when the Old Horde rampaged through Elwynn Forest and sacked Goldshire.",al={"why called heroes vigil","heroes vigil name meaning","who are the heroes honored here"},it="name",add="c198f6a4"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human of Stormwind, you see this sacred stone ring as a bitter reminder of the First War's blood price and the kingdom's failure to protect its heritage.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you find renegade wizards on sacred ground, practicing dangerous arts without the discipline or sanction of the Academy of Arcane Sciences."},kw={"elwynn forest","henze faulk","heroes vigil","heroes' vigil","rogue wizards","stone cairn lake","stone of remembrance"},rel={"subzone:stone-cairn-lake","zone:elwynn","subzone:goldshire","topic:first-war","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:defias-brotherhood"},src={"Heroes' Vigil"}}
E["subzone:jasperlode-mine"] = {t="subzone",n="Jasperlode Mine",z="elwynn",s="In north-central Elwynn, kobolds and giant spiders hold Jasperlode Mine. Its shafts once sent iron and minerals to Stormwind City, but the kingdom lacks the strength to reclaim them.",h="In north-central Elwynn, kobolds and giant spiders hold Jasperlode Mine.",sec={{t="A Lost Resource in Elwynn",b="Jasperlode Mine once sent a steady supply of minerals to Stormwind, as did nearby Fargodeep. Now the kingdom's forces are stretched thin by threats beyond its borders and unrest at home. Local garrisons cannot guard the shafts. Kobolds drove out the human miners and seized the mine, hoarding stolen gold and tallow candles.",sp=0},{t="Dangers in the Deep",b="Mine spiders have made their home beneath Jasperlode Mine's timber supports. A massive matriarch called Mother Fang leads them. They prey on kobolds who trespass and on unwary prospectors. Salvaging the mine means facing those dangers in its depths.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Jasperlode Mine overrun?",a="Stormwind's army is spread thin across the realm, leaving rural outposts like Goldshire short on manpower. Once the human miners lost their guards, kobolds swarmed the dig sites.",al={"why are there kobolds","who controls jasperlode","why abandoned"},it="ruin"},{q="What is the difference between Jasperlode and Fargodeep?",a="Fargodeep Mine lies south near the Maclure and Stonefield farms. Jasperlode sits north in the foothills near the river. Kobolds hold both major Elwynn mineral sites.",al={"jasperlode vs fargodeep","other elwynn mine"}},{q="What lurks in the back of the mine?",a="Predatory mine spiders lurk in the deepest shafts, led by a massive arachnid called Mother Fang. Even the kobolds avoid their webbed caverns.",al={"spiders in jasperlode","mother fang","what is at the bottom"},it="residents"},{q="Why hasn't Marshal Dughan cleared the mine?",a="Marshal Dughan lacks the troops for a prolonged clearing underground. He must cover Defias river patrols, gnoll incursions, and garrison duties, so the local militia relies on traveling adventurers to scout the mine and cull its threats.",al={"why no stormwind guard","dughan sending soldiers"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is Jasperlode Mine?",a="Jasperlode Mine is one of Elwynn Forest's vital mineral extraction sites, carved into the hills northeast of Goldshire. Alongside Fargodeep Mine, it long served as an essential supplier of precious ores and raw metals needed to sustain Stormwind City and its military campaigns. Today, however, the human miners have been completely displaced, leaving its winding tunnels claimed by subterranean monsters.",al={"what is jasperlode","about jasperlode mine","jasperlode elwynn"},it="place",add="ae82ecd7"},{q="What happened at Jasperlode Mine?",a="Jasperlode once operated steadily under the watch of Stormwind, fueling the kingdom's war efforts with fresh ore. When the kingdom's military grew thinly stretched and preoccupied with threats elsewhere, swarms of opportunistic kobolds surged into the tunnels, driving out the workers and seizing the mineral veins for themselves.",al={"jasperlode mine history","what happened to jasperlode","jasperlode backstory"},it="history",add="d5d7dec2"},{q="Is Jasperlode Mine dangerous?",a="Jasperlode Mine is exceptionally perilous for unwary travelers. Not only is it heavily infested with territorial kobolds who will ferociously defend their candles and dig sites, but its deepest caverns harbor a colony of predatory mine spiders led by the vicious broodmother, Mother Fang. Venturing into the dark without a weapon and a sharp eye is an easy way to end up dead.",al={"how dangerous is jasperlode","is jasperlode safe","jasperlode threats"},it="danger",add="6ca2598d"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Jasperlode's mineral veins draw prospectors willing to face kobold pickaxes and spider webs to stake a claim.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stormwind needs Jasperlode's raw metal to maintain its equipment supplies while the kingdom's borders face constant peril."},kw={"elwynn forest","fargodeep","gold dust","goldshire","jasperlode","kobold","marshal dughan","mother fang"},rel={"subzone:fargodeep-mine","zone:elwynn","npc:marshal-dughan","topic:kobold","quest:76","quest:47","quest:60","zone:stormwind"},src={"Jasperlode Mine"}}
E["subzone:jerod-s-landing"] = {t="subzone",n="Jerod's Landing",z="elwynn",s="Defias smugglers hold Jerod's Landing beside the Nazferiti River in Elwynn Forest. Its dock gives them a hidden route for stolen goods across the kingdom's waterways.",h="Defias smugglers hold Jerod's Landing beside the Nazferiti River in Elwynn Forest.",sec={{t="A Smuggler's Waypoint",b="Defias outlaws control the dock at Jerod's Landing, where Elwynn Forest meets the Nazferiti River. Once an ordinary boat dock, it now receives goods plundered from the Redridge Mountains. A Defias dockmaster watches over the cargo as the outlaws move it downstream toward holdings such as Klaven's Tower in Westfall.",sp=0},{t="Eyes in the Shadows",b="SI:7, Stormwind's covert intelligence network, watches Defias activity at Jerod's Landing. The operatives see the dock as a vital link in the syndicate's supply lines. Resourceful rogues slip inside to steal river shipment ledgers and work to unravel the wider conspiracy strangling the kingdom.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Jerod's Landing located?",a="Jerod's Landing lies in eastern Elwynn Forest, on the western bank of the Nazferiti River. The river marks the boundary between Elwynn and the Redridge Mountains.",al={"jerods landing location","where is jerod's landing","jerod dock map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who controls Jerod's Landing?",a="Members of the Defias Brotherhood occupy Jerod's Landing. A Defias dockmaster coordinates shipments while armed bandits guard the waterside.",al={"who is at jerods landing","defias at jerods landing","jerod landing mobs"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is the purpose of this dock for the Defias?",a="The Brotherhood uses Jerod's Landing to smuggle stolen goods and weaponry taken in the Redridge Mountains toward rogue strongholds such as Klaven's Tower in Westfall.",al={"why do defias use jerods landing","defias river smuggling"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is SI:7 interested in Jerod's Landing?",a="Master Mathias Shaw and his intelligence agents track Defias contraband through Jerod's Landing. They seek to expose the network linking Westfall, Elwynn, and Redridge.",al={"si7 jerods landing","rogue quest jerods landing"},it="threat"},{q="What is Jerod's Landing?",a="Jerod's Landing is a modest boat dock situated along the Elwynn Forest bank of the Nazferiti River. Though once a simple river crossing and wharf, it has fallen under the sway of criminals who use its remote waterside position to stage covert operations away from the gaze of Stormwind's guards.",al={"what is jerods landing","jerod landing elwynn","about jerod landing"},it="place",add="d69927bb"},{q="Who lives in or runs Jerod's Landing?",a="The landing is held by the Defias Brotherhood and overseen on-site by their Dockmaster and his crew. These bandits hold the waterfront, using muscle and watchfulness to secure incoming cargo and keep outsiders away from their river trade.",al={"who runs jerods landing","jerods landing dockmaster","who is at jerods landing"},it="residents",add="096cd4eb"},{q="Is Jerod's Landing dangerous?",a="Yes. The docks are crawling with armed Defias smugglers and thugs who will not hesitate to cut down any traveler or Alliance scout wandering near their smuggling operations. Approaching the shoreline without caution invites immediate violence.",al={"is jerods landing safe","how dangerous is jerods landing","jerod landing enemies"},it="danger",add="51e45e55"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue working for SI:7, you are sent to Jerod's Landing to test your stealth, pickpocket the Defias dockmaster, and recover sensitive trade ledgers.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see how thoroughly the Defias have compromised the waterways linking Elwynn to Redridge, right beneath Stormwind's nose."},kw={"defias dockmaster","jerod's landing","klaven's tower","mathias shaw","nazferiti river","smuggling","snatch and grab"},rel={"topic:defias-brotherhood","quest:2206","quest:2359","zone:elwynn","zone:redridge","zone:westfall","quest:65"},src={"Jerod's Landing"}}
E["subzone:library-wing-northshire"] = {t="subzone",n="Library Wing",z="elwynn",s="In Northshire Abbey, the Library Wing gathers scholars and new priests and mages. They prepare to join Stormwind’s defense.",h="In Northshire Abbey, the Library Wing gathers scholars and new priests and mages.",sec={{t="Haven of Arcane and Divine Study",b="The Library Wing opens south from Northshire Abbey’s Main Hall. Dusty shelves, lecterns, and quiet alcoves fill its rooms. Here aspiring mages and priests study the Arcane and the Holy Light. Across the abbey, recruits drill in the Hall of Arms.\n\nPriestess Anetta guides novice priests in faith and healing. Khelden Bremen teaches budding mages to shape primal elemental energy.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Library Wing located?",a="The Library Wing occupies the southern part of Northshire Abbey, just off the Main Hall and opposite the Hall of Arms.",al={"where is the library wing","how to find northshire library","library location northshire"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the purpose of this wing?",a="The wing is Northshire Abbey’s center for study and spiritual instruction. Recruits prepare to serve Stormwind through magical learning and prayer.",al={"why does northshire abbey have a library","library wing purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Library Wing?",a="The Library Wing is the southern annex of Northshire Abbey, set apart from the martial commotion of the Hall of Arms and the central hall. Dedicated to quiet study, mystical practice, and healing, it provides a sanctuary where novice casters and acolytes can learn the fundamental teachings of the Light and the arcane arts.",al={"what is library wing","library wing northshire","about library wing"},it="place",add="43e724fe"},{q="Who lives in or teaches at the Library Wing?",a="Priestess Anetta and Mage Trainer Khelden Bremen reside here to instruct the newest recruits answering Stormwind's call. Along with their pupils, you will find Wounded Trainees resting among the bookshelves and study alcoves, recovering under the watchful care of the abbey's healers.",al={"who is in library wing","library wing trainers","who teaches in library wing"},it="residents",add="cc13243a"},{q="Is the Library Wing dangerous?",a="The wing itself is completely safe, protected by the stout stone walls and vigilant defenders of Northshire Abbey. However, the presence of recovering wounded serves as a grim reminder that the surrounding valley is not at peace, plagued by aggressive wildlife and encroaching Defias bandits.",al={"is library wing safe","library wing danger","threats in library wing"},it="danger",add="240ac0ef"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you can learn from Priestess Anetta. She teaches fledgling priests to channel the Holy Light to heal wounds and smite foes.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can study in these quiet halls with Khelden Bremen. He teaches novice mages the foundations of fire and frost."},kw={"elwynn forest","khelden bremen","library wing","mage trainer","northshire","northshire abbey","priest trainer","priestess anetta"},rel={"subzone:northshire-abbey","subzone:main-hall-northshire","subzone:hall-of-arms-northshire","subzone:northshire-valley","npc:priestess-anetta","npc:khelden-bremen","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-army"},src={"Library Wing (Northshire)"}}
E["subzone:lion-s-pride-inn"] = {t="subzone",n="Lion's Pride Inn",z="elwynn",s="At the Lion's Pride Inn, travelers rest and find work just south of Stormwind. Innkeeper Farley welcomes them to Goldshire's gathering place in Elwynn Forest.",h="At the Lion's Pride Inn, travelers rest and find work just south of Stormwind.",sec={{t="Heart of Goldshire",b="Goldshire's crossroads bring travelers to the Lion's Pride Inn. Innkeeper Farley keeps the old motto: “Rest and relaxation for the tired and cold.” Hearths, strong drinks, and rooms welcome weary travelers from Northshire. The roads link Stormwind with Westfall, Redridge, and Duskwood, so town marshals, local crafters, and seasoned trainers gather here to share news and hire passing mercenaries.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who owns and runs the Lion's Pride Inn?",a="Innkeeper Farley runs the Lion's Pride Inn and welcomes weary travelers with its motto: “Rest and relaxation for the tired and cold.”",al={"innkeeper","who owns lions pride","who runs goldshire inn"},it="residents"},{q="What services are available inside the inn?",a="The inn offers food, drink, and lodging. Class trainers, visiting merchants, and locals seeking help with Elwynn Forest's gnoll, kobold, and bandit troubles can also be found there.",al={"trainers","what is inside","amenities"},gp=true},{q="Why is the inn such a central hub in Elwynn?",a="The Lion's Pride Inn is the chief rest stop for travelers between Stormwind, Westfall, and the Redridge Mountains. It stands at Goldshire's crossroads just south of Stormwind, and young travelers from Northshire Valley reach it as their first major gathering place.",al={"why so popular","goldshire crossroads","importance of lions pride"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the motto of the Lion's Pride Inn?",a="Innkeeper Farley gives the Lion's Pride Inn's motto as “Rest and relaxation for the tired and cold.”",al={"inn motto","motto"}},{q="What is Lion's Pride Inn?",a="The Lion's Pride Inn, also called the Goldshire Inn, is the bustling heart of Goldshire in Elwynn Forest. It serves as the primary gathering place, tavern, and lodging for locals, town guards, and weary travelers journeying along the high roads of Stormwind.",al={"what is lions pride inn","lions pride inn elwynn","goldshire inn lore"},it="place",add="3778d523"},{q="What is the history of the Lion's Pride Inn?",a="The inn has long stood as a central refuge in Goldshire. Run by Innkeeper Farley, it keeps an honest, welcoming hearth for those on the road under its motto, 'Rest and relaxation for the tired and cold.'",al={"lions pride inn history","goldshire inn background","farley family inn history"},it="history",add="4a999086"},{q="Is the Lion's Pride Inn dangerous?",a="The inn itself is entirely safe, guarded closely by the Stormwind garrison stationed in Goldshire. Outside, the road can see rowdy brawls and occasional skirmishes, while the surrounding woods teem with Kobolds, Defias bandits, and gnolls, but within its walls, you will find only rest and refuge.",al={"is lions pride inn safe","danger lions pride inn","is goldshire inn dangerous"},it="danger",add="b8029b33"}},ang={["race:Human"]="For humans leaving Northshire Abbey, the Lion's Pride Inn offers a first glimpse of the kingdom's wider life and the troubles beyond the monastery walls.",["faction:Alliance"]="As the main inn outside Stormwind's gates, the Lion's Pride Inn gives Alliance travelers a place to coordinate patrols and trade across the heartlands."},kw={"elwynn forest","farley","goldshire","goldshire inn","innkeeper farley","lion's pride inn","lions pride"},rel={"subzone:goldshire","npc:innkeeper-farley","zone:elwynn","topic:llane-wrynn-i","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:stormwind-army"},src={"Lion's Pride Inn"}}
E["subzone:maclure-vineyards"] = {t="subzone",n="Maclure Vineyards",z="elwynn",s="In southern Elwynn, grapes and wine from Maclure Vineyards go to Stormwind. The Maclure estate is known for its harvest and its bitter feud with the neighboring Stonefields.",h="In southern Elwynn, grapes and wine from Maclure Vineyards go to Stormwind.",sec={{t="A Bitter Harvest",b="In southern Elwynn Forest, the Maclures tend their fields and make wine. Yet the Stonefields, who live down the road, cast a shadow over that daily labor. Accusations of theft and old resentment keep tempers high between the households. Hungry boars prowl the land, while kobolds press toward both homesteads.",sp=0},{t="A Forbidden Romance",b="Maybell Maclure and Tommy Joe Stonefield have secretly fallen in love, though their families are bitter enemies. They meet in hidden groves, away from their parents' watchful eyes. Travelers through the vineyards carry secret messages, settle petty grievances, and help the young couple seek a life together beyond their families' grudge.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why are the Maclures and Stonefields fighting?",a="The Maclures and Stonefields have feuded for years, driven by mistrust, petty accusations, and stubborn pride. Each blames the other for lost goods and livestock, though neither has proof of foul play.",al={"maclure stonefield feud","why do they hate each other","family feud"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Maybell Maclure?",a="Maybell is the daughter of the Maclure household. She has secretly fallen in love with Tommy Joe Stonefield, defying her family's hatred of their neighbors and hoping they can find a way to be together.",al={"maybell","maclure daughter"},it="people"},{q="What threats do the vineyards face?",a="The vineyards face family disputes, hungry wild boars that trample crops and vines, and kobolds from nearby gold mines who raid the surrounding fields.",al={"vineyard dangers","boars at maclure"},it="threat"},{q="What do the Maclures produce here?",a="The Maclure family grows grapes for wine and fresh fruit. Their produce goes to tavern-keepers and merchants throughout Elwynn Forest and Stormwind City.",al={"what grows here","maclure crops"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Maclure Vineyards?",a="Maclure Vineyards is an agricultural homestead located in southern Elwynn Forest. Cultivated and operated by the Maclure family, the grounds produce grapes and fine wine for the Kingdom of Stormwind. Beyond the grape arbors, the farm features a family homestead and open fields, though it is currently plagued by unruly wild boars and tensions with its neighbors.",al={"what is maclure vineyards","maclure vineyards elwynn","maclure farm"},it="place",add="7abbd722"},{q="Who lives in Maclure Vineyards?",a="The vineyard is owned and worked by the Maclure family. The homestead is home to several generations of Maclures, including Gerard Maclure and young Maybell Maclure. Together, they tend the grapevines, defend their crops against intrusive wildlife, and manage the estate despite ongoing friction with the nearby Stonefield clan.",al={"who lives here","maclure family members","who runs maclure vineyards"},it="residents",add="d4181dc3"},{q="Is Maclure Vineyards dangerous?",a="While the farm itself is a peaceful Alliance homestead, you will find danger lurking in the vines. Aggressive wild boars constantly root through the fields, damaging crops and attacking anyone who strays too close. Additionally, kobolds from nearby mines occasionally wander toward the perimeter, making vigilance necessary for farmhands and travelers alike.",al={"is maclure vineyards safe","dangers at maclure vineyards","threats at maclure farm"},it="danger",add="6b11f938"},{q="Why is it called Maclure Vineyards?",a="The estate takes its name directly from the Maclure family, who cleared the land and planted the sprawling grapevines. For generations, their name has been synonymous with the local harvest and the sweet wines produced right here in Elwynn Forest.",al={"why is it called maclure vineyards","maclure vineyards name origin","name maclure vineyards"},it="name",add="5a643901"}},ang={["race:Human"]="For humans of Stormwind, the feud shows the stubbornness of the countryside. Even in the kingdom's heartland, neighbors quarrel over fences while greater perils loom.",["faction:Alliance"]="The estate supplies food and spirits to nearby Goldshire and Stormwind City."},kw={"boars","elwynn","gerard","maclure","maybell","stonefield","vineyard","wine"},rel={"zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom","quest:114","quest:86","quest:85","quest:16","quest:88","topic:kobold"},src={"Maclure Vineyards"}}
E["subzone:main-hall-northshire"] = {t="subzone",n="Main Hall",z="elwynn",s="Newcomers report to the Main Hall at Northshire Abbey in western Elwynn. From there, they reach the Hall of Arms, the Library Wing, and the abbey tower before receiving their first assignments defending Stormwind.",h="Newcomers report to the Main Hall at Northshire Abbey in western Elwynn.",sec={{t="Heart of the Abbey",b="Trainees and clerics pass through the Main Hall when they enter Northshire Abbey. The chamber joins the Hall of Arms, where recruits prepare for battle, to the Library Wing and the stairs to the abbey tower.\n\nStrife in the valley reaches even this quiet place. Officers gather able newcomers here to defend the kingdom's borders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Main Hall?",a="The Main Hall connects the Hall of Arms, the Library Wing, and the upper tower of Northshire Abbey. Recruits, priests, and visitors pass through this central chamber.",al={"what is main hall","northshire main hall use"},it="purpose"},{q="Who directs new recruits here?",a="Stormwind defense officers and clerics in the Main Hall assess newcomers and give them their first orders. They are told to clear threats from the abbey grounds.",al={"who gives quests here","abbey commander"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is the Main Hall of Northshire Abbey?",a="The Main Hall is the central entrance chamber of Northshire Abbey, nestled in the sheltered Northshire Valley of Elwynn Forest. It serves as the primary thoroughfare linking the abbey's tower, the Library Wing, and the Hall of Arms, making it the heart of activity for newly arrived defenders of the realm.",al={"what is main hall","northshire main hall","what is this hall"},it="place",add="23c998e2"},{q="Is the Main Hall dangerous?",a="The hall is guarded and offers shelter from the valley's dangers. Outside the abbey, aggressive wildlife and Defias bandits threaten the surrounding grounds.",al={"is main hall safe","main hall danger","are there enemies in main hall"},it="danger",add="c47795b4"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human of the kingdom, you begin serving Stormwind and the Holy Light in Northshire Abbey's Main Hall."},kw={"abbey","elwynn","hall of arms","library wing","main hall","northshire","stormwind"},rel={"subzone:northshire-abbey","subzone:northshire-valley","subzone:hall-of-arms-northshire","subzone:library-wing-northshire","zone:elwynn"},src={"Main Hall (Northshire)"}}
E["subzone:mirror-lake"] = {t="subzone",n="Mirror Lake",z="elwynn",s="Water falls into Mirror Lake beneath Stormwind’s cliffs in northwestern Elwynn Forest. An orchard stands nearby, where Defias bandits prowl and mages watch the forest’s arcane currents.",h="Water falls into Mirror Lake beneath Stormwind’s cliffs in northwestern Elwynn Forest.",sec={{t="A Troubled Idyl",b="Mirror Lake rests beneath Stormwind City's walls, where fishermen and tired travelers can seek a quiet rest. Yet Defias Brotherhood brigands stalk the surrounding orchards, making a long stay perilous for locals.\n\nMystical disturbances across Azeroth have begun to warp the forest's natural channels of arcane energy. Mages from the Wizard's Sanctum watch the lake closely. They send practitioners to sample its currents and guard against chaotic arcane runoff poisoning communities downstream.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Mirror Lake dangerous?",a="Defias bandits prowl around Mirror Lake and prey on travelers and farmers. Recent shifts in regional magic have also raised concern about the lake's water.",al={"is mirror lake safe","mirror lake enemies","defias mirror lake"},it="danger"},{q="Why are mages studying Mirror Lake?",a="Massive magical conflicts across Azeroth have unsettled ley currents throughout Elwynn Forest and Stormwind. The Wizard's Sanctum sends initiates to sample the lake's water for unstable arcane residue that could affect those who drink from it.",al={"wizard sanctum mirror lake","mirror lake quest","magic in mirror lake"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does the waterfall at Mirror Lake come from?",a="The waterfall comes from the high cliffs and waterways around Stormwind City. Its water feeds the lake before winding through the Elwynn river system.",al={"mirror lake waterfall","water source mirror lake"}},{q="What is Mirror Lake?",a="Mirror Lake is a small, scenic body of water nestled in western Elwynn Forest near an orchard. Fed by a rushing waterfall pouring down from the mountains beneath Stormwind, it would otherwise be a quiet haven for fishing and swimming if not for the criminal element currently controlling its shores.",al={"mirror lake elwynn","what is mirror lake","about mirror lake"},it="place",add="80ec8f44"},{q="Who controls Mirror Lake?",a="The lake is currently overrun by the Defias Brotherhood. These outlaws prowl the shoreline and surrounding orchards, driving off local fishermen and travelers while using the remote, sheltered waters as a base of operations right outside Stormwind's walls.",al={"who lives at mirror lake","mirror lake bandits","who runs mirror lake"},it="residents",add="e8bd98e7"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Initiates studying at Stormwind's Wizard's Sanctum come to Mirror Lake to gather water samples. Their work shows how turbulent arcane channels can seep into the natural world.",["faction:Alliance"]="Mirror Lake lies close to Stormwind's walls, while the kingdom's guards are stretched thin against Defias outlaws in the surrounding area."},kw={"defias","elwynn forest","mirror lake","stormwind","waterfall","wizards sanctum"},rel={"zone:elwynn","quest:1861","zone:stormwind","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Mirror Lake"}}
E["subzone:mirror-lake-orchard"] = {t="subzone",n="Mirror Lake Orchard",z="elwynn",s="Defias bandits now hold Mirror Lake Orchard on Mirror Lake’s southern shore in western Elwynn Forest. With Stormwind’s guards stretched thin, the grove near Thunder Falls lies exposed.",h="Defias bandits now hold Mirror Lake Orchard on Mirror Lake’s southern shore in western Elwynn Forest.",sec={{t="A Grove Under Seizure",b="Mirror Lake’s clean waters once sustained the farmstead. Now outlaws across Elwynn seek shelter in rural homes. The orchard’s cottage and grounds give the Defias Brotherhood a place to hide near Thunder Falls.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who controls Mirror Lake Orchard right now?",a="Defias bandits occupy Mirror Lake Orchard and its cottage. They drove away the honest folk who tended the trees, and now use the secluded grounds as a base in western Elwynn.",al={"who is at mirror lake orchard","who lives here","orchard enemies"},it="in_charge"},{q="Where is Mirror Lake Orchard located?",a="Mirror Lake Orchard lies on Mirror Lake’s southern shore in western Elwynn Forest, just east of Thunder Falls and north of the main road toward Westfall.",al={"mirror lake orchard location","where is the orchard","find orchard elwynn"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why hasn't Stormwind reclaimed the orchard?",a="Stormwind’s standing army is largely absent from rural Elwynn amid political deadlock and the mysterious disappearance of King Varian Wrynn. Local garrisons are short-handed, so distant farms and orchards are often left to face the Defias Brotherhood alone.",al={"why are defias here","where are the guards"},it="conflict"},{q="What is the connection between the orchard and Thunder Falls?",a="Mirror Lake drains into Thunder Falls, and the orchard sits just above the cascade. Its secluded position near the cliffs gives bandits a defensible place.",al={"thunder falls connection","orchard and waterfall"},it="ties"},{q="What is Mirror Lake Orchard?",a="Mirror Lake Orchard is a small, quiet farmstead nestled on the southern shore of Mirror Lake in western Elwynn Forest. Once a peaceful fruit orchard with an adjoining cottage, it has fallen into lawlessness like much of the surrounding countryside.",al={"what is this place","mirror lake orchard lore","about mirror lake orchard"},it="place",add="9fb3552d"},{q="What happened at Mirror Lake Orchard?",a="The peaceful farmers who once tended these trees were driven out or abandoned their home as unrest spread across Elwynn Forest. Seizing the opportunity, outlaws from the Defias Brotherhood moved in, turning the deserted cottage and orchard into another secluded staging ground for their operations.",al={"mirror lake orchard history","what happened here","orchard background"},it="history",add="fc4dc36b"},{q="Why was Mirror Lake Orchard abandoned?",a="With Stormwind's attention divided and local guards stretched thin, rural homesteads throughout Elwynn became prime targets for rogue brigands. The orchard was abandoned to the encroaching Defias bandits, who claimed the cottage and land for themselves.",al={"why is the orchard abandoned","why did farmers leave","who abandoned the orchard"},it="ruin",add="d58df7ba"},{q="Is Mirror Lake Orchard dangerous?",a="Yes. The area is currently overrun by hostile Defias bandits who patrol the groves and occupy the nearby house. Anyone venturing through the trees without their guard up risks being ambushed on sight.",al={"is it safe here","mirror lake orchard danger","enemies at mirror lake orchard"},it="danger",add="90c4a3ea"},{q="Why is it called Mirror Lake Orchard?",a="The orchard takes its name directly from its location along the southern shore of Mirror Lake, where its fruit trees were planted beside the calm, reflective waters.",al={"why is it named mirror lake orchard","mirror lake orchard name meaning","origin of orchard name"},it="name",add="626e53a6"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers, the occupied orchard is another sign of the Defias Brotherhood’s bold advance across the kingdom’s heartland.",["class:Rogue"]="As a Rogue, you can see the Defias strategy at the orchard: seize overlooked, defensible ground near water and cliffs to watch the roads and evade city patrols."},kw={"defias brotherhood","elwynn forest","mirror lake","mirror lake orchard","stormwind bandits","thunder falls"},rel={"zone:elwynn","quest:1861","subzone:thunder-falls","topic:alliance"},src={"Mirror Lake Orchard"}}
E["subzone:northshire-abbey"] = {t="subzone",n="Northshire Abbey",z="elwynn",s="Northshire Abbey trains the kingdom's newest defenders, in the foothills of Northshire Valley. It is the spiritual heart of the Brotherhood of Northshire. And for those who answer Stormwind's call, few schools in the land are finer. It has been built twice.",h="Northshire Abbey trains the kingdom's newest defenders, in the foothills of Northshire Valley.",sec={{t="A Legacy of Faith and Ruin",b="Centuries ago, clerics came south from Lordaeron to spread the Holy Light. They founded the Holy Order of Northshire Clerics, and they built its abbey. It soon became part of the life of the kingdom, caring for its sick. For years it tended the young Guardian Medivh, while he lay in his long coma.\n\nThen the First War came. Brigands and the Horde struck at the abbey again and again, until it lay in ruins. In the Second War, the Alliance of Lordaeron freed the region. Afterward, Archbishop Alonsus Faol helped to raise the abbey anew. And he refounded its protectors as the Brotherhood of Northshire.",sp=0},{t="The Training Grounds",b="Today the abbey takes in volunteers, militia recruits and novices, all of them hoping to defend Stormwind. In its halls, instructors teach the martial, arcane and holy arts. Scouts and rogues train out in the yards. And the Knights of the Silver Hand keep watch over it all.\n\nBut the peace here is fragile. Kobolds have overrun the nearby mines, and wolves prowl the orchards. Agents of the Defias Brotherhood stalk the valley roads. Not even the abbey's archives are safe from them. They steal its ancient scrolls and sacred librams.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Brotherhood of Northshire?",a="The Brotherhood of Northshire is a religious order of clerics, priests, and paladins based at Northshire Abbey. Clerics from Lordaeron founded it centuries ago, and Archbishop Alonsus Faol re-established it after the First War to train faithful defenders and preserve sacred scripture. Northshire Abbey stands in Elwynn Forest’s northern foothills.",al={"who runs northshire abbey","northshire clerics","brotherhood of northshire lore"},it="residents"},{q="Why was Northshire Abbey destroyed in the First War?",a="During the First War, the abbey was important to Stormwind's defenses and faith. Orcish forces incited human brigands to attack, and after the half-orc Garona was briefly held captive there, a great Horde assault leveled the holy grounds. The abbey lay in ruins until the Alliance drove out the orcish clans and rebuilt it.",al={"who destroyed northshire abbey","northshire first war","what happened to northshire"},it="history"},{q="Why are there Defias bandits and kobolds outside the abbey?",a="Stormwind's military is stretched thin protecting distant borders, leaving outlying regions poorly guarded. Kobolds have infested the local gold mines, while the Defias Brotherhood takes advantage of the gaps to rob travelers, harass local vineyards, and raid the abbey's library for arcane tomes and holy relics. Their agents steal ancient scrolls and sacred librams from the abbey’s archives.",al={"why is northshire under attack","kobolds in northshire","defias outside northshire"},it="threat"},{q="What is the connection between Northshire Abbey and the Deadmines?",a="During the First War, the ogre chieftain Turok stole the sacred Tome of Divinity from Northshire Abbey and retreated into the Deadmines. Sir Anduin Lothar led an expedition into the depths to recover it, became trapped, and was rescued by a royal party that returned the tome to the abbey.",al={"tome of divinity northshire","northshire deadmines lore","anduin lothar deadmines"},it="ties"},{q="What is Northshire Abbey?",a="Northshire Abbey is a revered holy sanctuary nestled in the quiet foothills of northern Elwynn Forest. Originally founded centuries ago by pious clerics from Lordaeron, it serves as the spiritual seat of the Brotherhood of Northshire. Following its reconstruction after the First War, the abbey functions as a recruitment center and proving ground for new champions defending the Kingdom of Stormwind, housing trainers of sacred magic, the martial arts, and arcane lore within its storied halls.",al={"what is northshire abbey","about northshire abbey","northshire abbey overview"},it="place",add="a3256ecc"},{q="Is Northshire Abbey dangerous?",a="The abbey itself remains well guarded by paladins and town watchmen, but the surrounding valley is growing perilously unsafe. Kobolds have overrun the nearby Echo Ridge Mine, aggressive wolves prowl the orchards and forests, and brigands from the Defias Brotherhood openly lurk around the vineyards. While novice adventurers can easily find their footing within the courtyard, wandering the valley unprepared invites sudden danger.",al={"is northshire safe","danger in northshire abbey","is northshire valley dangerous"},it="danger",add="d8226933"}},ang={["race:Human"]="For humans of Stormwind, Northshire Abbey is where your journey begins, and where the kingdom's resilience and devotion welcome every recruit who takes up arms.",["class:Paladin"]="For a paladin, Northshire carries the legacy of Archbishop Alonsus Faol and the early clerics whose sacrifices laid the foundation for the Knights of the Silver Hand."},kw={"abbey","brotherhood","clerics","defias","elwynn","faol","northshire","valley"},rel={"subzone:northshire-valley","topic:brotherhood-of-northshire","topic:church-of-the-holy-light","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:knights-of-the-silver-hand","quest:1598","quest:2997","npc:drusilla-la-salle"},src={"Northshire Abbey"}}
E["subzone:northshire-valley"] = {t="subzone",n="Northshire Valley",z="elwynn",s="Northshire Valley, in the hills of northern Elwynn, is where Stormwind's newest defenders begin. Mountain ridges guard it on every side but one. At its heart stands the ancient abbey, with fertile vineyards and a rich mine close by. But bandits and kobolds trouble the valley now, and wolves prowl its quiet pastures.",h="Northshire Valley, in the hills of northern Elwynn, is where Stormwind's newest defenders begin.",sec={{t="A Secluded Sanctuary",b="The only way out is the road south. It runs through a fortified gatehouse, on toward Goldshire and the rest of the forest. A clear river crosses the pastures and flows into Crystal Lake. In the abbey, recruits train under seasoned veterans and the Knights of the Silver Hand. With its vineyards and its mine, the valley has all it needs, far from the wars beyond its ridges.",sp=0},{t="Encroaching Troubles",b="But even here, Stormwind's defenses are stretched thin. In the valley, Marshal McBride and his detachment of the Guard struggle to keep order. So the commanders here take on every able-bodied soul who reaches the gates. They need every one of them.\n\nWolves have come north out of darkened Duskwood. Kobolds have overrun the tunnels of Echo Ridge Mine. And masked thugs of the Defias Brotherhood harass the vineyards. They threaten even the abbey grounds.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Northshire Valley so heavily guarded?",a="Northshire Valley guards Northshire Abbey, a spiritual center and training ground for Stormwind's forces, where recruits learn the Holy Light, as well as the vineyards and Echo Ridge Mine. With Stormwind's forces stretched thin, Marshal McBride holds the southern pass behind a guarded gate to keep threats from passing between the valley and greater Elwynn Forest.",al={"why guards northshire","gate in northshire","who protects northshire"},it="danger"},{q="Where did all the wolves in the valley come from?",a="Deputy Willem says wolves have recently crossed the river after fleeing Duskwood's darkened forests to the south. The spreading darkness there has driven wild beasts into the valley's tranquil pastures.",al={"why so many wolves","wolf infestation","wolves from duskwood"},it="threat"},{q="Why are kobolds attacking Echo Ridge Mine?",a="Kobolds are opportunistic burrowers drawn to underground mineral veins. As kingdom patrols thinned, a clan took advantage of the lack of protection to claim Echo Ridge Mine for its gold and candles, forcing the human miners out of the tunnels.",al={"echo ridge kobolds","why kobolds in northshire","kobold problem"},it="threat",nx={18}},{q="Who are the bandits harassing the vineyards?",a="The thieves near Milly Osworth's vineyard are agents of the Defias Brotherhood. They prey on the valley's outskirts to disrupt supplies, harass local farmers, and test the abbey's defenses.",al={"vineyard bandits","defias in northshire","red mask thugs"},it="threat"},{q="What happened to Northshire during the Second War?",a="During the Second War, Northshire Abbey fell into enemy hands and briefly served as a headquarters for Cho'gall's Twilight's Hammer clan. The Alliance later reclaimed and restored the valley.",al={"northshire second war","twilight hammer northshire","chogall northshire"},it="history"},{q="How do you leave Northshire Valley?",a="The only passable exit on foot is the southern road through the guarded gatehouse. It leads into central Elwynn Forest and points travelers toward Goldshire.",al={"exit northshire","path to goldshire","how to leave"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What is Northshire Valley?",a="Northshire Valley is a secluded, mountainous valley nestled in northern Elwynn Forest. It is best known as the home of Northshire Abbey and its surrounding vineyards. Bordered by sheer mountains and accessed only by a fortified southern gateway, it serves as the primary training and recruitment ground for fledgling defenders of the kingdom of Stormwind.",al={"where is northshire valley","tell me about northshire valley","where am i northshire"},it="place",add="9b50c77b",nx={8,9}},{q="Is Northshire Valley part of Stormwind?",a="Yes. Northshire Valley sits squarely within Elwynn Forest, the heartland of the kingdom of Stormwind. The garrison here flies Stormwind's banners, enforces its laws, and reports directly up the kingdom's military hierarchy.",al={"is northshire in stormwind","does stormwind own northshire"},it="place",add="3a470446"},{q="Why do all new recruits train in Northshire Valley?",a="The valley offers a protected, self-contained haven surrounded by high cliffs, making it an ideal staging area. With seasoned marshals, class mentors, and the spiritual presence of the Brotherhood of Northshire all centered at the Abbey, it provides everything necessary to prepare new recruits before they face the wider forest.",al={"why train here","why do recruits come to northshire"},it="place",add="52057ec0"},{q="Why am I here in Northshire Valley as a new recruit?",a="You arrived in response to the kingdom's urgent need for defenders. With Stormwind's regular army stretched thin across contested borders, the authorities opened Northshire Abbey to train any brave soul willing to swear service and keep the realm safe.",al={"why am i here","new recruit why here","what brought me here"},it="arrival",add="0f9fef82"},{q="What is Northshire Abbey?",a="Northshire Abbey is a venerable holy site and the historical seat of the Brotherhood of Northshire, an order of clerics founded centuries ago by missionaries of the Church of the Holy Light. Beyond its religious duties, it contains a library, a hall of arms, and quarters for training newly sworn champions of the Alliance.",al={"tell me about northshire abbey","what is the abbey"},it="place",add="0fbb181a",nx={12,13}},{q="Who runs Northshire Abbey?",a="While the clerics attend to the Abbey's spiritual upkeep, Marshal Douglas McBride commands the garrison on site and governs the defense of the entire valley on behalf of the Stormwind Army.",al={"who leads the abbey","abbey leader"},it="in_charge",add="385ef21f"},{q="Why is there an army garrison camped outside a church?",a="Recent troubles have forced martial forces directly into the Abbey's grounds. Bandits have overrun the adjacent vineyards and kobolds have burrowed into nearby mines, leaving the clerics unable to protect the holy grounds without direct military intervention.",al={"why soldiers at the abbey","why garrison at church"},it="place",add="ac0d723b"},{q="Who's in charge around Northshire Valley?",a="Marshal Douglas McBride oversees the defense of Northshire Valley. Stationed inside the Abbey, he directs the garrison, enlists arriving recruits, and coordinates efforts to repel the threats encroaching on the valley.",al={"who is in charge here","northshire commander","who runs northshire"},it="in_charge",add="2babcb98",nx={15}},{q="Who does Marshal McBride answer to?",a="Marshal McBride is an officer of the Stormwind Army serving the crown. His Northshire garrison is part of Elwynn Forest's defense, alongside the forces stationed in Goldshire.",al={"mcbride superior","who is mcbrides boss"},it="in_charge",add="5231335a"},{q="What is 'A Threat Within' about?",a="The phrase refers to the alarming breakdown of security inside the kingdom's own borders. Rather than an army attacking from beyond, Stormwind faces subversion, rogue thieves, and vermin taking root right in its sacred backyard.",al={"a threat within meaning","what threat within quest","what is the threat inside"},it="threat",add="0040026b"},{q="What are kobolds?",a="Kobolds are subterranean rat-like humanoids known for their obsessive tunneling and cowardice in small numbers. They scavenge minerals and dark corners of the realm, fiercely defending their underground warrens from any outsiders.",al={"kobolds lore","what is a kobold","who are kobolds"},it="threat",add="3e58992c"},{q="What is Echo Ridge Mine, was it ours first?",a="Echo Ridge Mine was a productive excavation worked by the kingdom until recently. Kobolds swarmed into the tunnels from the surrounding hills, driving out the human miners and claiming the site as an armed colony.",al={"who owned echo ridge mine","is echo ridge ours","what is echo ridge"},it="threat",add="1071f0ff"},{q="Why do I have to kill so many kobolds, what did they even do?",a="By overrunning Echo Ridge Mine, the kobolds cut off valuable resources and created a hazardous vermin nest adjacent to the Abbey. If left unchecked, their digging threatens to undermine the valley's stability and overwhelm nearby roads.",al={"why kill kobolds","why exterminate kobolds"},it="purpose",add="ffddbb43"},{q="Who are the guys with the red bandanas?",a="Those are agents of the Defias Brotherhood, led locally by Garrick Padfoot. Once skilled craftsmen and laborers from the Stonemasons Guild who rebuilt Stormwind, they turned to banditry and revolt against the crown after a bitter pay dispute.",al={"red bandana bandits","who wears red bandanas","red masks northshire"},it="threat",add="c35515fc"},{q="Why are Defias bandits attacking this close to Stormwind?",a="With royal troops deployed abroad and domestic garrisons starved of resources, the Defias have grown bold enough to seize farms and orchards throughout Elwynn. Northshire's vineyards offer them food, wine, and a staging ground right under the crown's nose.",al={"why bandits near stormwind","why defias in northshire"},it="history",add="c05e8af1"},{q="Why does the Abbey have a warlock trainer at all?",a="Drusilla La Salle trains warlocks in Northshire's cemetery, away from the Abbey's clerics and paladins. Her secluded position reflects the unease surrounding fel magic among those devoted to the Holy Light.",al={"warlock at abbey why","why is there a warlock trainer here"},it="other",add="660e62c8"},{q="Why is everyone asking me, a total beginner, to do all this?",a="The Stormwind Guard is stretched past its breaking point. With soldiers guarding major frontiers and royal forces away, the local garrison simply does not have the manpower to clear every mine or guard every vineyard, leaving recruits like you as their best available line of defense.",al={"why me a beginner","why do i do all the work","why ask recruits"},it="why_me",add="808e49f9"},{q="How did I end up in Northshire Valley?",a="You came seeking Northshire Abbey, the primary recruitment and training grounds for those willing to take up arms for the Kingdom of Stormwind. Surrounded by high mountains and guarded by a fortified pass, this peaceful valley serves as the first assembly point for new defenders. Whether you arrived by foot through Elwynn Forest or answered the crown's call for fresh recruits, Marshal McBride and the abbey's masters were expecting eager souls like you to report for duty.",al={"how did i get here","how did i end up here","why did i arrive in northshire"},it="arrival",add="99bf7d8e"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Northshire Valley?",a="You are here to hone your martial or magical skills under the abbey's trainers while aiding the local garrison. Marshal Douglas McBride and the Stormwind Guard are short-handed and urgently require recruits to deal with nearby threats. You need to cull the predatory wolves encroaching from the timberline, reclaim the Echo Ridge Mine from invasive kobolds, and protect Milly Osworth's vineyards from the Defias Brotherhood bandits lurking nearby before marching south into Elwynn Forest.",al={"what should i be doing here","what is my goal here","what do i do in northshire"},it="purpose",add="bb6d78ec"},{q="Why does a new Human start here, in Northshire Valley?",a="Northshire Abbey has stood for centuries as a foundational pillar of human resilience in the kingdom, home to the Brotherhood of Northshire and a gathering place for the Knights of the Silver Hand. With Stormwind's regular military stretched thin and King Varian Wrynn mysteriously missing, young humans eager to defend their homeland are directed to this sheltered sanctuary to begin their formal training, receive their letters of introduction, and prove their loyalty to the crown.",al={"why do humans start here","why do human characters begin in northshire","why is northshire the human start"},it="arrival",rc="Human",add="11801d7a"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human of Stormwind, your journey begins in Northshire Valley, where you enter the abbey grounds to answer the kingdom's call for help.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you find a vital place for recruitment and recovery in Northshire. The valley trains new defenders to stabilize the kingdom's heart."},kw={"abbey","defias","echo ridge","elwynn","kobolds","mcbride","northshire","vineyards","willem"},rel={"subzone:northshire-abbey","npc:marshal-mcbride","subzone:northshire-vineyards","subzone:echo-ridge-mine","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-guard","topic:defias-brotherhood","subzone:goldshire"},src={"Northshire Valley"}}
E["subzone:northshire-vineyards"] = {t="subzone",n="Northshire Vineyards",z="elwynn",s="East of Northshire Abbey, Northshire Vineyards are in Defias hands. Their grapes once supplied wine to the clerics, but thieves now plunder the harvest and threaten local farmers.",h="East of Northshire Abbey, Northshire Vineyards are in Defias hands.",sec={{t="A Plundered Harvest",b="Across the stream from Northshire Abbey, local workers once tended the grape fields. Milly Osworth was among them. Now Garrick Padfoot leads the Defias Brotherhood brigands who hold the acreage.\n\nThe vineyards give newly arrived Brotherhood recruits an easy foothold close to the abbey. The Defias presence has reached its fields.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who controls the Northshire Vineyards right now?",a="Defias Brotherhood thieves and cutthroats occupy Northshire Vineyards. Garrick Padfoot leads them as they plunder the crops and terrorize local workers.",al={"who is at the vineyards","who took over northshire vineyards","who is garrick padfoot"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why is the abbey letting bandits run rampant in the fields?",a="Stormwind's forces are stretched thin while King Varian Wrynn is missing. Abbey guards protect the abbey and watch the valley roads, so local farmers depend on newly arrived adventurers to recover their stolen goods.",al={"why no stormwind guards","why isn't the abbey defending the vineyards"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Milly Osworth?",a="Milly Osworth is a local farmer who worked the vineyards. When the Defias bandits seized the grape harvest, they drove her away. She now asks travelers to recover her stolen crates.",al={"milly osworth","who is milly"},it="people"},{q="What is Northshire Vineyards?",a="The Northshire Vineyards are agricultural fields located directly east of Northshire Abbey in Northshire Valley. Under ordinary circumstances, the fields provide grapes and harvest produce for the local settlement, but they have recently fallen into disarray due to criminal activity.",al={"what are northshire vineyards","northshire vineyards overview","about northshire vineyards"},it="place",add="d5ec287a"},{q="What happened at Northshire Vineyards?",a="Agents of the Defias Brotherhood swept in and seized control of the vineyards. Led by the bandit Garrick Padfoot, they pushed out the local workers, stole the harvest belonging to residents like Milly Osworth, and established an armed presence right at the abbey's doorstep.",al={"northshire vineyards history","what happened here","vineyards story"},it="history",add="1ba8e301"},{q="Is Northshire Vineyards dangerous?",a="Yes. The vineyard fields are crawling with hostile Defias bandits and thugs under Garrick Padfoot's command. Anyone wandering among the grapevines without a weapon risks being attacked on sight by cutpurses and brigands who have claimed the land for themselves.",al={"is it safe here","danger northshire vineyards","vineyards safe"},it="danger",add="af15433a"}},ang={["race:Human"]="For many young humans setting out into the world, the occupied vineyards offer a first encounter with the Defias Brotherhood's reach and the bitterness it brings.",["faction:Alliance"]="Unrest in these quiet grape fields shows how far lawlessness has spread, reaching even the most protected corners of the kingdom of Stormwind."},kw={"defias","elwynn","garrick padfoot","grapes","milly osworth","northshire valley","northshire vineyards"},rel={"subzone:northshire-valley","topic:defias-brotherhood","quest:3903","zone:elwynn"},src={"Northshire Vineyards"}}
E["subzone:ridgepoint-tower"] = {t="subzone",n="Ridgepoint Tower",z="elwynn",s="Stormwind guards watch eastern Elwynn from Ridgepoint Tower, where forest roads lead into neighboring wilderness. The garrison scans the valleys for threats to the kingdom’s farms and settlements.",h="Stormwind guards watch eastern Elwynn from Ridgepoint Tower, where forest roads lead into neighboring...",sec={{t="Sentinel of the Eastern Border",b="Ridgepoint Tower looks out from high ground at the eastern edge of Stormwind’s authority, with wild country beyond. Its guards watch the routes toward farms and settlements nearer Northshire and Goldshire. They remain alert for danger crossing the border.",sp=0},{t="Threats on Every Horizon",b="Threats press in from several directions. East lie the Redridge Mountains, where aggressive gnoll packs and blackrock orc raiders test human defenses. Across the southern river, undead horrors prowl Duskwood’s timberline. Nearby wilderness camps shelter rogue Defias Brotherhood bandits seeking gaps in the guard’s defenses.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Ridgepoint Tower?",a="Stormwind’s guards watch the kingdom’s eastern edge from Ridgepoint Tower, a fortified scout post in eastern Elwynn Forest.",al={"ridgepoint tower elwynn","what is this guard tower","east elwynn tower"},it="place"},{q="Who controls and mans the tower?",a="Guardsmen and scouts loyal to the Kingdom of Stormwind hold and garrison Ridgepoint Tower under the command of the Stormwind Guard.",al={"who is at ridgepoint tower","who owns ridgepoint tower"},it="residents"},{q="What threats does the garrison watch out for?",a="The garrison watches for aggressive gnoll packs and blackrock orc raiders from the Redridge Mountains, undead horrors from Duskwood, and Defias Brotherhood bandits in nearby wilderness camps.",al={"enemies near ridgepoint","what is attacking ridgepoint","why is the tower here"},it="threat"},{q="Where is Ridgepoint Tower located?",a="Ridgepoint Tower stands on high ground in eastern Elwynn Forest, near the borders of the Redridge Mountains and Duskwood.",al={"ridgepoint tower location","where is ridgepoint"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is Ridgepoint Tower dangerous?",a="The tower itself is secure and held firmly by the Stormwind Guard, but the surrounding land is fraught with danger. Sitting at a strategic border, the watchpost is constantly under threat from gnolls and orcs descending from Redridge Mountains, restless undead wandering north out of Duskwood, and Defias bandits lurking in nearby camps.",al={"ridgepoint tower dangerous","is it safe at ridgepoint tower","ridgepoint tower threats"},it="danger",add="eff326af"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can take Ridgepoint Tower as a reassuring sign of safety and order before crossing into Redridge’s perilous passes or Duskwood’s haunted roads.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you can respect the guardsmen’s resolve as they hold this exposed border outpost against surrounding hostiles."},kw={"defias","duskwood","elwynn forest","gnolls","redridge","ridgepoint tower","stormwind guard","watchtower"},rel={"zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-guard","zone:redridge","zone:duskwood","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:gnoll"},src={"Ridgepoint Tower"}}
E["subzone:stone-cairn-lake"] = {t="subzone",n="Stone Cairn Lake",z="elwynn",s="At Stone Cairn Lake in northeastern Elwynn, murlocs hold the southern shore. Renegade wizards camp beside Heroes' Vigil, a memorial to those lost in the First War.",h="At Stone Cairn Lake in northeastern Elwynn, murlocs hold the southern shore.",sec={{t="A Monument Besieged",b="Families and pilgrims once crossed the calm lake waters to honor the dead at Heroes' Vigil. The stone memorial rises on the central island, marking the heavy loss of human life in the First War against the Orcish Horde. Now the island is hostile, and those who come to pay their respects must face the wizards' camp beside the monument.",sp=0},{t="Shores of the Lake",b="Aggressive murlocs hold Stone Cairn Lake's southern banks. Crude huts line the water, and the murlocs harass anyone who comes near. Rich mineral veins run through the hills and rocky outcrops around the lake, drawing prospectors and miners despite the dangers along the shore.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is it called Stone Cairn Lake?",a="Stone Cairn Lake takes its name from Heroes' Vigil, a stone cairn on the central island honoring Stormwind's soldiers and civilians who died in the First War.",al={"stone cairn name","why stone cairn","origin of the name"},it="name"},{q="Who is currently occupying the central island?",a="Renegade wizards and other renegades occupy the central island. They drive away pilgrims and build a fortified camp around the memorial.",al={"who is on the island","island wizards","rogue mages on lake"},it="residents"},{q="Why are murlocs gathered around the water?",a="A local murloc tribe has settled the southern shallows and riverbanks. They build huts along the waterline and claim the plentiful fishing waters as their territory.",al={"murlocs at stone cairn","lake murlocs","south shore huts"},it="threat"},{q="What is the memorial on the island called?",a="The memorial is called Heroes' Vigil. Its stone cairn is also known as the Stone of Remembrance.",al={"island memorial name","monument name","stone cairn shrine"},it="history"},{q="What is Stone Cairn Lake?",a="Stone Cairn Lake is a ring-shaped body of water situated in northeastern Elwynn Forest. At its center lies an island bearing Heroes' Vigil, a solemn memorial honoring those who perished during the First War. Once a tranquil destination for travelers and mourners, the area has since grown wild and perilous.",al={"what is stone cairn lake","stone cairn lake info","tell me about stone cairn lake"},it="place",add="a25fa3d9"},{q="Is Stone Cairn Lake dangerous?",a="Yes, it poses significant danger to wandering travelers. Rogue wizards have seized the island at the center of the lake, aggressively defending their camp with arcane magic. Furthermore, hostile murlocs have overrun the shallows and erected settlements along the southern banks, attacking anyone who draws near.",al={"is stone cairn lake safe","stone cairn lake threats","danger stone cairn lake"},it="danger",add="9a875c99"},{q="Why was Stone Cairn Lake abandoned as a pilgrimage site?",a="Stone Cairn Lake was once a peaceful pilgrimage destination for citizens honoring fallen soldiers from the First War. However, Stormwind's guards could not keep it secure amid mounting unrest, allowing rogue spellcasters to commandeer the monument island and vicious murlocs to claim the shores.",al={"why is stone cairn lake abandoned","why is stone cairn lake ruined","pilgrimage stone cairn lake"},it="ruin",add="92ff0cce"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="The hills and bluffs around Stone Cairn Lake hold one of Elwynn Forest's heaviest concentrations of copper deposits, drawing aspiring blacksmiths and engineers.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you can see the island as a memorial to Stormwind's people. It honors those lost when the kingdom fell in the First War."},kw={"copper","elwynn forest","first war","heroes' vigil","murloc","rogue wizards","stone cairn lake","stone of remembrance"},rel={"subzone:heroes-vigil","zone:elwynn","topic:first-war","topic:murloc"},src={"Stone Cairn Lake"}}
E["subzone:stonefield-farm"] = {t="subzone",n="Stonefield Farm",z="elwynn",s="In southern Elwynn Forest, the Stonefield family works its fields while a long feud divides them from the Maclures.",h="In southern Elwynn Forest, the Stonefield family works its fields while a long feud divides them from the...",sec={{t="A Bitter Homestead",b="South of Goldshire, the Stonefields grow crops for the realm. For decades, they have quarreled with the nearby Maclure Vineyards. Each household accuses the other of theft and trespassing, and even small disputes keep tensions high. Gramma Stonefield, Ma Stonefield, and young Tommy Joe Stonefield make their home here.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the feud between the Stonefields and the Maclures?",a="The Stonefields and Maclures have quarreled for years in southern Elwynn Forest. They accuse each other of trespassing, theft, and other wrongs, and refuse to cooperate even on simple matters between neighbors.",al={"stonefield maclure feud","why are stonefields fighting","stonefield rivals"},it="conflict"},{q="Who lives at Stonefield Farm?",a="Gramma Stonefield, Ma Stonefield, and young Tommy Joe Stonefield live at the farm. The Stonefield clan manages it.",al={"stonefield npcs","who is at stonefield farm"},it="residents"},{q="What is Tommy Joe Stonefield's secret?",a="Tommy Joe Stonefield is secretly in love with Maybell Maclure, despite the hostility between their families. The two rely on sympathetic travelers to carry messages and gifts without their families noticing.",al={"tommy joe secret","tommy joe romance","stonefield love"}},{q="What is Stonefield Farm?",a="Stonefield Farm is a quiet homestead nestled in the southern reaches of Elwynn Forest, worked and tended by the Stonefield family. While it looks like an ordinary farmstead producing crops for the region, it is best known across the valley for its long, bitter rivalry with its neighboring homestead, the Maclure Vineyards. Visitors often find themselves caught squarely in the middle of domestic quarrels, missing heirloom squabbles, and the secret romantic pursuits of the younger generation.",al={"what is stonefield farm","stonefield farmstead elwynn","about stonefield farm"},it="place",add="60255a1c"},{q="Is Stonefield Farm dangerous?",a="The farmstead itself is generally safe and maintained by the family, but the surrounding fields are another matter. Like much of southern Elwynn Forest, wild beasts roam the outskirts, and local bandits and encroaching pests frequently threaten the livestock and crops. Travelers should keep their weapons ready when venturing out into the pastures or wandering down toward the nearby riverbanks and orchards.",al={"is stonefield farm dangerous","threats at stonefield farm","stonefield farm enemies"},it="danger",add="45c8f9cb"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human from Northshire, you can see the squabbles between the Stonefields and Maclures as a glimpse of rural life beyond the threat of bandits and gnolls."},kw={"elwynn forest","gramma stonefield","maclure","stonefield","stonefield farm","tommy joe"},rel={"zone:elwynn"},src={"Stonefield Farm"}}
E["subzone:stormwind-city"] = {t="subzone",n="Stormwind City",z="elwynn",s="Stormwind City leads the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance from its seat of power. Rebuilt after the First War, it is Azeroth's greatest remaining human stronghold since the northern kingdoms fell.",h="Stormwind City leads the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance from its seat of power.",sec={{t="A Beacon Rebuilt",b="Stormwind City rose over a thousand years ago, founded by Arathi descendants who migrated south. Its coastal ramparts sheltered a flourishing capital, where swift rivermills powered the city. In the First War, the Orcish Horde broke through its defenses and burned Stormwind to the ground.\n\nSir Anduin Lothar led the surviving refugees across the Great Sea to Lordaeron. After the Alliance won the Second War, the Stonemasons' Guild rebuilt the capital with white stone, canals and towering spires. The fortress now stands north of Elwynn Forest.",sp=0},{t="Heart of the Alliance",b="Stormwind City is mankind's chief refuge and stronghold after the Scourge shattered Lordaeron and the Third War left Dalaran heavily ruined. The disciplined Stormwind City Guard patrols its broad avenues and defensive walls. The Cathedral of Light's spires guide faith across the southern kingdoms.\n\nYet political troubles linger beneath the orderly districts and ceremonial gates. King Varian Wrynn has mysteriously vanished, and his young son Anduin sits on the throne. Highlord Bolvar Fordragon governs as regent, with the whispered counsel of royal advisor Lady Katrana Prestor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why was Stormwind rebuilt after the First War?",a="The Orcish Horde sacked and burned Stormwind during the First War. After the Grand Alliance of Lordaeron defeated the orcs in the Second War, human refugees reclaimed their ancestral kingdom. The royal court commissioned the Stonemasons' Guild to build a grander fortress city on the original ruins.",al={"who rebuilt stormwind","rebuilding of stormwind","why does stormwind look new"}},{q="Who rules Stormwind City right now?",a="Anduin Wrynn sits on the throne after his father, King Varian Wrynn, suddenly disappeared without explanation. Because Anduin is young, Highlord Bolvar Fordragon governs as regent and commands the Kingdom's defenses.",al={"who is king of stormwind","who runs stormwind","current ruler of stormwind"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why is Stormwind the main human capital instead of Lordaeron?",a="During the Third War, the undead plague and the Scourge devastated Lordaeron from within. With Lordaeron destroyed and other northern human realms devastated, Stormwind is the wealthiest, most intact and most populous human kingdom remaining on Azeroth.",al={"what happened to lordaeron","why not capital of lordaeron","is stormwind the last city"}},{q="What military forces protect the city?",a="The Stormwind City Guard keeps peace in the wards and along the battlement walls. The Kingdom's knights, soldiers garrisoned at Stormwind Keep and paladins affiliated with the Church of the Light maintain broader territorial defense and royal protection.",al={"who guards stormwind","stormwind army","city guards"}},{q="What is Stormwind City?",a="Stormwind City is the capital of the kingdom of Stormwind and the greatest human bastion left on Azeroth. Nestled north of Elwynn Forest along the western coast, it stands as the beating heart of the Alliance. Behind its towering white stone ramparts and deep canals lie thriving merchant districts, the seat of the Crown, and the Cathedral of Light, a beacon of faith for all who revere the Holy Light.",al={"what is stormwind","stormwind city overview","about stormwind city"},it="place",add="209accb7"},{q="What happened at Stormwind City?",a="Founded over a millennium ago by Arathi descendants, Stormwind weathered gnoll wars and troll assaults before facing utter devastation in the First War. The Orcish Horde besieged the capital, breached its defenses, and razed it to the ground, forcing survivors to flee north across the sea. After the Alliance triumphed in the Second War, the Stonemasons' Guild painstakingly rebuilt the city into the majestic stronghold standing today.",al={"stormwind history","what happened to stormwind","fall of stormwind"},it="history",add="38604972"},{q="Is Stormwind City dangerous?",a="Within its walls, Stormwind is one of the most secure settlements in the realm, patrolled constantly by the vigilant Stormwind City Guard. However, peace is not absolute. Shadows lurk in darker corners like the alleys of Old Town, political intrigue stirs in the royal court, and the kingdom's surrounding territories remain threatened by outlaws and encroaching monsters.",al={"is stormwind safe","is stormwind city dangerous","threats in stormwind"},it="danger",add="7f858f77"}},ang={["race:Human"]="For humans across Azeroth, Stormwind's white walls speak of endurance, survival and mankind's glory after the northern kingdoms were lost.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Stormwind is the chief military, naval and spiritual rallying point in the southern Eastern Kingdoms. It welcomes dwarves, gnomes and night elven envoys alike."},kw={"alliance","anduin","bolvar","elwynn","first war","stonemasons","stormwind","stormwind city","wrynn"},rel={"zone:stormwind","subzone:stormwind-keep","subzone:cathedral-of-light","subzone:valley-of-heroes","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:first-war","topic:alliance"},src={"Stormwind City"}}
E["subzone:stormwind-gate"] = {t="subzone",n="Stormwind Gate",z="elwynn",s="Stormwind Gate stands open between Elwynn Forest and Stormwind City, watched by sentries. Beyond its arch, stone monuments line the Valley of Heroes.",h="Stormwind Gate stands open between Elwynn Forest and Stormwind City, watched by sentries.",sec={{t="The Threshold of the Kingdom",b="The Stormwind City Guard holds this passage, and patrols march from the outer arch toward the Valley of Heroes. Unrest lingers in Elwynn, yet the iron and stone gates remain open. Travelers, merchants, and defenders returning from the road pass through toward the heart of the Alliance.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Stormwind Gate lead?",a="From Elwynn Forest, the gate opens onto the Valley of Heroes, Stormwind City’s grand entryway. Towering monuments to the Second War line the way.",al={"where does stormwind gate go","what is past the gate","stormwind entrance"},it="place"},{q="Why is the gate left open if Elwynn Forest is dangerous?",a="Stormwind keeps the passage open for trade and travel from Goldshire and across the Alliance. Guards watch for bandits and Defias activity in the woods as citizens and commerce pass through.",al={"why are the gates open","is stormwind gate closed","why open"}},{q="Who guards the gates?",a="The Stormwind City Guard garrisons the entryway. Two sentries watch outside in Elwynn Forest, two more guard the inner passage, and armed footmen patrol the bridge through the Valley of Heroes.",al={"stormwind gate guards","who defends the gate"},it="in_charge"},{q="Are there special events held at the gate?",a="Yes. The open ground around Stormwind Gate often hosts major citywide holidays and seasonal gatherings for the Alliance. It gives the city room to assemble beyond its crowded districts.",al={"holidays at stormwind gate","events at gate"}},{q="Is Stormwind Gate dangerous?",a="Not for members of the Alliance. The gate is heavily secured by Stormwind City Guards patrolling both sides of the threshold and the adjacent Valley of Heroes. However, hostile infiltrators or Horde travelers will find it nearly impossible to breach, as the stationed sentries will instantly attack any declared enemy of the crown on sight.",al={"is the gate safe","stormwind gate danger","stormwind gate safe"},it="danger",add="c23a16f5"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Stormwind Gate is a sign of safety and endurance. Traveling soldiers and young adventurers first glimpse the Grand Alliance’s majesty here.",["race:Human"]="For the people of Stormwind, passing back through these stone arches means coming home to safety after long journeys through Elwynn and beyond."},kw={"elwynn forest","goldshire","stormwind city guard","stormwind gate","valley of heroes"},rel={"zone:stormwind","zone:elwynn","subzone:valley-of-heroes","subzone:goldshire","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:alliance"},src={"Stormwind Gate"},nf=true}
E["subzone:thunder-falls"] = {t="subzone",n="Thunder Falls",z="elwynn",s="Bandits now hold a cottage beside the stream at Thunder Falls, high in northwestern Elwynn Forest.",h="Bandits now hold a cottage beside the stream at Thunder Falls, high in northwestern Elwynn Forest.",sec={{t="A Hidden Mountain Hollow",b="Above Mirror Lake, a mountain stream runs between the steep cliffs of Thunder Falls. From an unreachable cascade in the north, it spills down in falls on both sides. One pours into Mirror Lake, while the stream runs west toward Westfall’s rugged border.\n\nA cottage, a dock, and an outdoor forge stand beside the water. Bandits now claim the clearing.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How do you reach Thunder Falls?",a="From the northern side of Mirror Lake, a steep, narrow trail climbs into the hills beside the waterfall’s right side. Follow it into the ravine.",al={"how to get to thunder falls","thunder falls location","where is thunder falls"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="Who lives in the cottage at Thunder Falls?",a="The cottage appears to have belonged to a solitary fisherman or frontiersman. A dock, rowing boat, and outdoor anvil remain nearby, but bandits operating in Elwynn Forest now use the cottage as a remote hideout.",al={"who is at the cottage","thunder falls house","cottage bandits"},it="residents"},{q="Where does the river at Thunder Falls flow?",a="The stream runs through a narrow mountain gap from an upper cascade. It passes the cottage, then plunges down a steep waterfall near Westfall’s eastern boundary.",al={"where does the water go","thunder falls river"},it="place"},{q="What is Thunder Falls?",a="Thunder Falls is a secluded mountain ravine tucked away in the northwestern heights of Elwynn Forest. Fed by an inaccessible cascade dropping from the high northern bluffs, the river carves through a narrow gorge between double waterfalls, emptying down toward Mirror Lake on one side and cascading west toward the border of Westfall on the other. It is a quiet, hidden retreat featuring a solitary rural cottage, a small pier, and cold mountain waters.",al={"what is thunder falls","thunder falls lore","tell me about thunder falls"},it="place",add="1050bd39"},{q="Is Thunder Falls dangerous?",a="Despite its tranquil setting, you must tread carefully. Outlaws and Defias-affiliated bandits have made camp around the isolated cottage, taking advantage of its hidden, defensible location above the falls. In addition to hostile brigands, navigating the steep cliffs and roaring waterfalls requires caution, as one misplaced step can send you tumbling into the rapids below.",al={"is thunder falls safe","thunder falls bandits","threats at thunder falls"},it="danger",add="db2700a0"}},kw={"bandits","cottage","elwynn forest","mirror lake","thunder falls","waterfall"},rel={"quest:1861","zone:elwynn","zone:westfall"},src={"Thunder Falls"}}
E["subzone:tower-of-azora"] = {t="subzone",n="Tower of Azora",z="elwynn",s="At the Tower of Azora, Archmage Theocritus leads a scholarly outpost in eastern Elwynn Forest. The slender spire rises north of the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch, where its human master keeps watch over a silent magical feud with a hostile tower in the Redridge Mountains.",h="At the Tower of Azora, Archmage Theocritus leads a scholarly outpost in eastern Elwynn Forest.",sec={{t="A Spire of Arcane Vigilance",b="The Tower of Azora stands beside the eastern road to the Redridge Mountains. Gnome spellcasters staff most of the spire, where Archmage Theocritus guides their studies of strange curiosities and teaches wandering spellweavers. A wild magical aura surrounds the tower and sometimes warps nearby wildlife. Inside, gnome servants contend with enchanted household items and mutated insects that creep past the doorway.",sp=0},{t="The Feud with Ilgalar",b="The Tower of Azora wages a quiet war of scrying and sabotage. Atop the Redridge Mountains' eastern crags, the sinister Tower of Ilgalar belongs to renegade sorcerer Morganth. Theocritus and Morganth spy on one another through arcane means. They enlist daring adventurers to plant scrying relics such as the Eye of Azora, pierce Ilgalar's wards, and watch Morganth's dark machinations.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who rules the Tower of Azora?",a="Archmage Theocritus, an accomplished human wizard, presides over the Tower of Azora. He directs its servants and coordinates the tower's magical defenses against rival sorcerers.",al={"who leads the tower of azora","who is in charge here","tower of azora boss"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why are there so many gnomes here?",a="Most servants at the Tower of Azora are gnome researchers and acolytes. They help Archmage Theocritus with his studies, arcane experiments, and housekeeping when magic goes awry.",al={"why gnomes in elwynn tower","servants of azora"},it="residents"},{q="Who is the tower fighting against?",a="The Tower of Azora is locked in a magical rivalry with the Tower of Ilgalar in the Redridge Mountains, home to the evil sorcerer Morganth. Both towers spy on one another with scrying artifacts and contest each other's influence.",al={"azora enemy","tower feud","who is azora spying on"},it="conflict"},{q="What is the Eye of Azora on the top floor?",a="The Eye of Azora is an enchanted scrying focus on a table in the upper sanctum. Touching it lets an observer gaze across magical distance and watch the outskirts of the Tower of Ilgalar.",al={"orb on top floor","eye of azora","crystal ball azora"},it="power"},{q="What is the Tower of Azora?",a="The Tower of Azora is a prominent wizard's tower situated in central Elwynn Forest, east of Goldshire. Led by Theocritus, the Archmage of Azora, it serves as a magical sanctuary and study for arcane practitioners, staffed predominantly by gnomish servants and enchanters.",al={"tower of azora","what is this tower","about tower of azora"},it="place",add="e823b8a2"},{q="Is the Tower of Azora dangerous?",a="The tower is a safe refuge for Alliance travelers, offering shelter and training in enchanting. However, the potent magical aura radiating from the spire has been known to warp everyday objects and wildlife straying too close, forcing the servants within to deal with bizarre oddities like animated buckets and mutant butterflies.",al={"is tower of azora dangerous","danger at tower of azora","tower of azora threats"},it="danger",add="7c8bc76d"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage traveling beyond Stormwind, you can find a secluded place to study, arcane trainers, and a close view of the dangerous arts of remote divination at the tower.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you can take pride in seeing an arcane spire in human lands staffed by gnomes under Archmage Theocritus, a showcase of your people's mastery of the mystic arts."},kw={"azora","elwynn","enchanting","ilgalar","morganth","scrying","spire","theocritus"},rel={"zone:elwynn","subzone:tower-of-ilgalar","quest:94","zone:redridge","subzone:brackwell-pumpkin-patch","subzone:goldshire","topic:gnome"},src={"Tower of Azora"}}
E["subzone:westbrook-garrison"] = {t="subzone",n="Westbrook Garrison",z="elwynn",s="At Westbrook Garrison, Deputy Rainer's few guards watch Elwynn's western road. Gnolls and bandits threaten the border, and the outpost lacks the men and supplies to hold it alone.",h="At Westbrook Garrison, Deputy Rainer's few guards watch Elwynn's western road.",sec={{t="A Beleaguered Border Post",b="Westbrook Garrison watches the road where Elwynn Forest thins toward Westfall. Deputy Rainer and a handful of guards patrol the western roads, too few to cover them. Much of the Stormwind Army serves abroad, and indecision in the capital leaves the outpost without needed support.\n\nThieves grow bolder, and Riverpaw gnolls have overrun the southern woods. Marshal Dughan in Goldshire has sent no formal reinforcements, so the guards depend on travelers to help secure the highway.",sp=0},{t="The Menace of Forest's Edge",b="Riverpaw gnolls gather south of Forest's Edge, raiding supply lines and homesteads. The packs follow Hogger, a fearsome chieftain whose forces outnumber the garrison and overwhelm its guards with brute strength.\n\nA high bounty is posted across the outpost. It seeks fighters willing to enter the hills and bring down Hogger before the gnolls press farther east.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Westbrook Garrison so understaffed?",a="Most of the Stormwind Army serves abroad, while indecision among the House of Nobles in the capital leaves regional garrisons short of soldiers and supplies. Westbrook's commanders rely on wandering adventurers to help fill the gap.",al={"why so few guards","westbrook reinforcements","deputy rainer lacking troops"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is in command at the garrison?",a="Deputy Rainer commands Westbrook Garrison and answers to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire. His requests for more soldiers have largely gone unanswered.",al={"who leads westbrook garrison","deputy rainer role","westbrook commander"},it="in_charge"},{q="What threats does the garrison face?",a="Westbrook faces bandits from Westfall and Riverpaw gnolls camping in the surrounding woods. The gnolls follow their chieftain, Hogger.",al={"threats to westbrook","gnolls westbrook","who attacks westbrook garrison"},it="threat"},{q="What is the relation between Westbrook and Westfall?",a="Westbrook Garrison is Elwynn's last outpost on the western road before the bridge into Westfall. Its guards watch the border as lawlessness rises from the west.",al={"is westbrook in westfall","border to westfall"},it="ties"},{q="What is Westbrook Garrison?",a="Westbrook Garrison is a Stormwind Guard barracks standing near Forest's Edge on the western border of Elwynn Forest. Situated just across the river from Westfall, this military outpost guards the primary road linking the capital's heartland with the western plains. Though fortified with a sturdy guard tower and barracks, it currently serves as the final, struggling line of defense protecting local homesteads from outlaws and feral gnolls.",al={"what is westbrook","westbrook garrison elwynn","about westbrook garrison"},it="place",add="2e1647ed"},{q="Is Westbrook Garrison dangerous?",a="The garrison itself remains a secure refuge held by the Stormwind Guard, but the surrounding wilderness is perilous. The woods directly to the south teem with the vicious Riverpaw gnoll pack, led by the monstrous chieftain Hogger. In addition, Defias bandits spill across the border from Westfall to prey upon travelers, making any unescorted journey off the garrison's immediate grounds hazardous.",al={"is westbrook dangerous","danger at westbrook","is westbrook garrison safe"},it="danger",add="9e78a278"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a Warrior, you can help Westbrook's overstretched guards hold back wilderness predators and fight the gnoll war bands.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion traveling from Elwynn toward Westfall, you can help secure Westbrook's perimeter and claim the bounty on Hogger to guard the kingdom's western border."},kw={"deputy rainer","elwynn forest","forest's edge","hogger","marshal dughan","riverpaw","westbrook garrison","westfall"},rel={"npc:deputy-rainer","quest:176","quest:11","subzone:forest-s-edge","subzone:goldshire","npc:marshal-dughan","zone:elwynn","zone:westfall"},src={"Westbrook Garrison"}}
E["zone:elwynn"] = {t="zone",n="Elwynn Forest",z="elwynn",s="Elwynn Forest is good green country, and Stormwind lives off its timber and gold, its fish and grain. It ought to be a peaceful place. But vermin, stray beasts and brigands roam the woods. So Northshire Abbey sends its recruits out to deal with them.",h="Elwynn Forest is good green country, and Stormwind lives off its timber and gold, its fish and grain.",sec={{t="The Breadbasket of the Realm",b="The forest runs south from Stormwind's gates, all the way down to the Nazferiti River. It rains a good deal here, and the fields are the richer for it. Behind the fields grow thick hardwoods, and their timber goes to the capital. Carts roll up from Goldshire and the Eastvale Logging Camp, loaded with grain and livestock, lumber and raw copper. Elwynn breeds horses too, and knights and travelers all over the kingdom are glad to own a sturdy Evendale horse.",sp=0},{t="A Precarious Peace",b="But these are uneasy days. The Stormwind Army is busy far away, so the marshals and deputies must make do with recruits who have never been tested. Kobolds have overrun the Fargodeep and Jasperlode mines. Riverpaw gnolls prowl the southwestern borders, and murlocs have taken the shores of Stone Cairn Lake and Crystal Lake.\n\nEven the wolves are newcomers. They fled the corruption across the river in Duskwood, and came over into Elwynn.",sp=0},{t="The Red Bandana Threat",b="The Defias Brotherhood has spread through Elwynn as an organized band of outlaws. Its members came from Edwin VanCleef’s Stonemasons Guild after bitter disputes over pay with the House of Nobles.\n\nThey have taken the Northshire Vineyards, the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch, Jerod’s Landing, and Mirror Lake Orchard. Rumors say their agents are guiding nearby gnolls and kobolds to unsettle the realm. Guards Rolf and Malakai went to investigate murlocs near Stone Cairn Lake; both were killed and left on its banks.",sp=1,bt={"defias.masons"}}},faq={{q="Why is the Stormwind Guard barely policing the forest?",a="Stormwind’s armed forces are stretched thin. The kingdom sent large forces south into Stranglethorn Vale, piling up debt and draining local manpower. Westbrook Garrison and Goldshire now rely on small crews and volunteer recruits to face bandits, gnolls, and murlocs.",al={"where are the guards","why no stormwind army","why is elwynn undefended"},it="threat"},{q="Why are there kobolds inside all the mines?",a="Guards are scarce, and kobolds have swarmed into Fargodeep Mine, Jasperlode Mine, and Echo Ridge Mine for gold and minerals. They drove out the human prospectors and miners, then defended their claims with candles, crude picks, and scavenged tools.",al={"why are kobolds in the mines","elwynn kobolds","fargodeep infested"},it="threat"},{q="Who are the bandits wearing red masks?",a="The red-masked bandits are the Defias Brotherhood, outlaws who have seized farms and mines across Elwynn and Westfall. The People's Militia at Sentinel Hill in Westfall is still trying to learn who leads them and why.",al={"red masks","red bandana bandits","who are the defias in elwynn"},it="threat"},{q="Where does the road south lead?",a="The road south crosses the Nazferiti River into Duskwood. Once peaceful, the territory has fallen into unnatural darkness and is infested with undead, monstrous spiders, and ravenous beasts.",al={"what is across the river","where does duskwood bridge go","bridge across the nazferiti"},it="place"},{q="What is the feud between the Maclures and Stonefields?",a="The Stonefields and Maclures are neighboring farming families in southern Elwynn, locked in a bitter, longstanding grudge. Their younger kin, Maybell Maclure and Tommy Joe Stonefield, have secretly fallen in love, making the rivalry more fraught.",al={"maclure vs stonefield","elwynn farm rivalry","stonefield maclure feud"},it="conflict"},{q="What is the Tower of Azora?",a="The Tower of Azora is an arcane spire beside the road between Goldshire and the Eastvale Logging Camp. Secluded mages live there, including Theocritus, who studies the region’s leylines and conducts magical research beyond the direct oversight of Stormwind’s Wizard’s Sanctum.",al={"tower on the road to eastvale","wizard tower elwynn","who lives in the tower of azora"},it="place"},{q="What is Elwynn Forest?",a="Elwynn Forest is the verdant heartland of the Kingdom of Stormwind. Nestled below the foothills of the Burning Steppes, these ancient woods of stately hardwoods, rolling hills, and rushing rivers supply the kingdom with lumber, fish, crops, and ore. Its majestic canopy shelters small farmsteads, winding country roads, and towns like Goldshire, while the capital city of Stormwind watches over the realm from the northwestern ridge.",al={"what is elwynn","where am i","elwynn forest lore"},it="place",add="23586590"},{q="What happened to Elwynn Forest in the past?",a="Founded centuries ago by human migrants of the Arathi bloodline, Elwynn flourished into a thriving realm. During the First War, however, the Orcish Horde swept through the forest, burning its woodland glades and encircling Stormwind City before razing Goldshire and the capital. After the Second War, Supreme Commander Turalyon helped oversee the repatriation of its people and the forest was rebuilt anew, leaving only scattered, rotting catapults as reminders of the invasion.",al={"history of elwynn forest","elwynn forest past","elwynn first war"},it="history",add="4e6f8475"},{q="Is Elwynn Forest dangerous?",a="Though Elwynn appears idyllic, its peaceful exterior hides rising turmoil. Kobolds have overrun the realm's crucial gold mines, while hostile Riverpaw gnolls raid from the western border. Vicious murlocs have established camps around Crystal Lake and Stone Cairn Lake, ambushing guards and travelers alike. Worse, the red-masked Defias Brotherhood works from the shadows, occupying orchards and farmsteads while Stormwind's forces struggle to maintain control.",al={"is elwynn safe","elwynn forest threats","threats in elwynn"},it="danger",add="2f8050d9"},{q="Is this part of Stormwind?",a="Yes, Elwynn Forest is the core territory of the Kingdom of Stormwind. The forest directly borders the capital city's gates and feeds its markets with lumber from Eastvale, crops from rural farmsteads, and ore from regional mines. The Stormwind Guard maintains outposts throughout the woods, including Westbrook Garrison and Northshire Valley, though royal resources are currently stretched thin across the realm.",al={"is elwynn stormwind","stormwind kingdom territory","elwynn allegiance"},it="place",add="41d1722e"},{q="Why is it so peaceful here compared to everywhere else?",a="Elwynn sits in the sheltered center of the kingdom, right beneath the protective walls of Stormwind City. Unlike Duskwood to the south, which fell to a creeping magical curse, or Westfall to the west, which was abandoned to drought and banditry, Elwynn saw extensive rebuilding after the Second War. Its close proximity to the throne keeps it shielded from the worst horrors lurking in neighboring lands.",al={"why is elwynn peaceful","elwynn vs duskwood","why is elwynn not ruined"},it="history",add="36c6d40e"},{q="What is Goldshire?",a="Goldshire is the central crossroads village of Elwynn Forest, located just south of Northshire and southeast of Stormwind City. Founded centuries ago, it serves as the vital hub linking trade roads to Westfall, the Redridge Mountains, and Duskwood. It hosts busy crafters, local trainers, and the famous Lion's Pride Inn, offering hospitality to travelers passing through the heart of the kingdom.",al={"goldshire","tell me about goldshire","goldshire lore"},it="place",add="7bf05012"},{q="Who is Marshal Dughan and why does everyone send me to him?",a="Marshal Dughan is the municipal commander and chief law enforcer for Goldshire and the surrounding forest. Stationed in town, he oversees local security, coordinates regional patrols, and attempts to protect travelers and supply lines. Because the Stormwind military is overextended elsewhere, Dughan relies heavily on capable adventurers to investigate threats and restore order across Elwynn.",al={"marshal dughan","who is dughan","dughan goldshire"},it="in_charge",add="2eb13bb0"},{q="Does Marshal Dughan answer to Stormwind?",a="Yes, Marshal Dughan is an officer of the Stormwind Guard and answers directly to the kingdom's high command in Stormwind City. He enforces the crown's laws and attempts to uphold royal authority throughout the central forest, though he must constantly petition the capital for troops and supplies that rarely arrive.",al={"dughan stormwind","who does dughan report to","is dughan stormwind guard"},it="ties",add="68a6801b"},{q="Why did I start at Northshire Abbey?",a="Northshire Valley is a sheltered, fortified haven designed to train and enlist promising new recruits for the Kingdom of Stormwind. Guarded behind stone walls and natural cliffs, the valley houses Northshire Abbey, where novice warriors, priests, paladins, and other aspirants hone their craft and assist local commanders before marching out into the wider world.",al={"why northshire","northshire start","starting in northshire"},it="arrival",add="6c2b38d9"},{q="What is Northshire Abbey?",a="Northshire Abbey is the historic seat of the Holy Order of Northshire Clerics, an order of the Holy Light that aided Stormwind through its darkest eras. Comprising the Main Hall, Hall of Arms, and Library Wing, it once sheltered the Guardian Medivh during his coma and preserved sacred tomes like the Tome of Divinity. Rebuilt after the Second War, it now trains recruits and champions of the Light.",al={"northshire abbey lore","what is northshire","the abbey in northshire"},it="place",add="f22f39d1"},{q="Who is Marshal McBride?",a="Marshal McBride is the municipal law enforcer and military commander in charge of Northshire Valley. Based at Northshire Abbey, he oversees local defenses, monitors threats from the infested Echo Ridge Mine and encroaching Defias brigands, and recruits capable new citizens into service for the defense of the realm.",al={"marshal mcbride","mcbride northshire","who is mcbride"},it="in_charge",add="c283ebda"},{q="What is the Fargodeep Mine?",a="The Fargodeep Mine is an abandoned gold and copper mine located south of Goldshire. Once an essential source of revenue and metal for Stormwind's treasury, the mine fell into chaos when a clan of kobolds invaded its tunnels. Now overrun, it remains a contested hazard right near local farmsteads, prompting Marshal Dughan to send adventurers into its depths to scout and clear out the infestation.",al={"fargodeep mine","fargodeep","fargodeep lore"},it="place",add="16daccd8"},{q="Who are the Riverpaw gnolls and why are they attacking us?",a="The Riverpaw pack is a savage clan of hyena-like gnolls entrenched along the western border of Elwynn near Westbrook Garrison. Aggressive and predatory, they have long contested human expansion and raided farms and unwary travelers. They have set up encampments along the Forest's Edge and Stone Cairn Lake, pushing aggressively into human lands.",al={"riverpaw gnolls","why do riverpaw attack","riverpaw pack"},it="threat",add="e239f261"},{q="Are the Riverpaw gnolls working for someone?",a="While gnolls usually act out of raw ferocity and greed, rumors across the forest suggest they may be in league with the Defias Brotherhood. Strange ties and bounties, including dealings with shady collectors near Ridgepoint Tower, hint that the bandits may be arming or coordinating with the gnolls to destabilize Elwynn's western frontier.",al={"who leads riverpaw","are gnolls with defias","riverpaw defias connection"},sp=1,it="ties",add="da4445a3"},{q="Why is everyone so worried about murlocs by the river?",a="Murlocs have moved in force into the waterways of Elwynn, infesting Crystal Lake and Stone Cairn Lake. These primitive amphibious creatures are fiercely territorial, ambushing local fishermen, travelers, and town patrols. Guard Thomas fears that if their expanding shoreline settlements are left unchecked, they will overrun local roads and push their skirmishes right into Goldshire itself.",al={"murloc threat elwynn","why worry about murlocs","murloc problem"},it="threat",add="29c0080a"},{q="What happened to Rolf and Malakai?",a="Guards Rolf and Malakai were Stormwind sentries dispatched to investigate growing murloc activity near the eastern waterways and Stone Cairn Lake. They have not reported back, and Guard Thomas asks travelers to investigate.",al={"rolf and malakai","lost guards elwynn","what happened to guards hartford and stone"},sp=1,it="history",add="f8d7f725"},{q="What is going on at the Eastvale Logging Camp?",a="The Eastvale Logging Camp is the heart of Elwynn's bustling timber industry, nestled in the eastern woods along the border with the Redridge Mountains. Its loggers fell the forest's massive hardwoods to provide lumber for construction, wagons, and fortifications throughout Stormwind's realm, though hostile wolves and bears frequently threaten its work crews.",al={"eastvale logging camp","eastvale lumber","what is eastvale"},it="place",add="0c4f3fe8"},{q="Where does all this lead after Elwynn?",a="Once you finish assisting Marshal Dughan, the roads from Goldshire branch out toward harsher frontiers. The western bridge across the river Nazferiti leads to the dust and wind of Westfall, where the Defias hold sway. To the east lies the elevated frontier of the Redridge Mountains, while crossing the southern bridges takes you into the cursed, haunted gloom of Duskwood.",al={"where to after elwynn","next zone after elwynn","after elwynn forest"},it="next_step",add="9effb187"},{q="What is Westfall like?",a="Westfall is an arid, windswept agricultural territory southwest of Elwynn. Once the breadbasket of the kingdom, its rolling pastures now lie fallow and dry, infested by rogue mechanical harvest watchers, ravenous carrion birds, and bandits. The Defias Brotherhood holds almost complete control over the region, leaving only a desperate local militia at Sentinel Hill to resist them.",al={"what is westfall","about westfall","westfall overview"},it="place",add="cd54a445"},{q="How did I end up in Elwynn Forest?",a="If you are human, Elwynn Forest is the heartland of your people. You likely took your first steps in the sheltered valley of Northshire Abbey, answering the call of the realm to train your abilities and aid the local authorities. Once you dealt with the early troubles in the valley, Marshal McBride directed you south along the road to Goldshire. Travelers of other races usually journey here from the Deeprun Tram into Stormwind City, stepping through the capital's grand gates directly out into the forest.",al={"how did i get here","why am i in elwynn forest","how did i get to elwynn","how did i end up here"},it="arrival",add="4080ef4d"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Elwynn Forest?",a="With Stormwind's army stretched thin across the realm, Elwynn's defense has fallen to local deputies and able-bodied recruits like you. Marshal Dughan in Goldshire needs help clearing out kobolds infesting the gold mines, repelling Riverpaw gnolls along the western border, and fighting off vicious murlocs around the lakes. At the same time, red-masked Defias bandits have overrun local farms and orchards, while squabbling landowners like the Maclures and Stonefields need their disputes resolved. Once you help restore order here, the road leads west into Westfall or east toward the Redridge Mountains.",al={"what should i do in elwynn","what am i doing here","what is my mission in elwynn forest","why am i here"},it="purpose",add="f92572cc"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, you begin in the ancestral heart of the kingdom. You train at Northshire Abbey before setting out to defend your homeland from bandits, beasts, and political ruin.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you find Elwynn crossed by the Defias Brotherhood’s shadow, with thievery, smuggled goods, and underground rebel signals.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you find copper veins in Echo Ridge, Fargodeep, and Jasperlode. Kobolds infest these mines, but they remain an important early proving ground.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help protect the Alliance’s primary human kingdom. Stormwind City depends on Elwynn’s lumber, ore, and grain routes."},kw={"defias","eastvale","elwynn","elwynn forest","fargodeep","goldshire","hogger","jasperlode","nazferiti","northshire","northshire abbey","vancleef"},rel={"zone:stormwind","subzone:goldshire","subzone:northshire-abbey","zone:westfall","zone:duskwood","zone:redridge","subzone:fargodeep-mine","quest:65"},m={levels="1-10"},src={"Elwynn Forest (Classic)","Elwynn Forest"}}
